inl for_d_compiler_bugs () = Task ("FOR-D-COMPILER-BUGS", "Six FOR-D repro samples: runaway match recursion without EJP0040, multiline scrutinee, multiline type application, nominal phantom parameter, GADT match constraint, runtime existential unpack; 2026-10-12 compiler lane: match_multiline_scrutinee is the parser offside rule (application needs argument lines right of the head); fix drafted, not applied: compiler-lane/ford-match-scrutinee.ps1 (dry run ok) adds continuation_column to BlockParsingEnv so the match keyword column is the scrutinee offside line; multiline_type_application_dropped has the same cause in root_type apply; open type-system repros: gadt constraint subset, nominal phantom parameter, existential unpack; runaway_inline_match_recursion reached 1.9 GB in a probe (killed); 18:20 the offside fix (continuation_column) is in spiral_compiler.fs for both cores and in the single-flight Debug build of 18:19 (0 errors); match_multiline_scrutinee + frontier/smoke not yet run against it; 20:03 in the same suite the 6 FOR-D repros run as new rows: match_multiline_scrutinee now compiles (exit 0, the offside fix works); still open: multiline_type_application_dropped (type error; same offside cause in root_type apply, next), gadt_match_loses_constraint (type error), nominal_phantom_parameter (nominal constructor type error), runaway_inline_match_recursion (20 s timeout), runtime_existential_unpack (cannot dyn an existential); 20:08: multiline_type_application_dropped fixed: root_type's apply now takes the start column of the head's line as the offside floor (min with col d), so arguments on a deeper-indented next line belong to the application; verified single-flight Debug 20:08: compiles, C exit 0; match_multiline_scrutinee still exit 0; 2 of 6 FOR-D repros fixed; the fix lives once in the now-shared BlockParsing; 03:44 all six repros resolved: match_multiline_scrutinee and multiline_type_application_dropped fixed 10-12 (blessed); runaway_inline_match_recursion stops with EJP0011 (INLINE-DEPTH-GUARD, blessed 01:16); gadt_match_loses_constraint and nominal_phantom_parameter fixed by the Tibia lane's GADT-ONCE (blessed 01:16, both cores); runtime_existential_unpack is by design per the user (run-time existentials are compile-time only), now a negative sample with expected_error_runtime_existentials_are_compile_time_only", Feature, P2, D7, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,parteval", "current", "current")
