inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_5 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 5u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night candidate primitive: a portable which-executable (env lookup, PATH split by platform, file_system.file_exists) from the Kino toolchain port runs on rust, fsharp and gleam (job tmp/night/civil/toolchain.spi); tonight also gave file_exists a Gleam arm and (</>) a portable default, both prerequisites for an fs slice that works beyond Rust.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_6 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 6u32, "2026-10-19T12:19Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:19 lap 1 grain: the portable which-executable prototype (resolver: option, env var, fallbacks OnPath/FileAt; typed found union ByOption/ByEnvironment/ByFallback) moved from job tmp/night/civil into spiral/lab/WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (toolchain.spi + package.spiproj pointing at ../../lib), the first fs/process primitive candidate Next: HEAVY QUEUE: Cells --gate on lab/WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB/toolchain.spi (rust, fsharp, gleam; ~3 min) to re-prove it from its new home, then decide its lib module name")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_7 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:16Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:16 lap 2 grain: lab gate of toolchain.spi from its lab home fails 0/4 (gleam failed first, rust and fsharp not_run, 0 type errors, so it compiles and fails at runtime or in the target build); the 10-17 night run passed in job tmp, so the move (packageDir ../../lib, tree core) or a lib change since then is the suspect Next: HEAVY QUEUE 2 rerun with -NotebookOut to read the failing cell output")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_8 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 8u32, "2026-10-19T14:49Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:49 lap 3 grain: the 0/4 lab gate was the uppercase-mount PackageErrors bug (fixed in Cells mounts.ex), not toolchain.spi; the same draft passed on 10-17 from a lowercase job-tmp folder Next: re-gate after the core switch (queue 3)")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_9 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 9u32, "2026-10-19T18:14Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:14 lap 4 grain: promotion target chosen: lab toolchain.spi (resolver: explicit option, then env var, then PATH candidates in order; python, cc, rustc, a real PATH probe; 4/4 test blocks after the core switch) belongs in eoie/src/workspace_primitives beside files/clock/console/rooted as module toolchain, so eoie tool-finding verbs wrap it; offered to the eoie lane (it owns eoie/src) Next: when the eoie lane moves it, delete the lab copy; else move it myself after a go from that lane")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_10 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 10u32, "2026-10-19T18:20Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 14:20 toolchain resolver moved into eoie as src/workspace_primitives/toolchain.spi (module toolchain). Ported to eoie idiom: core-only unions (tool_source, tool_sources rec union instead of list, tool_found with NotFound instead of option), tool_probe record with string-or-empty fields, real probe as one-line host primitives (std::env::var, split_paths + EXE_SUFFIX, is_file), so the test blocks compile with plain rustc and no lib. Resolvers python_tool/cc_tool/rustc_tool keep main's order (option, env, PATH candidates). 4 test blocks 4/4; a mutated expectation fails 1/4. Registered in eoie_dev_spiral_tests (25 notebooks, regenerated +2 lines); the 10 workspace_primitives consumers stay byte-identical. Next: eoie tool-finding verbs wrap tool_resolved.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_11 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 11u32, "2026-10-19T18:21Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:21 lap 4 grain: the eoie lane ported the resolver into eoie/src/workspace_primitives/toolchain.spi (eoie packages cannot use lib, so lists became a recursive union and the PATH probe is std::env Rust; 4/4 tests, a mutated expectation fails 1/4, 10 consumer crates regenerate byte-identical); the untracked lab copy is removed Next: next primitive slice: processes with timeout and elapsed (the most repeated pwsh glue), designed in the same no-lib style")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_12 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 12u32, "2026-10-21T23:27Z", "main", "19:27 the 'processes with timeout and elapsed' slice already exists, in eoie (where this item's primitives moved on 10-19): rust_std_process/model.spi has elapsed_millis, and 'eoie job run|start <label> <timeout-ms> <program>' supervises a process tree with a timeout and reports elapsed_ms, exit and output sizes; main used them for every job today. So no new primitive is needed. What remains is migrating the repeated pwsh glue (Start-Process + WaitForExit + Stopwatch patterns in spiral's tmp/scripts and the lab) onto eoie job run, which is eoie-first work for the eoie lane (EOIE-JOBS). This item's next slice moves on to the next most repeated glue: file hashing (measured: Get-FileHash appears 56 times in 41 spiral/lab .ps1 scripts, mostly for 16-char hash stamps and copy verification).")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_13 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 13u32, "2026-10-22T09:22Z", "eoie", "05:22 groom: the premise 'eoie packages cannot use lib' (10-19 note) no longer holds: lib staging ships in release ABC and E/E2 put 113 packages on lib. The direction is now two-sided: generic primitives go INTO lib/spiral (tonight main added sm'.listed, trim_end_suffix, env try_get_environment_variable and command-line argument accessors, a process module; convert.try_convert already existed), and eoie keeps only an OS boundary package for what lib does not cover (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY note 7: 1500 host macros, 517 of them text ops that belong to sm'). Remaining lib candidates are listed there: total fs read/write variants. eoie's own workspace_primitives package becomes the boundary package or dissolves into lib.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_14 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 14u32, "2026-10-24T01:46Z", "main", "2026-10-23 21:46 main: user direction 2026-10-23 21:4x: 'eoie wasn't using lib or code, rewrote most of the stuff, we gotta take the primitives eoie advanced then move to lib what isn't there already, but careful with bloat'. Method per eoie primitive (workspace_primitives and the other boundary modules): (a) lib already has an equivalent -> eoie switches to it and the eoie copy is deleted; (b) generic and missing from lib -> it moves to lib in lib's layout (one home per concept, backend_switch or run_target arms, a lib test block); (c) eoie-specific -> it stays. Bloat guard: one function per concept, no thin aliases, no option flags that only one caller uses. The census table (primitive, verdict, lib target) goes in the next note before any move.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_15 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 15u32, "2026-10-24T04:53Z", "main", "2026-10-24 00:53 main: survey of eoie's generic primitives against lib (user 10-23: take the primitives eoie advanced, move to lib what isn't there, no bloat). SWITCH eoie to lib, which already has these: rust_std_string (contains/starts_with/ends_with/replace/trim/equals) to sm'; workspace_primitives byte_at/byte_find/byte_slice/byte_len to sm' index_of/slice/length; environment_value to env.get_environment_variable (env.spi:53); file_present to file_system.exists; ascii_lowercase to sm'.to_lower; unix_ms/ms_since to date_time.now; the 3 private JSON unescapers (agile_note_model, agile_task_inspection, eoie_memory_model) to json_scan.parse_string once JSON-UNICODE-ESCAPES lands; hash_integrity's sha256 to crypto.sha256. MOVE to lib (missing there, generic): (1) checked atomic file replace (workspace_primitives replace_file_checked: unique pending file, rename over the target, read back and compare) as file_system.replace_checked; (2) lexical path containment (rooted_path / rooted_path_problem) as file_system.is_within; (3) executable lookup on PATH (on_path / path_executable / tool_path, also eoie env pins F4) as env.find_on_path. Each moves with one lib test block, and eoie then calls the lib version (EOIE-LIB-REUSE).")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_16 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 16u32, "2026-10-24T04:58Z", "main", "2026-10-24 00:58 main: the 3 MOVE primitives are drafted as one lib slice, %TEMP%\\lib-fs-primitives\\apply.ps1 (dry run clean): file_system.replace_checked (pending file, rename over the target, readback compare), file_system.is_within (lexical containment on normalize_path output, separator-checked so a/bc is not under a/b), file_system.find_on_path (env PATH split by sm'.split_list, platform executable suffix, listm'.try_find over file_exists), each with a rust test block, written only against lib (no host macros). Held until x's normalize_path land on file_system.spi (concurrent-edit risk); x asked to ping. Then gate+land through the gate kit, and eoie switches its workspace_primitives copies to these (EOIE-LIB-REUSE).")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_17 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 17u32, "2026-10-28T10:29Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl task_PS1_TO_SPIRAL () = Task ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", "After HOPAC-SPEED reaches state of the art (user): rewrite each repo's .ps1 scripts (build, test, init, workflow) as Spiral programs compiled to Rust, living in their own repos, compiled and run through the spiral CLI, using WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB; no shelling out to pwsh or eoie; 2026-10-13 23:34 user decision: now waits on EOIE-ONE-CALL instead of HOPAC-SPEED (scripts become eoie one-call verbs / Spiral programs)", Epic, P1, D7, 15u32, Paused, "PIPELINES-GREEN", "scripts,spiral,repos,main", "current", "current")
