inl ci_spiral_wasm_native () = Task ("CI-SPIRAL-WASM-NATIVE", "spiral Windows CI 07:03: apps/wasm built through bash/WSL (cargo: command not found); now native on every platform like apps/spiral: near-workspaces default-features=false (its build.rs install panicked Unsupported platform), sandbox fetched at runtime; RUST-OK apps/wasm locally on Windows; confirm on next push; local preflight of the steps after wasm on Windows: apps/plot RUST-OK (native), scripts/outdated.ps1 exit 0; polyglot CI path (spiral app, parser, lib/fsharp 6/6, wasm, lib/math has no F# cells) checked; lib/spiral/build.ps1 step: the two notebooks that failed yesterday (file_system, parsing) now exit 0 when run alone (outputs to tmp), the other 36 passed yesterday; 20:0x CI on the 18:34 push: dice windows-2025 still red here: contract build runs process_rust wasm through SPIRAL_WASM_COMMAND with -Linux (bash on the Windows runner) from D:\\a\\dice\\spiral, `workspace/target/release/spiral_wasm: No such file` (exit 127), while dice scripts/init.ps1 builds and ships spiral_wasm.exe under polyglot/deps/spiral/workspace; needs the native (non-Linux) invocation with the .exe from the same checkout; 21:5x decided: dice windows contract run stays on the WSL path (spiral_wasm deploys into near_workspaces.sandbox_worker, Linux-only), so it is WSL work and waits for the WSL-last phase; no Windows skip switch; 03:55 local no-WSL repro: workspace/target/release/spiral_wasm is an ELF leftover (2026-10-07) beside spiral_wasm.exe (PE, 2026-10-08). Native exe --help exits 0. exe -w a file -t debug retries 15 times with Could not initialize sandbox node (near-workspaces 0.11.1 InitFailure) then exits 0, because spiral_wasm.run turns an exhausted Error into Ok and main returns 0. near-sandbox-utils platform() is None on Windows through 0.15.1 (linux x86 and darwin arm only). The GitHub windows runner has no ELF, so bash -Linux reports the unsuffixed path missing. Pointing that job at the exe would not run the sandbox; 2026-10-13 23:57 sweep lane: spiral Windows CI builds apps/wasm natively: run 38327352498 windows job 115069009880 printed RUST-OK apps/wasm, shipped spiral_wasm.exe to workspace/target/release, then RUST-OK apps/plot (the job was later cancelled only because ubuntu failed first under fail-fast); run 38389311114 windows reached the native cargo build of spiral_wasm before the same cancel; dice windows contract stays WSL-last (WORKFLOW-END-TO-END); open gap for that phase: spiral_wasm exits 0 when the NEAR sandbox never initializes (run turns an exhausted Error into Ok), a silent false pass; 2026-10-14 00:22 closing on run 38327352498 (windows job 115069009880: RUST-OK apps/wasm natively, spiral_wasm.exe shipped, RUST-OK apps/plot); the newest run 38508233036 (d94dc380) never reached it on windows (cancelled by fail-fast after ubuntu failed in the apps/wasm Kino step, see CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION); the spiral_wasm exit-0-on-sandbox-failure false pass stays open for the WSL-last dice contract work (WORKFLOW-END-TO-END)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "ci,spiral,wasm,windows", "current", "current")
