inl self_checking_samples () = Task ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", "Samples and tests as self-checking source (user design session 2026-10-12, nothing fixed yet; dogfood before committing): no prose, code only; expectations live inline in the source of truth, expect-test style (ppx_expect, Rust expect-test/insta, Zig test blocks): a promote run rewrites the expected blocks in place, git diff is the review, a clean run leaves the file untouched, dev mode can persist cell results and clear them after a successful run; the oracle backend is configurable per file or cell (C default) and other backends are checked against it, replacing hand-written per-backend copies and the uncommittable cache EXPECTED.tsv; end state: .spi itself is the notebook (compiler-understood test blocks with inline expectations, Zig/Rust #[test]-like), .livemd becomes a view, so edits are plain file edits; negative samples stay as test blocks whose expectation is a diagnostic (rustc UI tests, clang expected-error); multi-file packages must work (package-manager litmus): measure the dice symlink cost on Windows, then compare compiler-resolved path dependencies (Cargo path/workspaces) with junctions. Phases: 1 benchmark the same sample family through the matrix and through Kino (warm workers, parallel cells: KINO-PARALLEL-CACHE); 2 measure dice symlink package resolution on Windows; 3 dogfood one family (ebpf_* 27 samples) as an inline-expectation file with promote mode, keeping matrix rows byte-identical; 4 decide; phase 2 first look 2026-10-12: dice reaches lib through two chained symlinks (dice/deps/polyglot -> polyglot, polyglot/deps/spiral -> spiral); raw I/O over the 315 lib .spi/.spir files through the chain is 1.4-2.5x slower warm (hundreds of ms at worst, not the main cost); the compiler normalizes package paths with Path.GetFullPath, which collapses .. but does not resolve links, so a package identity is the path spelling: the same lib reached as dice\\deps\\polyglot\\deps\\spiral\\lib and as spiral\\lib is two packages (parsed, cached and watched twice), the likelier cost and a blocker for one canonical identity per package in a package manager; next: time a dice compile via the link path vs the direct path, then try canonicalizing package roots (FinalPath/ResolveLinkTarget) in the compiler; test block prototype 2026-10-12: survey of the 39 lib notebooks: 1,904 cells, 364 test cells (44 static, 12 in .spir real code, 11 print_code), targets fsharp 169 / cuda 126 / rust 107 / gleam 93 / typescript 93 / lua 34 / c 1, per-target options (rust -d crates, gleam -t javascript -d), all timeouts default; test cells hold top-level-only statements (open, nominal, #r), so a test is a scoped group of top-level statements, not a function: syntax `///> target opts` lines then `test name [static] [print_code] =` with an indented body; semantics = file prefix up to the block + the body (Kino notebook-prefix semantics, Spiral is top-down so position preserves scope); compiler: blockParsingParse returns Error [] for a block starting with `test` (both cores; the same no-statement result as comment-only blocks), unbuilt; converter livemd -> spi/spir with test blocks reproduces the current exports byte for byte in 38 of 40 files (benchmark and lustre carry stale doc text from cell outputs); spi -> livemd adapter round-trips all 37 notebooks with every test source preserved (order of .spir tests and one directive line moved); next: run original vs regenerated notebooks through Kino and compare per-test results, then the build with the parser change; dice package identity fix (2026-10-12, unbuilt): canonical_directory in the shared SpiProj schema resolves every path component with Directory.ResolveLinkTarget (symlinks and junctions), used for packageDir/moduleDir combines and the default package dir, so a package reached through deps/polyglot/deps/spiral and through spiral/ is one package; no matrix path crosses a link (checked), so sample outputs must stay byte-identical; to measure: a dice compile through the link path before and after, and dice/alphabet packageDir pointing straight at the sibling ../spiral/lib (CI and local init already create that layout); dice measured 2026-10-12 (cold compile of lib/dice.spi to Rust, one process each): old compiler through the symlinks 19.3 s, new compiler (canonical package dirs + tonight batch) through the symlinks 17.4 s, new compiler with packageDir ../spiral/lib (no links) 18.0 s; the new compiler output is byte-identical through links and without them (one package identity), so dice can drop the links; a single cold compile shows no real symlink cost, so the slowdown the user saw likely sits elsewhere (cargo/rustc over symlinked dirs, Kino watching, repeated warm compiles): measure those next. Test blocks: with the new parser all 364 test blocks embedded in 35 lib files compile to byte-identical C (pristine-copy check; an earlier failure came from stale files in a reused copy, not from test blocks); 2026-10-12 lib/spiral migrated (unstaged): the 39 lib notebooks are now their .spi (370 test blocks; sm' keeps its real-mode code and tests in sm'_real.spir); the 39 .livemd are deleted; Kino document domain (apps/kino/spi/document.spi, Spiral) gained to_spi_tested/to_spir_tested (test cells -> test blocks named by heading) and from_spi/parse_spi (blocks -> test cells), byte-identical to the validated prototype on all 37 notebooks (644 cells); run_notebook.ps1 --path x.spi runs a source file as a notebook and never writes over it; lib/spiral/build.ps1 and near/wallet/build.ps1 run .spi and write <nb>.spi.ipynb (README links -> .spi.html); evidence: per-test A/B original livemd vs round trip 353 tests in 31 notebooks same outcome, .spi run directly math/seq/sm' 79 tests same, the 7 lib-dependent matrix samples 53 rows identical to the accepted repro, Kino mix test 140/0; open: the full lib build from .spi (running 09:30), then folder samples -> test blocks; 10:10 user committed the lib migration (dc7b955c 09:51); all 39 lib notebooks run from .spi with exit 0 (Kino run_notebook, 2 at a time), 268 tests in 29 notebooks have the same outcome as the original livemd runs (physics/parsing/rust outputs vanished before comparison, both matched in the A/B); .spi -> .livemd kept for a cell UI: from_spi now restores /// doc runs as markdown cells and adds a #### name (test) heading only when the name would not re-derive; run_notebook --livemd-path writes the Livebook view, --with-tests exports back; 39/39 lib notebooks .spi -> .livemd -> .spi byte-identical, 26/39 livemd byte-identical to the deleted originals, 3,503 of 3,531 old cells verbatim (sm' real cells move ahead of the rest); Kino mix test covers both properties; UI direction: Zed (LSP + runnables, ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES) as the editor, Livebook via --livemd-path for rich outputs; split 2026-10-12 into SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS, TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST, CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE, KINO-RUN-ONE-TEST, NOTEBOOKS-TO-SPI-SIBLINGS, SPIR-INTERLEAVED-LIVEMD, ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES; children also TEST-RUN-REPORT, TEST-IDENTITY-I18N, SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY (from the 2026-10-12 external review of dc7b955c)", Epic, P1, D7, 55u32, Active, "SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", "samples,kino,compiler,dogfood,packages,main", "current", "current")
