inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_4 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:34Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:34 lap 1 grain: unchanged: only the user's manual gutter check in Zed remains (runnables 420/420 against the compiler's test blocks); test-at-row.ps1 + spiral/.zed/tasks.json in place Next: nothing for agents until TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL's extension rev switch; then the user check")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_5 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:32 lap 2 grain: unblock condition made exact. The grammar side is done and pushed: extension.toml pins rev 3c76d3ed on github-i574n/main with no grammar change since, runnables.scm tags test_header as spiral-test, spiral/.zed/tasks.json runs apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 for the cursor test, the tagged test and the file. Lib holds 402 test headers today, all matched by the runnable query (TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL note). The only open step is the user's: in Zed, install the dev extension from apps/zed, open e.g. lib/spiral/sm'.spi, and confirm a run button on each test line and that one runs. Nothing for agents")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_6 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 6u32, "2026-10-19T15:22Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:22 lap 5 grain: re-verified the task half against today's tree: test-at-row.ps1 resolves apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 (exists; the old apps/kino path is gone), and -DryRun gives the right --test for rows inside lib testing.spi tests (assert_approx_eq, _2, _3) and, for a definition row in tibia src/coins.spi, the 5 of 6 tests that reach it. Gap found: the tagged spiral-test task lives only in spiral/.zed/tasks.json and calls ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, so in every other worktree (tibia, eoie, x, dice, alphabet, blog, polyglot: none has .zed/tasks.json) the gutter button has no task to run. Proposed fix (not applied; check in Zed with the user's step): ship the tasks with the extension as apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json (Zed loads language tasks from extensions) and resolve the script through the sibling layout (ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, as Cells finds lib), or a repo-local .zed/tasks.json per consumer repo. User check unchanged: install the dev extension, confirm the gutter button in spiral and in tibia.")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_7 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 7u32, "2026-10-19T15:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:40 lap 6 grain, closed the worktree gap from lap 5 in the tree: Zed loads an extension language's tasks.json (zed crates/extension_host/src/extension_host.rs:2364-2376, load_plugin_language reads language_path/tasks.json, TaskTemplates::FILE_NAME = tasks.json, into a ContextProviderWithTasks), so apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json now ships the tagged spiral-test task and the file-tests task with the extension. The script path goes through the sibling layout, ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, which resolves from tibia, eoie and spiral itself (checked). The gutter button therefore gets a task in every repo beside spiral. The spiral worktree may now list the tagged task twice (the extension's copy and spiral/.zed/tasks.json); drop the .zed copy once the user's check confirms the extension one. User check unchanged: dev-install apps/zed, then a run button on a test line in spiral and in tibia.")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_8 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 8u32, "2026-10-19T16:01Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:01 lap 7: real-dialect files work as well. test-at-row.ps1 -DryRun on lib sm'_real.spir resolves rows to their test blocks (test sm static, symbol_to_string), and config.toml's path_suffixes include spir, so the gutter task covers .spir files with no extra work. (The dry run asks the compiler for --source-blocks, so it is a short compiler process, not text-only.)")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_9 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 9u32, "2026-10-19T16:37Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:37 lap 8 grain: apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json now also carries the untagged spiral: run test at cursor task (the keybinding target), with the sibling-layout script path, so every repo beside spiral gets it. The language file is now a superset of the tracked spiral/.zed/tasks.json: all 3 .zed tasks duplicate it (same labels, same script, only the path spelling differs), so in the spiral worktree each would show twice. Valid JSON, LF. For the user after the Zed check: remove .zed/tasks.json (tracked; left in place by me)")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_10 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 10u32, "2026-10-19T17:12Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:13 lap 9 grain: the sibling-layout path of the language tasks.json checked from a non-spiral worktree: with ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT=C:\\home\\git\\dice the script path dice/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 exists, and -DryRun on dice/lib/dice.spi row 3 resolves the enclosing block (run_notebook --test dice_dice). So the language tasks work in sibling repos without a per-repo .zed. Next: user's Zed check (gutter button + keybinding), then the user drops spiral/.zed/tasks.json")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_11 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 11u32, "2026-10-19T17:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:36 lap 10 grain: checked what Zed actually loads: extension.toml pins grammar rev 3c76d3ed on i574n/spiral (path apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral), that commit is on github-i574n/main, and the worktree grammar has no diff against it, so the user's Zed check exercises the committed grammar; the new language tasks.json is untracked (?? in git status) and runnables.scm +3 lines vs the rev, so the user's check needs those two staged with the Zed dev-extension reload. Next: user's Zed check, then the user drops spiral/.zed/tasks.json")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_12 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 12u32, "2026-10-19T17:54Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:54 lap 11 grain: validated the language tasks.json against Zed's task docs (zed.dev/docs/tasks): every key it uses (label, command, args, use_new_terminal, allow_concurrent_runs, reveal = always, tags) is a documented task key, and the docs give runnable-tag precedence as workspace tasks.json, then global, then language-provided bindings; so while spiral/.zed/tasks.json exists, its tagged task overrides the language one inside the spiral worktree, which is one more reason the user drops it after the check (other repos get the language task). Next: user's Zed check, then git rm .zed/tasks.json (user)")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_13 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 13u32, "2026-10-19T23:46Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 19:46 lap 22 grain, the runnable query checked without Zed: tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 query of apps/zed/languages/spiral/runnables.scm, on a scratch copy of the committed grammar, over the 40 tracked lib/spiral files with test blocks gives 416 spiral_test_name captures, exactly the 416 lines that start with test (grep), each run capture spanning the header line only (json.spi: test json static = at 3:0, test name json at 3:5). So the tag spiral-test fires on every test block and carries its name; what is left is only the user's in-editor check of the task wiring (tasks.json + dev-extension reload)")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_14 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 14u32, "2026-10-24T02:25Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main grooming: Paused by rule (Active, no note since 2026-10-19T23:46Z, no child item noted in 3 days). Resume when picked; progress kept at 90%.")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_15 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 15u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 3 10:09 (subagent2): blocked on the user's in-Zed check (unblock step recorded lap 2) -> next: user check | lap 4 10:32 (subagent2): blocked: user's in-Zed check -> next: user check | lap 12 14:24 (subagent2): extension.toml grammar rev 3c76d3e is on github i574n/main and its grammar.js has test_header with field name (test_name), the exact nodes runnables.scm captures (both query copies identical); apps/zed has no uncommitted diff -> next: user's Zed check, then drop .zed/tasks.json | lap 13 14:41 (subagent2): path check: the language tasks.json resolves the runner as $ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, which inside the spiral worktree is spiral itself, so dropping spiral/.zed/tasks.json loses nothing there; it breaks only for a worktree that is not a sibling of the spiral checkout (e.g. opening C:\\home\\git as one worktree, or a spiral.new project elsewhere) -> next: user's Zed check; later: a SPIRAL_ROOT fallback through pwsh -Command if non-sibling worktrees matter | lap 14 15:03 (subagent2): waiting on the user's Zed check (grammar rev, queries, tasks verified) -> next: user's Zed check | lap 15 15:10 (subagent2): the language task file apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json is untracked (git status ??): a dev extension loaded from apps/zed sees it, but it must be in the user's commit before .zed/tasks.json is dropped, or other checkouts lose the runnable task -> next: user: Zed check, commit languages/spiral/tasks.json, then drop .zed/tasks.json | lap 17 16:43 (subagent2): unchanged -> next: user's Zed check | lap 19 18:56 (subagent2): unchanged -> next: user's Zed check")
inl ci_after_spi_migration () = Task ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", "First CI runs after the 2026-10-12 commits (dc7b955c lib .livemd -> .spi with 370 test blocks, Kino from_spi/--livemd-path, DeadPureLetElision, Wasm str_cmp, canonical package dirs): spiral, dice, alphabet, polyglot must build lib from .spi with a compiler built from the same commit (an older compiler fails Package not loaded on test blocks); lib/spiral/build.ps1 runs 4 notebooks at once and was reaped locally at 16 GB, check runner memory and lower the throttle if needed; outputs are now <nb>.spi.ipynb/.spi.html; 2026-10-12 11:30 CI read: spiral ubuntu red on 2 runs (before and after the migration) in lib/spiral/near/wallet: gleam build --target javascript rejects the Erlang-only @external spiral_math_pow the Gleam integer prelude bundles (handed to the compiler lane); eoie ubuntu red: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/env.ps1:98 Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA null on Linux in Swift tool detection, fixed (guarded like BendMain, verified with LOCALAPPDATA unset); alphabet red (ALPHABET-CI-XELATEX); i574n.github red since 05:22; dice and spiral 10:44 runs in progress; 11:40: spiral run 38265092981 (10:44 push 52311f0a, first CI of the .spi lib) died differently: exit 143 (SIGTERM, not a script error) 26 min into lib/spiral/build.ps1 -sequential 1 with zero output in between (15:01:11 -> 15:27:49Z; the build buffered each notebook's log until the end), so the culprit notebook or memory pressure is unknowable from that log; lib/spiral/build.ps1 now prints start/done lines per notebook (exit, attempts, seconds) as they happen; the near_wallet Gleam pow failure would still follow later in that job; 11:58 dice 10:44 run red on windows in contract/: process_rust runs spiral_wasm through invoke-block -Linux (exit 127 on the Windows runner); already decided in CI-SPIRAL-WASM-NATIVE: the NEAR sandbox is Linux/macOS only (near-sandbox-utils), so it is WSL-last work, no skip switch; 12:05 correction: the fine-grained-cells hypothesis for the 26 min SIGTERM was wrong; the Kino lane measured per-test planning (sm' 195 -> 38 steps) at 374 s -> 369 s, math 87 -> 86 s: definition-only steps compile fast, the cost is test steps building once per ///> backend (gleam/fsharp/cuda dominate; sm' summed: target 552 s, compile 507 s, daemon queue 521 -> 303 s, rustc 44 s); my 622 s was contention; the SIGTERM cause stays open until the per-notebook progress lines show it; CI-time levers: per-backend batching of a file's tests (one gleam project per file), cached target builds, fewer targets in CI; 12:42 lib/spiral/build.ps1 done lines now also carry the test counts (spiral-tests JSON: passed/failed/skipped, failed test names, a total line) and available memory (MemAvailable on Linux), so the next 143 shows which notebook ran and whether memory was falling; hypothesis to confirm, not act on yet: runner memory exhaustion with Kino's default 4 concurrent cells building gleam/fsharp/cuda targets (SPIRAL_KINO_CELL_CONCURRENCY=2 in CI would be the lever); 14:20 spiral CI GREEN on feb8b9f7 (run 38280264212, 1h18m, ubuntu + windows, pages deployed): the NEAR wallet Gleam build passes with the target-neutral pow, lib/spiral/build.ps1 reports 39 files / 368 tests passed / 0 failed from .spi on ubuntu, slowest sm' 162 s, parsing 146 s, base 124 s; available memory on the runner never under 8.2 GB, so the earlier exit 143 stays unexplained (not memory in this run; possibly runner-side); my earlier \"parsing 33/40\" came from a text heuristic in my A/B script, the Kino report says 40/40; still to confirm on the next pushes: eoie ubuntu (env.ps1 LOCALAPPDATA fix lands when eoie CI clones spiral), alphabet xelatex (packages + diagnostics step, uncommitted), i574n.github (same near_wallet fix); 14:35 eoie run 38280533281 (12:50 commits incl. the eoie lane's in-progress typed-fields crates) fails on windows in agile_planning_rollup/tests/planning_cli.rs: mutating verbs refused with \"lease authority blocked mutating effect because should_wrap=1\" (tests depend on the fixture's lease clock), handed to the eoie lane; the env.ps1 LOCALAPPDATA fix is confirmed on the next eoie run; alphabet: root cause found (texlive-lang-greek), fix uncommitted; 2026-10-13 23:57 sweep lane: eoie run 38327253830 green on windows and ubuntu (env.ps1 LOCALAPPDATA fix confirmed); spiral 38389311114 and .github 38389289826 (push 8a89893a) red on ubuntu only in lib/spiral/near/wallet: lib build itself 39 files / 369 passed / 0 failed, but near_wallet.spi tests still called lustre.start without a DOM (let assert Ok panics under bun) once Kino dropped build_only; fixed by mirroring lustre.spi (init/update/view -> to_html -> expect_html exact HTML), landed in d94dc380 (23:49), CI 38508233036 / 38508243993 running; earlier xsim heavy-churn failure (runs 38312827285, 38295906353) has a test fix in 8a89893a with no CI evidence yet (later runs died before xsim); alphabet 38327247780 ubuntu green, windows red: tectonic cannot find font NanumGothicCoding for test.hangul.md.pdf (contradicts DOCUMENTS-TECTONIC Hangul check, which was local only); fix uncommitted in alphabet/scripts/init.ps1: on Windows, when C:/Windows/Fonts/NanumGothicCoding.ttf is missing, download naver/nanumfont VER2.5 NanumGothicCoding-2.5.zip (same files, same sizes as the local fonts tectonic uses), copy both ttf into the Windows fonts dir and register them in HKLM Fonts (download/extract dry-checked locally); dice 38265106556 ubuntu green, windows red only in the WSL-last contract; polyglot has no push since 10-09; 2026-10-14 00:22 push d94dc380 (incl. the near_wallet fix): spiral 38508233036 and .github 38508243993 red on ubuntu earlier, in apps/wasm: Kino now pins rustc +1.99.0 (kino.ex @rust_toolchain, new in d94dc380); the runner has only nightly-2025-05-09, rustup auto-installed 1.99.0 (3 components) while concurrent cells called rustc, and every attempt then failed error[E0463] can't find crate for std (rustup is not safe for concurrent installs; all 3 retries hit the same broken toolchain); fix (uncommitted, apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino.ex): before the first rustc through a rustup proxy, one cell under a :global lock checks rustup toolchain list and runs rustup toolchain install 1.99.0 --profile minimal --no-self-update if missing (rustup next to the rustc proxy, skipped when absent), cached in :persistent_term; kino compiles (private MIX_BUILD_PATH) and the rustup path/listing probe resolves locally; windows jobs of both runs were cancelled by fail-fast, so near_wallet, xsim and windows wasm still lack CI evidence; eoie 38508234661: ubuntu green, windows red in eoie_proxy_edit_contracts (runner temp path C:/Users/RUNNER~1 got quoted), fixed under EOIE-FRICTION-2026-10-12; next: commit kino.ex + alphabet init.ps1 + eoie, push, read the next spiral/.github/alphabet/eoie runs; 2026-10-14 00:25 near_wallet.spi (d94dc380) verified locally: run_notebook.ps1 --path lib/spiral/near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi (private MIX_BUILD_PATH, output to scratch): discovered 2, executed 2, passed 2 under gleam -t javascript; the rustc race is a hypothesis: spiral_wasm.livemd has 5 Kino cells, cell concurrency defaults to 4, the pin is the only change since the green wasm step in 38389311114, and rustc is the only caller of @rust_toolchain; if the next run still shows E0463 after the serialized install, preinstall 1.99.0 (rustup toolchain install 1.99.0 --profile minimal) in the workflows before any Kino step; 2026-10-14 04:29 review fixes (uncommitted): (1) apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino.ex ensure_rust_toolchain marked the toolchain ready even after a failed rustup install and ran the install unbounded inside :global.trans: now readiness is set only when rustup lists 1.99.0 or the install exits 0, both rustup calls go through Runner.run bounded by the cell's budget, and a failure returns a ProcessError with rustup's output tail (the next Rust cell tries again); prepare_rust_toolchain is public for tests; kino_test adds fake-rustup cases (already listed -> ok, install exit 0 -> ok, offline install exit 1 -> error naming the failed install and the offline text); proven in a private copy: that test passes and a real host-Rust notebook (convert.spi, rustup proxy, private port) 2/2; (2) alphabet scripts/init.ps1 font install no longer needs admin: it checks both %WINDIR%\\Fonts and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Fonts, installs into the per-user dir with HKCU Fonts values (full paths), and verifies the zip's SHA-256 (F4C9B108...619A3F) before extracting; proven by running the block with WINDIR/LOCALAPPDATA redirected to scratch (installs both ttf + HKCU values, second run is a no-op, the 2 HKCU values removed afterwards) and with a wrong hash (throws, nothing installed); tectonic and xelatex both find per-user fonts (a per-user-only font, Aller, renders under both; an unknown font fails)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY,PIPELINES-GREEN", "ci,lib,kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ci_after_spi_migration () = Planning ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Pair)
inl samples_to_test_blocks () = Task ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", "Folder samples (apps/compiler/tmp/samples, ~3,770 matrix rows) become test blocks in .spi files, the way lib/spiral did on 2026-10-12: one file per family, each test block names its backends (///> targets) and its expected exit/stdout inline; the matrix reads expectations from source instead of the cache-only EXPECTED.tsv; start with one low-signal family (heap_/closure_/union_ combinatorics, TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS) and measure suite time before/after; negative samples become test blocks expecting a diagnostic", Story, P1, D6, 40u32, Active, "TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS,TEST-RUN-REPORT", "samples,tests,harness,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_samples_to_test_blocks () = Planning ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", Minutes 1800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_1 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:39Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:39 touch: first family chosen by size and uniformity: ebpf_* (31 samples, 166 rows, all expected exit 0); conversion must keep the 166 rows byte-identical before the folders go")
