inl tree_sitter_spiral () = Task ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", "A real tree-sitter grammar for Spiral (both editions) to replace the borrowed tree-sitter-rust in apps/zed: top-level inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open, test blocks with ///> targets, doc runs, macros ($\"...\" $'...' !!!!), so highlights/outline/indents are exact and runnables.scm can tag each `test name =` for gutter run buttons; generate edition-3 symbol tokens from the same table as the compiler tokenizer (SPIRAL3-EDITIONS); 2026-10-14 01:25 lane 1 built the cheapest unblocking grammar (uncommitted, apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral: grammar.js, generated src/ parser.c ABI 14 with tree-sitter-cli 0.25.10, queries/highlights.scm, runnables.scm, outline.scm, test/corpus/test_headers.txt): every token is a whole line; kinds test_header (prec 6: test_keyword /test[ \\t]+/, test_name, test_signature as immediate tokens), target_directive (///>), doc_comment (///), line_comment (//), definition_line (inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open/and at column 0), indented_line, other_line; tree-sitter test 3/3; gate on the 583-file corpus (spiral lib+apps, eoie src, dice, alphabet, polyglot lib): 375 real test blocks, 375 headers found, 375 correct by row and name, recall 100%, precision 100%, files with parse errors 0 of 583 (the borrowed Rust grammar scored 71%/82%); highlighting lost vs the Rust-borrowed queries (corpus captures): keyword 18144, number 65914, operator 61920, punctuation 145808, string 8214 nodes covering 1.33 MB of the 3.35 MB corpus (40%: Spiral primes open Rust char literals, so most of it was wrong), string.escape 32452, type 11466, type.builtin 4701, boolean 465, variable.special 1128; the new queries capture test_keyword 375, test_name 375, target_directive 660, doc_comment 2042; the spiral-zed language server's semantic tokens (legend: variable, symbol, string, number, operator, unary_operator, comment, keyword, parenthesis, type_variable, escaped_char, unescaped_char, number_suffix, escaped_var, type; a Spiral-aware scanner with macros, (* *) comments, primes) cover keyword, type, string, escapes, number, operator, brackets, comment; not covered: builtin types (i32 etc. come back as variable), booleans (variable), delimiters as their own class; wiring left for after a commit: extension.toml [grammars.spiral] repository https://github.com/i574n/spiral, rev = the commit with apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, path = apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral; languages/spiral/config.toml grammar = spiral; replace languages/spiral/{highlights,outline}.scm with the grammar's queries, add runnables.scm, drop brackets.scm and indents.scm (they name Rust nodes); set languages.Spiral.semantic_tokens to combined; then the manual Zed check in apps/zed/README", Feature, P0, D6, 95u32, Blocked, "", "zed,grammar,editor,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tree_sitter_spiral () = Planning ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", Minutes 900u32, Load Light, Assigned User)
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_1 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:54Z", "lane-b", "wired (uncommitted): extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev 3c76d3ed path apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, grammar = spiral, grammar queries + runnables.scm, brackets/indents.scm emptied (old brackets query fails to compile on this grammar; user: git rm), .zed/settings.json semantic_tokens combined; generate reproduces src byte-identical, test 3/3, all 5 queries compile; left: Zed manual check")
