inl kino_source_diagnostics () = Task ("KINO-SOURCE-DIAGNOSTICS", "Found by xsim 2026-10-12: Kino diagnostics embed the per-request temp path (\".../Temp/spiral_kino/1791819891254-162/main.spi:10:8: Unbound variable ...\") so identical inputs give different text and the location points at a throwaway file; map diagnostics back to the source (.spi path + line, or cell index + line within the cell) so results are deterministic and clickable (Zed problem matcher); xsim normalizes the temp dir meanwhile; temp dir now stripped case-insensitively (either slash, optional file:///), messages read main.spi:10:8 and identical inputs give identical text (regression test); mapping main.spi lines back to the .spi line / cell is still open; 2026-10-13 12:25 done by the Kino lane: compile errors of .spi runs read <file>.spi:L:C (main.spi:L:C): Spiral.Kino.SourceMap matches the main.spi line to the source by its text (context lines break ties, column shifted by the indentation difference), ambiguous or unknown lines stay main.spi:L:C; tests in notebook_report_test.exs (real compile-error shape, ambiguity, context tie-break)", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,diagnostics,xsim", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_source_diagnostics () = Planning ("KINO-SOURCE-DIAGNOSTICS", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl test_prelude_semantics () = Task ("TEST-PRELUDE-SEMANTICS", "Found by xsim 2026-10-12: lib .spi files carry test-only imports inside the first static test block (math.spi `test math static =` / `open testing`), and later test blocks only see _assert_* because Kino chains every earlier cell, tests included, into each prefix; a single test run in isolation (--test, Zed run-at-cursor, per-test planning) or a test-only program built from definitions + its own body fails with Unbound variable _assert_approx_eq; define the semantics explicitly (a test prelude block, or each test program = definitions + earlier static test bodies + own body), keep it identical across run_notebook, --test, plan: :tests and the edition-3 spec, regression: --test square alone on math.spi passes; resolved same day by the Kino lane: a static test block is kept as a definition, so its body reaches every later step's program in per-cell, per-test and --test runs; regression in notebook_report_test.exs (--test square_2 alone carries open testing); the xsim failure came from xsim's own branching-tests model, now linear like Kino", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,semantics", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_test_prelude_semantics () = Planning ("TEST-PRELUDE-SEMANTICS", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_daemon_start_race () = Task ("KINO-DAEMON-START-RACE", "Found by xsim 2026-10-12 12:20 on the real path: two concurrent Spiral.Kino.Notebook.evaluate calls from a cold start: one returns {:error, \"compiler on port 13905 did not start\"} (no verdict, no outputs) while the same program passes sequentially; the run took 208 s vs ~26 s at concurrency 1 (the loser waits out a start timeout); hypothesis: concurrent CompilerClient.ensure callers race to start the daemon on one port and the loser fails instead of waiting for the winner; fix with a single-flight start (lock or registered starter, a live daemon with the right banner counts as success) and a test of N concurrent evaluate calls on a cold daemon; repro: mix xsim.run --spi lib/spiral/math.spi --cells 3 --executor kino --max-concurrency 2 after stopping daemons; 12:25 two causes found by the Kino lane and fixed in apps/kino: (a) the daemon code stamp was the CompilerDaemon .beam mtime, so two builds of identical code (apps/kino vs apps/xsim's dep copy) kept retiring each other's daemon; now the md5 of the loaded code; (b) a port that dropped mid-handshake waited the full 180 s instead of launching; daemon tests 14/14 + a stamp test; cold 2-concurrent xsim repro pending; 12:30 verified by xsim: the cold 2-concurrent repro passes every invariant in 26.6 s (was a start failure after 208 s); warm daemon at concurrency 4 over 8 prefixes also passes", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,concurrency,xsim", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_daemon_start_race () = Planning ("KINO-DAEMON-START-RACE", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_daemon_memory () = Task ("KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", "Found by xsim + the resource sampler 2026-10-12: the Kino compiler daemon (dotnet compiler server) grows with every distinct program it compiles and is never trimmed: a 22-prefix math.spi scenario at 4 in flight took it from 4.4 GB (12:52) to 7.0 GB (13:00), free memory stayed under ~1 GB for 13 min and the heavy queue stalled 20 min until it was stopped; also the best lead for the spiral CI exit 143 (a 39-notebook sequential lib build feeding one daemon on a 16 GB runner); fix: the daemon retires itself (drain, exit, next client relaunches) above a working-set threshold (env, default ~2.5 GB) or after N compiles, with a test; verify with xsim + sampler (peak daemon GB under the threshold); 13:20 implemented by the Kino lane (uncommitted): after each compile the daemon reads its .NET compiler server's working set and, past SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_MB (default 2500) or SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_COMPILES (default off), stops that server and logs \"compiler recycled after ...\"; the daemon keeps its port and queue, so no client relaunch; verification with a 700 MB cap running; main session will re-verify with xsim + sampler; 13:35 verified by the Kino lane: math.spi with SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_MB=400 passed 15/15 with 3 recycles (\"compiler recycled after reaching 411/416/407 MB\"), compiler server peak 412 MB, 249 s wall (each recycle costs a cold compile); tests for the recycle policy and the working-set reader; caveat: checked after each compile, so one huge compile can overshoot before recycling; also seen: a cold daemon start costs ~1 min because its own mix waits for the build lock held by the client's mix (KINO-COLD-START-LOCK); 2026-10-13 12:19 with the pool default each compiler recycles at max(SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_MB/workers, 1200) MB and a new compiler starts only with free memory >= 2.5 GB, so the pool's total stays bounded", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,memory,ci,xsim", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_daemon_memory () = Planning ("KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_cold_start_lock () = Task ("KINO-COLD-START-LOCK", "Found 2026-10-12 by the Kino lane: a cold Kino compile daemon takes ~1 min to start because the daemon's own `mix` waits for the build lock held by the client's `mix` (\"Waiting for lock on the build directory\" in kino-<port>.err.prev.log); start the daemon from the already-compiled code path (no mix, e.g. elixir -pa _build/.../ebin) or release the client lock first; 2026-10-13 10:17 done: clients launch the daemon as elixir -pa <_build>/<env>/lib/*/ebin -e Spiral.Kino.CompilerDaemon.serve_app() (Application.ensure_all_started + serve; mix fallback when no compiled ebin), so it never waits for the client's build lock; cold first request (daemon boot + compiler boot + compile) 17.5 s end to end with queue 11.8 s, was ~1 min; tests in compiler_daemon_test.exs (command line both ways, ebin wildcard)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,startup", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_cold_start_lock () = Planning ("KINO-COLD-START-LOCK", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_result_memo () = Task ("KINO-RESULT-MEMO", "User priority 2026-10-12 13:58 (\"each cell run should be instant, memoized by the compiler and kino\"): memoize every Kino plan step on disk keyed by a hash of what determines its result (full program text = prefix + body, target/backend set, compiler build identity, Kino code md5, relevant options); bounded store under the spiral-bin cache, SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 opt-out, memo hit|miss per test in the report and hit counts on the spiral-tests lines; acceptance: re-running an unchanged .spi is near-instant with identical outputs/report, editing one test re-runs only steps whose program changed; baseline (tibia lane, warm daemon, unchanged files): geometry.spi 8 tests 65 s, vitality.spi 5 tests 30 s, coins.spi 5 tests 35 s (6-8 s per test block); assigned to the Kino lane 14:00, xsim verifies; the compiler-side layer is QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER; 16:05 landed in apps/kino (lib/spiral/kino/memo.ex + notebook.ex, uncommitted): only successful steps are stored (failures/timeouts/unsupported always rerun); key = full step program + module, ///> lines, compiler dll path/size/mtime, package dir prints, md5 of every Kino module and the Gleam domain, tool options; store %LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/kino-results (newest 5000); report rows memo hit|miss, spiral-tests memo_hits; opt-out SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 / memo: false; measured on math.spi with an isolated daemon: cold 201.1 s (15/15) -> unchanged re-run 6.2 s wall including pwsh+mix startup, memo_hits 15, no daemon started; xsim cross-check (memoized runner vs memo-free sequential baseline, breaking edits must still fail) pending; 17:10 sm' cold vs memo unmeasured: both full runs passed the 15 min cap under the bless + strict renewal load (single compiles 51-121 s at 1.0 GB free); sm' --test format (C) re-run = 300 s cell timeout, inconclusive, not an assertion failure; verified figure stands: math 201 s cold -> 6.2 s memoized (15/15 hits); xsim cross-check 17:21 (main, isolated daemon 13925, fresh memo dir, math.spi 6 cells, 3 users, 1 edit, 1 breaking edit, 3 shuffled schedules with duplicates, runner memoized vs memo-free sequential baseline): schedule 1 62.8 s (hits 10 / misses 11), schedule 2 9.6 s (18 / 3), schedule 3 8.3 s (18 / 3); every schedule sequential_equivalence, no_stale_results, one_compile_per_prefix, withdrawn_demand_hidden and breaking_edits_fail ok, commute ok: memoized results equal uncached ones and a breaking edit still fails; with the tibia lane's apps/tibia numbers and the math 201 s -> 6.2 s timing this closes the item", TaskKind, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "KINO-C-FALSE-PASS", "kino,cache,performance", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_result_memo () = Planning ("KINO-RESULT-MEMO", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl upstream_syntax_sync () = Task ("UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC", "Found 2026-10-12 by the tibia lane probing mrakgr's Spiral-s-ML-Library: upstream head (Dec 2025) uses syntax the fork's compiler lacks (unary deref `*x`: 135 errors; nullary `forall t. : t`), and the Feb-2025 snapshot 0f76adf breaks because the fork made '#' an escape inside $\"...\" (upstream writes `# type: ignore`); port the upstream syntax into both cores and make the # escape edition-aware (SPIRAL3-EDITIONS) so upstream programs keep compiling; also compiler CLI --default-int/--default-float on the direct --backend path (the ML lib assumes i32/f32, the fork defaults f64), queued to the compiler lane; user decision 2026-10-12 19:14: sync the language from mrakgr's host_cpp_and_cuda_backend branch (98 commits ahead of the 2025-04-05 merge base, last 2025-11-14: unary deref, nullary forall, inferencer fixes, C++/CUDA backend) into both cores; take only repo/tooling commits from master (26 ahead, last 2026-06-30, dependabot); the fork merged mrakgr/master on 10-04, so it lacks the cpp branch; future PRs target the cpp branch; the '#' escape is edition-aware: edition 2 keeps upstream's literal '#' inside macro strings; 2026-10-13 09:10 main: ported unary deref *x (RawLayoutIndex, new ETY-ExpectedLayout) and type-level if (if type a = b then .. else .., RawTypeIfThen/Else via unify_gadt + TypeEq) into both cores from mrakgr host_cpp_and_cuda_backend; verified on both Debug cores with probes (C exit 7, negative ETY-ExpectedLayout); nullary forall already worked; ML library head (80d6a1a) enumerative_kms_cfr_train now type-checks with SPIRAL_DEFAULT_FLOAT=f32 (was 135+ errors), next blocker is in PartEval for the GADT pickler (union_map pickler t evaluated with the outer t = ()); also seen: Debug-only process crash from the inherited assert (0 = errors.Count) in fill (lazy psucc thunk sees errors from later statements; same in upstream); lands with pack 2; 2026-10-13 12:35 main: type-level if landed in pack 2 (sample upstream_type_if, C=Rust=7); the *x surface syntax was withdrawn the same morning: lib/spiral defines its own ~* and writes *state.level (old unary fallback = ~* over the field chain), upstream's case reads only a var or parenthesised term, so every lib program broke 10:05-10:17; RawLayoutIndex plumbing stays for SPIRAL3-EDITIONS (edition 2 = upstream * as layout index); pack 3 candidate adds the next ML-lib blockers: GADT payloads stay lazy (single-flight ty_is_uninhabited catches PartEvalTypeError like hopac) and nominal constructors accept records in another field order (re-keyed to the declared order); ML lib head needs the edition gate for its *x sites before it can compile end to end; 2026-10-13 13:04 main: with the pack-3 candidate (edition gate --edition 2 / SPIRAL_EDITION=2, lazy GADT payloads, record-order alignment for nominal and union-case payloads) Spiral-s-ML-Library head enumerative_kms_cfr_train passes parsing, type checking and partial evaluation on both cores (SPIRAL_DEFAULT_FLOAT=f32); it now stops in codegen: 'Non-standard functions are not supported in the Python backend', the same message upstream's CodegenPython has, so the remaining gap is routing join_backend Cuda function pointers to the CUDA/C++ generator in our Python + Cuda backend (next step); 2026-10-13 15:08 main: the ML lib's last error (a non-standard function reaching CodegenPython's closure join point) is not a routing gap: our Python + Cuda already routes join_backend CudaDevice through CodegenCpp.codegen' exactly like upstream 0cb0fda0, and upstream's CodegenPython rejects the same closure kind; the ML lib head (80d6a1a, 2026-02-05) postdates the cpp branch's last commit (2025-11-14), so it likely needs unpublished upstream compiler work; stop here until mrakgr publishes, keep the ML lib as the parity oracle; 2026-10-14 02:01 lane-3 parser comparison (read only; mrakgr host_cpp_and_cuda_backend 0cb0fda0 Tokenize/BlockParsing vs the fork's shared sections; corpus ML lib 80d6a1a + upstream core + compilation_tests): cpp-branch syntax the fork still lacks: the 2.17.7 annotation wrap (join_point builds RawAnnot(RawJoinPoint) in let rec bottom-up; test108; 2-line port) and prefix * outside edition 2 (163 corpus lines; needs edition per package); already in the fork: if type, #x/#(e)/## macro vars, stack_refs/heap_refs, UnsafeBackendSwitch; fork changes that alter upstream programs: pattern as scope (upstream binds the whole pair, fork the last element; 5 lines, e.g. test13 a,b,c as q), (* comment opener vs kind (* -> *) (test77b), operator precedence (|> 10 upstream vs 41 fork; 0 real corpus lines), edition-3 tokens such as ^ (0 uses), macro \\n escapes (0), field order by declaration; all belong behind UpstreamEdition2; X-compat: #name is the one upstream construct edition 3 must respell; full table C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\upstream-syntax\\diff.md; 2026-10-14 02:08 correction to the lane-3 note above: the pattern-as claim was wrong; both grammars build :: and | over pairs, so a,b as x binds the whole pair in both (test13 and (i,target as s) behave the same); the real differences are narrower and unused in the corpus (0 lines): upstream accepts any pattern after as (the fork only a variable) and reads p as x, q as p as (x, q) (the fork (p as x), q); diff.md row B2 corrected; 2026-10-14 06:02 A4 (upstream 2.17.7 join_point annotation wrap, with the annotation kept inside too per the review) is in spiral_compiler.fs, unaccepted: pack-2 rung 1 single-flight-20261014-051955 (night cache) changes no non-Bend residual (0 of 4,240 rows); the regression sample is still missing: both the pre-A4 and A4 compilers reject a main whose body is a real block with 'Cannot apply a forall with a term' at main (line 1 col 10), so the sample needs upstream test108's full context (a separate typed main calling into a real-block helper); drafts in the job scratch night/pending-samples", Feature, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "HOPACSOTA", "compiler,upstream,syntax", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_upstream_syntax_sync () = Planning ("UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC", Minutes 600u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_c_false_pass () = Task ("KINO-C-FALSE-PASS", "Found 2026-10-12 ~14:15 by the tibia session: Kino targets.ex cell_exit returns exit_status 0 for `///> c` (and Delphi via run_dcc) and moves the program exit code into value, so a failing assertion passes (hunt_sim.spi golden_seed_7_on_c with expected 7 -> 8: \"__assert_eq { actual = 7; expected = 8 }\", value=1, status=passed, run exit 0); a ///> c cell also runs only C; fix like the Rust path (value line + exit 0, non-zero only on failure) with a deliberately failing C test as regression, then re-run lib notebooks with ///> c/delphi tests and list tests that flip to failed (hidden failures); assigned to the Kino lane before KINO-RESULT-MEMO; fixed 14:20 by the Kino lane (uncommitted): for c/cpp/delphi a non-zero program exit now fails the cell (\"builder failed (exit N)\" + output) and exit 0 passes with no value; regressions in targets_test.exs (C __assert_eq exit 1 -> error, cpp exit 7 -> error); the old test encoding the bug was removed; a ///> c cell running only C is by design (a cell's ///> lines are its whole target list, README says so); blast radius in lib: only sm'.spi test format targets C (re-run queued); no false pass was memoized (memo not landed yet); verified 14:25 by the tibia session: hunt_sim.spi golden_seed_7 with ///> rust + ///> c passes with both target streams, the 7 -> 8 mutation fails (run exit 1); apps/tibia regression 7 files / 40 tests / 0 failures, 489 s under load (also the KINO-RESULT-MEMO baseline)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,correctness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_c_false_pass () = Planning ("KINO-C-FALSE-PASS", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia () = Task ("TIBIA", "Tibia as the dogfood project (user 2026-10-12): typed Tibia rules in Spiral (apps/tibia, .spi modules with test blocks, Rust on CPU and WGSL on GPU from one source) and agents measured on a published OT Agent Arena against the best open-source bots; tooling improves first, the goal advances only where the road is clean; latest of everything (Canary 3.6.1, OTClient Redemption 4.1); plan in apps/tibia/*.md (transitional, see TIBIA-DOCS-TO-CODE)", Epic, P1, D8, 35u32, Active, "", "tibia,dogfood", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia () = Planning ("TIBIA", Minutes 9600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_1 () = Note ("TIBIA", 1u32, "2026-10-15T01:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 21:14 NEXT AUTONOMOUS SESSION, in order (reprioritized after the 2026-10-14 harness fault and PR-4..PR-6): (1) TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY (P0): live lands ~67% of cyclops swings vs ~82% simulated; cadence and mitigation ruled out; measure the defense path (blocked swings per clear, needs a server-side log or a client build exposing effects), then model it and the queued drink during the 1 s potion exhaust; validate with a fresh pre-registered clear (not 3- or 2-cyclops rules, already seen). Until it holds, no simulator-designed policy goes live. (2) TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH (P1): second baseline; bisect _Loader.lua phases with the bot's own logging; then PR-3 as registered. (3) TIBIA-BASELINES: rules vs vBot was never pre-registered; consider PR-7 with the clean harness. Parked: TIBIA-PARTY, TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES, TIBIA-AGENT (stop rules reached; learning waits on fidelity). Rules: live blocks run alone (no Kino suites alongside), foreground chunks under 10 min, harness columns checked per block, final gate with SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0.")
inl note_of_tibia_2 () = Note ("TIBIA", 2u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: road so far: typed rules (24 modules, 69 tests, C+WGSL), local world, OTClient harness with parity, vBot and nExBot baselines, 8 pre-registered live checks. Roadmap order now: POTION-FIDELITY (P0) -> BASELINES -> RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD -> POLICY-FEATURES -> AGENT; headless client and release stay deferred.")
inl note_of_tibia_3 () = Note ("TIBIA", 3u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 PAUSED by the user: priority moves to dogfooding the tooling (eoie, backends, cells). Resume in a few weeks, aiming at GPU rental. State: rules level with vBot on a fair harness (PR-11); model mirrors live in-sample, misses on policy sensitivity (PR-10). Resume plan in order: TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY, TIBIA-START-SYNC, PR-12 (TIBIA-BASELINES), TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES, TIBIA-TOOLS-TO-EOIE, TIBIA-AGENT, TIBIA-GPU-RENTAL. Tooling items it waits on (generic): GPU-RENTAL-READINESS, EOIE-EXPERIMENTS, CELLS-REPIN, CELLS-GATE, CELLS-PROBES.")
inl note_of_tibia_4 () = Note ("TIBIA", 4u32, "2026-10-17T20:59Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:59 moved to its own repo (user): the 31 files of spiral/apps/tibia now sit at the root of C:\\home\\git\\tibia (origin github.com/i574n/tibia), hashes verified; docs' self-references fixed and spiral-tool paths prefixed spiral/. Verified from the new location, memo off: views 7, creatures 8, terrain 10, geometry 11, hunt_sim 11, gpu_sim 6 pass; live.spi compiles to the same Lua (7FD3D538...93E5). tibia-local run-arena.ps1 and run-policy-scenario.ps1 point at the new path. Titles and older notes that say apps/tibia refer to the old location.")
inl note_of_tibia_5 () = Note ("TIBIA", 5u32, "2026-10-17T21:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 17:54 repo completed sibling-style (user: the first move was sloppy): AGPL LICENSE, .editorconfig/.gitattributes/.gitignore/.devcontainer like alphabet; scripts/init.ps1 (clones polyglot, links deps/polyglot + deps/spiral, mesa-vulkan-drivers on Ubuntu, builds the WGSL runner into target/), build.ps1 (every test file through cells, fails unless all rows executed and passed), publish.ps1, workflow.ps1; .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml (Ubuntu + Windows, gh-pages push on main) with gh actions-lock. Harness moved from tibia-local into harness/ (paths.ps1: repo vs TIBIA_WORLD), results/ holds the cited TSVs and diagnostics; tibia-local keeps the world only (originals archived in job tmp). i574n.github init/build/workspace register tibia next to dice and alphabet. Verified locally: init -fast ok, build.ps1 23 files / 162 tests green (12 min), live smoke from harness/ cleared (82.8 s, 0 foreign). CI not run yet: needs the user's push. nExBot stays out of the repo (no license).")
inl note_of_tibia_6 () = Note ("TIBIA", 6u32, "2026-10-17T23:05Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 19:05 repo root slimmed (user): the Spiral package moved to src/ (package.spiproj + 24 modules), the five design docs to docs/; README, scripts/build.ps1 (src/*.spi; -Files now splits on commas), harness/paths.ps1 (TibiaSource) and the arena snapshot follow. Verified: build.ps1 -Files views,creatures green from src/, live.spi from src/ compiles to the same Lua (7FD3D538...), snapshot copy 25 files. Rewrite plan for the non-Spiral code: TIBIA-PROBES-IN-SPIRAL (Lua probes, biggest gain), TIBIA-TOOLS-TO-EOIE (analyses and orchestration onto generic eoie verbs), TIBIA-MAP-TOOL-IN-SPIRAL (Python map tool); apps/arena and apps/map folders come with those rewrites.")
inl note_of_tibia_7 () = Note ("TIBIA", 7u32, "2026-10-18T06:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 02:54 ACTIVE again (user correction: Tibia is not paused; advance everything until it is good enough to start Dota 2). Order: finish TIBIA-PROBES-IN-SPIRAL; TIBIA-WGSL-SHADER-SIZE (decide by experiment) and TIBIA-WINDOWS-CI-GPU (lavapipe on Windows); TIBIA-REUSE-EXEMPLAR; then CELLS-NEW-PROJECT, then Dota 2. Repo layout now: src/ (package), docs/, live/ (renamed from harness/ by session git-0e), results/, apps/arena/ (probes in Spiral), scripts/, CI on both OSes (Ubuntu green; Windows fails only the 4 long GPU twins). The user commits and pushes.")
inl note_of_tibia_8 () = Note ("TIBIA", 8u32, "2026-10-18T11:21Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 07:21 session summary toward 'good enough for Dota 2'. Done: TIBIA-PROBES-IN-SPIRAL (all 9 live probes are Spiral, no probe Lua left; lua.spi has tests), TIBIA-WGSL-SHADER-SIZE (inline everything, let start: 3.63 -> 2.36 MB, cold driver compile 167 -> 68 s; every extra let measured slower). Active: TIBIA-WINDOWS-CI-GPU 80% (lavapipe + LunarG loader on Windows CI, DXC as local fallback; waits for the spiral runner commit and a tibia push), TIBIA-REUSE-EXEMPLAR 40% (lua.spi / client.spi / probe.spi layering is the Dota template), TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY 85% (first swing folded into the mirror; over-count analysed: no single mechanism, needs clean runs). New: DOTA epic with DOTA-HEADLESS-WORLD, DOTA-LUA-BINDINGS, DOTA-FIRST-SCENARIO; CELLS-EXPORT-ATOMIC-WRITE. Compiler lane fixed SPIRAL-LUA-CLOSURE-RECORD-ARG and SPIRAL-LUA-PAREN-STATEMENT (verified here). Remaining before Dota: CELLS-NEW-PROJECT (its deps are cells/eoie items), green CI on both OSes after the pushes, renting the CPU box.")
inl note_of_tibia_9 () = Note ("TIBIA", 9u32, "2026-10-20T06:03Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 02:03 parking state after the 10-19/20 night (all uncommitted in tibia): core v1 migration applied (80 edits) and verified; arena spot widened to radius 45 with road speed at the spot (apps/map + terrain, WGSL twins bit-exact; terrain 10/10, pack_sim 31/31 fresh, hunt_sim 11/11, gpu_sim 6/6); hunter clear-rate gap diagnosed and recorded as open (BENCHMARK PR-14 post-hoc row, README fidelity table), no PR-15. Closed: TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK, TIBIA-REUSE-EXEMPLAR. Paused with resume conditions: POTION-FIDELITY, STANDARDS, DOCS-TO-CODE, HUNTING-GROUND. Left before parking: PR-12 chunks 2-4 (30 pairs, ~3 h live, slid by main to 07:00+ for P0 work; closes TIBIA-BASELINES and adds retreat runs for RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD), the Zig LLVM pack_sim measurement (closes TIBIA-ZIG-ORACLE), then a last pass on FIDELITY, LIVE-POLICY and COMBAT-FIDELITY. Waiting on the user: deleting docs/WORKFLOW.md.")
inl note_of_tibia_10 () = Note ("TIBIA", 10u32, "2026-10-20T21:09Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 17:09 parking state after the 2026-10-20 run (PR-12 complete; PC-4, PC-5, PC-6, PR-15 run; all 27 test files green on the final tree incl. the new formatter layout gate in scripts/build.ps1). Closed today: TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD (protection zones + teleports in map and model, live check 5/5), TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND (PR-15: kills match, potions over-counted), TIBIA-COMBAT-FIDELITY (PC-4 knight speed, PC-6 swing after step; retreat-step bug fixed; six-means sum t^2 17.5 -> 8.8), TIBIA-ZIG-ORACLE (C stays oracle). Tooling found and fixed along the way: Cells WGSL tests could not fail (WGSL-TEST-STATUS-IGNORED, fixed by main; all 28 GPU twins now honest), formatter vs generated code (apps/map formats through SpiralCompiler format; elif chains), harness reset left shielding at 12 (fixed), eoie table min/max/count/logs and experiment ledger validated on tibia data. Open for a later Tibia session: potions over-counted on protection-free arenas (crowding at the spot's pocket: model 4.0 vs live 11.5 retreat steps), hunter clear gap (16/25 vs 87/100), the headless client chain (P4). Every open item carries a resume pointer in its latest note.")
inl note_of_tibia_11 () = Note ("TIBIA", 11u32, "2026-10-21T02:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 22:02 grooming for an overnight window (until 07:00; not a go). Closed now: TIBIA-STANDARDS and TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG (verified in code/tests), WGSL-TEST-STATUS-IGNORED (main's fix verified). Advanceable overnight, in order: (1) TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY (P0, 360m): adopt the source-backed monster timing as one opt-in camp rule (think-gated re-path + grid swing cadence, no head start), re-pin, score protected-arena means separately as older-harness data, pre-register a new live check (PR-16) and run it through 'eoie window run live-gui' (~1.5 h live, needs main's go); (2) TIBIA-FIDELITY (120m): re-predict the hunter clear rate under the new timing (the 87/100 vs 16/25 gap) with the existing probe, no live needed; (3) TIBIA-TOOLS-TO-EOIE (90m): pc4-analysis onto 'eoie experiment --test median' style recipes, pr12-secondary waits on eoie --since, pc3 on a grid-share test; (4) TIBIA-DOCS-TO-CODE: blocked on the user's yes for WORKFLOW.md and eoie's BENCHMARK import. Not overnight: TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES (after the model ranks policies), PARTY, AGENT, ARENA-RELEASE, GPU-RENTAL, 2048, STORAGE-BOUNDARY, the headless-client chain (P4).")
inl note_of_tibia_12 () = Note ("TIBIA", 12u32, "2026-10-21T02:07Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 22:07 overnight decision protocol (written before any measurement; applied mechanically). D1 model adoption: candidate monster-timing rule sets C0 tree, C1 think-gated re-path, C2 grid swing cadence (Canary canUseSpell rounds), C3 C1+C2; score S = sum of t^2 over the four current-harness targets: PR-11 rules parity 14.42 (se 0.47, shield 11), PR-12 retreat parity 12.75 (se 0.46, model at 0.25 x shield11 + 0.75 x shield12, matching its chunks), PR-15 kills 12.80 (se 0.59) and potions 12.70 (se 0.52) at shield 12. Adopt the candidate with the lowest S if it beats C0; ties go to fewer rules. It becomes a new bundle 'mirroring_the_current_arena' (protection ended at login) so the protected-arena bundle and its pins stay; protected six means are reported, not decisive. D2 PR-16: 20 spiral-policy + 20 spiral-retreat, alternating, parity arena, shield reset to 11, predictions from the adopted bundle at shield 11; one-sample t per arm, holds iff both |t| <= 2.09 (19 df); registered in an eoie experiment ledger (tibia docs/ledger) before any run. D3 live slot: ask main; run only through an eoie live-gui window; if PR-16 has not started by 03:30, skip it and record why. D4 hunter: re-predict with the adopted bundle; read against the Wilson band 45-80 of 100 like PC-5. D5 WORKFLOW.md: no explicit yes, so it stays. D6 any test failure caused by adoption: fix within 30 min or revert to C0 entirely. D7 a missing eoie verb: message eoie and continue without new PowerShell replacements.")
inl note_of_tibia_13 () = Note ("TIBIA", 13u32, "2026-10-21T11:05Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 07:05 Day protocol 'finish the Tibia lane' (user 07:0x: iterate until 21:00, get closer to finishing the lane for good), written before any measurement. Definition of done for the day: every TIBIA item is Done, or Paused with a written resume condition; lab/ empty; live/ only generic harness; results/ only cited evidence; all tests green; README/BENCHMARK current. Rules: E1 PR-17 runs through live/pr17-block.ps1 only after main confirms no compiles and Cells suites during the block; start-by 18:00, otherwise it stays the first item of the next day. Verdict mechanical per its pre-registration. E2 after PR-17, D16 (TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY note 106) is the only adoption path; candidates are the three lab/tibia-event-time patches alone, then the passing ones combined; nothing else is adopted today. E3 if no candidate passes D16, TIBIA-EVENT-TIME and the hunter/hunting-ground gaps are Paused with resume condition 'an event-queue engine scored under D16', not iterated further today. E4 cleanup: a file leaves lab/ or live/ only after a stem grep across C:\\home\\git repos finds no consumer outside tibia/lab; reusable pieces are promoted (prediction probes -> one entry under apps/, scoring -> scripts/), the rest deleted; the user commits. E5 results/: keep TSVs cited by a BENCHMARK row or ledger verdict, delete diagnostics already summarized in BENCHMARK. E6 ledger vs BENCHMARK stays the user's decision (not taken). E7 eoie verbs: migrate a live/ analysis only when the verb is installed (r26d --last/--since/--values, r28 table test); a missing verb is a message to eoie.")
inl note_of_tibia_14 () = Note ("TIBIA", 14u32, "2026-10-21T11:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 07:13 E4 applied to live/: the stem check finds BENCHMARK citing pr1/pr2/pc3-analysis (tracked) and pr12-secondary, pz-in-traces and pr15-analysis as the analysis of record for pre-registered rows, so they are methods, not junk. Decision: they move to a new top-level analysis/ folder (with pc4-analysis and start-sync-check), keep their names, get their paths.ps1 reference fixed and have their BENCHMARK citations updated. live/ keeps only the harness (run-*, world, paths, parity.lua, bot shims, arena-check, arena-summary) and the scenario assets (hunting-ground XMLs, vbot-arena.json), plus one generic block.ps1 that replaces pr15/16/17-block after PR-17 ends (pr17-block's job is live now).")
inl note_of_tibia_15 () = Note ("TIBIA", 15u32, "2026-10-21T11:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 07:32 Closing pass, progress: PR-17 queued (live-gui request waits for the heavy builds, start expected around 09:45, start-by 18:00); candidates moved from lab to off-by-default src options (pins unchanged); predictions promoted to apps/predict + scripts/predict.ps1, D16 scoring to scripts/score.ps1 (verification running); analysis methods of record moved live/ -> analysis/ with BENCHMARK citations updated; live/block.ps1 added (replaces the pr15/16/17 block scripts after PR-17); results/ trimmed to cited evidence plus map-tool data (22 superseded tracked files removed, recoverable from git); lab/cells-* moved to spiral by main (verified), lab/tibia-standards removed; README repository table updated; GPU-RENTAL, STORAGE-BOUNDARY and 2048-ANCHOR parked with resume conditions. Left in lab: tibia-event-time, tibia-fidelity, tibia-potion-fidelity (removed once predict.ps1 reproduces the registered numbers).")
inl note_of_tibia_16 () = Note ("TIBIA", 16u32, "2026-10-21T11:36Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 07:36 lab/ is EMPTY. scripts/predict.ps1 reproduced the registered PR-17 predictions exactly (rules 14.55, retreat 12.81, steps 12.38, hits 68.70/62.33, clear 90.1/92.2 s, hunter 99/100), so lab/tibia-potion-fidelity, tibia-fidelity and tibia-event-time were removed (their candidates live in src as off-by-default options; their methods are described in BENCHMARK rows, with a dated note on the removed lab paths). The PR-17 BENCHMARK row now cites scripts/predict.ps1. Pre-scoring the candidates under D16 now (every criterion but the PR-17 arms) so the post-PR-17 decision is arithmetic; nothing is adopted before PR-17 (E2).")
inl note_of_tibia_17 () = Note ("TIBIA", 17u32, "2026-10-21T11:44Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 07:44 live/ is harness-only now: arena-check, arena-summary, block.ps1 (generic: -Results -Ledger -StartBy plus pass-through run-arena arguments; checked that unknown flags pass through and that -Ledger needs the comma split it now does), bot shims, parity.lua, paths, run-*, world, and the scenario assets (hunting-ground XMLs, vbot-arena.json). pr15/16/17-block.ps1 removed; PR-17 runs through block.ps1 (BENCHMARK setup row and runbook updated). The working tree shows the user's earlier commit: what remains is 37 deletions (lab, moved analysis scripts, superseded results) and 15 new paths.")
inl note_of_tibia_18 () = Note ("TIBIA", 18u32, "2026-10-21T12:39Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 08:39 E8, written before any PR-18 run: PR-18 (hunter arena, 20 spiral-policy runs; tests bundle 99/100 against all3 77/100 out of sample) runs only after PR-17 has ended and only if it can start by 16:00, through live/block.ps1, with main and x told first. Otherwise it is the next day's first live item. Its verdict feeds D17's hunter criterion (TIBIA-EVENT-TIME note 27) in place of the in-sample 16/25 band.")
inl note_of_tibia_19 () = Note ("TIBIA", 19u32, "2026-10-21T20:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 16:49 Pre-commit hygiene check (nothing deleted; the results-retention rule from the 07:56 drift audit still awaits the user's go). lab/ empty. Untracked results cited by a ledger verdict or BENCHMARK: PR-12/16/17/18/19 tables and secondaries, hunter PR-13/PR-14, hunter-diag-1019 (BENCHMARK:406); PR-20 is being written now. Cited only by backlog notes, so kept as evidence: arena-results-cyclops-pz-check.tsv (TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD note 18) and arena-results-cyclops-startsync-1018.tsv (TIBIA-START-SYNC note 4). Cited nowhere: results/arena-region-r45.txt. live/hunting-ground-spawns.xml (untracked) is the PR-15 input BENCHMARK cites; the tracked live/hunting-ground-monster.xml is the 10-14 staged variant (TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND note 5; center 1957 vs 1953, z 7 vs 0), superseded by the spawns file and referenced by no script, so it is a deletion candidate after a stem grep across sibling repos and the user's yes.")
inl note_of_tibia_20 () = Note ("TIBIA", 20u32, "2026-10-21T22:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:54 DAY SUMMARY 2026-10-21 (iterate-until-21:00 run). ADOPTED for 2026-10-22, each by a rule written before measuring and held out of sample: D17 all3 (PR-17 arms t -0.05/0.24; PR-18 14/20 clears); D18 all4 = all3 + sighting_like_canary (PR-19: 15/20 clears, hits 20.45 vs 21.03, t -0.40; all3 alone rejects t 3.86); D19 pace = all4 + pacing_retreats_like_the_live_probe (PR-20: steps 10.1 vs 11.73 t -0.54, potions 12.80 vs 13.32 t -0.65; the all3 contrast also holds, t -1.65). Recipe and exact pins: EVENT-TIME note 40; the pace builder is in src, off by default; full build check green on the rerun (all 27 test files, pack_sim 36/36 with the pin unchanged; the first try had timed out from my own CPU contention). REJECTED in sample (scratch only, nothing built): D20-D25 hunter candidates (sight gate, Canary step table, nearby counter, both, stay-fled, flee table). OPEN GAPS, decomposed with next steps: hunter clear time (knight chase matches; model hunters walk 30-55% slower at 2-3 tiles from diagonal-first steps and the slowdown; a run's fate is set by its first chase: live uncleared runs kill first 22.5 tiles out with only the target in view, FIDELITY notes 19-44); hunting-ground potions (+9% from two-cyclops episodes lasting 23.4 s vs 17.4 s because the second cyclops joins with 76% vs 60% of the current target's health left, +4% the block-charge share; knight output, kill mix, cyclops hit rate and crowd shares match, POTION-FIDELITY notes 120-136); retreat shape (the model's opening is identical every clear because its cyclopses start frozen on the summon tiles; idle wandering reproduces the live layout; W from the new timeline lines, rule D21; the 'cornered 62 vs 375' gap was a counting artifact, EVENT-TIME notes 46-53). TOOLING: arena-summary on eoie table verbs; 36 BENCHMARK pre-registrations imported into the ledger (6 wait for eoie r34, with the pr1/pr2 swap). USER DECISIONS: WORKFLOW.md deletion; BENCHMARK shrink; results retention rule; live/hunting-ground-monster.xml (superseded); TIBIA-AGENT go. TOMORROW: adopt pace with its pins; a short live calibration run with the timeline lines (W for D21); then PR-21/PR-22 as rules qualify.")
inl note_of_tibia_21 () = Note ("TIBIA", 21u32, "2026-10-22T00:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:30 EVENING ADDENDUM to note 20. Build: scripts/build.ps1 green (all 27 test files; pack_sim 36/36, the pin unchanged with the pace builder off by default; the competitor's new 'wall' note compiles). Hunter gap after D20-D27 (eight candidates, all rejected in sample, nothing built): with Canary's step table the hunters' per-second move mix matches live (30/33/12/25 vs 31/31/12/27), target commitment matches (0 switches before the first kill everywhere), the knight's chase speed matches, and continuous chasing makes companions keep up; what no candidate reproduces is that about half the live first chases become a straight 20+ tile flight (25.5 s, target adjacent 24%), which decides whether a run clears. The map edge is ruled out. Hunting ground: the joining cyclops is the north spawn's fresh one, first seen 3-7 tiles out, arriving 8.6 s into the current fight in the model vs 10.2 s live. D21's W is bracketed short (cyclopses 0-1 tiles off their summon tiles at the first sample). Corrections today: note 34's fleeing-survivor reading, the cornered counter artifact, a guessed time, note 56's speculation. Process: idle passes 19:38-20:06 behind a self-made blocker, caught by the user; memory rule fixed.")
inl note_of_tibia_22 () = Note ("TIBIA", 22u32, "2026-10-22T00:50Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:50 late addendum to notes 20-21: the hunter clear-rate gap now has a concrete cause (TIBIA-FIDELITY notes 62-64). In the model, once the knight lines up on a fleeing hunter's row, terrain.step_away runs the hunter straight along that row, the same path in every seed, into one east pocket. Live hunters break off, and half of the live long chases end south. Terrain matches the dump, and the tie-break order is not the cause (checked with a mirrored variant). D28 (random pick among the distance-increasing steps when aligned) is pre-registered in FIDELITY note 65 with the usual hunter score; its scoring is the first hunter item for 2026-10-22, after the pace adoption (EVENT-TIME note 40).")
inl note_of_tibia_23 () = Note ("TIBIA", 23u32, "2026-10-22T01:38Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 21:38 Decision rules for the five items I had listed as user decisions (user 2026-10-21 after 21:00: 'why do i need to decide about tibia agent? try deciding everything autonomously and deterministically with tests/benchmarks or research'). Written before any check, applied mechanically; deletions stay recoverable from git and the user commits. F1 docs/WORKFLOW.md: delete iff a stem grep for WORKFLOW across C:\\home\\git (skipping target, .cache, node_modules) finds no consumer other than a link I repoint, and each of its instructions is enforced by a script or already stated in README/BENCHMARK/PLAN. An instruction found nowhere else moves to the README section that owns it first. Otherwise it stays, with the reason recorded. F2 BENCHMARK shrink: a pre-registration section in docs/BENCHMARK.md becomes a one-line pointer to its ledger entry iff that entry is imported in docs/ledger and 'eoie experiment analyze' reproduces the BENCHMARK verdict. Sections not yet imported (PC-1, PC-2, PC-4, PC-5, PR-15, waiting on eoie r34) stay in full. The RESULT table, setup and method sections stay. F3 results retention: a file in results/ stays iff its name (or stem) is cited in BENCHMARK, README, MODELING, docs/ledger, analysis/, scripts/, live/ or a backlog note; otherwise it is deleted. F4 live/hunting-ground-monster.xml: delete iff the stem grep across C:\\home\\git finds no reference except backlog notes calling it superseded and no tibia script reads it. F5 TIBIA-AGENT: no user go needed. It resumes (Active, scheduled by WSJF) once all three hold: (1) the pace bundle is adopted with build.ps1 green; (2) TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES has scored its simple-behavior candidates on that bundle; (3) the hunter gap is closed or Paused with a resume condition. It promotes a policy only under the criteria in its title (beats the best baseline, random control at chance, independent seed windows reproduce, declared budget).")
inl note_of_tibia_24 () = Note ("TIBIA", 24u32, "2026-10-22T01:44Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 21:44 Rules F1-F5 (note 23) applied. F1: docs/WORKFLOW.md deleted. The stem grep across C:\\home\\git found one consumer, the README Documents link, now removed. Its still-valid rules that were stated nowhere else moved to README Ground rules: target reasons (c oracle, wgsl GPU, lua live client, rust only on the 2 golden seeds, checked in src: 225 tests, the 27 untargeted are the per-module static type-check tests), tooling first, every item names a claim. The rest was enforced by scripts (build.ps1 via Cells, the standards check's target-above-every-test) or obsolete: assert-in-body until inline expectations, the gates table, and the old/new workflow table are history the backlog holds. F3: every results/ file is cited (exact-name match); three only by backlog notes (arena-region-r45, cyclops-pz-check, cyclops-startsync-1018), which the rule counts; nothing deleted. The user's 22 staged deletions agree with the rule. F4: live/hunting-ground-monster.xml deleted (no reference in any repo, tibia-local or tibia script; recoverable from 014a5ce). F5: TIBIA-AGENT note 4. F2: 44 of 50 ledger entries reproduce their recorded verdict exactly when re-analyzed from the cited TSV on a scratch copy of the ledger (secondary TSVs for PR-19 hits and PR-20 steps). Not reproducible by analyze, so they stay in full: PC-3 (derived 'late' metric), PC-6 (no table), PR-1 (VOID), PR-3 (never run). That makes 18 sections eligible (PR-2, 3a, 4-14, 16-20). Precondition found while applying: the ledger evidence pointers are working-tree 'docs/BENCHMARK.md@line'. None of the 72 resolve in HEAD, and sections after PR-20 have already drifted 2 lines since the 19:45 import. Shrinking now would break them. So the shrink runs right after the user's next commit of BENCHMARK: amend each entry's evidence to '<commit>:docs/BENCHMARK.md@<line>' (lines re-found by heading), then replace the 18 sections with one-line pointers (ID, title, verdict, ledger IDs). Reported to eoie: import evidence should pin a commit or content hash.")
inl note_of_tibia_25 () = Note ("TIBIA", 25u32, "2026-10-22T03:07Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:07 Night protocol (user 23:06: 'iterate autonomously until 7am'), written before any measurement and applied mechanically. N1 order: (a) FIDELITY live gap check on the 40 PR-18+PR-19 logs (no compile); D29 pre-registered from it before any D29 run. (b) In parallel, a read-only LIB-MIGRATION census: each of the 172 host macros mapped to a lib function or a recorded gap, plus the lib path tibia's CI resolves. (c) EVENT-TIME pace adoption per note 40 (default bundle plus pins), then one full build.ps1 as a heavy job with no compile beside it. (d) D28 R/RK and D29 candidates scored one at a time on scratch copies under the note-65 score. (e) LIB-MIGRATION: predict first (done = scripts/predict.ps1 reproduces the registered predictions exactly), then arena module by module (done = probes regenerate, standards and format clean). (f) live block 05:30-06:30 only with main's go and no compile beside it: D21 calibration plus an arena smoke clear; otherwise both slide to the morning. N2 adoption: a pace build failure is fixed within 30 min or the adoption is reverted entirely. N3 FIDELITY hard stop: if no hunter candidate passes the note-65 score by 06:00, FIDELITY goes Paused with the resume condition 'a candidate that passes the registered hunter score'. N4 lib gaps: a missing generic helper goes to lib/spiral in the backend_switch shape only if it compiles on every backend the lib tests; otherwise the macro stays and the gap is recorded on LIB-MIGRATION and messaged to eoie/main. N5 no per-experiment scripts in the repo; scratch work stays in the session scratchpad and target/. N6 at 06:30: final build.ps1, README/BENCHMARK current, report; at 07:00 the deadline file is removed.")
inl note_of_tibia_26 () = Note ("TIBIA", 26u32, "2026-10-22T03:48Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:48 Night rule N7 (live window 05:30-06:30), written before any D29/D30 score. If a D29 or D30 candidate passes note 65's score and is built off by default, the window runs PR-21 first: 20 hunter-arena runs (spiral-policy, as PR-19's arguments), with predictions taken mechanically from that candidate's score (clears k of 20 with the central 95% binomial range for its predicted rate; hits per run, one-sample |t| <= 2.09). It is pre-registered in BENCHMARK before the window opens. The D21 calibration then takes whatever time remains (at least 5 cyclops runs, or it slides to the morning). If no candidate passes, the window runs the D21 calibration (10 cyclops retreat runs) and the arena smoke clear is dropped, since the lib migration is blocked.")
inl note_of_tibia_27 () = Note ("TIBIA", 27u32, "2026-10-22T11:10Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 07:10 DAY PROTOCOL 2026-10-22 07:10-21:00 (user: iterate until 21:00), rules written before measuring. Q1 D33 verdict by notes 91-92 when W 11900 lands. Q2 PC-7 instrumentation in the competitor (logging only: chase on/off and knight/target moves with @t+ms), compile-checked, landed outside any live block. Q3 PR-22 (BENCHMARK, pre-registered before any run): 20 hunter runs with PR-21's command line plus the PC-7 lines, in a live-gui window granted by main, no compiles from any lane during it; rule: clears <= 16 -> PR-21's 19/20 was an outlier (PR-18/19 rate stands, 10..18 is its central 95% range); >= 19 -> the live rate moved up (PR-21's p 0.95 range 17..20); 17-18 -> inconclusive; descriptive: per-run login delay and summon-to-policy gap against cleared. Q4 LIB-MIGRATION resumes on main's install message (note 4), never before. Q5 records: README/BENCHMARK only carry verdicts once decided; scratch flags stay in scratch. Tie-break between ready items: WSJF; no new candidate model is scored before PR-22 says which live clear rate to target.")
inl note_of_tibia_28 () = Note ("TIBIA", 28u32, "2026-10-22T16:18Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 12:18 State refresh. Day protocol (note 27) gate cleared: PR-22 cleared 14 of 20, so the hunter target is 0.725 (FIDELITY note 105) and hunter candidates may be scored; D37 is pre-registered (FIDELITY note 106). PR-23 closed TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY (Done, noise). D36 rejected (EVENT-TIME note 77; Paused). TIBIA-LIB-MIGRATION landed in the tree (verify passed; build check running; smoke in the next window). TIBIA-PARTY resumed by its condition: duo harness in live/, rule P1 written, PR-24 planned for the 13:45 window. New: TIBIA-CELLS-APPS (CELLS-EVERYWHERE child; tests drafted for 9 files). Lib items LIB-SPLIT-LUA-C and LIB-FORMAT-FIXED-DECIMAL drafted, waiting on a coordinated lib change with main.")
inl note_of_tibia_29 () = Note ("TIBIA", 29u32, "2026-10-22T16:50Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 12:50 Moved from docs/PLAN.md (TIBIA-DOCS-TO-CODE, rule DC1), the order of work inside a phase: (1) the types and the negative packages first (what must not compile); (2) then the CPU path and its fixtures; (3) then the WGSL path, checked bit for bit against the CPU path; (4) then measurements, recorded with date, machine, load and command.")
inl note_of_tibia_30 () = Note ("TIBIA", 30u32, "2026-10-22T19:15Z", "tibia-lane", "State refresh 15:2x. PR-24 (first live duo, 10 hunts) failed rule P1 on both metrics: party potions 5.1 vs 7.56, kills 16.6 vs 15.36; gap named on TIBIA-PARTY (who the cyclopses attack; the model put 94 percent of the healing on one knight, live split it 55 to 45). The Canary-source targeting candidate is judged by rule P2, then PR-25 at ~18:00 after main review. TIBIA-CELLS-APPS: 12 src package lines green under Cells; 12 of 17 app files have test drafts waiting on the Cells pack. TIBIA-AGENT: M1 harness queued after x run 8, M2 harness drafted and dry-run patched. LIB-MIGRATION stays Paused on Cells-pack step 11.")
inl note_of_tibia_31 () = Note ("TIBIA", 31u32, "2026-10-23T00:49Z", "tibia-lane", "State at the end of the 2026-10-22 day run (07:07-21:00). Live: PR-22 (14 of 20 clears, PR-21 an outlier), PR-23 (hunting-ground potion gap closed as noise), PR-24 (first duo, failed rule P1; target order fixed from Canary source in candidate 2, potions and split now match; a troll-kill shortfall of about one late troll per hunt remains: the model knight reaches about 3.0 distinct late trolls per hunt vs live 3.8, and live late kills cluster because trolls reach the knight together more often: live clusters after a cyclops kill hold more trolls while the cyclops fights themselves match in count and length, PARTY notes 50-57). Model: F34 (flee at health <= runHealth, Canary monster.cpp) ADOPTED 17:45 with 11 refreshed literal pins; W38 lead from Canary walk-event timing matches live per-hunter lead moves in shape (once per hunter, never twice) but D40 rejected it on retreat steps (the W38 knight leaves the pocket through its mouth about ten times as often as live). The live lead gap itself (0.73 vs 1.00 moves per hunter) is 14 of 16 one walled-in hunter on the summon tile, which live never retries within the lead while Canary source and W38 retry each think; the model moves it in 100 of 100 runs (vs live 6 of 20), in most runs through exactly that retry, and still in 100 of 100 with Canary-like random think phases (EVENT-TIME notes 100-108; server-side probe drafted for the next live block). Every candidate was ruled by notes written before scoring. Library: three lib/spiral landings in sm prime (split/slice/format_fixed arms 13:29; exact format_fixed_digits for C 17:13; Gleam and Zig arms 18:40). Agent: M1 run 3 inconclusive by rule A1-T: rules arm 13.94 potions per clear (= PF1), network.evolve 13.47, but the CEM arm hit the 3 h cap with the same 512 fitness calls, so its per-call cost is the question (timing on a quiet machine next, AGENT notes 27-30); no M2. Harness: duo login order now deterministic (ally after the knight); live competitor logs nearby monsters on every step-away. Next live block is prepared (not run): C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--home-git\\ac4b4e98-9c58-4dbb-a7f7-3c93d9627107\\scratchpad\\block-next-session.ps1 (10 hunter and 10 cyclops retreat runs with the server probe, read by rules L2 and L3, EVENT-TIME notes 105 and 109, then 10 solo hunting-ground hunts as PR-23B, read by rule P5, PARTY note 58; all rules written before any run). Open next: the server-probe live block and the source reason live does not retry a blocked first step (EVENT-TIME), more solo hunting-ground hunts in the next live block before more late-troll tracing (PARTY note 57), the M1 timing run and CEM rerun (AGENT, rule A1-T), Cells-pack step 11 for the arena test drafts (CELLS-APPS, LIB-MIGRATION).")
inl note_of_tibia_32 () = Note ("TIBIA", 32u32, "2026-10-23T03:14Z", "tibia-lane", "Night run to 07:00 (user 23:0x). Queued 23:13 as job tibia-night-block (scratch night-block.ps1): one live-gui window (win-1792725191752-128236-live-gui, 180 min, gives up if not granted by 04:15) for 10 hunter and 10 cyclops arena runs with the Canary server probe (read by rules L2 and L3, EVENT-TIME notes 105 and 109; probe installed only after the grant and removed in a finally block), then 10 solo hunting-ground hunts as PR-23B (rule P5, PARTY note 58). Results go to results/arena-results-hunter-leadtrace.tsv, -cyclops-leadtrace.tsv and -hunting-ground-pr23b.tsv; traces to scratch lead-trace-hunter.log and lead-trace-cyclops.log. The request waits behind the two heavy windows (eoie F6, main next5b); window admission is first-come, so my own compile jobs would also queue behind it: CPU-light work only until it ends, and no src or apps/arena edits while it runs (run-arena recompiles them per run). Announced to main, eoie and x.")
inl note_of_tibia_33 () = Note ("TIBIA", 33u32, "2026-10-23T03:37Z", "tibia-lane", "Night block moved behind eoie F7 (23:36): at eoie's request (F6 times out at ~00:47; F7 carries the user's job-host fix and must land tonight), I released win-1792725191752 and stopped job tibia-night-block before any grant (probe never installed). Plan: re-request right after F7's heavy-build window is held, with the give-up moved to 04:40 (night-block.ps1 -GrantBy); one-shot check scheduled for 00:51. Expected start 03:30-04:00, end before about 06:30. Meanwhile my compiles are free again; first one is the CEM floor check (AGENT note 32). Announced to main, eoie and x.")
inl note_of_tibia_34 () = Note ("TIBIA", 34u32, "2026-10-23T03:50Z", "tibia-lane", "Night block re-queued 23:49 as job tibia-night-block2 (scratch night-block.ps1 -GrantBy 04:40 -AfterHeldLabel eoie-release-F7 -AfterJob <F7 job>). The script polls eoie window list every 30 s and makes its live-gui request only once F7's heavy-build window is held, or F7's job settles (if F6 installs, F7 exits at its gate). So F7 stays ahead, as eoie asked, and the request still predates main's and x's later heavy requests. Detection checked against main's held next5c window. Same content as note 32; give-up 04:40.")
inl note_of_tibia_35 () = Note ("TIBIA", 35u32, "2026-10-23T04:17Z", "tibia-lane", "Night block yielded again at 00:16 at eoie's request: F7 failed in 13 s on an argument error, and F8 (job-1792728931011, the user's job-host fix) needed the slot. Job tibia-night-block2 was stopped, then win-1792727526737 released (no probe was ever installed). Re-queued as job tibia-night-block3, which requests only once eoie-release-F8's window is held, give-up 04:40. Expected start about 03:00 (after F8 at ~2.5-3 h and main's next5c at ~02:42), end about 05:15.")
inl note_of_tibia_36 () = Note ("TIBIA", 36u32, "2026-10-23T04:20Z", "tibia-lane", "Window state 00:19: F8 holds a heavy window with a 360-min declared lease, and main's unattended chain moved from next5c to next5d (181 min, granted by backfill because it ends inside F8's lease, admission.spi:25). My request (win-1792729009215) waits first in line. Expected: when F8 ends (~03:00) the backfill horizon shrinks to next5d's end (~03:20), so the block starts about then and ends about 05:35, inside the 04:40 grant limit. Risk: if F8 runs long, new heavy requests that end inside its lease can keep backfilling past 04:40, and the block then waits for the next session.")
inl note_of_tibia_37 () = Note ("TIBIA", 37u32, "2026-10-23T04:44Z", "tibia-lane", "Harness (00:4x, live/block.ps1, descriptive output only): after a block, block.ps1 now prints the boosted creature found in the block's logs (Today's boosted creature lines), and a WARNING when it is Troll or Cyclops, or the block's own -Monster kind. Canary halves the spawn interval of the boosted creature (spawn_monster.cpp:359-367, TIBIA-PARTY note 66), so such a block's spawn-based results are not comparable. Tested on PR-23's logs (Wasp, no warning) and on a fake boosted Troll (warning); parses.")
inl note_of_tibia_38 () = Note ("TIBIA", 38u32, "2026-10-23T06:51Z", "tibia-lane", "Night block STARTED 02:50:35 (job tibia-night-block3, win-1792729009215, 180 min lease): eoie stopped F8 after a 1-of-269 timing race (stop_cli after_waits_for_the_named_job) and handed over the window. The probe is installed and the 10 hunter probe runs come first, then 10 cyclops, then PR-23B. Announced to main, eoie and x; eoie runs F9 (stop_cli rerun, then F8 lab steps and install) after block end. No compiles or src/apps/arena edits from tibia until then.")
inl note_of_tibia_39 () = Note ("TIBIA", 39u32, "2026-10-23T08:56Z", "tibia-lane", "Harness (04:5x, live/ only, no src or apps/arena change): live/run-arena.ps1 takes -ServerProbe <lua>. It installs that Canary Lua probe into data/scripts before the runs and refuses if one is already installed. A finally block removes it and moves its trace (<stem with - for _>.log from the canary folder) into the arena logs as <stamp>-<label>-<trace>.log. block.ps1 passes it through with its other arena arguments. Tested on a scratch world folder by running the two new blocks verbatim: install, cleanup, trace kept, and the refusal. The probes landed from scratch into live/server-probes/: lead_trace.lua (proven in tonight PC-8 block) and ground_trace.lua (stub-tested, named by draft PR-26 and rule TIBIA-PARTY note 68). Their trace reader stays an eoie use case (EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES notes 12-13), not a repo script. Restage live/run-arena.ps1 and live/server-probes/.")
inl note_of_tibia_40 () = Note ("TIBIA", 40u32, "2026-10-23T10:43Z", "tibia-lane", "Retirement estimate given 06:4x (10-14 h) is SUPERSEDED by note 42 (07:1x, summed per item, about 40 h after the 07:2x re-correction). Kept from this note: Prediction scoreboard given: first-order solo predictions hold (PR-17, PR-19 all4, PR-20, PR-22, PR-23); second-order and multi-agent ones fail (PR-18 bundle, PR-21, PR-24 duo, P5 late trolls, the cyclops opening in PC-8, M1).")
inl note_of_tibia_41 () = Note ("TIBIA", 41u32, "2026-10-23T11:05Z", "tibia-lane", "SUPERSEDED by note 42 (07:1x). Kept: TIBIA-AGENT is in the retirement scope and is never a parking candidate (user 10-23; TIBIA-AGENT notes 44-45). The arena-orchestration reading in an earlier version of this note was a misread of the user question.")
inl note_of_tibia_42 () = Note ("TIBIA", 42u32, "2026-10-23T11:12Z", "tibia-lane", "THE END, retirement grooming 07:1x (user: groom so we properly know the end, after estimates moved from 4 h to 10-14 h to 55-65 h). The earlier figures were top-down guesses; this one is summed from per-item notes written at 07:11, with AGENT re-corrected at 07:2x from rule A1 (TIBIA-AGENT note 45): the 07:1x version wrongly sized a full library port. In scope, remaining: EVENT-TIME 4 h, PARTY 10 h, FIDELITY 1 h, LIB-MIGRATION 2 h, CELLS-APPS 5 h, TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5 h, BACKEND-MAP 4 h (classification only), AGENT about 12 h (M1 verdict pending; M2 about 3 h CPU; M3 types only, about 6 h; the promotion check; A1's stop rule bounds it). Total about 40 h of work. Out of the estimate, each with its reason in its own note: BASELINES (user pause), ARENA-RELEASE (publishing, user's call), GPU-RENTAL (paid, user approval), STORAGE-BOUNDARY (trigger not met), the headless-client chain (OTClient to the end), 2048-ANCHOR (P4); POLICY-FEATURES is folded into AGENT M2. Laptop time inside the total: about 12-15 h of CPU jobs (the M1 attempt, M2, M3 checks, the Cells app runs, candidate scoring) and about 4 h of live windows in two batchable blocks (L5 with PR-26 and a smoke clear; the PARTY verification with PR-25). The rest is CPU-light code and analysis that runs in parallel with those jobs. Critical path: AGENT M1 verdict, then M2, then M3, in sequence; the PARTY chain (two live windows with a model change between them) runs beside it. Unbounded and outside the total: AGENT's promotion bar, implementing what BACKEND-MAP chooses, and the external dependencies (main's Cells pack with step 11; eoie's EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES), which gate 3.5 h. Any change to this scope is a note-edit here, never a new guess. UPDATE 2026-10-23 14:2x, same method (per-item rules, nothing top-down): about 18.5 h left, from 40. EVENT-TIME about 1.5 h (L5 done: (a), note 127; left PC-10 under L8 and PC-11 under L9, both pre-registered, about 1 h live in one window, then the close). PARTY about 2.5 h (P6 (c), P7 (a), P8 (B) done; S1 is one plain rerun from adoption under D38B; then P9, a 10 min model job, and PR-25, about 65 min live if P9 passes). FIDELITY about 0.5 h (close with pointers once EVENT-TIME and PARTY close). LIB-MIGRATION 2 h and CELLS-APPS 5 h, unchanged, both gated by main's Cells pack. TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5 h, gated by EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES. BACKEND-MAP about 0.5 h in scope (classification done; arena host core, executor and launcher landed; the Gleam executor and the Rust trainers wait on LIB-OTP-ACTORS and LIB-PAR-MAP and stay outside the total, as before). AGENT about 5 h (M1 failed by A1; A4 continues with network.evolve: M2e-2 is in its 4 h window, then M3 if it passes, harness ready, then A5's promotion check; A5 needs 10.25 potions, and the 8-input arm sits at 13.47, so the likely outcome is the final stop note). Live time inside the total: about 2.2 h, batchable into one block (PC-10, PC-11, PR-25). UPDATE 15:1x: AGENT closed by its stop rule (TIBIA-AGENT note 53: M2e failed A4 with no traced fix, so M3 and promotion do not start; the item is Done with a negative result), so about 13.5 h left in scope. S1 is adopted (PARTY note 78), and P9 is running. UPDATE 15:2x: P9 passed (PARTY note 79), and PR-25 is pre-registered, so PARTY is down to its live run and reading (about 1.5 h). About 12.5 h left. The next tibia live window (PC-10, PC-11, PR-25, about 2.2 h, script scratch block-pc10-pc11.ps1) comes after main's cells-pack. UPDATE 20:4x: about 14 h left. The evening block closed L8 (a, with a named source line), L9 (b) and PR-25 (both fail, gap named: the ally logs in 19 s after the knight). EVENT-TIME about 2 h (H1 scoring under L10, then close). PARTY about 2.5 h, up from 1.5 because PR-25 failed: a login-gap rule, likely a harness change so both knights log in within one think, and one more duo window. FIDELITY 0.5, LIB-MIGRATION 2, CELLS-APPS 5 (main's step 11 still unlanded), TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5 (eoie release O), BACKEND-MAP 0.5, as before. UPDATE 2026-10-23 23:08, grooming before the night run (every open item read in full, blockers checked against the tree and the machine): about 14 h left, unchanged. POLICY-FEATURES closed with AGENT (its note 7). Still external: the Cells sibling mount is not in spiral apps/cells (gates LIB-MIGRATION 2 h and CELLS-APPS 5 h, both now needing a fresh compile after main's 22:27 formatter-only compiler pack), and eoie release O is not installed (installed eoie.exe is from 10-23 09:51, no table sequences; gates TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5 h). Night order: CPU-light first while main holds both heavy slots (PARTY login-gap read and its rule, the arena_host new_with_init move); heavy queue in order: the full build.ps1 gate (25 files, also the first tibia check on the new formatter), then H1 scoring under L10, then the arena_host gate; a duo window only if the PARTY rule picks the harness fix and the heavy holders are within about 15 min of ending. UPDATE 2026-10-23 23:31 (night run): about 11 h left. EVENT-TIME closed (H1 rejected by L10 (c); EVENT-TIME note 136 records the boxed-hunter opening as a known limit). BACKEND-MAP's night item done (call timeout 10000 ms, 7 of 7; the new_with_init move dropped, BACKEND-MAP note 16); its in-scope part is done, and only the OS-port arm waits outside the total. PARTY about 2 h: rule P10 (PARTY note 84) chose the harness fix for the 15 s login gap; the patch lands after tonight's full build (job tibia-p10-land), then PR-27 (pre-registered in BENCHMARK) needs one live-gui window of about 75 min. FIDELITY 0.5, LIB-MIGRATION 2, CELLS-APPS 5, TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5, unchanged and externally gated. UPDATE 2026-10-24 05:52 (night run close-out, per item, nothing top-down): about 15 h left. EVENT-TIME closed. PARTY about 4 h: PR-27 ran 02:34-03:39 and failed its pre-registered harness acceptance (ally login within 1000 ms in 4 of 10, median 1155 ms, against PR-25's 14.5 s mean, PARTY note 87), so its tests are unread. Rule P11 (note 88, design note 89) moves the measured entry delay into the model: about 1.5 h of sim code and pins, a predictions job, PR-28's pre-registration, about 80 min live, the read. FIDELITY 0.5, unchanged, after PARTY. LIB-MIGRATION about 3 h: re-land after the Cells mounts fix (gate green, land chained), the S1 and S2 Lua-retire slices proven, S3 designed (am'.sort Lua landed), then a smoke clear. CELLS-APPS about 1 h (from 5): 16 candidates ready, landed by the chained after-block, then the Cells runs. TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5, unchanged and gated. BACKEND-MAP about 2.5 h, now in scope because LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE's granular handle and the world_port owner are proven (5 of 5 and 2 of 2): the joint land plus executor wiring. New TIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL about 2.5 h (user P0 umbrella): offscreen.spi landed, three client.spi slices proven (22 to 9 sites), 9 multi-statement sites left. UPDATE 2026-10-24 07:22 (grooming): about 18.5 h left (from 15). CELLS-APPS about 2.5 h (from 1): the overnight land went red and restored itself, with four reds: competitor lua over 200 locals, measure infrastructure, and scan and map on c missing lib C arms (CELLS-APPS note 19). LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE's split by subject (the user's 06:56 review) adds about 2 h ahead of BACKEND-MAP's 2.5 h. PARTY 4, LIB-MIGRATION 3, GRANULAR-HEAL 2.5, FIDELITY 0.5, TOOLS-TO-EOIE 1.5 unchanged (eoie.exe still 10-23 09:51). UPDATE 2026-10-24 21:13: the park scope and the end estimate moved to TIBIA-PARK (note 1 has rule K1-K4 and the in/out list, note 2 the per-chain hours and calendar: about 25 h plus a 1 h closing pass, park around 2026-10-26). From here on, a change goes there, not here. Changes against the 07:22 figures: TIBIA-NO-HAND-LUA enters (7 h, user 19:4x); CELLS-APPS includes restoring commit 695c708's test blocks; LIB-MIGRATION includes the RED file_exists arm; TOOLS-TO-EOIE leaves the park scope under K2 (an eoie release) and parks with its resume condition. AGENT stays Done.")
inl tibia_local_world () = Task ("TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "Local world, all prebuilt: Canary 3.6.1 (opentibiabr/canary 2026-07-01, canary-windows-cmake-release.zip, map otservbr.otbm, GPL-2.0) + OTClient Redemption 4.1 (opentibiabr/otclient 2026-08-15, otclient-windows-solution-opengl.zip) + MariaDB + the official 15.x client assets the client needs; exit: log in, walk, kill a creature; keep binaries outside the repos; 2026-10-13 06:14 exit met: log in and walk (2026-10-12) and a verified kill (skeleton, experience +52, 2026-10-13) through tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA", "tibia,server", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_local_world () = Planning ("TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl tibia_typed_rules () = Task ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", "Hunt subset of Canary's rules as Spiral modules in the apps/tibia package (grid and floors, creatures melee/ranged/flee, cooldown groups, HP/mana, potions, loot, death penalty); integer-only so CPU and WGSL traces are bit-identical; started 2026-10-12, all passing through run_notebook: geometry.spi (8 incl. prelude), vitality.spi (5, GADT typestate living/fallen), coins.spi (5, gold/platinum/crystal conservation), rng.spi (6, counter-based lowbias32 keyed by seed/tick/entity/purpose, reference values from an independent implementation), cooldowns.spi (6, spell groups plus own cooldown), hunt.spi (4, uses other modules via ///- --package .), hunt_sim.spi (6, deterministic 600-tick hunt, golden seed 7 = 7 kills/140 gold/69 health); every rules test lists ///> rust and ///> c (40 tests, 0 failures, 489 s full run 2026-10-12)", Feature, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA,TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC", "tibia,spiral,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_typed_rules () = Planning ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", Minutes 1800u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_fidelity () = Task ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", "Diff the simulator against Canary as the oracle: deterministic mechanics bit-exact, RNG mechanics through a seeded local Canary build or distribution tests of its damage/loot formulas; one verdict per mechanic, every gap named", Feature, P2, D6, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-TYPED-RULES,TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD,TIBIA-EVENT-TIME,TIBIA-PARTY", "tibia,oracle", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_fidelity () = Planning ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: status was stale (Planned 0%). Verdicts so far: walk steps pinned; step timing and road speed hold (PC-1, PC-2); monster wake holds; melee hit distribution holds (33.6 vs 34.97); swing delay after a step holds (PC-3); potion use still off for retreat (POTION-FIDELITY).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 2u32, "2026-10-18T19:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:28 verdicts added 2026-10-18, each against Canary 3.6.1 source or data-canary: floor change onto an up-ramp holds (geometry.climbed, the live 1940,1372,7 -> 1940,1373,6 pinned); death experience loss is formula-equal (ceil(e*0.1) = (e+9)/10 exhaustive to 50M, level <= 7 spared), live 'loses a level' reproduced; death skill loss is formula-equal (getReqSkillTries table plus the loss loop, against a C# replica), live 'a skill point' reproduced; gear drop is formula-equal (blessing.lua DropLoot), not yet measured live; line of sight is bit-exact (Map::checkSightLine port, against a C# replica); block charges match source (refill per think, zero rolls spend charges, distance spells spend a charge without shield defense); post-step swing: the model has Canary's onCreatureMove resumption (the attack-command path does not apply to our probe, because OTClient's attack toggles); ranged hunters: formulas typed, behavior (keep-distance and cornering) unverified and in gap. Open gaps: potion use (POTION-FIDELITY, damage per landed hit 35.2 live vs 36.5 model), ranged-monster movement, and the RNG mechanics' seeded oracle (ORACLE-RNG).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 3u32, "2026-10-18T21:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 17:04 PR-13 pre-registered in docs/BENCHMARK.md before any hunter run: 3 hunters on the arena spot, spiral-policy (rules heal 160), 10 runs; model prediction 2.67 potions (sd 1.89), 63.6 s with the 200 s cap, 99/100 clear; holds if both one-sample t within 2.26 and 9+/10 clear. First live test of the ranged rules (keep-distance slow-down, checkSightLine port, arrows skip the shield). Live slot granted by the compiler lane after its core compile census tonight.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 4u32, "2026-10-19T01:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 21:51 PR-13 (ranged hunters on the arena spot, pre-registered 17:04) FAILS on its clear-rate rule: 5 of 10 live runs clear against the model's 99 of 100. Potions t 0.40 (3.00 per run vs 2.67); clear time t -0.40 over the 5 clears (61.6 s vs 63.6). No deaths; health conservation 44/44. Uncleared runs end at the 200 s cap with 225 or 450 experience. The log shows the knight targeting a hunter for about 1,000 ticks with no strike, so live hunters escape reach more often than the model's keep-distance slow-down allows. Next: compare the hunter's live step pattern (positions every tick from the probe) with Monster::getDistanceStep and the arena geometry, then fix the model and pre-register PR-14. Results in results/arena-results-hunter-pr13.tsv, logs in tibia-local/arena-logs 20261018-21*-hunter-*. pr2-analysis.ps1 prints 'predicts' because it only checks the two t values.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 5u32, "2026-10-19T06:39Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 02:39 Correction to the PR-13 note: the uncleared runs do not keep a hunter targeted with no strike. They log 'attacking nothing'. All five uncleared runs (1, 2, 4, 6, 9) make their last kill far east (x 1942-1957) after chasing a fleeing hunter along y 1352-1354, and the other two hunters never come back into the client's view. The cleared runs kill at x 1920-1937. Model side (lab/tibia-fidelity, hunter_stall_probe.spi and hunter_companions_probe.spi, outputs saved next to them): the model knight also ends up to 22 tiles east and 21 north, yet clears 100/100, because the remaining hunters shadow it at about 4 tiles (keep-distance approach while within the 11x11 view). Canary's MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT_X/Y = 11/11 matches the model's view, and the Hunter stats (speed 105, targetDistance 4, runHealth 10, staticAttackChance 90) match creatures.spi. So the gap is in how live companions follow. Next: apps/arena now logs a 'seen at x,y: <monster hp% x,y; ...>' line every 10 ticks (competitor.spi, client.monsters_described, scoreboard.due_for_trace); a 5-run diagnostic block (not pre-registered) in main's slot around 03:15-03:30 will show what the companions do.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 6u32, "2026-10-19T09:27Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 05:27 diagnostic block (5 runs, 05:02-05:14, not pre-registered): 4/5 clear (9/15 with PR-13). Uncleared run: knight drags a fleeing hunter 30 tiles east, third hunter falls behind at 5 tiles, leaves view, knight idles to the cap. Live follow pace beyond 4 tiles 0.83-0.93 tiles/s vs model 1.15-1.19 (lab/tibia-fidelity/follow-pace.ps1 on live and model seen-at traces). Model change: ranged hunter beyond target distance steps only on its creature think (hunting_pack.thinks_now) -> model pace 0.91-1.00, 94/100 held-out clears (was 100), stranding reproduced. Canary cause not pinned (path re-plans on every knight move; A* start node satisfies at target distance). Remaining gap 94% vs 60% live. pack_sim test updated (hits 286->173 open, 121->135 arena; kills unchanged) + new test a_hunter_beyond_four_tiles_closes_one_tile_per_think. BENCHMARK PR-13 diagnostic row. Next: find the remaining live stall (walk-back on empty screen, monster idle when no player on screen) before pre-registering PR-14.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 7u32, "2026-10-19T10:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:00 Canary source checks for the residual hunter gap (local canary/src): view is MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT 11x11 (map_const.hpp, matches model); follow re-plans on every followed-creature move (creature.cpp onCreatureMove isUpdatingPath + updateCreatureWalk, async pathfinder) plus every 2 s on think (walkUpdateTicks); A* start node already at target distance returns a path (map.cpp getPathMatchingCond), so hasFollowPath stays true; hunter speed 105 (data-canary hunter.lua) = 600 ms. None explains the slower live pace, so thinks_now stays a calibration. Model gap found: a monster whose target list empties walks back to its spawn (monster.cpp updateIdleStatus -> isWalkingBack, doWalkBack until a player is on screen), the model stands still; same stranding outcome, matters only if the knight returns. Residual 94% vs 60% needs more traced live runs: only 1 of 15 uncleared-capable runs had the trace. Next live slot: trace-on PR-14 pre-registered on the calibrated model.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 8u32, "2026-10-19T10:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:02 PR-14 pre-registered in docs/BENCHMARK.md (before any run): hunter clear on the calibrated model, 10 traced live runs into results/arena-results-hunter-pr14.tsv. Prediction (lab/tibia-fidelity/hunter_pr14_prediction_probe.spi, 100 held-out, 200 s cap): 94/100 clear, 2.36 potions (sd 1.51), 62.0 s per clear (sd 11.8), 15.9 hits, 0 deaths. Holds at >=9/10 clears and both t within 2.26; fails at <=7 clears (P=0.019 under 0.94) or a t beyond; 8 inconclusive. Alternative: pre-rule model 100/100.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 9u32, "2026-10-19T10:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:29 PR-14 RESULT (06:03-06:28, 10 runs, results/arena-results-hunter-pr14.tsv): FAILS on clear rate, 7/10 (pre-registered fail at <=7). Potions 4.10 (t 2.15) and clear time 60.4 s (t -0.31) within. Follow-pace rule holds live (1.00/0.91 tiles/s at gap 5/6 vs model 0.91/1.00). New finding: over 15 traced runs all 4 uncleared reach knight x 1960-1967, all 11 cleared stay <=1953. Model arena spot is radius 30 (terrain.arena_spot_radius, wall at x 1963 = model 130), so fleeing hunters get cornered at the window edge in the model while live the road continues east. Next: widen the scanned spot in apps/map (needs more than two u32 words per row), rerun the probes and the cyclops tests, then a new pre-registration.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 10u32, "2026-10-19T10:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:31 Confirmed the window cut: a lab copy of apps/map with spot_radius 45 (lab/tibia-fidelity/map-wide, walkability-radius-45.txt) shows walkable ground continuing east of x 1963 (rows y 1351-1353 and 1356-1360 open well past it); live tiles 1963,1352 / 1964,1352 / 1967,1334 read walkable. The model's radius-30 window walls this off. Fix path: raise arena_spot_radius past 45 in apps/map (rows need 3 u32 words), regenerate terrain tables, rerun the 251/252 live scan check and the cyclops pack_sim tests, re-predict, then pre-register PR-15.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 11u32, "2026-10-19T10:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:32 Scope for the wider spot (read-only check): apps/map/map.spi row_words packs a row into a (low, high) u32 pair (low_word_bits 32), so spot_radius tops out at 31; terrain.spi reads the pair at arena_spot_low/high, arena_road_low/high, region_high_bits and the region router (lines 106-142, open_low/open_high, marked_low/high). Plan: a typed row of two u64 words (radius up to 63) in both files, radius about 45, regenerate with apps/map/run.ps1 -Update. The lab map-wide radius-45 tables wrap past 64 columns; only its readable grid dump is valid evidence.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 12u32, "2026-10-20T05:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 01:00 arena spot widened to radius 45 (apps/map emits N 32-bit words per row; terrain router generalized; WGSL twins pass) and road speed applied at the spot. Hunter clear-rate gap diagnosed, not closed: live the knight chases a distance-keeping hunter east along the y1353 road at ~2 tiles/s and strands out of sight of its companions; model knight 1.2-1.3 tiles/s. Two knight-speed rules tried and reverted (formula step: 100/100 clears in 45 s; think-gated follow: 97/100). Prediction now 87/100 vs live 16/25; no PR-15 registered. Details: tibia docs/BENCHMARK.md PR-14 post-hoc row.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 13u32, "2026-10-20T06:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 02:04 parking pass: paused. Open gaps named: (1) hunter clear rate (live 16/25, model 87/100 with radius 45 + road speed; diagnosis in BENCHMARK PR-14 post-hoc row), (2) the knight's live step speed (see TIBIA-COMBAT-FIDELITY note), (3) potion means (TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY, paused). Resume with PR-12's 30 retreat runs as fresh data or a new mechanism lead.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 14u32, "2026-10-20T19:17Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 15:17 state after 2026-10-20: closed today: protection zones and teleports (PC-5, model rule, no effect on the arena clear), knight step speed (PC-4: formula speed confirmed; model keeps the client pace), swing after step (PC-6 on fresh logs; retreat-step bug fixed, think period 1083 ms; six-means sum t^2 17.5 -> 8.8), Canary respawn timing (PR-15: kills match), distributional fits for cyclops melee, knight melee and hunter arrows (TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG). Open: (1) hunter clear rate (live 16/25, model 87/100; zones ruled out), (2) potions over-counted on every protection-free arena (parity cyclops +1.4 retreat, hunting ground +2.4 of which shield 12 explains ~0.4): the model's retreating knight is in contact from second 1 and pinned in the dead end (4.0 vs 11.5 retreat steps per clear, 0.3 vs 4.4 s free), see TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY notes 2026-10-20.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 15u32, "2026-10-21T02:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 22:29 D4 (protocol TIBIA note 12) applied, and the hunter clear-rate gap traced to a scenario error: PR-13/PR-14 ran on the arena where protection ends at login (parity layer since 2026-10-15 14:17), but their predictions and PC-5 used mirroring_the_live_arena, which freezes monsters for the 10 s login wake. With the wake removed (mirroring_the_live_arena |> waking_at 0, or the new mirroring_the_current_arena; identical, since hunters are ranged and the new melee timing does not touch them): 45 of 100 clear (was 87), cleared in 59.0 s on average (live 60.4), 2.97 potions per run (live PR-14 4.10), no deaths (lab/tibia-fidelity/hunter_current_arena_probe.spi). Live 16 of 25; Wilson band 45-80, so by D4 the gap is explained within sampling (at its lower edge). Remaining hunter difference: potions (model low by ~1.1 per run).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 16u32, "2026-10-21T09:10Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 05:10 Overnight update (details: TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY notes 79-107, TIBIA-EVENT-TIME). Superseding the 15:17 note: the model's knight no longer keeps the client pace. mirroring_the_current_arena now steps the knight at Canary's formula (paced_like_canary, PR-16 retreat fit), adds the monster dance step, steps everything by Canary's formula on the map's ground speed, and orders the knight before the foes (tick-late view). Hunter clear rate with that bundle: 99/100, above the 16/25 band again, consistent with the 2026-10-20 01:00 note (formula step gave 100/100). Lab traces put it on within-tick order: knight-first 99, foes-first 59, a poll-phase landing 94. Next: TIBIA-EVENT-TIME (event queue), adoption by rule D16 after PR-17 (TIBIA-PR17-BLOCK).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 17u32, "2026-10-21T17:01Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 13:01 Source fact not yet in the model: hunter.lua lists COMBAT_PHYSICALDAMAGE percent -10, a weakness, so hunters take 10% more physical damage (cyclops 0, unaffected). creatures.stats_of has no elemental modifiers. Live PR-18: the knight lands 15.9 hits per hunter clear at 28.6 damage each (257 hits, 14 clears). Expected direction if added: model hunter clears get faster, which widens the clear-time gap (live 64.2 s vs model 55.9 s). So that gap sits in swing opportunities (chase time, swings cancelled by steps), not in damage. Add it only together with a rule written before measuring, scored on clear time, hits and potions per run (PR-18/PR-19).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_18 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 18u32, "2026-10-21T20:41Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 16:41 Hunter clear-time gap (live 60.5 s PR-19 and 64.2 s PR-18 vs all4 55.9), live side measured before the model's (descriptive). Probe status lines every 10 s in the 29 cleared PR-18/PR-19 runs: the knight's target is adjacent in 46 of 165 samples (27.9%), so a ranged hunter is out of reach about 72% of the clear. Live landed knight hits per clear about 15.9 (13-21, slow clears land more: 86.7 s -> 21). Model side (scratch hunter-trace.ps1, runs after the live block): per clear, landed knight hits from per-tick foe-health diffs and ticks with the target in reach, chasing, or none. Reading fixed now: if the model's in-reach share is clearly above 28%, the gap is the chase (hunters keep distance or flee more effectively live: target_distance, flee pathing, the follow walk); if it matches, the gap is in swing outcomes per reach time (hit chance, swings cancelled by steps). A candidate change still needs a rule written before scoring.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_19 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 19u32, "2026-10-21T21:18Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:18 Hunter clear-time gap, model side (hunter-trace, all4, 100 held-out runs, 77 clears; read by the rule fixed in note 18): the knight's target is in reach (distance 1) in 43.4% of the model's ticks with a target, against 27.9% live (46 of 165 10-s samples, Wilson 95% about 21-35%). Distance 2: model 45.0% vs live 51.2%; distance 3: 6.5% vs 19.5%; 4+: 5.1% vs 1.2%. So by the fixed reading the gap is the chase: live hunters hold distance 2-3 more effectively than the model's (their targetDistance 4, runHealth 10 and speed 105 already match hunter.lua, so the difference is in how they move: Canary's distance-keeping step choice, getDistanceStep / flee pathing, or their think cadence while the knight closes). Landed knight hits per clear: model 14.61, live about 15.9 (live hunters take 10% more physical damage, which the model lacks, so live needs fewer hits; the counts are close). Caveat: hits per in-reach second exceed the 0.5 swing ceiling in both, since end-of-tick distance misses momentary adjacency, so compare shares, not rates. Next, under a rule written before scoring: a Canary-sourced distance-keeping step for ranged monsters (Monster::getDistanceStep), scored on hunter clear time, clears and hits (PR-18/19).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_20 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 20u32, "2026-10-21T21:22Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:22 Source read for the hunter chase gap (note 19; no change made). Canary Monster::getDistanceStep (monster.cpp:1733): (1) returns false and lets A* path when distance > targetDistance OR the projectile sight line is not clear (isSightClear(..., true)); holds at distance == targetDistance; steps away only when closer. (2) Its step choice is a fixed table: for a diagonal target it prefers the two orthogonal moves away (boolean_random between them), then the diagonal, and only when fleeing does it try the side moves. (3) stepDuration rises to 2 while the target is adjacent and slows non-fleeing monsters' steps (creature.cpp:1485, WALK_TARGET_NEARBY_EXTRA_COST): the model already copies this (f.nearby, target_nearby_step_factor). Model differences found: (a) its distance-keeping branch (hunting_pack.spi, ranged && distance <= target_distance && geometry.sees) gates on geometry.sees, which is view range only, with no sight line; Canary gates on the projectile sight line (now terrain.sight_blocks via sighting_like_canary); (b) the away step is terrain.step_away, not getDistanceStep's orthogonal-first table with its random tie. (a) alone may push the wrong way (Canary paths toward the knight without a line of sight), so neither is a confirmed cause; both are candidates for a rule written before scoring, scored on the in-reach share (live 27.9%, model 43.4%), clear time, clears and hits on PR-18/PR-19.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_21 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 21u32, "2026-10-21T21:23Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:23 RULE D20, written before any measurement of the candidates. Gap: hunter clear time (live 62.3 s pooled over PR-18/PR-19's 29 clears, model 55.9) with the in-reach share as its mechanism (live 27.9%, Wilson 95% 21-35%; model 43.4%; note 19). Candidates, each a Canary fact from monster.cpp getDistanceStep (note 20), off by default, on top of pace: K1 keeping_sight_like_canary (the distance-keeping branch gates on the projectile sight line, terrain.sight_blocks, instead of view range, and without a line the hunter follows the chase path); K2 stepping_away_like_canary (the away step follows getDistanceStep's table: orthogonal moves first with a seeded random tie, then the diagonal); K12 both. Score (100 held-out runs, the hunter table plus the hunter trace): (i) in-reach share inside 21-35%; (ii) clears inside the central 95% binomial range of k = 29 of 40 (PR-18 + PR-19), i.e. 57-85 of 100; (iii) hits per run within 2 SE of the pooled live mean, 22.15 (sd 8.78, n 40), i.e. 19.37-24.93; (iv) cyclops arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged (ranged-only change; checked by scripts/score.ps1). Tie: fewest changes, then the clear time closest to 62.3 s. Found on PR-18/PR-19 data, so never adopted in sample: a passing candidate only qualifies for a fresh pre-registered hunter block (PR-21) on a later day. If none passes, the gap stays open and the builders stay unused (deleted rather than left as dead options if they move nothing). [Edited before any candidate result was read: 62.0 corrected to 62.3 (arithmetic slip), and the bands for (ii) and (iii) computed.]")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_22 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 22u32, "2026-10-21T21:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:29 D20 K1 (keeping_sight_like_canary, scratch patch on a copy under target/; compiled C differs, so the patch applied) is identical to the base on every measure: 77 of 100 clears, 21.03 hits, 55.9 s, in-reach share 43.8% over all 100 runs (base 43.8%; the 43.4% in note 19 counted cleared runs only), arms unchanged (S 3.01). On the arena spot the projectile line between a hunter within distance 4 and the knight is evidently always clear, so the gate never fires. K1 fails (i) and moves nothing; by D20 it is not built as an option. K2 and K12 are scoring now (jobs tibia-d20-k2, tibia-d20-k12).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_23 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 23u32, "2026-10-21T21:36Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:36 D20 VERDICT (note 21, applied mechanically by scratchpad d20-judge.ps1; scratch patches on copies under target/, pace bundle, 100 held-out runs): no candidate passes, the gap stays open. base: reach 43.8%, 77 clears, 55.9 s. K1 (sight gate): identical to base, moves nothing. K2 (getDistanceStep's step table): reach 48.1% (fails i: band 21-35, live 27.9), 99 clears (fails ii: band 57-85), hits 24.92 (inside 19.37-24.93), potions 4.62, 54.0 s; arms unchanged (S 3.01). K12: reach 48.3%, 100 clears, hits 24.99 (just outside), 54.1 s. So the hypothesis behind K2, that the model's hunters back off diagonally at 3x step cost and get caught, is refuted: Canary's orthogonal-first table moves the model further from live, not closer. Nothing is built into src (the patches lived only in target/ copies). What remains for the hunter gap: the live hunters at distance 3 (19.5% vs 6.5%) are not explained by the step choice; untested leads are the hunters' think cadence when the knight closes (they move only on thinks in the model), Canary's A* re-path to maxTargetDist when they lose the line, and the knight's own chase speed and path (the model's knight follows at its step formula; live it is client-driven follow).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_24 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 24u32, "2026-10-21T21:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:54 Hunter chase gap, one lead closed by source reading (no measurement needed): think cadence is not it. Canary's goToFollowCreature sets hasFollowPath after a distance step (creature.cpp:1006), and onCreatureMove re-paths whenever the followed creature moves (creature.cpp:475-477), so a hunter backs off on every knight step. The model's distance-keeping branch already runs whenever now >= next_step_at with no think gate (the thinks_now gate at hunting_pack.spi:756 applies only to the chase branch). Remaining leads after D20 and this: the knight's own chase. Live, the knight follows by client chase mode (server-side Player follow, re-pathed asynchronously on each target move, WalkStartPolicy and the ImmediateWhenReady start); the model's knight steps toward its target at its step formula. Live, the hunters sit at distance 3 in 19.5% of samples against 6.5%, so the live knight closes more slowly. A trace of the knight's step timestamps while chasing a hunter (live: the probe's position samples; model: per-tick) would show it.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_25 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 25u32, "2026-10-21T21:55Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:55 Hunter chase, live side at 1 s resolution (the probe's 'seen at' trace, about one line per second; 2037 samples over the 40 PR-18/PR-19 runs), measured before the model's: nearest live hunter at distance 1: 26.5%, 2: 51.7%, 3: 17.5%, 4: 3.4%, 5+: 0.7% (confirms the 10-s status-line estimate of 27.9% in reach). The knight moves 1.28 tiles per second while the nearest hunter is 2 or more away (n 1461; 0 tiles 175, 1 tile 761, 2 tiles 477, 3+ 48), against a straight-step ceiling of 2 per second at 500 ms. Model side queued (scratch hunter-chase.ps1: the same two measures sampled every 10 ticks). Reading fixed now: if the model's knight covers clearly more than 1.28 tiles per second while chasing, the gap is the knight's chase (its follow path or start delay); if it matches, the gap is in how the hunters keep their distance.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_26 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 26u32, "2026-10-21T21:58Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 17:58 Hunter chase, model side (scratch hunter-chase trace, all4, sampled every 10 ticks, in-view samples only as live): knight moves 1.31 tiles per second while the nearest hunter is 2-7 away (n 2664) vs live 1.28 (n 1461), so by the reading in note 25 the knight's chase matches and the gap is in how the hunters keep their distance. Nearest-hunter distance: model 1: 46.1%, 2: 44.5%, 3: 4.6%, 4-7: 4.8% vs live 26.5 / 51.7 / 17.5 / 4.1. Already checked and matching or ruled out: targetDistance 4, runHealth 10, speed 105, the step table (D20 K2 moves the wrong way), the sight gate (K1 moves nothing), think cadence (note 24), WALK_TARGET_NEARBY_EXTRA_COST 2 and the diagonal cost 3 (same constants). One structural difference left: Canary's nearby slowdown is a counter (stepDuration, updated in getDistanceStep) that persists and applies to every step of a non-fleeing monster, while the model applies it only in its distance-keeping branch, but that would make live hunters slower, the wrong direction. Next measurement, live-only and cheap: the hunters' own step rate from the 1-s 'seen at' positions while the knight is adjacent vs 2-3 away (hunters can be told apart by their health % between samples), against the model's; that says whether live hunters out-walk the model's or start walking sooner.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_27 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 27u32, "2026-10-21T22:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:00 Hunter gait, the clearest signal so far (live: hunters matched between consecutive 1-s 'seen at' samples by nearest neighbour; model: hunter-gait trace, per slot every 10 ticks). Tiles moved in the next second by distance from the knight: live 0.86 (n 533) / 0.93 (1086) / 1.01 (612) at distance 1 / 2 / 3; model 0.95 (2139) / 0.66 (2587) / 0.44 (853). Model hunters at distance 2-3 walk 30-55% slower than live, which fits the in-reach excess (46% vs 26.5%) with the knight's chase speed matching. Source-backed candidate: Canary's nearby slowdown counter (Monster::stepDuration) changes on every getDistanceStep call, which runs on each move of the followed knight and on each think (onCreatureMove -> updateCreatureWalk; goToFollowCreature), so the x2 cost decays within a step or two of the knight leaving; the model's f.nearby changes only on the hunter's own distance-keeping steps, so the slowdown lingers at distance 2-3. Candidate for a rule written before scoring (D22): update the nearby counter on each knight step and each hunter think, as Canary does; score on the gait at distance 2-3, the in-reach share (21-35%), clears (57-85) and hits (19.37-24.93). In sample (found on PR-18/19), so it would need a fresh hunter block.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_28 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 28u32, "2026-10-21T22:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:02 RULE D22, written before any measurement of the candidate. Diagnosis (hunter-why trace, all4): model hunters at distance 2-3 wait on their step clock in 93.8% of ticks, 61.8% with the nearby slowdown on, and step in 4.2%; live hunters at 2-3 walk about 1 tile per second. Candidate K3 (one Canary fact, off by default, on top of pace): the nearby counter (Monster::stepDuration) is updated on each getDistanceStep call, i.e. on each move of the followed knight and each think, as well as the hunter's own step (creature.cpp onCreatureMove -> updateCreatureWalk -> goToFollowCreature; monster.cpp:1748-1755): +1 up to 2 when the knight is adjacent, -1 down to 0 otherwise. Score on 100 held-out runs (scratch patch, then score.ps1 plus traces): (i) in-reach share inside 21-35%; (ii) clears inside 57-85; (iii) hits per run inside 19.37-24.93; (iv) arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged; plus descriptive: the gait at distance 2-3 against live 0.93 / 1.01 tiles per second. In sample (found on PR-18/19), so passing only qualifies K3 for a fresh pre-registered hunter block (PR-21) on a later day; failing leaves the gap open and K3 unbuilt.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_29 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 29u32, "2026-10-21T22:09Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:09 D22 VERDICT (note 28, applied mechanically by d20-judge.ps1): K3 fails. Reach 43.7% (band 21-35), 78 clears, hits 21.09, 55.8 s, arms unchanged; gait at distance 1/2/3: 0.95 / 0.66 / 0.47 (base 0.95 / 0.66 / 0.44, live 0.86 / 0.93 / 1.01). Updating the nearby counter the Canary way barely moves anything, so the lingering slowdown is not the main cause either. Arithmetic: a speed-105 hunter steps 601 ms on arena ground, rounded to 650 (700 on the 100 ms tick); a diagonal step is about 2 s and is never slowed; the model's hunters at 2-3 step on 4.2% of ticks, about 2.4 s per step, which points to mostly diagonal steps (best_step tries the diagonal first). K2, which tries orthogonal moves first, made reach worse, so its gait is being measured now (job tibia-gait-k2) to see whether orthogonal steps make the hunters faster but walk them into the knight's path.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_30 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 30u32, "2026-10-21T22:10Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:10 Hunter gait under K2 (getDistanceStep's orthogonal-first table, scratch): tiles per 1 s at distance 1/2/3: 0.78 / 0.66 / 0.80 (base 0.95 / 0.66 / 0.44; live 0.86 / 0.93 / 1.01). So K2 moves the gait toward live at distances 1 and 3, as the diagonal-cost arithmetic predicted, but not at distance 2, where live hunters spend half their time (51.7%), and the in-reach share still rose (48.1%). Open question, stated precisely: why does a model hunter at distance 2 from the knight move only 0.66 tiles per second under every variant tried (base, K1, K2, K3), while live it moves 0.93? Distance 2 is where getDistanceStep's straight cases try the sideways moves (W/E with offsetx <= 0 etc.) that keep the distance; the model's best_step only accepts strictly improving tiles, and K2's table applies only while distance < targetDistance. Next session: split the distance-2 waiting ticks by cause (diagonal cost, slowdown, stuck, shot) under K2, before writing D23.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_31 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 31u32, "2026-10-21T22:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:13 Distance-2 step split (hunter-steps trace, hunters at Chebyshev 2 from the knight at the tick start). Base: one step per 3.35 s, diagonal 444 / slowed straight 116 / unslowed straight 247 of 807 steps (55% diagonal, each leaving a 2 s cooldown). K2 (getDistanceStep table): one step per 1.85 s, diagonal 148 / slowed 148 / unslowed straight 960 of 1256 (12% diagonal). Live hunters at 2 move about 0.93 tiles per second, roughly one step per second. So best_step's diagonal-first order is a real, source-backed difference that roughly halves the hunters' step rate at distance 2; K2 fixes that half. But stepping whenever allowed, K2's mix predicts about 0.9 s per step, and it observes 1.85 s, so something still holds K2's hunters back about half the time they could step, and K2's reach rose instead of falling (D20). Next session: per-tick causes of a K2 hunter at distance 2 not stepping while its clock allows (no improving or sideways tile free, the knight's tile, other hunters), then a D23 candidate that keeps K2's step table and fixes that cause.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_32 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 32u32, "2026-10-21T22:16Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:16 K2 distance-2 free/wait split (hunter-free trace): of 23233 hunter-ticks at distance 2, 94% wait on the step clock with 755 ms left on average, 5.4% step, 0.6% are free but stay. So K2's hunters are not blocked by terrain or crowding; their cooldowns are long. K2's step mix (76% straight at 700 ms on the 100 ms tick, 12% slowed 1400, 12% diagonal 2000) would leave about 580 ms on average for a tick sampled inside a cooldown; 755 ms says the cooldowns are longer than that mix. Known small contributor: the 100 ms tick rounds Canary's 650 ms (50 ms beat) up to 700 (+8%). Not yet explained: the rest. Next session: log each hunter step's cooldown length and kind directly (per-step, not per-tick), compare with the live step interval from the 1-s trace (about one tile per second at distance 2-3), then write D23. Hunter thread paused here for today.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_33 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 33u32, "2026-10-21T22:25Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:25 Per-step hunter cooldowns at distance 1-3 (hunter-cool trace, slain-slot resets filtered): base 4597 steps, mean 1233 ms: diagonal 29% at 1909, slowed straight 32% at 1300, plain straight 38% at 663; K2 5434 steps, mean 1094: diagonal 8% at 1950, slowed 52% at 1300, plain 40% at 652. K2 removes the diagonals, and then the nearby slowdown catches half its steps; K3 (Canary's counter updates) did nothing alone because the base's diagonal steps are never slowed. The two Canary facts interact and were only tested apart. RULE D23, written before measuring: candidate K23 = K2 + K3 (getDistanceStep's step table and stepDuration updated on each knight move and think, both from monster.cpp), off by default, on top of pace. Same score as D20/D22: (i) in-reach share 21-35%, (ii) clears 57-85, (iii) hits 19.37-24.93, (iv) arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged; descriptive: gait at distance 1/2/3 against live 0.86 / 0.93 / 1.01. In sample, so passing only qualifies K23 for a fresh hunter block (PR-21) on a later day.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_34 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 34u32, "2026-10-21T22:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:30 Live uncleared hunter runs, examined (11 of 40 in PR-18/PR-19): each killed 1 or 2 hunters, then the survivors were last seen at 4-24% health and were in view in only 15-46 of the run's 149 one-second samples. So a live failure is wounded hunters fleeing (runHealth 10, Canary getDistanceStep with flee = true plus A* to the view-port edge, getPathSearchParams maxTargetDist = MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT_X) and staying out of sight. That is why D20-D23 keep failing the clears band in one direction: every candidate changed distance-keeping, and whenever the model's hunters keep their distance the Canary way (K2: 99 clears, K23: 96) they die before they can flee away. The clears criterion is decided by the flee/escape mechanics (the model: step_away while below run_health, and a reset to spawn at escape_distance 8), so the next hunter rule should pair the distance-keeping facts with Canary's flee: the flee step table (getDistanceStep flee branch), flee paths to the view-port edge, and no return to spawn.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_35 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 35u32, "2026-10-21T22:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:31 RULE D24, written before any measurement of the candidates. Source: summoned monsters (the arena's /m) have no spawn: Monster::isInSpawnRange returns true when spawnMonster has expired (monster.cpp:2414-2417) and nothing walks them home; with no player in view a monster goes idle (monster.cpp:369). So a wounded hunter that flees out of the knight's view stays there, idle, with its low health, which matches the live uncleared runs (note 34). The model instead resets an escaped foe to fresh_foe at its spawn tile with full health (hunting_pack.spi flee branch, escape_distance 8). Candidates (off by default, on top of pace): F = escaped foes in a camp without Canary spawns stay where they fled with their health and lose the knight as target (no reset); K23F = K2 + K3 + F. Score as D20/D22/D23: (i) in-reach share 21-35%, (ii) clears 57-85, (iii) hits 19.37-24.93, (iv) arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged (the hunting ground uses respawning_like_canary, which keeps its own spawn rule, and must stay unchanged); descriptive: gait at distance 1/2/3. Tie: fewest changes, then clear time closest to 62.3 s. In sample, so passing only qualifies the candidate for a fresh hunter block (PR-21) on a later day.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_36 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 36u32, "2026-10-21T22:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:32 D23 VERDICT (note 33, mechanical): K23 (K2 + K3) fails: reach 47.7% (band 21-35), 96 clears (band 57-85), hits 24.46 (inside), 53.9 s, arms unchanged; gait 0.77 / 0.67 / 0.81 at distance 1/2/3 (live 0.86 / 0.93 / 1.01). Like K2 it raises the clears far above the band, which note 34 traces to the flee/escape mechanics; D24 (note 35) tests that next: F alone and K23F (job tibia-d24).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_37 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 37u32, "2026-10-21T22:37Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:37 D24 F alone (stay where fled in summoned camps): identical to the base (77 clears, hits 21.03, arms unchanged), so the escape reset never fires on the arena spot. The base model's uncleared runs already fail the live way: 23 of 100, kills 1 (10) or 2 (13), and the knight has no target for 85% of the run (the survivors are out of view), against live 11 of 40 with kills 1 (9) or 2 (2) and a hunter in view in 15-46 of 149 samples. So the base gets the clear rate right for the right reason, and K2/K23 break it by keeping the hunters in view until they die (96-99 clears). Implication for the next hunter rule: a distance-keeping fix has to leave wounded hunters able to get out of view, i.e. it must pair K2's step table with Canary's flee (getDistanceStep flee branch plus the A* to the view-port edge, note 34), not with the escape reset. K23F is scoring now for completeness.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_38 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 38u32, "2026-10-21T22:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:40 Design for the next hunter candidate (D25, rule still to be written before scoring), from source: a fleeing Canary monster (health <= runHealth) calls getDistanceStep(flee = true), whose table adds the flee-only moves (sideways and, as a last resort, toward the player), and paths with getPathSearchParams' fleeing branch: maxTargetDist = MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT_X = 11 (client view 8 + 3), keepDistance, no clear-sight requirement (monster.cpp:2683-2688, map_const.hpp:12-14). The model flees with terrain.step_away (strictly improving tiles only) and resets at escape_distance 8, which never fires on the arena spot (D24 F). Candidate pairing per note 37: K2's step table for distance-keeping plus Canary's flee (the flee branch of the same table, stepping until 11 tiles away, then idle where it stands), so wounded hunters can still leave the knight's 15x11 screen while healthy ones keep their distance the Canary way. Score as D20-D24 (reach 21-35%, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, arms unchanged; gait descriptive).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_39 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 39u32, "2026-10-21T22:41Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:41 D24 VERDICT (note 35, mechanical): no candidate passes. F alone is identical to the base (77 clears, hits 21.03; the escape reset never fires on the arena spot). K23F = K23 (96 clears, outside 57-85; hits 24.46), so F adds nothing to it either. Today's hunter chain D20-D24 is closed with every candidate rejected and nothing built into src; what it established is in notes 19-38: the knight's chase matches, model hunters walk slower at 2-3 tiles because of diagonal-first steps and the x2 slowdown, and the base fails clears the live way; the next candidate (D25, design in note 38) pairs Canary's step table with Canary's flee so wounded hunters still leave the screen.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_40 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 40u32, "2026-10-21T22:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:42 RULE D25, written before any measurement. Candidate K25 = K2 + K3 + Canary's flee step (scratch patch, off by default, on top of pace): while health < run_health the hunter steps by getDistanceStep's flee table (monster.cpp:1733-2222 with flee = true: the distance-keeping moves, then the flee-only sideways moves regardless of the offset sign, then the diagonals, then a step toward the player as a last resort), instead of terrain.step_away. Left out on purpose: Canary's A* fallback (getPathTo with keepDistance up to MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT_X = 11) when the table gives no step; if K25 fails on clears, that fallback is the next candidate. Score as D20-D24: (i) reach 21-35%, (ii) clears 57-85, (iii) hits 19.37-24.93, (iv) arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged; gait descriptive. In sample, so passing only qualifies K25 for a fresh hunter block (PR-21).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_41 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 41u32, "2026-10-21T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:49 D25 VERDICT (note 40, mechanical): K25 (K2 + K3 + Canary's flee step table) fails: 96 clears (band 57-85), hits 24.45, arms unchanged, hunting-ground kills 13.18 (trolls also flee through the patched branch; within band). The flee table alone does not let wounded hunters leave the knight's view in the model, as D25 anticipated. The next candidate is the part D25 left out: Canary's A* flee path (getPathTo with the fleeing search params: keepDistance, maxTargetDist 11, no clear-sight requirement) when the table gives no step, i.e. a path search away from the knight rather than one greedy step. That needs a keep-distance path search in terrain (the model has route_between for approach paths), which is next session's work. Hunter-gap chain for today: D20-D25, every candidate rejected, nothing built; established facts in notes 19-40.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_42 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 42u32, "2026-10-21T22:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:51 Design detail for the A* flee candidate (next session; from reading terrain.spi, no compile): route_between (terrain.spi:2396) is a bit-parallel BFS over the arena region's open tiles that returns the first step from 'from' toward a target (GoEast/West/South/North, Arrived, NoRoute), already used by routed_step for approach paths. A Canary-like flee needs a target tile first: the open tile nearest the hunter by BFS (same region bitmap, taken tiles excluded) whose Chebyshev distance from the knight is at least MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT_X = 11, else the farthest reachable one; then route_between toward it gives the step. Canary's keepDistance/fullPathSearch = false also stops the search early at the first qualifying tile. Cost: one extra BFS per fleeing hunter step (a handful per clear), cheap. Score it under a new rule (D26) on the same criteria as D20-D25, as K2 + K3 + table flee + path flee.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_43 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 43u32, "2026-10-21T22:52Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:52 CORRECTION to note 34 (and the motivation of D24/D25; their rejections stand): reading an uncleared live log in full (PR-19 run 2) shows the knight chased one hunter about 25 tiles east (1932 -> 1957,1354), killed it at 21.8 s, and from then on saw nothing ('attacking nothing', every 'seen at' line 'none') for the rest of the run. The 'survivors last seen at 4-24% health' in note 34 were the hunter being killed in its last seconds, not wounded survivors fleeing. The live failure is the one README already describes (PR-14 post-hoc): the knight chases a distance-keeping hunter far along the road, its companions fall out of view, and after the kill it stands with nothing in sight. So the clears criterion is about how far a chased hunter leads the knight from the others, which is distance-keeping again; K2/K23 raising clears to 96-99 means the Canary step table lets the model's knight catch its target sooner or nearer, which fits K2's higher reach share. The flee-path design (notes 38, 42) loses its motivation; the next hunter step is to measure, live and in the model, how far from the start the first kill happens and how many hunters are still in view at that moment.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_44 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 44u32, "2026-10-21T22:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 18:53 The first chase decides a live hunter run (PR-18/PR-19, the 'seen at' line just before the first 'Loot of a hunter'): uncleared runs make their first kill 22.5 tiles from the start tile on average (14, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 23, 25, 25, 26, 29) with 1.18 hunters in view just before it (essentially only the target); cleared runs 16.2 tiles (2 to 33) with 2.38 in view. So a run fails when the first target leads the knight far from its companions before dying. Model side next (after the build): the same two numbers per run from a trace (knight's Chebyshev distance from its start at the first kill; hunters within view range then), split by cleared. Any distance-keeping candidate (K2, K23) should be judged on this too: it raised clears to 96-99, so it should show shorter first chases or more hunters in view at the first kill.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_45 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 45u32, "2026-10-22T00:07Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:07 First-chase trace, model side (hunter-firstkill, read by note 44): base uncleared 23 runs, first kill 18.5 tiles from start with 1.26 hunters on screen (live 22.5 / 1.18, same pattern); base cleared 77, 14.5 tiles with 1.17 on screen vs live 16.2 / 2.38; K2: 99 clears, first kill only 5.2 tiles out with 2.78 on screen. So live, the companions follow the chase and are on screen at the first kill even 16 tiles from the start; the model's companions fall behind (base) or nobody leads the knight away (K2). Lead: the model's ranged monsters take chase steps only on think ticks (hunting_pack.spi: 'camp.ranged && stats.target_distance > 1 && thinks_now seed index now = false then p'), while Canary monsters walk their follow path continuously between thinks (eventWalk over listWalkDir) and re-path when the followed creature moves (onCreatureMove -> updateCreatureWalk). Hunting-ground join trace: the second cyclops arrives when the current fight is 8.6 s old in the model vs 10.2 s live (median 5, n 13: weak), in view 4.4 s vs 3.1 s before adjacency.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_46 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 46u32, "2026-10-22T00:07Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:07 RULE D26, written before any measurement: candidate C = ranged monsters chase continuously, as Canary's follow walk does (drop the thinks_now gate on the ranged chase branch; their step cost and the nearby slowdown unchanged), off by default, on top of pace. Score as D20-D25: (i) in-reach share 21-35%, (ii) clears 57-85, (iii) hits 19.37-24.93, (iv) arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged; descriptive: first-kill distance and hunters on screen (live cleared 16.2 / 2.38). In sample, so passing only qualifies C for a fresh hunter block (PR-21).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_47 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 47u32, "2026-10-22T00:09Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:09 Live reference for D26 (PR-18/19 1-s 'seen at' trace, written while D26 scores): companion hunters (every hunter except the nearest, matched between consecutive samples) change their distance to the knight by -0.089 tiles per second on average (n 1594; closer 29%, unchanged 47%, farther 24%) while the knight moves 0.89 tiles per second, i.e. live companions keep pace with the fight instead of falling behind. A model-side companion trace (same measure) is the next check for any chase candidate; D26 is read first on its rule's own criteria.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_48 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 48u32, "2026-10-22T00:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:12 D26 VERDICT (note 46, mechanical): C (ranged monsters chase continuously) fails: reach 44.8% (band 21-35), 97 clears (band 57-85); hits 22.71 per run (inside 19.37-24.93, closest to live 22.15 of any candidate today), arms unchanged, 53.5 s. Like every distance-keeping change today it pushes clears toward 100: once the model's hunters stay with the fight, the knight finishes them all. So the live 28% uncleared runs need something that separates a hunter from the group, which no single Canary movement fact tested today supplies; the first-kill and companion traces (running) say how C changes the first chase. Today's hunter chain D20-D26: seven candidates, all rejected in sample, nothing built.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_49 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 49u32, "2026-10-22T00:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:13 First-chase length decides clears (live vs base vs D26's C): first kill 20+ tiles from the start in 21 of 40 live runs (9 of them uncleared, 43%), 20 of 100 base runs (11 uncleared, 55%), 20 of 100 C runs (1 uncleared, 5%). C's typical chase matches live (cleared: 15.5 tiles, 1.93 hunters on screen vs live 16.2 / 2.38). Two separate gaps: (1) live first targets lead the knight on long chases about 2.6x as often as the model's (52% vs 20%), the part no candidate today changed; (2) on long chases live companions lose contact 43% of the time, base 55%, C 5%, so continuous chasing over-corrects. Next hunter rule should first explain (1): what makes a live target run 20+ tiles (its distance-keeping toward open road, the knight's ReachFirst choice of a far target, or the hunters' spread at the start); live logs give the target's path from the 'approach Hunter at' lines and the 1-s positions, cheap to read.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_50 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 50u32, "2026-10-22T00:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:13 Live long chases, first look (PR-18/19): the knight's first target is at the same two tiles whether the chase ends short or long (1930,1352 and 1933,1351 in 18 of 19 short and 20 of 21 long), so the knight's choice is not what makes a chase long. Long chases end far south (offset -5,+24 x4; -4,+29; -4,+32) or far east (+21,+4 x2; +25,+9 x2), so the target's flight path varies: a hunter keeping its distance sometimes runs down the road south or east and the knight follows. Next: the target's route in the model vs live (the model's hunters may be held by the arena's terrain bits or their path choice), via the 1-s positions of the target, for the next hunter rule.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_51 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 51u32, "2026-10-22T00:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:14 Companion trace, model side (read by note 47): change in a companion hunter's distance to the knight per 1 s: base +0.163 (n 3606, companions drift away), C +0.009 (n 4219, they hold), live -0.089 (n 1594, they close in slightly). So D26's continuous chase moves companions the right way and even stays a little short of live on this measure, yet clears overshoot (97 vs 72%); the clears gap therefore sits in how often a first chase becomes long (live 52% vs model 20%, note 49), not in how well companions keep up. C stays a good component for a future combined rule, paired with whatever makes live targets run 20+ tiles.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_52 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 52u32, "2026-10-22T00:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:14 RULE D27, written before measuring: candidate K23C = K2 + K3 + C (getDistanceStep's step table, stepDuration updated per call, and continuous chase between thinks: the three Canary movement facts that each moved one measure toward live today). Score as D20-D26: (i) reach 21-35%, (ii) clears 57-85, (iii) hits 19.37-24.93, (iv) arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged; descriptive: first-kill distance (live 20+ tiles in 52% of runs) and companions on screen. In sample, so passing only qualifies it for a fresh hunter block (PR-21).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_53 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 53u32, "2026-10-22T00:15Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:15 Live signature of a long first chase (PR-18/19 1-s trace, first approach to first kill): long chases (kill 20+ tiles out, n 21) last 25.5 s with the target adjacent only 24% of the time and the knight's net travel about 0.99 tiles per second, i.e. the target runs in a sustained line and the knight follows; short chases (n 19) last 18.5 s, target adjacent 32%, net travel 0.58 tiles per second, i.e. the fight circles near the start. The model-side equivalents (chase duration, adjacency, net travel) are cheap per-tick measures for the next session; together with notes 49-51 they define what a hunter rule must reproduce: a straight sustained flight about half the time, with companions that keep up only partly.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_54 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 54u32, "2026-10-22T00:18Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:18 Hunter-arena analog of the D21 bracket: at the first 'seen at' after 'policy starts' (40 PR-18/19 logs), hunters stand 0 tiles from the nearest summon-phase sighting 39 times, 1: 33, 2: 35, 3: 13 (mean 1.18), so they move more than cyclopses before the first sample, partly by keeping their distance from the arriving knight, and the summon listing covers only what the GM probe saw. If D21's opening rule is adopted, its hunter-arena effect should be scored as well (opening layout and first-chase length, notes 49-53).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_55 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 55u32, "2026-10-22T00:19Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:19 D27 VERDICT (note 52, mechanical): K23C (K2 + K3 + C) fails: 100 clears (band 57-85), hits 24.96 (just outside 19.37-24.93), arms unchanged; reach and first-chase numbers follow from its traces (descriptive). Combining the three facts that each moved one measure toward live drives clears to the ceiling. Today's hunter chain D20-D27: eight candidates, all rejected in sample, nothing built. The open question for the next session is unchanged and now precise: what makes about half of live first chases a straight 20+ tile flight (25.5 s, target adjacent 24%, net travel ~1 tile/s; notes 49-53), which no movement fact tested today reproduces.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_56 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 56u32, "2026-10-22T00:21Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:21 D27 first-kill trace (descriptive): K23C clears all 100 with the first kill only 5.2 tiles from the start and 2.85 hunters on screen, the same as K2 alone (5.2 / 2.78) and far from live (cleared 16.2 / 2.38). So the getDistanceStep table, as implemented in the scratch patch, makes the model's hunters hold their ground near the spawn instead of leading the knight away; whatever live hunters do to produce 20+ tile flights, the table in this form suppresses it. Checked at once by reading the patch: the K2 table replaces only the step in the distance < targetDistance branch, and at distance 4 the model still dances as Canary holds, so that is not the cause; why the table keeps hunters near the spawn stays open.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_57 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 57u32, "2026-10-22T00:22Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:22 Hypothesis for why the K2 table keeps hunters near the spawn (from reading the table, not yet measured): when the straight step away is blocked, getDistanceStep tries sideways moves that keep the distance (W/E with offsetx <= 0, N/S with offsety <= 0) before the diagonals, so a hunter slides around the knight instead of fleeing in a line; the base best_step accepts only strictly improving tiles, so it always runs away, which gives straight flights but in a slow diagonal gait. Live shows straight sustained flights in about half the runs (note 53), between the two. Testable next session with a per-step trace of the K2 hunter's move kind (straight away / sideways / diagonal) while distance < 4, against live, where sideways moves show as a 1-s position change that keeps the distance.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_58 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 58u32, "2026-10-22T00:22Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:22 Two last measures. (1) Live hunter moves within 3 tiles of the knight, per 1 s (n 2210): farther 31%, same distance but moved (sideways) 31%, still 12%, closer 27%. Sideways sliding is common live, so K2's sideways moves are live-like in themselves; note 57's hypothesis does not explain K2's short chases and stays open. (2) Model first-chase signature (chase-sig trace): base and C are identical (C changes only the companions): short chases 16.0 s, target adjacent 44%, net travel 0.86 tiles/s; long (n 20) 23.2 s, 47%, 0.95; live short 18.5 s, 32%, 0.58; long 25.5 s, 24%, 0.99. The model's knight is adjacent to its target almost twice as often during the first chase as live in both kinds, the same gap as the in-reach share (note 19), and its short chases travel further than live's (0.86 vs 0.58 tiles/s), so live short chases circle near the start more.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_59 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 59u32, "2026-10-22T00:25Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:25 Hunter move kinds within 3 tiles of the knight, per 1 s (hunter-movekinds trace; read against note 58's live 31 / 31 / 12 / 27 for farther / sideways / still / closer): base 35 / 28 / 7 / 30 (n 5779); K2 30 / 33 / 12 / 25 (n 6326). K2 matches live's per-second move mix almost exactly, yet its first chases are short (5.2 tiles) and it clears 99 of 100. So with Canary's step table the hunters' local behavior looks right, and the remaining hunter gap (long first chases, companions losing contact) lies in what the knight does: its pursuit or target choice (ReachFirst picks the nearest reachable; the live competitor's targeting and follow are client-driven). Next session's hunter work starts there: compare the knight's target switches and pursuit path, live vs model, with K2 + C as the hunter side.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_60 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 60u32, "2026-10-22T00:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:28 Knight target switches before the first kill: base 0 (100 of 100 runs without a switch), K2 0, live 0 (one engage line per run in all 40). Target commitment is ruled out: the model's knight, like the live one, follows its first target until it dies. State of the hunter gap at the end of 2026-10-21: with Canary's step table (K2) the hunters' per-second move mix matches live (note 59), targeting matches, the knight's chase speed matches (note 25), yet K2's first chases end 5.2 tiles out vs live 16.2 (cleared runs), and live first targets run 20+ tiles about half the time. Remaining candidates for the next session: the target's route (live long chases run south or east along open ground: compare with the arena's road/ground bits and the model's route choices), and the knight's pursuit start (follow walk from a stop, following_like_canary) in the first seconds, when the target decides its flight direction.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_61 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 61u32, "2026-10-22T00:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:30 Map edge ruled out for the hunter long-chase gap: only 3 of 40 live PR-18/19 runs took the knight beyond 30 tiles from the arena center (the model's arena_spot_radius), none of them uncleared, max 34; hunters were seen beyond 30 in 6 runs. (results/arena-region-r45.txt, the walkability dump at radius 45 listed as uncited in TIBIA note 19, is the reference for this and for the next route comparison, so it now has a use.)")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_62 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 62u32, "2026-10-22T00:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:33 KEY FINDING for the hunter gap (first-kill spot trace, base, 100 runs): all 20 of the model's long first chases end east (kill offsets from the start +20..+24, +4..+6), none south; live long chases split 10 south (-5,+24 x4; -4,+29; -4,+32; ...) and 11 east (+21,+4 x2; +25,+9 x2; ...), with 19 short (n 40). So the model is missing the southern flight route entirely, about half of live's long chases, which matches the 52% vs 20% long-chase gap (note 49). In results/arena-region-r45.txt (walkability, radius 45 around 1933,1350) the south route is the open ground west of the walled building (columns about -10..-6, rows +1..+34; the building's west wall at about column -5 from row +4 to +17). Next session, first: check the model's walkability bits and spawn-to-route geometry along that strip (terrain arena_spot_bits vs the dump, and where the model's hunters stand when the chase starts: live first targets at 1930,1352 and 1933,1351), then a rule (D28) for whatever separates the two. This replaces the pursuit/target leads of notes 59-60 as the first thing to check.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_63 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 63u32, "2026-10-22T00:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:42 follow-up to note 62, two diagnostic traces (base camp, 100 held-out runs each; scratch copies only, nothing in src): (1) terrain is not the cause: the model's arena_spot_bits decoded over rows +1..+36, columns -12..+30 match results/arena-region-r45.txt in all but 2 of 1,505 cells (row +22, columns +7..+8); the open south strip at columns -12..-6 exists in the model. (2) The flee tie-break is not the cause: terrain.best_step tries x+1 before x-1 when blocked (left = shifted 1 sy). Mirroring it for the hunter's step_away (W, both call sites) still gives 18 long first chases, all east (kills at (21,4) x9, (23,3) x5, (22,4) x3, (25,3) x1). (3) K2 (Canary's getDistanceStep table) gives 0 long first chases out of 100, which is why it clears 96. So the base model's long chases all come from one east pocket around (+21..+25,+3..+4). The ArenaSpot spawn trio (99,101 / 98,102 / 98,103) sits at the building's NW corner with its north wall one row south (row +4, columns -4..+4), so a fleeing hunter there has every south and diagonal step blocked. Next session, before writing D28: a per-tick trace of the long-chase target over its first 40 ticks, showing which branch moves it (flee step_away, spawn return, idle wander, or follow) and the tick where it turns east; and from the live logs, the first 10 positions of the 10 south-route targets. Scripts: scratchpad eval-bits.ps1, hunter-killspot-W.ps1.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_64 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 64u32, "2026-10-22T00:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:46 follow-up to note 63, cause of the model's long first chases found (per-tick path trace, base camp, 100 held-out runs; scratch copy, nothing in src). Of the long chases, 7 of 8 printed are the same trajectory tick for tick across different seeds (runs 4, 10, 12, 29, 33, 40, ...): the hunter spawned at (0,+2) from the knight's start steps to (1,4) by t10, the knight reaches (0,3) by t30 and lines up directly west on the same row, and from then on the hunter flees straight east along row +4 (just north of the building's north wall) with the knight adjacent behind it: x +2 at t30, +9 at t120, +19 at t200, killed at about (21,4) after 21-28 s. Cause: terrain.step_away only accepts steps that increase Chebyshev distance, and with sy = 0 its first choice (both = across) is straight east; nothing ever makes it leave the row, so the chase is one deterministic line into the east pocket. Live hunters leave that line: 10 of 21 live long chases end south (-5..-4,+24..+32), through the gaps in the wall row. So the gap is the deterministic, aligned flee step, plus seed-independence (the seed doesn't reach this path). D28 candidates for next session, to be written with the hunter score before measuring: (a) when the threat is aligned (sx = 0 or sy = 0), choose randomly among the distance-increasing steps, as Canary's getDistanceStep does with its random picks; (b) K2's table with only its random aligned picks, without its other changes (K2 as a whole kills every long chase: 0 of 100). Diagnostic to add: each candidate's long-chase share (live 52%) and south/east split (live 10/11). Scripts: scratchpad hunter-path.ps1 + read-path.ps1.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_65 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 65u32, "2026-10-22T00:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:46 D28 pre-registration (written before any D28 measurement; diagnostics in notes 62-64 only). Candidates on the all4 + pace camp (pins in EVENT-TIME note 40), hunter flee step only, knight unchanged: R = when the threat is aligned (sx = 0 or sy = 0) and more than one free step increases Chebyshev distance, pick uniformly among them with a draw keyed by (seed, tick, foe index, new purpose 21); otherwise the current best_step order. RK = K2's getDistanceStep table restricted to its random aligned picks. Score on the 100-run held-out block, as for D20-D27: pass = in-reach share 21-35%, clears 57-85 of 100, hits 19.37-24.93, arms and hunting-ground kills unchanged (|t| < 2 vs all4). Required diagnostics, reported but not gating: long first chase share (live 52%, n 40), south/east split of long chases (live 10/11), first chase seconds (live long 25.5 / short 18.5). Decision: build into src (off by default, builder named for the behavior) the passing candidate whose long-chase share is closest to 52%; tie-break, fewer changed lines; deadline end of the 2026-10-22 session; if none passes, record it and treat the aligned flee step as a known gap in the README fidelity table.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_66 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 66u32, "2026-10-22T00:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:51 D28-R diagnostic, run before the full score (scratch copy, killspot trace only, 100 held-out runs; this is not the D28 verdict, which needs the note-65 score): R (uniform pick among free distance-increasing steps when aligned, both step_away call sites in foe_turn) gives 0 long first chases and 100 of 100 runs cleared within 2,000 ticks, the same over-correction as K2. So any sidestep off the row lets the knight close the gap; the straight-line flee is the only thing that makes the model's chases long at all. Implication for D28: R almost surely fails the clears band (57-85). The live mix (52% long, half south) must come from something that keeps a fleeing hunter ahead even off the row: candidates are the hunter's step cost on diagonals vs the knight's (Canary's diagonal cost x3 on both sides vs our step_cost), or the knight's pursuit re-path delay when the target sidesteps (Canary re-paths on onCreatureMove, but its walk ticks lag). Next: a per-tick trace of R's first chase (gap per tick after a sidestep), compared with the live logs' gap after a direction change, before RK or any other D28 candidate is scored. Script: scratchpad hunter-killspot-R.ps1.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_67 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 67u32, "2026-10-22T00:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:53 D28 diagnostics, part 2 (killspot trace only, not the verdict): R's sidesteps are 2 of 3 diagonal, and geometry.step_cost charges diagonals x3, which alone could explain its over-correction. So R2 = R with straight sidesteps ((0,+-1) when the threat is on the row, (+-1,0) when it is on the column) instead of diagonals: 1 long first chase in 100, 100 of 100 cleared. Also over-corrected. So any flee step that does not increase distance lets the model's knight close in, whatever it costs. The only way the model produces long chases is the straight run, and live hunters turn and still stay ahead. The remaining candidates sit on the knight's side: its pursuit after the target turns (re-path delay, a step queued toward the old tile, or the cost of its own diagonal catch-up steps). First check next session, needing no compile: in the live logs, the knight-target gap over the 3 s after each change in the target's flee direction, then the same from a per-tick trace of R2. D28's candidates R and RK stay registered (note 65) but are expected to fail the clears band; a knight-side candidate needs its own pre-registration. Scripts: scratchpad hunter-killspot-R.ps1 / -R2.ps1.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_68 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 68u32, "2026-10-22T00:55Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 20:58 pointer for the note-67 live check: per-run live logs are C:\\Users\\i574n\\tibia-local\\arena-logs\\<yyyymmdd-hhmmss>-hunter-spiral-policy-<run>.log. Run numbers repeat across blocks (5 logs per run number), so pick each row's log by its results-TSV timestamp, within 5 s of the filename stamp, as scratchpad live-exposure.ps1 does; a bare '*-<run>.log' filter is ambiguous. The 40-run live set behind the 52% long / 10 south / 11 east split is most likely PR-18 + PR-19 (results\\arena-results-hunter-pr18.tsv + -pr19.tsv, 20 + 20 rows). Confirm by recomputing the 21 long / 19 short split from those 40 logs before the gap check. Sample lines read '[tibia-probe] seen at <kx>,<ky>: Hunter <hp>% <x>,<y>; ...', with the knight's tile, then each visible hunter's health and tile. Kills and the current target come from the periodic '[tibia-probe] ticks N ... kills K ... attacking Hunter <hp>% at x,y,z player at x,y,z' lines.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_69 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 69u32, "2026-10-22T02:07Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 22:07 path change for notes 62-63: the walkability dump is now generated at target/map/arena-region-r45.txt by apps/map/run.ps1 (CipSoft-map-derived, never published), and the live client scan lives at TIBIA_WORLD/scans/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt (TIBIA-DOCS-TO-CODE note 11).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_70 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 70u32, "2026-10-22T03:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:12 Live gap check (night N1a, no compile) and D29 pre-registration. Live, 40 PR-18+PR-19 first chases (21 long, 19 short; this confirms note 68's set), samples about 1 s apart: target adjacent (gap <= 1) 30%, gap >= 2 70%, gap >= 3 17%, mean 1.90. Target turns 106 (2.65 per run); after a turn the gap grows 1.78 -> 1.94 -> 2.03 -> 2.04 over 3 s. Model base trace (100 runs): gap <= 1 45%, >= 3 6%, mean 1.61, turns 13 (0.13 per run). Model R2 trace (straight sidesteps): turns 373 (3.73 per run, near live), but gap >= 3 only 6% and flat after turns (1.60 -> 1.67), with 1 long chase. So live targets turn often and still open leads the model's knight never allows. Knight-side fact on record: PC-4 measured the live knight's straight step at a median 558 ms (122 intervals, range 537-566), slower than the formula's 486 that the model's knight uses on grass; PC-4's decision text attributes the extra time to the probe's decision loop, which a chase goes through too. D29, written before any D29 run: candidates on the all4 + pace camp, knight chase steps only (player_approaches, both next_step_at sites): D29a, chase step = max(server step, 558 ms), the PC-4 median; D29b = D29a + R2 (aligned straight sidesteps, note 67); D29c = D29a + R (note 66). Score: the note-65 hunter score on the 100-run held-out block (in-reach 21-35%, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, arms and hunting-ground kills |t| < 2 vs all4). Required diagnostics: long-chase share (live 52%), south/east split (live 10/11), gap >= 3 share (live 17%), turns per run (live 2.65). Decision: build into src (off by default, named for the behavior) the passing candidate whose long-chase share is closest to 52%; tie-break, fewer changed lines; D28's R and RK are scored in the same pass as registered. If none passes by 06:00, N3 applies.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_71 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 71u32, "2026-10-22T03:43Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:43 No-compile measurement and D30 pre-registration. Knight movement while the first-chase target is 2+ tiles ahead, per ~1 s sample: live (40 PR-18+19 runs, 720 pairs) 0.93 tiles/s overall, 1.50 when moving, standing still in 38% of samples; model base (850 pairs) 1.30 overall, 1.31 when moving, still 1%. So the live knight is not slower per step; it stops for whole seconds mid-chase. That makes D29a (558 ms floor) unlikely to matter, since the model's moving pace is already slower than 558 ms per tile; it stays registered and is scored as written. Source: the live knight chases through the server's follow (competitor engage: chase mode + g_game.attack, apps/arena/competitor.spi 251-257), and Canary re-paths a follower only while it has a follow path (creature.cpp 472-477, onCreatureMove); otherwise it waits for onThink, which re-paths when walkUpdateTicks reaches 2000 or on forceUpdateFollowPath (creature.cpp 117-137). A knight standing adjacent has no path, so when the target steps away it stands until the next 2 s update. D30, written before any D30 run: F30 = in player_approaches' fresh-walk branch (the knight idle, the target out of reach), the knight's next step waits for its next follow update at phase + k x 2000 ms (phase per seed, uniform 0-1999, new rng purpose), instead of one step's cost; a knight already walking keeps re-pathing at once on target moves, as now. Candidates on the adopted bundle: F30, and F30 + R2. Score: note 65's hunter score; diagnostics: still share (live 38%), chase speed (live 0.93 tiles/s), gap >= 3 (17%), long-chase share (52%), turns per run (2.65). Decision as D29's (closest long-chase share among passers; tie-break, fewer changes). Scored after the D29 chain; N3's 06:00 stop covers D30 too.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_72 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 72u32, "2026-10-22T03:45Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:45 D30 support, measured before any D30 run (no compile): live knight stall lengths while the first-chase target is 2+ tiles ahead (same 40 runs, ~1 s samples): 177 stall episodes, 273 standing samples; 1 sample 110 (62%), 2 samples 43 (24%), 3 samples 19 (11%), 4 samples 5 (3%). 86% of stalls last 1-2 samples, which fits a follow update every 2 s with a uniform phase (expected stall 0-2 s). The longer tail fits blocked steps (Canary forces a re-path after a failed step) or a target that turns back. This is consistent with F30's mechanism, but the verdict is still the note-65 score.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_73 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 73u32, "2026-10-22T03:48Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:48 Scope of D30, measured before any D30 score (no compile): with the nearest wounded foe 2+ tiles away, the live knight is still in 100% of 1-s samples in PR-17's rules clears (20 logs), 89% in PR-20's retreat clears (moves are the competitor's own retreat steps, not follow), and 98% on the hunting ground (PR-15, 10 logs). The monsters come to the knight there, so follow-driven chasing is specific to the hunter arena. Prediction, written before the scores: F30 leaves the gated cyclops arms and the hunting-ground kills within their bands, and moves only the hunter-arena measures.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_74 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 74u32, "2026-10-22T03:50Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:50 Caveat for D30, written before any D30 score: within live, follow stalls are about as common in short first chases (19 runs: 6.5 stall seconds per run, 41% of 302 chase pairs) as in long ones (21 runs: 7.1 s, 36% of 418). Cleared 17 of 19 short vs 12 of 21 long. So stalls are a general feature of the live knight's chase, not what separates long chases from short ones. F30 may reproduce the stalls and the leads they open (gap >= 3) without moving the long-chase share to 52%. The note-65 score decides either way; the long share is a diagnostic.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_75 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 75u32, "2026-10-22T03:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:53 Where the south routes come from (no compile, 40 PR-18+19 runs). (1) The first target's spot when first wounded decides the long chase's direction: east-side targets (x 0..2, y 2..3; 17 runs) give 8 long-east, 0 south, 9 short; southwest targets (x -3..-5, y 4..14; 20 runs) give 10 long-south, 0 east, 10 short. (2) At the first sample after policy start (about 1 s in), live hunters stand at (-1,4) x39, (-1,3) x31, (-3,4) x27, (2,2) x13 (+ singles) from the knight's start. The model spawns them at (0,2), (-1,3), (-1,4) (ArenaSpot spawn points, Canary's /m ring scan order, manage_monster.lua createCreaturesAround). Two match. The third, nearest to the knight in the model, has stepped away live, to (-3,4) in about two thirds of runs or (2,2) in one third, before the policy's first act. (3) The knight targets the nearest hunter: live it is the (2,2) one (east chase) or (-1,3) (southwest, then south or short); in the model always (0,2), hence 20/20 east. Mechanism: the live knight is in the game and visible before its policy starts (login, then the policy-start delay that D21's +2.8 s term covers), and the ranged hunters keep their distance meanwhile; the model's knight acts at tick 0. Next: a rule (D31) for 'knight present but passive for P ms before the policy acts', with P taken from tonight's timeline lines (05:30 block, the same lines as D21's W), not fitted. It goes in after the block; it also bears on D21's builder design (note of 2026-10-21 17:53), which places the knight only after W, with no passive presence.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_76 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 76u32, "2026-10-22T03:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:54 Correction to note 75's mechanism, from the log stamps (40 runs): @t counts from client start; the login message arrives at a median 6.0 s (3.8-7.3), and the policy starts tens of ms later (e.g. 'last visit' @t+5970, boosted-creature texts @t+5986, then 'policy starts'). So the knight is not visible-but-passive for any real time. The hunters move earlier, between the summon and the knight's login, with no knight present: e.g. summoned and seen at 1931,1353 (-1,+4), first approached at 1930,1352 (-2,+3). That is exactly D21's mechanism (monsters idle-wander for W ms with no knight, then the knight is placed; rule of 2026-10-21 17:53). So D21's W also accounts for the hunter arena's first-target variety and the south routes. No separate D31: when D21 is scored with the measured W, its criterion (d) already scores the hunter arena (clears within band); the long-chase share and south/east split are added there as diagnostics.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_77 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 77u32, "2026-10-22T05:15Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 01:15 Interim scores under note 65 (adopted bundle, 100 held-out runs; d29-judge). D28: R fails (reach 46.2%, clears 100); RK fails (reach 43.9%; clears 85, hits 21.59, arms and kills hold). D29: P29 PASSES every criterion: reach 33.7% (band 21-35), clears 74 (57-85), hunter hits 23.66 (19.37-24.93), arms hold, hunting-ground kills hold. P29+R2 fails (reach 37.7%, clears 90, hits 25.94). P29+R still running. Correction to note 71: I wrote that the 558 ms floor 'is unlikely to matter'; it matters. Why is not yet traced; a guess, not checked: the floor slows the knight's approach steps that ran below 558 ms (straight steps on fast ground, the first step of each fresh walk), even though the average moving pace at gap >= 2 was 1.31 tiles/s. P29's path trace (queued) will show it. D29's verdict waits for P29+R; D30 (F30, F30+R2) is scored next.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_78 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 78u32, "2026-10-22T05:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 01:32 VERDICTS (notes 65, 70, 71; d29-judge on the adopted bundle, 100 held-out runs; band: reach 21-35%, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, arms and hunting-ground kills hold). D28 REJECTED: R (46.2%, 100 clears, 24.42) and RK (43.9%, 85, 21.59) fail on reach. D29: P29 PASSES (33.7%, 74, 23.66, arms and kills hold); P29+R2 fails (37.7%, 90, 25.94), P29+R fails on hits (34.0%, 76, 25.57). D30 REJECTED: F30 over-corrects (34.1%, 20 clears, 15.07 hits); F30+R2 fails (40.2%, 88, 27.59). F30's 20 clears suggest my stateless form (wait for the 2 s update whenever the knight was idle a tick) stalls far more often than Canary's 'has a follow path' state; a faithful version needs that state, so it stays a lead, not a retry tonight. Decision (D29): P29 is the only passer, so it is built into src off by default as chasing_at_the_live_probe_pace (chase step = max(server step, 558 ms), PC-4's median) once the last patch-based chain job has copied src. Rule N7: the 05:30 window runs PR-21 first (20 hunter runs; predictions 74 of 100 -> 11..18 of 20, hits 23.66), pre-registered in BENCHMARK and target/ledger before the window.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_79 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 79u32, "2026-10-22T05:35Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 01:35 P29 built into src, off by default (src/hunting_pack.spi): union chase_pace (ChasesAtTheServerPace, the default in all 3 camp constructors, or ChasesAtTheProbePace), live_chase_step_ms 558, builder chasing_at_the_live_probe_pace, chase_step_ms_at, and both player_approaches sites. The default arm reproduces the old step time exactly, so the pins should not move; a full build.ps1 is queued (tibia-p29-build) after the chain. Required diagnostics for P29 (note 70): long first chases 31 of 100 (base 20, live 52%), all 31 east (live 10 south / 11 east); target 3+ tiles ahead 11% of samples (base 6%, live 17%); knight still mid-chase 1% (live 38%). So P29 brings the hunter score into its bands and moves every shape measure toward live, but the south routes (D21, notes 75-76) and the follow stalls (a stateful F30, note 78) remain open. PR-21 tests P29's predictions in the 05:30 window (BENCHMARK PR-21; target/ledger PR-21-CLEARS and PR-21-HITS registered 05:33Z).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_80 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 80u32, "2026-10-22T08:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 04:02 P29 build check, partial and not yet green (tibia-p29-build2, 02:16-04:00, timed out at its 80-min cap on a saturated machine: several dotnet compilers, 2 GB free). Layout clean; 17 files ran: 15 green (hunt_sim 11/11, hunt, network, policy, lua and the small modules). gpu_sim 2 of 6 failed on a 300 s cell timeout. pack_sim 6 of 36 failed; the one detail printed is an expected-diagnostic test that got a dead compiler worker (GenServer call ended :normal) instead of its Unification failure, which is infrastructure, not P29. But the other five aren't detailed, so P29 isn't cleared yet. Unreached: rng, search, skills, standards, terrain, views, vitality, vocations, wire. Rerun queued as tibia-p29-build-rest2 (only those 11 files), guarded: it skips if it can't start by 04:40 and stops its own tree at 05:20, before the live block. If it isn't green by then, PR-21 still runs (it tests the live competitor, which P29 doesn't touch; the probes build from src at block start) and the check repeats after the block.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_81 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 81u32, "2026-10-22T09:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:28 P29 build check (src with chasing_at_the_live_probe_pace, off by default): pack_sim 36/36 and rng, search, skills, terrain, views, vitality, vocations, wire green (tibia-p29-build-rest2); gpu_sim 4/6, the two long cells (troll hunt + five cyclops clears, hunting ground routing) killed at the 300 s cell timeout while both heavy slots and other lanes' dotnet were busy. Rule: after the live block, rerun gpu_sim alone; green = build check closed; a timeout again on an idle machine = investigate as a P29 cost (the builder adds a branch per chase step).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_82 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 82u32, "2026-10-22T09:35Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:35 No-compile measurement (scratch stall-after-diagonal.ps1 on PR-18+19's 40 live logs; model-stall-origin.ps1 on the path traces), correcting the 'knight still 1% vs 38%' framing of notes 71/79. Notes 71/79 counted a 1-s pair as a stall when the gap was 2+ at its START; split by the gap one sample earlier, the live and model knights differ in two separate places. (1) The target steps away from an adjacent knight (gap <= 1 -> 2+): live knight still through the next second 141 of 144 (98%); model base 191/334 (57%), P29 278/406 (68%), F30 356/416 (86%). (2) Target already 2+ ahead: live still 73 of ~340 (21%); base 6/416 (1%), P29 6/392 (2%), F30 173/889 (19%). Diagonal steps are not the cause: live stalls start after a straight 1-s move 11% (24/228), after a diagonal one 5% (2/42). No 'Sorry, not possible' or 'not enough room' text in any of the 40 hunter logs, so failed steps (forceUpdateFollowPath) don't occur. Canary source (read only): the A* start node already adjacent counts as found (map.cpp 915-919), so hasFollowPath stays true at adjacency (note 19 holds); Player::goToFollowCreature skips for 2 s after a FAILED path (player.cpp 6030-6040, lastFailedFollow); a fresh walk from standing waits stepDuration x lastStepCost from the re-path, where lastStepCost is the cost of the knight's PREVIOUS step, 3 after a diagonal (creature.cpp 1493-1501, 443-451, RespectDelay; ImmediateWhenReady only for client single-step input, game.cpp 4141-4348). The model's fresh walk charges the NEXT step's cost (hunting_pack.spi player_approaches, the delays_a_fresh_walk branch). F30's (2) matches live, but F30 failed the score (note 78), so the stall shape alone does not fix the hunter score.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_83 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 83u32, "2026-10-22T09:36Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:36 RULE D31, written before any F31 measurement. Candidate F31 (one Canary fact, note 82; scratch flag F31 in d20-patch.ps1, sites checked on a copy, not compiled): the knight remembers whether its last step was diagonal (hunter field last_step_diagonal, set in hunter_steps), and a fresh walk from standing waits the chase step times that step's cost (x3 after a diagonal), from Canary's getEventStepTicks RespectDelay, instead of the next step's cost. Runs: F31 on the bundle as it stands after PR-21 (P29 included if PR-21 adopts it, else F31 and P29+F31 both). Score: note 65 on 100 held-out runs (reach 21-35%, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, cyclops arms and hunting-ground kills hold), via d29-run/d29-judge. Pass = every criterion. Several passers: take the one whose hits are nearest 22.15 (band midpoint); tie = fewer flags. A passer is built into src off by default with a builder, then a live pre-registration like PR-21. Required diagnostic, not a gate: model-stall-origin.ps1 (1) leaving-adjacency still share, prediction written now: rises from P29's 68% toward live 98%, and (2) stays near 2% (F31 changes only fresh walks from adjacency). Deadline: first compile slot after the 2026-10-22 night (not tonight: the live block holds 05:30-06:31 and a 100-run score takes about 40 min plus build).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_84 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 84u32, "2026-10-22T09:38Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:38 Correction to note 83, from a no-compile bound before any F31 run (scratch f31-reach.ps1 on the 100 ms path traces): in P29's traces the target leaves an adjacent knight 406 times; the knight's last step before it was diagonal in 94 (23%), and all 94 already stall through the next second (the model's post-step x3 wait covers them); after a straight last step 184 of 312 stall. F31 changes only fresh walks after a straight step whose next step is diagonal (x3 -> x1), so it can only LOWER the leave-adjacency still share, at most to the 68% ceiling it already has. Note 83's diagnostic prediction ('rises toward live 98%') is withdrawn and replaced: F31 lowers or keeps (1) and leaves (2) near 2%. The D31 gate (note-65 score) stands as written; F31 is a source-faithful fix, not a stall fix. What the live 98% implies, by arithmetic: with a fresh-walk wait of D after the target leaves, the chance the knight is still at the next 1-s sample is about min(1, D/1 s); 98% needs D >= ~1 s nearly always, while Canary's documented path (re-path on the target's move, then step after stepDuration x lastStepCost, 558 ms straight) gives ~56-68%, which is what the model shows. So something in the live chain adds ~0.5 s or more before the first step after adjacency; candidates not yet checked: the async pathfinder round trip (goToFollowCreature_async + dispatcher), the probe sampling the client view rather than the server, or the client's own chase/attack packets. Next step, no compile: the probe's 'seen at' cadence and any per-step timestamps in a PR-21 log (written tonight) to time the first knight step after the target leaves.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_85 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 85u32, "2026-10-22T09:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:40 Mechanism found for the live knight's stalls (source reading, no compile; answers note 84). The competitor turns chase mode OFF whenever its target is adjacent: engage (target_code = 2) (apps/arena/competitor.spi 292, 317), client.chasing sends DontChase (client.spi 107-109), and Canary's Player::setChaseMode(false) calls setFollowCreature(nullptr) plus stopWalk (player.cpp 6059-6080). So an adjacent live knight follows nothing, and the target's step away triggers no server re-path. The next probe tick (100 ms) sees target_code 2 and turns chase back on: setFollowCreature only sets isUpdatingPath (creature.cpp 1053-1056), serviced in the player's onThink, every 1000 ms at a fixed per-creature phase (creature.cpp 134-137, game.cpp 7429); the new path then starts with RespectDelay, one full step (stepDuration x lastStepCost) before the first move. First step after the target leaves = probe tick + U(0, 1 s) + ~558 ms; the chance the knight is still at the next 1-s sample is about 0.90 by that arithmetic (live 98%, model base 57%, P29 68%), and short re-adjacencies mid-chase produce part of the 21% 'already ahead' stalls. Differences from F30 (rejected): F30 waited for a 2 s grid on every idle tick and put the step itself on the grid; Canary waits for the next 1 s think, then a full step, and only after the knight stood adjacent.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_86 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 86u32, "2026-10-22T09:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:40 RULE D32, written before any F32 measurement (mechanism note 85). Candidate F32 (scratch flag F32 in d20-patch.ps1, sites checked on a copy, not compiled): a fresh walk from standing (the existing ApproachesAfterAFreshWalkDelay branch of player_approaches, i.e. the knight was idle at least one tick, in the hunter arena almost always adjacent with chase off) starts at the knight's next 1 s think, at a per-run phase in whole ticks (rng purpose 23), plus the existing chase step cost. Candidates, each on the bundle as it stands after PR-21: F32; P29+F32 (when PR-21 does not adopt P29). Score: note 65 on 100 held-out runs (reach 21-35%, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, arms and hunting-ground kills hold) via d29-run/d29-judge. Pass = every criterion; several passers: hits nearest 22.15, then fewer flags. Passer: built into src off by default with a builder, then a live pre-registration. Diagnostics, not gates, predictions written now: model-stall-origin.ps1 (1) leave-adjacency still share 85-95% (live 98%), (2) already-ahead still share up from 1-2% (live 21%), and the long-chase share (live 52%) reported. D31 (F31) stays registered and is scored in the same batch; if F32 passes and F31 fails, F31 is dropped; both pass: F32+F31 is scored once more before any build. Deadline: first compile slot after the 2026-10-22 night.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_87 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 87u32, "2026-10-22T09:44Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:44 PC-7 (live timing check of note 85's mechanism) is pre-registered in docs/BENCHMARK.md (PC-7, written 05:45): instrumentation, scenario, predictions and the decision that applies to D32 live there. Its measure waits for an eoie event-latency verb (requested from eoie 05:46).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_88 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 88u32, "2026-10-22T09:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 05:46 Support for note 85's second claim (no compile, same 40 live logs): of the 73 live 'already ahead' still seconds, the sample before was adjacent (gap <= 1) in 37, the knight was moving in 25, already still in 8, unknown 3. So about half continue a stall that began when the target left adjacency (chase off -> next 1 s think -> full step, often longer than one sample); the 25 after a moving second are not explained by the mechanism and stay open. PC-7's measure now names eoie's planned EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES latency commands (table logs --latency, table query --quantile/--share-at-least; eoie 05:47: lands after its pending releases).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_89 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 89u32, "2026-10-22T10:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:14 PR-21 RESULT (runs 05:30-06:09, all 20 counted, no crash, no death). Clears 19 of 20, outside the pre-registered 11..18 band (central 95% for p 0.74): PR-21-CLEARS FAILS. Hits 23.8 per run (CI 20.42-27.18) against 23.66, t 0.09: PR-21-HITS holds. By rule D29 + N7 (both must hold), chasing_at_the_live_probe_pace stays OFF by default; src unchanged. The live arena cleared far more often than P29 predicts (95% vs 74%) and more than the adopted bundle (77%); PR-18 and PR-19 cleared 14 and 15 of 20 (29 of 40, 72.5%), so live clears vary between blocks more than one binomial rate allows, or something in the live arena changed since 2026-10-21 (to check: the server and client builds, the datapack, the competitor's source snapshot). No compile overlapped any live run: main's four compile windows were granted 06:09:52.9-06:09:54.5, after PR-21's release at 06:09:52, and stopped about 06:10:25, before the D21 window (main, 06:14). eoie friction: experiment analyze reported reject_h0=no from a one-sided p_at_most while the registration's test was the two-sided band 11..18, so the band verdict was read by hand (EOIE request: band tests in experiment register/analyze). Next: the clear rate is now the open hunter-arena gap. D31/D32 slow the knight's chase, which pushes model clears DOWN, against this result; recorded before any D32 score.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_90 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 90u32, "2026-10-22T10:16Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:16 Lead for PR-21's 19/20 clears (no compile, observation only, no causal claim yet): the knight logged in later after client start in PR-21: 'Your last visit' text at a median @t+7.3 s (range 4.9-15.9) against PR-18 3.9 s (3.8-5.1) and PR-19 4.3 s (3.8-6.0). PR-21's logs also carry the summon-to-policy wall gap (the hunters' wander time before the knight acts): median 9.1 s (6.9-17.8); PR-18/19 logs predate that line. Hunters wander for longer before the knight arrives, which is D21's W mechanism (notes 75-76), so the hunter arena's clear rate may depend on the client's login delay, which varies with machine load (PR-21 ran right after a saturated night). The competitor's engage/chase code is unchanged since PR-19 (the staged apps/arena diff is a formatter re-lay plus retreat-only helpers; hunter runs use retreat-at 0). Test, to pre-register with D21's W: score the hunter arena at PR-21's wander times (W21 with per-run W from the 20 logs) vs PR-18/19's; if clears move toward 95% at the longer W, the clear gap is the opening, not the chase.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_91 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 91u32, "2026-10-22T10:17Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:17 RULE D33, written before any score (lead: note 90). Question: does the hunters' wander time before the knight acts explain the live hunter clear rate (PR-18/19 29 of 40, login ~4 s; PR-21 19 of 20, login ~7.3 s, summon-to-policy 9.1 s)? Runs: the hunter arena on the adopted bundle with scratch W21 (idling_before_the_knight, D20_FLAGS W21, d29-run) at D21_W = 4000 and 9100 ms, 100 held-out runs each, plus the existing W = 0 baseline (77 of 100). Bands (Wilson 95%): PR-18/19 29/40 -> 57.2%-83.9%; PR-21 19/20 -> 76.4%-99.1%. Verdict: the opening explains the gap when clears at W 4000 fall in the PR-18/19 band AND clears at W 9100 fall in the PR-21 band AND hits at both stay in 19.37-24.93. Then the next model step is per-run W from each live log's login delay (not a constant), pre-registered separately. Neither inside: the opening is not the explanation; W stays a cyclops-arm question only (D21). One inside: inconclusive, report the curve (clears at 0, 4000, 9100). Deadline: first compile slot after the night, in the same batch as d31-d32 (W21 jobs serialized after them).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_92 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 92u32, "2026-10-22T10:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:29 AMENDMENT to D33 (note 91), before any D33 run: W21's D21_W is the D21-defined W (summon-to-policy wall gap + 2800 ms, EVENT-TIME note 47, d21-w.ps1), and note 91's 4000/9100 used the raw gap without the offset. Corrected runs: D21_W = 11900 (PR-21: raw gap median 9.06 s + 2.8 s) and 8700 (PR-18/19: their logs lack the timeline line; estimated from their login text arriving ~3.2 s earlier than PR-21's, 4.1 vs 7.3 s median; an estimate, labelled as such in the verdict). Bands, hit band and verdict rule unchanged. For reference, tonight's cyclops calibration gave W 9700 (EVENT-TIME note 61).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_93 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 93u32, "2026-10-22T10:35Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:35 P29 build check CLOSED by note 81's rule: gpu_sim rerun alone (job tibia-gpu-sim-rerun, 06:29-06:35, after the live block) 6 of 6 green in 262 s; the two cells that hit the 300 s cell timeout overnight ran fresh and passed (memo_hits 4 = the four that had passed), WGSL compile 152 s and 179 s on the Quadro K1100M. With tibia-p29-build-rest2 (pack_sim 36/36, rng, search, skills, terrain, views, vitality, vocations, wire), every test file is green on src with the P29 builder off by default. The overnight failures were machine load, not P29.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_94 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 94u32, "2026-10-22T10:45Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:45 D33 free data point (from the D21 score job, W21 at W 9700, adopted bundle, 100 held-out runs): hunter clears 89 of 100, hits 23.35, against W 0's 77 and 21.03. 89% sits inside PR-21's band (76.4-99.1%) and above PR-18/19's (57.2-83.9%). So wander time before the knight acts does raise model clears, in the direction of PR-21; D33's two registered runs (W 8700, 11900; queued) decide it. Caveat for D33's reading: W21 also delays the knight on the hunting ground (kills 9.19 fail), so a D33 pass would call for a per-arena W, not the bundle-wide flag.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_95 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 95u32, "2026-10-22T10:48Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:48 D31 interim (rule note 83, amended 84): F31 alone FAILS on reach. Job tibia-d3132-F31 (06:32-06:45, 100 held-out runs, adopted bundle): in-reach share 46.7% (band 21-35), clears 79 (57-85), hits 20.70 (19.37-24.93), cyclops arms hold (t within 1.61), retreat steps 11.7, hunting-ground kills 13.19 hold. Reach is about where the bundle without it sits (43.8% in the 2026-10-21 base trace, which predates the pace adoption, so the comparison is approximate; P29 33.7%, W21 at 9700 45.8%), so F31 neither causes nor fixes the reach excess. P29B+F31 is running next in the same batch; D31's verdict is final when it lands (pass = every criterion; then hits nearest 22.15).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_96 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 96u32, "2026-10-22T10:50Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:50 D31 diagnostic for F31 (path trace job tibia-d3132-F31-path, model-stall-origin.ps1): target leaves an adjacent knight 325 times, knight still through the next second 189 (58%; base 57%, live 98%); already-ahead stalls 0 of 399 (live 21%). As note 84's corrected prediction said: F31 keeps (1) and leaves (2) near zero; the chase-mode mechanism (D32, F32) is the candidate for the stall gap.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_97 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 97u32, "2026-10-22T10:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:51 D31 VERDICT (rule note 83, amended 84): REJECTED, no candidate passes. F31: reach 46.7% (note 95). P29B+F31 (job tibia-d3132-P29B-F31, 06:32-06:50, 100 held-out runs): reach 37.1% (band 21-35) fails; clears 75, hits 22.22 (closest yet to the 22.15 midpoint), retreat steps 11.1, cyclops arms and hunting-ground kills (11.75) hold. F31 adds about 3 points of reach on either base (P29 alone 33.7% -> 37.1%), so the previous-step cost is a source fact the hunter score does not reward; it stays a scratch flag. D32 (F32, P29B+F32) and D33 (W 8700, 11900) continue in the same batch.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_98 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 98u32, "2026-10-22T10:52Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:52 D31 diagnostic for P29B+F31 (path rows hunter-path-P29B,F31-rows.tsv; the path runner keeps the comma in the name): leave-adjacency still 282 of 406 (69%; P29 alone 68%, live 98%), already-ahead stalls 0 (live 21%). Same as F31 alone: the previous-step cost leaves the stall shape where it was.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_99 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 99u32, "2026-10-22T10:56Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:56 D32 interim (rule note 86): F32 alone FAILS on clears. Job tibia-d3132-F32 (06:51-06:55, 100 held-out runs, adopted bundle): in-reach 31.5% (band 21-35, the first candidate tonight inside it without P29), clears 53 (57-85) fails, hits 20.83 (19.37-24.93), cyclops arms hold (t within 1.61), retreat steps 11.7, hunting-ground kills 12.72 hold. Direction as note 89 predicted before any D32 score: the chase-mode restart delay slows the knight and pushes clears down. P29B+F32 is next in the batch; D32's verdict is final when it lands.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_100 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 100u32, "2026-10-22T10:56Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 06:56 D32 diagnostics for F32 (path job tibia-d3132-F32-path, model-stall-origin.ps1), both inside note 86's written predictions: leave-adjacency still 387 of 427 (91%; predicted 85-95%, live 98%, every earlier model 57-69%); already-ahead stalls 122 of 871 (14%; predicted up from 1-2%, live 21%). So the chase-mode mechanism (note 85) reproduces the live stall shape, the first candidate to do so, yet the model's clears fall to 53 (live 72.5-95%). Stalls and clears are now in tension: with live-like stalls the model knight catches too few hunters, so something else in the live arena makes clearing easier (candidates already named: the opening/W, note 90 and D33; the hunters' own pace). Recorded before P29B+F32 and D33 land.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_101 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 101u32, "2026-10-22T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 07:00 D32 VERDICT (rule note 86): REJECTED, no candidate passes. F32 (note 99): reach 31.5% in band, clears 53 fail. P29B+F32 (job tibia-d3132-P29B-F32, 06:55-07:00): reach 26.6% in band, but clears 19 (57-85), hits 17.27 (19.37-24.93) and hunting-ground kills 10.99 fail; arms and retreat steps (11.1) hold. Both slow the knight's chase, and stacking P29's 558 ms floor on the chase-mode restart collapses clears. F32 stays a scratch flag: it is the only model of the live stall shape (note 100), so it is the base for D33's follow-up if the opening (W) restores clears. D33 (W 8700, 11900, on the bundle without F32) still runs.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_102 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 102u32, "2026-10-22T11:11Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 07:11 D33 VERDICT (rule note 91, amended 92): INCONCLUSIVE (one condition inside). W 8700: clears 89, outside PR-18/19's band 57.2-83.9% (hits 24.06 in band). W 11900: clears 87, inside PR-21's band 76.4-99.1% (hits 22.94 in band). The curve, as the rule asks: clears 77 at W 0, 89 at 8700, 89 at 9700 (D21 job), 87 at 11900; in-reach 44.9-46.3% throughout; hunting-ground kills fall to 9.6-10.0 under W21 (bundle-wide flag). Reading: any wander before the knight acts lifts model clears from 77 to about 88 and then saturates, so the login-delay difference between PR-18/19 (est. W 8700) and PR-21 (W 11900) cannot by itself produce 72.5% vs 95%. Next by the day protocol (TIBIA note 27): PR-22 decides which live rate the model should target before any further candidate is scored.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_103 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 103u32, "2026-10-22T11:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 07:13 Login delay vs clears across every live hunter block on disk (spiral-policy, no compile; descriptive, no causal claim): PR-13 5/10 clears, median login @t+4.4 s; PR-14 7/10, 8.5 s; PR-18 14/20, 3.9 s; PR-19 15/20, 4.3 s; PR-21 19/20, 7.3 s. Runs with login < 6 s 39 of 55 cleared (71%), >= 6 s 21 of 25 (84%, 19 of the 25 from PR-21). PR-14 had an even later login than PR-21 and cleared 7 of 10, so login delay alone does not track the rate (D33 found the same in the model: clears saturate once the hunters wander). PR-22 records login and summon-to-policy for every run; its rule (BENCHMARK) decides which live rate stands.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_104 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 104u32, "2026-10-22T12:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 08:14 Link to EVENT-TIME's D35 (notes 70-72 there), recorded before PR-22: the 2.5 s protected lead (cyclops and hunters random-step between login and the policy start because the knight is login-protected until its first attack) applies to the hunter arena too, which summons its hunters the same way. In D35's score job (W21 at W 2500, adopted bundle, 100 held-out runs) the hunter arena gave 85 clears and 24.37 hits, against 77 and 21.03 without the lead (in-reach share 43.4%, above the 21-35% band, like the bundle without P29 at about 44%). So the protected lead moves both hunter measures toward PR-21's live 95% clears and 23.8 hits. Which live clear rate the model should target is still PR-22's call (day protocol, TIBIA note 27); if PR-22 lands at 19 or more clears, D35's lead is the first candidate to score against that band, together with D33's finding that the opening saturates clears near 88.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_105 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 105u32, "2026-10-22T15:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 11:28 PR-22 result (BENCHMARK): 14 of 20 cleared, k <= 16, so PR-21 (19 of 20) was an outlier and the hunter target is PR-18/19 rate 0.725 (live without PR-21: 43 of 60). The adopted bundle predicts 77 of 100, consistent with it. Login delay does not explain clears here (cleared runs logged in after 5.47 s, uncleared 6.34 s). Hits taken 20.45 per run vs the bundle 21.03. Per TIBIA note 27, hunter-arena candidates may now be scored against 0.725.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_106 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 106u32, "2026-10-22T15:37Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 11:37 D37 RULE, written before any score. Basis: PR-22 set the hunter target at 0.725 (note 105); D32 named F32 (chase-mode restart, the only model of the live stall shape) as the base for a follow-up if the opening restores clears; D35 (EVENT-TIME note 72) showed the 2.5 s protected lead lifts clears 77 to 85. Candidate: W21 at W 2500 plus F32 on the adopted bundle, one score job (d21-score -W 2500 -Flags W21,F32, 100 held-out runs). Pass needs ALL of: hunter in-reach 21-35 percent, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, cyclops arms hold, hunting-ground kills hold (score d_kills), and D35s retreat criteria (b) Welch abs t <= 2 vs 11.05, (c1) 32.26-53.43 percent, (c2) 42-63 percent. Pass: pre-register a live block (PR-24) before adoption; nothing joins the bundle on the score alone. Any failure: REJECTED, F32 and W21 stay scratch flags, and the verdict names which criteria failed. Prediction written now: clears near 60 (F32 53 plus the lead), c1 near D35s 32, so c1 is the likeliest failure. Runs after the LIB-MIGRATION verify job.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_107 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 107u32, "2026-10-22T16:44Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 12:44 D37 VERDICT (rule note 106): REJECTED, 3 of 8 criteria fail. Job tibia-d37-w2500 (W21 at W 2500 plus F32 on the adopted bundle, 100 held-out runs). Pass: hunter in-reach 33.3 percent (21-35; computed from hunter-trace-W21F32 rows the d20-judge way), clears 79 (57-85), cyclops arms (t PR-11 1.19, PR-12 0.36, PR-16 0.97/0.17, PR-17 1.45/-1.20), (b) retreat steps 13.19 vs 11.05 Welch t 1.20, (c2) first pin 46 percent (42-63). FAIL: hunter hits 26.13 (19.37-24.93), hunting-ground kills 11.17 (score d_kills false), (c1) first retreat from 1933,1350 28 percent (32.26-53.43), the failure the rule predicted. Reading: the lead plus the chase-mode restart puts clears and in-reach where live is (the first candidate to hit both with the live stall shape) but over-counts hits by about 1.2 per run above the band top and under-counts hunting-ground kills, as W21 did before (D33: kills 9.6-10.0 at long W). F32 and W21 stay scratch flags; nothing is adopted.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_108 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 108u32, "2026-10-22T16:45Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 12:45 PAUSED with a mechanical resume condition. State: against PR-22s target (0.725) the adopted bundle holds clears (77) and hits (21.03); the open hunter gap is the in-reach share (bundle about 44 percent vs 21-35) with the live stall shape (leave-adjacency 98 percent live). Every source-backed candidate named so far is scored and rejected (P29, F31, F32, P29B+F32, W21 at 8700/11900, D35 W21 2500, D37 W21+F32). Resume when either holds: (1) eoie ships the sequences verb (EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES, latency kind) so PC-7s pre-registered measure runs on PR-22s 20 logs (knight first step after the target leaves), or (2) a new Canary source fact names a mechanism for the in-reach gap not yet scored. Either resume writes its rule here before any score.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_109 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 109u32, "2026-10-22T19:50Z", "tibia-lane", "RESUMED by condition (2) of note 108: a new Canary source fact names an unscored mechanism for the in-reach gap. monster.cpp:960 isFleeing is getHealth() <= runAwayHealth; the model flees on health < run_health at three sites (hunting_pack foe step, the fleeing foe holding fire, the fleeing network feature). So a hunter (runHealth 10, Canary hunter.lua) at exactly 10 health keeps fighting in the model and runs away in Canary, and so does a troll at exactly 15. Fleeing moves a hunter out of reach, so the model over-counts in-reach in the direction of the gap (bundle about 44 vs live 21-35 percent); size unknown. Fatal Hold (iobestiary.cpp:180) needs a charm and does not apply. D38 RULE, written before any score: candidate F34 (scratch d20-patch.ps1 -F34, all three sites to <=) on the adopted bundle, one score job (d21-score -W 0 -Flags F34, 100 held-out runs), D37 criteria unchanged: hunter in-reach 21-35 percent, clears 57-85, hits 19.37-24.93, cyclops arms hold, hunting-ground kills hold (d_kills), retreat (b) Welch abs t <= 2 vs 11.05, (c1) 32.26-53.43, (c2) 42-63. (A) All pass: pre-register a live block before adoption. (B) In-reach still fails but every criterion the adopted bundle passes today still passes: F34 joins the bundle as a source-exact fix (FIDELITY title: deterministic mechanics bit-exact), build.ps1 green first, and the in-reach gap stays named. (C) Otherwise REJECTED with the failing criterion named; a source-exact fix that breaks a passing criterion means a second mechanism hides behind it, which becomes the next named gap.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_110 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 110u32, "2026-10-22T20:01Z", "tibia-lane", "D38 VERDICT (rule note 109): outcome (B), F34 JOINS THE BUNDLE as a source-exact fix; the in-reach gap stays named. Job tibia-d38-f34 (15:52-15:59, 100 held-out runs, W 0): cyclops arms hold (t PR-11 rules -1.02, PR-12 retreat 0.80, PR-16 -0.63/1.61, PR-17 0.05/0.12), hunter clears 76 (57-85; bundle 77), hunter hits 20.93 (19.37-24.93; bundle 21.03), hunting-ground kills 13.18 (d_kills holds), retreat (b) 11.73 vs 11.05 Welch t 0.45 holds; failing exactly as the bundle does today: in-reach 43.8 percent (bundle 43.8; band 21-35), (c1) 0 percent and (c2) 25 percent (bundle 0 and 25, D21 baseline note). So the threshold fix moves no criterion: a hunter at exactly 10 health is rare enough not to show in the in-reach share, which rules this mechanism out as its cause. Applied to src/hunting_pack.spi at 16:0x (the three sites, < to <=); build check job tibia-f34-build (hunting_pack, pack_sim, hunt_sim) must be green before the change counts as adopted; a pinned number that moves is updated only if the test pins a model output, and named here.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_111 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 111u32, "2026-10-22T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "D38 (B) NOT COMPLETED, F34 reverted from src (16:3x): the adoption condition build.ps1 green failed. Job tibia-f34-build (16:01-16:27; hunting_pack, pack_sim, hunt_sim): hunt_sim 11/11, pack_sim 30 passed 9 failed: golden_seed_7_troll_pack (6 vs 7), current_first_targeting_finishes_fleeing_trolls_over_twenty_seeds, mixed_camp_from_the_catalog_over_twenty_seeds, mixed_arena_camp_evolved_rules_dominate_the_tuned_cavebot_and_kind_aware_cyclops_rules_drink_less, on_the_hunting_ground_walking_pays_and_the_evolved_shuttle_edges_the_hand_route, the_random_control_stays_far_below_every_rule, the_live_wake_delay_brings_the_arena_clears_toward_the_live_potion_counts, mirroring_the_live_arena_predicts_rules_and_retreat_within_the_live_noise_at_two_and_three_cyclops, a_hunter_keeping_four_tiles_away_only_falls_where_walls_corner_it_and_walking_beside_the_knight_halves_its_pace. Several are exact pins (troll counts move when a troll at exactly 15 health flees), but some are property claims checked against live data, which the D37/D38 score does not cover; under the rule a source fact may not be adopted while it breaks them unexplained. F34 stays a scratch flag (d20-patch -F34). Next for this item: per failing test, classify pin vs claim from its body, and for each claim say whether F34 moves it outside its band; only then a re-adoption rule. Lesson for every (B)-style adoption: pack_sim is part of the criteria, run it inside the score job, not after it.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_112 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 112u32, "2026-10-22T20:34Z", "tibia-lane", "Superseded by note 113 (16:36): a first classification from run times alone guessed a timeout for mixed_arena_camp; the run own mismatch records show all 8 real failures are exact pins.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_113 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 113u32, "2026-10-22T20:36Z", "tibia-lane", "Correction to note 112 from the run own records (target/ci-metrics/pack_sim.out, spiral-tests mismatches): all 8 recorded failures are exact pins of model outputs at the first assert of each test, none a property band: golden_seed_7 kills 6 vs 7; current_first_targeting reach_kills 71 vs 75; mixed_camp_from_the_catalog 340 vs 328; mixed_arena_camp 38366 vs 38365 (616 s was its run time, not a timeout); on_the_hunting_ground (120, 104390, 108290, 114470, 119900, 119110) vs (120, 104920, 108270, 114470, 119950, 119280); the_live_wake_delay 3710300 vs 3708400; the_random_control (54420, 927, 0, -1145992, 7206, 0, 9353800) vs (54310, 915, 0, -1146134, ...); a_hunter_keeping_four_tiles (0, 173, 11, 82) vs (..., 86). The 9th, mirroring_the_live_arena_predicts, is cyclops-only (run_health 0, which F34 cannot change) and failed in 1.5 s with no mismatch: transient. Each test stops at its first assert, so the property checks after those pins never ran. D38B RULE, written before any rerun: re-apply F34 to src only while no tibia job that copies src is queued or running; refresh the moved pins with the Cells accept mode on pack_sim; adopt only if every accepted site is an exact model-output literal (no comparison, band or boolean property assert changes), then a plain rerun of pack_sim, hunt_sim and hunting_pack is fully green (properties included). Any changed property or red rerun: F34 stays a flag and the failing claim is named. Runs after main matrix end, on a box without heavy contention.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_114 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 114u32, "2026-10-22T21:40Z", "tibia-lane", "D38B in progress (17:4x): Cells accept refreshed 6 pins and 3 nested pins were set by hand, every change a numeric literal in place (scratch f34-review.ps1); plain rerun 1 (job tibia-f34-rerun): hunt_sim 11/11, pack_sim 38/39, the one failure mixed_arena second nested pin (only reachable once the first pin passed), its dominance property checked by hand with the new numbers (false, false, true, true: holds) and the pin refreshed. Plain rerun 2 (job tibia-f34-rerun2) STOPPED by me at 548 s under memory pressure (829 MB free beside main gates and eoie release F); not a verdict. src keeps F34 and the refreshed pins (backup in scratch f34-backup) until rerun 3 decides; nothing that copies src starts before that.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_115 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 115u32, "2026-10-22T21:45Z", "tibia-lane", "D38B VERDICT: F34 ADOPTED (rule note 113). src/hunting_pack.spi flees at health <= run_health at all three sites (Canary monster.cpp:960 isFleeing). Pins refreshed in src/pack_sim.spi, every change a numeric model-output literal in place (scratch f34-review.ps1): golden_seed_7 kills 7 -> 6; current_first_targeting reach 75/381 -> 71/393 and current 330/10 -> 303/20; mixed_camp_from_the_catalog 328/13 -> 340/1; mixed_arena first pin 38365 -> 38366 and second pin (190, 0, 38774), (135, 0, 37807), (67, 1, 37889) -> 38608, 37806, 37866; on_the_hunting_ground route tuple; the_random_control tuple; the_live_wake_delay 3708400 -> 3710300; a_hunter_keeping_four_tiles arena hits 86 -> 82. Six were rewritten by Cells accept, three nested tuples by hand (accept refuses nested tuples); every property assert (booleans, dominance, bands) is unchanged and passes. Plain reruns: hunt_sim 11/11 (job tibia-f34-rerun), pack_sim 39/39 (job tibia-f34-rerun3, 17:42-17:45; all 39 were memo hits, i.e. the identical programs had passed in rerun2 before I stopped it under memory pressure, and the memo key covers compiler, core and program text). Side effect named for TIBIA-PARTY: a troll at exactly 15 health now flees, so troll-only camps lose kills (330 -> 303 over 20 seeds in the current-first pin), in the direction of the open hunting-ground troll shortfall; D38's hunting-ground kills criterion still held (13.18 vs 13.19). The in-reach gap stays named; FIDELITY back to Paused with note 108's resume conditions.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_116 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 116u32, "2026-10-23T03:47Z", "tibia-lane", "Pointer, not a resume (23:4x): FIDELITY's open cyclops-opening gaps (in-reach 43.8 percent vs band 21-35, c1 0 and c2 25 percent, note 115) may share a cause with TIBIA-EVENT-TIME notes 100 and 108. In every model run the cyclops created on the walled-in tile 1931,1353 steps out before the policy starts, while live hunters in the same spot mostly stay. If tonight's cyclops probe runs (rule L3, EVENT-TIME note 109) show live cyclopses also staying, the model's opening differs in most runs, and these criteria join the D40 set for any no-retry candidate. The resume condition is unchanged: a Canary source line for the missing retry (rule L2).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_117 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 117u32, "2026-10-23T04:10Z", "tibia-lane", "RETRACTED 00:1x, written in error: I read Monster::getDistanceStep (monster.cpp 1733-2090) as a new source fact and resumed this item with a rule D41 for a candidate F36, but the same mechanism was already scored as K2 (stepping_away_like_canary, getDistanceStep's orthogonal-first table with a seeded random tie) under rule D20 on 2026-10-21 (notes 21-23): it moved in-reach the wrong way (48.1 vs base 43.8 percent) and hunter clears to 99, so the diagonal-backing-off hypothesis was refuted then, and note 26 lists the step table among the mechanisms ruled out. No new fact, so resume condition (2) is not met; D41 and F36 are withdrawn unbuilt, and the item goes back to Paused. Lesson: search this item's notes for the function name before calling a source fact new.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_118 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 118u32, "2026-10-23T07:18Z", "tibia-lane", "Pointer, no resume (03:1x): rule L2 was applied on tonight 10 server-probe hunter runs (TIBIA-EVENT-TIME note 118). Live retries the boxed hunter in 8 of 10 runs, so the resume condition (a Canary source line for a missing retry) is not met and has lost its premise for probed runs. Rule L5 (EVENT-TIME note 117) decides next window whether PR-22 low mover count was load or the probe. Item stays Paused.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_119 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 119u32, "2026-10-23T07:45Z", "tibia-lane", "Pointer, no resume (03:4x): rule L3 applied (TIBIA-EVENT-TIME note 119). The live cyclops on 1931,1353 stays until the policy in 8 of 10 probe runs, while every model run moves it, so the model cyclops opening differs from live in most runs, as the note-115 pointer asked. The live cause reads as timing (the neighbour leaves late, median about 1500 ms, and the boxed cyclops then needs one think plus about 750 ms), not a missing retry. That is a model-side question for the next session: when the model cyclops slot 1 leaves, and its walk lag. Any candidate needs its own pre-written rule, scored on the D40 criteria. The resume condition (a source line for a missing retry) stays unmet.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_120 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 120u32, "2026-10-23T11:11Z", "tibia-lane", "Retirement grooming 07:1x: in scope, about 1 h left. Its open gaps now live in EVENT-TIME (L5 and the misses) and PARTY (P6); close this item with pointers once those close.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_121 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 121u32, "2026-10-23T20:06Z", "tibia-lane", "Finding 16:0x (tibia-lane, during S1's gpu_sim check): F34's adoption (D38B verdict, note 115) refreshed pack_sim and reran pack_sim and hunt_sim, but not src/gpu_sim.spi. gpu_sim pins the same seed-7 troll hunt as pack_sim's golden_seed_7 (kills 7 -> 6 under F34), so its oracle pin (7, 18, 0, 84, 0, 453000) and its WGSL twin have been red since 10-22 (today: actual (6, 18, 0, 84, 0, 453000)). uniform_camp uses Respawning, so today's S1 cannot move it. Being fixed in the S1 gpu_sim pass (TIBIA-PARTY notes 80-81): oracle pin by Cells accept, WGSL twin set to the same numbers, then a plain rerun in which the GPU must reproduce the oracle. Lesson for D38B: a pin refresh reruns every test file that simulates the changed path, found by grepping for the camp constructors, not just the files named in the rule.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_122 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 122u32, "2026-10-23T20:52Z", "tibia-lane", "F34's stale gpu_sim pin fixed (16:5x, note 121): the troll-hunt oracle pin is (6, 18, 0, 84, 0, 453000), set by Cells accept, and the WGSL twin's equality chain is set to kills 6; the plain rerun (job tibia-s1-gpu3) has both green, so the GPU twin reproduces the F34 oracle.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_123 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 123u32, "2026-10-24T03:09Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-23 23:09 grooming: Paused -> Blocked, with TIBIA-EVENT-TIME and TIBIA-PARTY added as dependencies (its old deps are Done). By TIBIA note 42 its remaining 0.5 h is the close with pointers once both close, so it waits on them, not on a user pause.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_124 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 124u32, "2026-10-28T10:32Z", "tibia-lane", "GROOM 10-28 06:4x: Blocked -> Active. Its 10-24 blockers are cleared: TIBIA-EVENT-TIME is Done, and TIBIA-PARTY's model work is closed (P12, note 107; PARTY is now Paused with only the ally gap open). What remains is the 0.5 h close with pointers, scheduled today right after the 08:30 P-EXEC1 block.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_125 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 125u32, "2026-10-28T10:33Z", "tibia-lane", "CLOSE 10-28 06:5x, with pointers (per the 10-23 retirement note: close once EVENT-TIME and PARTY close). ADOPTED from this item and in the bundle: F34, monsters flee at health <= run_health at all three sites, source-exact to Canary monster.cpp:960 isFleeing (D38B verdict, note 115). pack_sim, hunt_sim and gpu_sim pins were refreshed to it; gpu_sim's oracle and WGSL twin were fixed in the S1 pass (note 121). The per-mechanic verdicts stay in this item's notes through D38B. OPEN GAPS AND WHERE THEY ENDED: (1) the cyclops opening (in-reach 43.8 percent against band 21-35, c1 0 and c2 25 percent, note 115) went to TIBIA-EVENT-TIME, which closed on 10-24 (its note 136). The server probe isn't the cause (PC-9); CPU load doesn't reproduce it (PC-11); the walled-in misses are follow-mode skipped steps (PC-10); hold-at-range H1 was rejected (L10 c). Known limit kept: the boxed hunter on 1931,1353 moves before the policy line live in 30 of 40 runs; the W37/W38 lead models stay scratch flags. (2) Party mechanics (P6, respawn clustering) went to TIBIA-PARTY, whose model work closed on P12 (note 107, saturation stands). Its only open gap, the ally potion share (note 98), parks with PARTY. Nothing else is open here.")
inl tibia_baselines () = Task ("TIBIA-BASELINES", "Arena baselines on a frozen scenario pack: headless protocol client (Spiral/Rust), nExBot (github.com/mCodex/nExBot, pushed 2026-09-01, no license file detected: confirm), vBot (OTClient Redemption 4.1 ships mods/game_bot with default_configs/vBot_4.8 and cavebot_1.3, so it runs on Canary's protocol 1511; also in OTCv8/otclientv8, which stops at 11.x), a scripted cavebot, a random-policy control; parity rules (15x11 view, one action-rate cap, same character/supplies/seeds); real-time evaluation budget ~150 h of play per pass at 2-3 client+server pairs; 2026-10-13 07:46 first baseline live: vBot_4.8 (OTClient Redemption's mods/game_bot) runs headless-configured through tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1 -Bot vBot (fresh copy of the shipped config, TargetBot config vbot-arena.json: troll, chase, priority 1; storage enables it; probe-vbot-body.lua only enables the bot through g_settings and observes); 3 trolls, balanced, axe 30: vBot +90 experience (3 kills) in ~105 s, lowest health 181; the Spiral policy (CurrentFirst) +90 (3 kills) in ~103 s, lowest 178: a tie on this small scenario; next: the parity layer (action-rate cap, 15x11 view) and harder scenarios (cyclops, mixed packs) with seeds; 2026-10-13 08:44 parity layer live (tibia-local/parity.lua, prepended to every probe unless -NoParity): one shared gate admits at most one action per 250 ms across g_game attack/follow/walk/turn/talk/use*/move/cancel* and LocalPlayer.autoWalk, and g_map.getSpectators returns only creatures within the 15x11 client screen; 3 trolls under parity: vBot +90 experience in ~80 s (17 actions allowed, 7 dropped), Spiral policy +90 in ~90 s (16 allowed, 5 dropped); next: repeated seeds per competitor and harder scenarios (vBot needs HealBot configured for anything dangerous); 2026-10-13 09:26 first repeated arena table (tibia-local/run-arena.ps1, 5 alternating runs each, 3 trolls, parity on, policy compiled from a snapshot; arena-results.tsv): full clears Spiral 4/5 (mean 92.1 s over full clears, actions 15.2), vBot 5/5 (mean 108.0 s, sd 21.7, actions 22.8); Spiral's missed clear came from its own stop rule (no visible target) when a fleeing troll left the 15x11 parity view; the stop rule is now full experience for both; no significant difference at n=5; next: more runs, the harder cyclops scenario (vBot needs HealBot); 2026-10-13 10:06 cyclops arena live layer: run-policy-scenario.ps1 gains -Level (experience, max health 185+15(L-8), mana derived), -HealBelow/-StrikeAbove (TIBIA_ARENA_HEAL_BELOW/STRIKE_ABOVE read by both probe bodies, troll defaults unchanged), potion 266 restocked to 100 in the reset, vBot TargetBot regex from -Monster and a seeded HealBot.json (potion 266 below the same hp threshold, profiles 0 and 1); run-arena.ps1 passes them through, sets the full-experience stop rule, and keeps every run's full output in tibia-local/arena-logs; smoke round (level 30, axe 60, 3 cyclops, heal below 150): BOTH competitors died within 10 s of the summon (vBot log: dead before t=10s, 7 actions), while the simulator's same knight survives most 5-minute hunts; potion (125-175) and cyclops melee (0-105 per 2 s) match Canary's scripts, so the gap is elsewhere (heals not landing live, or extra damage); diagnosis run was reaped for low memory at 10:05, retry after the compiler chain frees memory; 2026-10-13 10:17 cyclops smoke deaths explained: (1) no potions: deaths in earlier runs dropped the backpack's contents and the reset only updated an existing row, so the 'Sorry, not possible' heal had nothing to drink; the reset now deletes and re-inserts 100 potions in the backpack (verified live: 'Using one of 100 health potions', heals 141-170); (2) the probe marked a heal done even when the parity gate dropped it; it now retries next tick; (3) a cyclops kill gives 225 experience on this server (rate stage), so three cyclops need -FullExperience 675; 2026-10-13 12:19 cyclops clear arena v1 (BENCHMARK pack v1 'cyclops clear', forge off, heal below 70 for all, tibia-local/arena-results-cyclops.tsv since 11:35, arena-summary.ps1): kiting network 4/5 cleared, 85.5 +- 8.2 s, 13.6 +- 4.4 potions, 2425 +- 634 damage; rules 4/5, 92.7 +- 15.2 s, 14.2 +- 1.9, 2506 +- 232; vBot 3/4, 90.0 +- 17.3 s, 12.0 +- 6.9; every competitor died once; no significant separation at n=4-5 (the first-run kiting gain was noise); heal 70 is unsafe live, which the simulator missed (fixed since: Canary block charges, diagonal x3 and chase x2 steps, the 250 ms action gap as a typed readiness witness, live spawn layout); live layer fixes during v1: vBot HealBot Visible=false, vBot probe logs damage, -Competitors parsing; v2 next: probe retreats only onto walkable tiles (live kiting walked into walls), threshold re-tuned on the corrected simulator; 2026-10-13 13:39 cyclops clear arena v2 (heal below 100 for all, probe v2 with walkable retreats, arena-results-cyclops-v2.tsv): vBot 5/5 cleared, 0 deaths, 88.0 +- 11.0 s, 15.8 +- 4.3 potions; rules 4/5, 1 death (that run also had the parity gate reporting admitted potions as dropped, fixed 13:12), 86.6 +- 4.9 s, 14.2 +- 6.5; kiting 2/5, 3 deaths (the simulator also ranks it worst; the arena spot is walled in, 38 of 39 retreat decisions found no walkable tile); live layer asymmetry found: vBot's HealBot macro runs every 100 ms while our probe decided every 250 ms, both behind the same 250 ms action gate, so vBot reacted faster to bursts; the probe now ticks every 100 ms like vBot (the gate still caps actions), and clear time is measured in ms by both probes; v3 next: rules vs vBot only; 2026-10-13 14:16 cyclops clear arena v3 (first with matched decision rates: our probe ticks every 100 ms like vBot's HealBot macro, same 250 ms action gate, heal below 100 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v3.tsv): Spiral rules 4/5 cleared, 80.1 +- 7.0 s, 13.4 +- 6.3 potions, 2369 +- 871 damage, 1 death; vBot 4/5, 90.0 +- 11.5 s, 13.8 +- 6.3, 2461 +- 882, 1 death; clear-time difference not significant (Welch t = -1.47, n = 4 each); next: 10+ runs per competitor before claiming a gap, and the simulator's learned policies once they dominate by more than noise; 2026-10-13 14:46 ARENA DATA INVALIDATED after 12:02: deaths dropped the knight's equipment (no blessings) and the reset restored only potions, so from the first death on the knight fought with less gear (clean runs: 33.6 mean per landed hit, max 86; afterwards 38-45, max up to 101; by 14:27 helmet, armor, legs, shield and backpack were all gone and every run died with 0 potions); v1 rows after 12:02, all of v2 and v3 are void (files renamed *-gear-lost-invalid); the reset now deletes the knight's items and inserts the canonical set (brass helmet, backpack, brass armor, dwarven shield, steel axe, brass legs, leather boots, store inbox, 100 potions); also void: the 'live mean 37.6 over 794 hits' used as evidence for block charges; block charges stay as Canary's mechanic, but the clean data (33.6) sits closer to always-blocked; 2026-10-13 15:26 cyclops clear arena v4, the first clean comparison (full inventory restored before every run, forge off, same 250 ms action gate and 100 ms decision tick, heal below 160 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v4.tsv): Spiral rules 6/6 cleared, 87.9 +- 14.3 s, 14.7 +- 2.9 potions, 2471 +- 420 damage, 0 deaths; vBot 6/6, 90.0 +- 8.9 s, 14.8 +- 2.6 potions, 2486 +- 395, 0 deaths; a tie (Welch t -0.31 on time, -0.10 on potions), as the simulator expects for two threshold healers; next: the arena spot's terrain in the simulator, then a scenario where terrain or positioning separates policies; 2026-10-13 16:33 arena v5 (clean, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v5.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst) 7/7 cleared, 83.3 +- 6.3 s, 12.1 +- 2.8 potions, 2101 +- 432 damage; vBot 6/6, 83.4 +- 15.1 s, 13.0 +- 3.1, 2201 +- 469; Spiral rules 6/6, 83.1 +- 11.0 s, 14.2 +- 2.2, 2376 +- 337; no deaths; retreat uses the fewest potions at equal time, the simulator's direction, but smaller than predicted (-15% vs rules live, -33% in the simulator) and not yet significant (Welch t -1.45 vs rules, -0.52 vs vBot); 10 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 18:25 arena v5 final (16/16/15 runs, clean): Spiral retreat-at-2 13.8 +- 2.9 potions, 88.9 +- 9.9 s; vBot 14.1 +- 2.5, 88.0 +- 10.8 s; Spiral rules 14.4 +- 2.6, 86.8 +- 12.4 s; no deaths; no significant differences (retreat vs rules t -0.58); the early retreat advantage regressed to the mean; the simulator's ~30% saving does not transfer; live retreats mostly did not move the knight (sampled positions barely change): the probe left ChaseOpponent on, so the server walked the knight back toward its target; the probe now sets DontChase before each retreat step (diagnostic: 14 retreats, 3 positions, 12 potions); v6 (retreat vs rules, 8 rounds) running; 2026-10-13 19:11 arena v6 (retreat probe with DontChase, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 9/9 cleared, 13.3 +- 1.9 potions, 2281 +- 337 damage, 90.5 +- 8.3 s; Spiral rules 8/8, 15.0 +- 2.7 potions, 2566 +- 387, 90.2 +- 10.1 s; no deaths; 11% fewer potions and less damage at equal time, the simulator's direction at about a third of its predicted size (8.8 vs 12.4 per clear), not yet significant (Welch t -1.44, a retreat run beats a rules run in 68% of pairs); 8 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 19:57 arena v6 final (16-17 runs each, clean live layer, heal 160): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 16/17 cleared, 88.4 +- 9.8 s, 13.1 potions on cleared runs, 2178 +- 491 damage taken; Spiral rules 16/16, 88.2 +- 11.8 s, 14.9 potions, 2544 +- 432 damage; no deaths; damage -14% (Welch t ~ -2.3), potions -13% (t -1.93; one-sided p ~0.03 for the direction the simulator predicted beforehand), equal clear time: the first live effect of a simulator-designed policy, about half the simulator's predicted size; one retreat run never cleared (it retreated out of the fight: 806 gate drops, no kills), a failure mode to handle (re-engage when no attacker is adjacent); 2026-10-13 20:39 arena v6 FINAL (23-24 runs each, clean live layer, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv since 18:21): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 23/24 cleared, 12.6 potions on cleared runs, 2125 damage taken, 88.6 s; Spiral rules 23/23, 15.5 potions, 2639 damage, 91.7 s; no deaths; potions -19% (Welch t -3.89), damage -19% (t -4.20), clear time not different (t -0.96): the first statistically clear live win, for a policy the simulator found and evolution rediscovered (the simulator predicted -29%); vBot was at 14.1-14.8 potions in v4/v5 under the same live layer, a head-to-head retreat vs vBot round is next; 2026-10-14 00:23 PAUSED at the user's request (account switch): arena v7 (retreat vs vBot, arena-results-cyclops-v7.tsv) stopped after 8 vBot and 7 retreat runs (retreat 11-15 potions, vBot 8-18; summarize with arena-summary.ps1); next on resume: finish v7, rescan the arena at radius 12 (probe-scan-body.lua, live knight leaves the +-7 window), mixed cyclops+troll camp probe (cavebot 240 potions/37.7 s vs evolved rules 431/43.5 s per 200 clears: rules tuned for cyclops lose on mixed camps); 2026-10-14 01:59 arena v7 final (retreat vs vBot, clean live layer, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v7.tsv since 2026-10-13 23:30, 20 retreat / 21 vBot runs, all cleared, no deaths): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 12.1 sd 1.8 potions, 2083 sd 263 damage taken, 89.3 sd 10.3 s; vBot 13.8 sd 3.3 potions, 2371 sd 502 damage, 92.4 sd 13.4 s; potions -13% (Welch t -2.14, df 31, one-sided p 0.02), damage -12% (t -2.32, one-sided p 0.014), clear time not different (t -0.85): retreat beats vBot on supplies and damage at equal speed, smaller than its -19% margin over rules in v6; vBot is also less consistent (potion sd 3.3 vs 1.8); live layer asymmetry found: probe-vbot-body.lua samples experience and health only every 10 s, so vBot clear times are rounded up to the next 10 s (about +5 s bias: corrected vBot clear 87.4 s, t +0.50, still no difference) and vBot lowest health is a 10 s sample, not a true minimum; the vBot probe now also watches every 100 ms for v8 on; v7 pools two policy snapshots (23:29 and 00:31) whose only difference is an additive Scored targeting case in policy.spi that live.spi does not use; 2026-10-14 02:18 arena spot rescanned at radius 12 (probe-scan-body.lua, tibia-local/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt: raw grid, 25 row bitmasks with bit i = column dx -12+i is #, and a client-loaded check): the knight was centered at 1933,1350 in that scan (one tile off the 1932,1349 reset; a second scan logged in at 1932,1349, so the knight's login tile varies run to run); the radius-12 scan cannot see past the client's loaded 18x14 window (x 1924..1941, y 1343..1356 in both scans): g_map.getTile returns nil outside it and the probe prints nil as #, so the outer band of solid # rows and columns is unknown terrain, not walls (probe-scan-unknown-body.lua prints ? there); a wider live map needs the knight to walk the area or a server-side or OTBM read, not a bigger client scan radius; inside the window the grid matches the radius-7 scan; 2026-10-14 03:24 arena v8 (heal below 120 for both, Spiral rules vs vBot, 10 runs each, arena-results-cyclops-v8.tsv since 2026-10-14 02:18, first round with the vBot probe watching experience and health every 100 ms): all 20 cleared, no deaths; Spiral rules 84.4 sd 6.0 s, 12.8 sd 1.6 potions, 2233 sd 235 damage, lowest health mean 67 (min 52); vBot 88.8 sd 16.0 s, 13.2 sd 3.7 potions, 2299 sd 572 damage, lowest mean 65 (min 28); no significant difference (Welch t -0.82 time, -0.31 potions, -0.34 damage); against heal 160 (v4-v7) both drink 1-2 fewer potions at equal damage and speed and run about 35-40 hp closer to death, still survivable with 3 cyclops; vBot stays the less consistent one (sd 3.7 potions, its two worst runs bottomed at 28 and 30 hp); earlier rounds' vBot lowest health (mean 169-192 at heal 160) was a 10 s sampling artifact, so vBot never had the larger safety margin those tables showed; 2026-10-14 03:32 vBot probe now stops at clear (100 ms watch, finish 'cleared', post-finish HealBot drinks not counted); smoke run cleared 93.7 s, 13 potions, lowest 109, log ends right after clear; 2026-10-14 04:43 arena v9 cyclops 12+12, retreat at 2, ReachFirst (spiral-retreat) vs CurrentFirst (spiral-retreat-current): potions 13.3+-2.6 vs 13.5+-3.4 (t -0.14), damage 2243+-373 vs 2290+-482 (t -0.27), clear 90.1+-9.0 vs 92.6+-11.8 s (t -0.59); all cleared, 0 deaths; no difference on the three metrics. Post-hoc: lowest health 91.6+-28.9 vs 113.1+-12.1 (t -2.38, two reach runs dipped to 34/36) - CurrentFirst never went below 93; 2026-10-14 04:59 arena v9 vBot reference (fixed probe, stops at clear, block after the Spiral runs, not interleaved) n=6: potions 14.0+-3.6, damage 2418+-575, clear 91.1+-9.9 s, 0 deaths; vs spiral-retreat t potions -0.40, damage -0.68, clear -0.21; vs spiral-retreat-current t -0.28, -0.47, +0.29 - no significant difference; vBot runs now ~2.8 min instead of ~3.8; 2026-10-14 05:51 arena v9 pooled (12 alternating + 6 interleaved with vBot, all cleared, 0 deaths): ReachFirst vs CurrentFirst n=18/18 potions 12.7+-2.3 vs 13.4+-3.2 (t -0.72), damage 2172+-326 vs 2263+-462 (t -0.68), clear 89.6+-9.1 vs 91.7+-11.3 s (t -0.61) - no difference, ReachFirst nominally ahead; lowest-health gap did not replicate (pooled 97.2 vs 109.2, t ~-1.6). vBot (fixed probe) n=12: potions 14.1+-3.2, damage 2397+-492, clear 90.7+-10.9; spiral-retreat vs vBot t potions -1.27, damage -1.39, clear -0.29 (interleaved-only n=6/6: potions t -2.06, damage t -1.80); 2026-10-14 05:53 all 12 v9 vBot logs end 'finish: cleared' (no run complete/timeout, 0 post-finish drinks); v8 vBot logs had 0 potions after clear either, so the old 150 s tail cost wall time only and did not bias v8 potions/damage. v9 95% CI ReachFirst-CurrentFirst: potions -0.7 [-2.6,+1.2], damage -91 [-363,+181], clear -2.1 s [-9.1,+4.9]; 2026-10-14 05:54 pooled verdict, retreat (ReachFirst) vs vBot over v7 and v9 (38 vs 33 runs, potions from server messages, unaffected by the old vBot sampling): 12.4 vs 13.9 potions, -11%, Welch t -2.36, same clear time; v9 alone (vBot via the fixed probe, 12 runs) t -1.27, so the effect is real but modest; damage pooled not quoted because log matching picked up extra vBot logs (44 logs vs 33 rows); targeting during retreats (ReachFirst vs CurrentFirst) is a wash live (18 each, |t| < 0.8); 2026-10-14 06:38 CORRECTION of the vBot claim: arena v10 (9 more pairs, 05:55-06:38, arena-results-cyclops-v10.tsv) went the other way (retreat 13.6 vs vBot 13.0 potions); pooled v7+v9+v10 (47 vs 42 runs): retreat 12.6 vs vBot 13.7 potions (-8.2%, Welch t -1.89, not significant), clear 90.7 vs 92.0 s, no deaths; the two rounds with identically measured probes (v9+v10) give t -0.75; verdict: the retreat policy is level with vBot, perhaps slightly better; it clearly beats our rules policy (-19%, t -3.89); the v7 result was a high draw that regressed; lesson: decide the run count before looking (sequential peeking inflated the first claim); 2026-10-14 08:37 nExBot prepared as the second open-source baseline: pinned at 19632d4 (v4.0.4, default branch head 2026-07-15; the benchmark table said pushed 2026-09-01, other branches), copied to tibia-local/bots/nExBot-19632d4 without git/tests/docs; its README links an MIT LICENSE file that is missing from the repo (matters for publication only); it ships an auto-updater and an analytics module that call GitHub and nexbot.cc, so tibia-local/bot-network-sandbox.lua stubs g_http, HTTP and g_platform.openUrl for every competitor (silent no-ops; the updater's no-HTTP fallback would open a browser); its HealBot compares every potion threshold against HP percent, even rules marked absolute HP, so parity with heal-below-160 is HP% 31 (about +-5 hp); probe-nexbot-body.lua selects config 'nExBot'; next, after PR-1 and PR-2: one live run to let it create its per-character UnifiedStorage, then seed HealBot.json, targetbot_configs/arena.json and the storage the way vBot is seeded", Feature, P1, D5, 95u32, Paused, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,benchmark", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_baselines () = Planning ("TIBIA-BASELINES", Minutes 2400u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:58Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 09:58 nExBot seeding prepared offline (read-only reading of nExBot 19632d4): HealBot.json in bot/nExBot/nExBot_configs/profile_{0,1}/ (same profile shape as vBot); the engine collapses HP and HP% into one hp threshold compared to floor(health*100/max) with <=, so heal below 160 at 515 max is hp% <= 30 (fires for health <= 159, exact); UnifiedStorage at nExBot_configs/characters/knight sample/UnifiedStorage.json (targetbot.enabled, selectedConfig arena, healbot.enabled), and vbot-arena.json is format-compatible (targeting/looting). The network sandbox is prepended to the runtime copy of _Loader.lua. Staged in run-policy-scenario.next.ps1 (-Bot nExBot) and run-arena.ps1 (competitor nexbot); swapped in after PR-1. Earlier note said 31%: that was wrong (floor semantics).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 2u32, "2026-10-14T14:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 10:30 CORRECTION: every live spiral-* run since 2026-10-13 11:48 ran with vBot's HealBot and TargetBot active alongside our policy (the vBot probe enabled the client's bot setting for the character; nothing reset it; the policy probe never disabled it). Signature: server-reported potions our policy never drank in almost every spiral run (tibia-local/harness-check.ps1 scans all logs). All live policy comparisons and the live check of the simulator's clear prediction are therefore hybrids; PR-1 is void and stopped at 61 rows. Fix: run-policy-scenario writes the bot node per competitor and removes other bots' folders, the policy probe disables the bot before login, and run-arena records foreign potions/actions per run. Re-measurement: BENCHMARK PR-4. Server-mechanics fidelity rows and the 10-13 03:34 troll targeting run are unaffected.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 14:53 PR-4 (fixed harness, 30 runs each, 0 harness failures, 0 deaths): potions rules 11.53, retreat 12.90, vBot 14.00; retreat vs vBot difference -1.10 (CI -2.62 .. 0.42, t -1.45) no difference shown; retreat vs rules +1.37 (t 1.82) no difference shown, direction against retreat. Clear times 87.6 / 91.3 / 92.7 s match the simulator's 88.6 / 88.1; potions do not (predicted 13.23 rules, 9.09 retreat; t -3.69 and 6.44). The live retreat win and the 'simulator predicts live' claim from the hybrid runs are withdrawn.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 4u32, "2026-10-14T20:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:31 live random control (PR-5, probe-random-body.lua, 10 runs, clean): 94.1 potions per clear (simulator 90.5, holds), 102.7 s (simulator 117.0, gap: live auto-attack persists between random picks). Control far below rules 11.5, retreat 12.9, vBot 14.0.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 5u32, "2026-10-14T20:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:33 nExBot: 3/3 PR-3 check runs crash the client (TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH); PR-3 not run today.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 6u32, "2026-10-15T07:06Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 03:06 PR-8 (pre-registered replication, rules vs vBot, 30 each, clean): 12.90 vs 14.17 potions, difference -1.27 (CI -2.99 .. 0.46), t -1.47: no difference shown; PR-4's descriptive 11.53 for rules did not replicate. Both Spiral policies sit ~1.2 potions below vBot without significance at n=30.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 7u32, "2026-10-15T10:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 05:50: nExBot 4.0.4 is now a running baseline (three harness shims, BENCHMARK PR-3a). Pre-registered results on the clean harness: retreat vs vBot no difference shown (PR-4, t -1.45), rules vs vBot no difference shown (PR-8, t -1.47), retreat vs nExBot significant (PR-3a, 12.2 vs 14.6 potions, t -2.14, narrow). Left: OTCv8 bot module, scripted cavebot as a live competitor.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 8u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: open parts: OTCv8 bot module, scripted cavebot as a live competitor, and nExBot's license (see TIBIA-ARENA-RELEASE).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 9u32, "2026-10-15T11:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:04 correction: nExBot's license is not a task (no interaction with public projects); open parts are the OTCv8 bot module and a scripted cavebot as a live competitor.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 10u32, "2026-10-15T16:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 12:54 PR-9 (pre-registered 08:13, 50 runs each): Spiral rules 12.46 vs vBot 14.66 potions per cyclops clear, diff -2.20 (CI -3.35..-1.05), Welch t -3.80: SIGNIFICANT, rules use fewer potions; same clear time (88.7 vs 87.9 s), 0 deaths, damage 2145 vs 2479 (the saving is damage avoided). First well-powered live win over an open-source baseline. One disclosed interim look at 10:37 (fixed n, no early stop).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 11u32, "2026-10-15T18:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 14:14 PR-9 explained (post-hoc): the whole rules-vs-vBot difference is the knight's login protection. Canary ends it on the player's own move/autowalk/turn/say/item use/attack cancel, not on starting an attack; our probe keeps it, vBot ends it. Hits in the first 10 s: vBot 9.14, rules 1.58; after 10 s level (60.1 vs 60.4). So PR-9 measures a scenario artifact, not hunting skill. Harness fix next: end the protection for every competitor right after login (one native turn outside the parity gate), then re-test rules vs vBot (PR-11).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 12u32, "2026-10-15T22:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:40 PR-11 (pre-registered 14:21; parity.lua now ends login protection for every competitor with one native turn after login): rules 14.42 vs vBot 14.78 potions, diff -0.36 (CI -1.58..0.86), t -0.58: NO DIFFERENCE SHOWN; hits 69.1 vs 69.2, first 10 s 9.6 vs 9.0, clear 88.3 vs 87.4 s, 0 deaths. Our rules policy and vBot are level; PR-9's win was the login-protection artifact. Next for a real win: a behavior that changes exposure live (the model's policy effects are too strong, PR-10), not thresholds.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 13u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 remaining harness asymmetry after the protection fix: parity.lua ends login protection at 0.3 s for everyone, but the policy probe starts deciding about 2.5 s after login while vBot acts at once (PR-11 first-10-s hits 9.6 vs 9.0, consistent). Does not change PR-11's no-difference verdict; a test for a win should start every competitor's logic at the same moment. Recorded in BENCHMARK.md Parity.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 14u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 paused (user). On resume: TIBIA-START-SYNC, then run the written PR-12 (fair nExBot re-test); the OTCv8 module and a scripted live cavebot stay open.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 15u32, "2026-10-18T19:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:30 resuming per the 10-17 note: TIBIA-START-SYNC is implemented (uncommitted, verification in today's live block), and PR-12 is amended in docs/BENCHMARK.md before any run: both competitors start at login + 2.5 s, and runs go in chunks across days into results/arena-results-cyclops-pr12.tsv, still with no interim looks. First chunk planned for today's live block after the start-sync and stray-server checks: alternating spiral-retreat and nexbot, cyclops pack v1, heal 160, level 30, axe 60, experience 675.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 16u32, "2026-10-18T19:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:42 PR-12 chunk 1 started at 15:42: run-arena -Runs 10 alternating spiral-retreat / nexbot (cyclops 3, level 30, axe 60, heal 160, retreat at 2, experience 675) into results/arena-results-cyclops-pr12.tsv, with synchronized starts (TIBIA-START-SYNC verified live 15:41). No looks at potions until all 40 per competitor are in.")
