inl qualified_union_cases () = Task ("QUALIFIED-UNION-CASES", "Union cases cannot be qualified by module: `vitality.Slain _` in a pattern fails with \"The module does not have the key: Slain\" (apps/tibia/hunt.spi 2026-10-12), so every caller needs a local `open vitality`; decide per edition whether cases become module members (edition 3 candidate); user decision 2026-10-12 18:53: both: module.Case accepted in patterns and constructors (resolved through the module path like values), plus a clearer error when an unqualified case is ambiguous between opened modules; 02:34 module.Case done in patterns (constructors already worked) in both cores, uncommitted, rides pack-0004: a qualified PatNominal path that resolves on the term side to a union-case constructor (ho_fun -> nominal whose body is TyUnion) is typed as that case (scrutinee unified with the nominal, then the PatUnbox path), recorded by node identity in qualified_union_case_patterns, and Infer's fill pass rewrites it to PatUnbox so Prepass lowers a plain case test; plain nominal patterns (mod.num x) are untouched; probes on both cores (Debug): qualified case patterns with open exit 4, without open (qualified constructor + patterns) exit 6, qualified plain nominal exit 7; open: the clearer ambiguity error for an unqualified case shared by two opened modules; no harness sample added (standing no-new-samples rule; ask the user); 05:11 in pack-0004 Release (both suites DISAGREE 0, blessed); 06:22 also stable in pack-0005 (both cores parity); 07:02 regression sample added (user allowed regression samples 10-13): samples/qualified_union_case_pattern (two modules, qualified constructor + patterns without open, expected exit 6; C exit 6 on the pack-0005 DLL); enters the oracle at the next pack's bless", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,language", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_qualified_union_cases () = Planning ("QUALIFIED-UNION-CASES", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl test_file_prelude () = Task ("TEST-FILE-PRELUDE", "A file opens lib modules for its tests through a pseudo-test `test name static = open testing`, which reports count as a discovered and passed test (geometry.spi reports 8 = 7 tests + the prelude); give test-only opens their own header so reports count real tests; 2026-10-13 17:33 done in Kino without a new header (the compiler skips every top-level block whose first token is test, so a new header would need parser and document round-trip work plus a lib-wide migration): the Spiral domain (apps/kino/spi/document.spi test_mode_of) classifies a --test static block whose body is only open lines (after ///) as mode prelude; reports give it status prelude, count it in preludes and leave it out of discovered (sm'.spi now discovered 36, preludes 1, static 0); a static block that defines something stays static; tests: notebook_report_test (prelude/static/test modes; the prelude file reports discovered 2, preludes 1), notebook/document suites 37/37; README updated", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "tests,kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_test_file_prelude () = Planning ("TEST-FILE-PRELUDE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_standards () = Task ("TIBIA-STANDARDS", "Settle executable standards for apps/tibia (user 2026-10-12: everything before is drift): integer-only rules (i32: WGSL has no i64), bit-exact CPU/GPU, typestate unions for phases, conservation tests for money/items, every rules test lists ///> rust and ///> c (later ///> wgsl), counter-based RNG keyed by seed/tick/entity/purpose (rng.spi), unsigned arithmetic for hashing (wraps on every backend: Rust wrapping_mul, C unsigned), explicit test names, no comments, one module per file in the apps/tibia package; turn each into a check (eoie verb or test) instead of prose", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA", "tibia,standards", "current", "current")
