inl note_of_core_pair_unification_23 () = Note ("CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION", 23u32, "2026-10-19T18:40Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:40 lap 4 grain: recount from pair-drift -Table (14:3x): 8 pairs remain (BlockParsingGpt5parallel layer, InferAdapter 6/6 lines, PrepassAdapter 12/5, PartEval 104,783/2,979, CodegenAdapter 653/28, GraphIdentity 36/20, SignalRSupervisor 3,736/829, ServerHooks 62/13); InferAdapter is the smallest real pair, 6 lines a side Next: try unifying InferAdapter (6 vs 6 lines) as a hook, the cheapest proof that the adapter pattern works, in the next pack")
inl note_of_core_pair_unification_24 () = Note ("CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION", 24u32, "2026-10-19T18:40Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:40 correction to note 23: InferAdapter is not a unification candidate, it IS the hook (error reason type, reason text, module-application report, failed-declaration recovery differ per core and keep Infer itself shared); the same holds for PrepassAdapter, CodegenAdapter and ServerHooks, so the only pairs that still duplicate logic are PartEval (104,783 vs 2,979 lines), SignalRSupervisor and GraphIdentity, and those retire with gpt5parallel at HOPACSOTA-P6, as note 22 says. Next: none until P6.")
