inl python_main_return_print () = Task ("PYTHON-MAIN-RETURN-PRINT", "the Python (and Cuda-hosted Python) backend's generated main prints main's return value after the program's own output (found 00:57 by the Kino lane's agreement sweep; Kino normalizes it away); make the generated entry return the value as the exit code like the C backend instead of printing it, so stdout carries only the program's output; user decision 2026-10-13 07:11: exit code like C: the generated entry exits with main's int result (sys.exit) and prints nothing extra; stdout carries only the program's output on every backend; then drop the trailing-value normalization from Kino and the harness; 07:28 compiler side in spiral_compiler.fs (pack 1): an i32 main already exited via sys.exit; non-i32 results are no longer printed (entry is just main()); 2026-10-13 09:52 main: pack 1 verified (both Release cores, both suites DISAGREE 0, sf vs hopac differ only on the expected Delphi format_any row) and blessed (3843 rows reproduced row for row; baseline 3936 -> 3949 lines)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,python,output", "current", "current")
