inl datetime_fraction_python () = Task ("DATETIME-FRACTION-PYTHON", "lib date_time time_span_format_3 diverges (found 01:38 by the Kino agreement sweep): fsharp 10:11:12.999 vs cuda/python 10:11:129990000; the Python path formats fractional seconds without the separator and with the wrong precision; fix lib's Python branch so every backend prints the same text; 01:54 fixed (uncommitted, lib/spiral/date_time.spi): the Python branch of time_span_format dropped the '.' after days and before the fraction (and Lua the fraction '.'); the tests time_span_format and time_span_format_3 had encoded the wrong Python text as a per-backend expectation (39710:11:120130000, 10:11:129990000), so they 'passed'; both tests now assert one value for every backend (397.10:11:12.0130000, 10:11:12.9990000); the remaining per-backend expectations in lib (sm' format/format_debug, parsing none_of) are intentional native-representation tests; verify with the Kino re-run of date_time on cuda/python; 2026-10-13 23:57 sweep lane: fix committed in 8a89893a (Python and Lua branches add the '.' before the fraction, both tests assert one value for every backend, date_time.spi:776-792 and 803/823 unchanged by d94dc380); spiral CI 38389311114 ubuntu: date_time done exit 0, passed 32 failed 0 skipped 0 (per-backend detail not in the log); local cuda/python run of time_span_format* pending until the verify chain frees the machine; 2026-10-14 00:13 verified locally: run_notebook.ps1 --path lib/spiral/date_time.spi --test time_span_format,time_span_format_2,time_span_format_3 (output to scratch, 73 s): 3/3 passed on every target, cuda (.py) printed 397.10:11:12.0130000, 10:11:12 and 10:11:12.9990000, the same text as fsharp, rust -d chrono and typescript", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,datetime,python,agreement", "current", "current")
