inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_11 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 11u32, "2026-10-19T23:00Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 19:00 eoie-lane: binary-driving Rust tests become Spiral notebooks on a shared harness package src/eoie_cli_harness (module cli: fixture roots, cli_args union, eoie_run/racing/closing-stdout runs, receipt normalizers, digests, symlink-or-skip, rustc_program for fake tools); notebooks include it with '///- --package ../eoie_cli_harness' + 'open cli' (a notebook compiles standalone, so this is how test code shares helpers). Ported and retired 9 Rust files (896 lines): agile_note_receipts, proxy_receipts, agile_receipts, batch_completion (eoie_contracts), agile_cache, agile_listing (eoie_agile_contracts), archive_publication, self_upgrade, eoie_cli tests/windows. New notebooks: agile_task_notes/notes_cli 6, eoie_contracts/receipts_cli 8, eoie_agile_contracts/agile_cli 9, archive_cli 3, upgrade_cli 2, eoie_cli/windows_cli 4 = 32 tests; each passed a mutation check (mutated expectations fail exactly the mutated tests); official eoie-dev run (build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease, 5 packages, heavy job) green. Traps: a runtime (~) flag that picks between cli_args shapes makes the compile-time joined recursion diverge (EJP0011), keep shape flags static; Spiral string literals cannot hold a backslash before a quote, build it with char 92/34.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_12 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 12u32, "2026-10-19T23:48Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 19:48 eoie-lane batch 2: native_paths.rs (4 binary tests -> eoie_coverage_prune/coverage_cli.spi with a rustc-built fake cargo; the pure eoie_coverage_jobs test -> a test block in coverage_prune_model/model.spi next to coverage_jobs_binding), evidence.rs -> eoie_coverage_prune/evidence_cli.spi (coverage-assess, prune-uncovered, coverage-export through proxy verbs, fake grcov), hygiene_confinement.rs sidecar half -> eoie_release_contracts/hygiene_cli.spi (junction helper with CREATE_NO_WINDOW). Kept in Rust on purpose: hygiene transient tests (prune-release-transients has no proxy verb; a test-only verb is not worth it), prune_transaction.rs (one case pre-creates a backup named after the test's own PID, which only collides in-process). False-pass trap found: through a binary, a refusal test passes on 'unknown proxy operation'; refusals now also assert that text is absent. Full gated release job-1792451451481 green with 34 notebooks / 99 Spiral tests, topology gate passed, eoie.exe 19:43 sha256 52FEFE97...; hand-written Rust test files 41 -> 30 (11 retired, 1 shrunk, 1,162 lines gone).")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_13 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 13u32, "2026-10-20T00:45Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 20:45 eoie-lane batch 3: hash_boundary.rs Windows/Linux test -> eoie_proxy_search/hash_cli.spi (proxy hash with EOIE_HASH_LIMIT_BYTES=3, junction ancestor), the Rust file keeps only the Linux FIFO test (36 lines). Flake found by the official run and fixed: the agile cache fixture read the clock twice for the lease start and deadline, and eoie rejects a 1 ms skew (deadline mismatch); the fixture now reads now_ms once. Pack 12 (unaccepted) was installed at 20:36, so the rerun skips regeneration (only notebooks and the harness changed, no generated output).")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_14 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 14u32, "2026-10-21T13:53Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 09:53 eoie team: inventory today: 26 eoie-owned hand-written Rust test files remain (9 [[test]] targets, 17 tests/*.rs; vendored crates excluded). command_spec_domain's help_catalog.rs (30 lines) is ported into the r30 command-spec slice's Spiral notebook as every_advertised_proxy_has_its_own_usage_and_unknown_names_get_none (catalog alignment, four exact usages, five unknown names). The .rs file is NOT deleted in r30: evidence/coverage/current.lcov and replay-seed.lcov list it as a source and state/evidence.spi hashes those files, so deleting it could trip the GPT-era evidence currentness checks; delete it in the release that next refreshes coverage evidence. Rule for the rest: port one file per slice into the slice's own notebook only when that slice already touches the crate.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_15 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 15u32, "2026-10-21T20:35Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:35 eoie team: shipped in the combined r28+r29 release, installed 15:38 (one-call spec 34/34, all 67 notebooks green): the notebook phase lists every failure instead of stopping at the first.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_16 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 16u32, "2026-10-22T09:23Z", "eoie", "05:23 remaining scope, measured on the live tree (vendor excluded): 14 hand-written tests/*.rs files, 846 lines, in 11 packages (eoie_bundle_manifest 3, rust_std_fs 2, eoie_agile_lease, eoie_compiler_discovery, eoie_coverage_prune, eoie_process_observation and 5 more with 1 each). These are the last .rs without a Spiral owner. Each converts to a Spiral test block in its package, std-only primitives only (crate-backed ones are covered end to end by the one-call runner, per spiral-macro-gotchas).")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_17 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 17u32, "2026-10-22T09:25Z", "eoie", "05:25 first conversion drafted, composed into release E: apply-test-portable-policy.ps1 turns eoie_bundle_manifest/tests/portable_policy.rs into the Spiral test archive_permissions_keep_executable_and_readonly_intent in bundle_manifest.spi (all four modes: 420/292/493/365 = 0o644/0o444/0o755/0o555), adds the package header and the registry notebook, deletes the .rs. The module's rust_global blob is reached only from main, so the plain-rustc test compile should not see it; E's preview and notebook phase confirm. 13 test files remain.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_18 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 18u32, "2026-10-22T09:27Z", "eoie", "05:27 classification of the 13 remaining test files (after portable_policy): all are OS integration tests of Rust blob code against the real filesystem or processes: symlinks and renames (compiler_discovery identity, release_contracts hygiene_confinement, tree_copy, legacy path_mutation), a Linux FIFO child process (proxy_search hash_boundary), zip expansion limits (bundle_manifest archive_limits), Unicode and limit edges in directory listing (rust_std_fs directory_names), Windows-only behaviors (3 windows.rs), the lease package inputs and the coverage prune transaction. None tests a pure Spiral function, and Spiral test blocks compile with plain rustc without crate dependencies, so they cannot convert one-to-one. Path: each moves with its code. When the code under test becomes Spiral (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY / EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE), its test becomes a test block; until then the behavior is covered end to end as one-call runner cases, which run the real binary.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_19 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 19u32, "2026-10-22T21:45Z", "eoie-lane", "17:45 inventory (no compile): 12 hand-written tests/*.rs remain in src (617 lines). portable_policy.rs (8 lines, a pure function test) migrates with GE2 (apply-test-portable-policy in apply-rE); the other 11 are the OS integration tests classified at 05:27. Outside src, compiler-contracts holds 9 test-*.ps1 contract scripts (1,148 lines); CI runs test-dev-workflow from them, which was red since 10-18 and is fixed in the tree today (EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW). After GE2: 11 .rs files, all needing OS boundaries (symlinks, FIFOs, zip limits, Windows-only behavior), so they move only with the OS boundary package (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY), where a Spiral test block can drive the primitive.")
