inl note_of_x_client_3 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 3u32, "2026-10-16T01:19Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 21:19 -04:00) build.ps1 green: Spiral->Rust compile, cargo release, e2e 8 tutorial steps + 4 extra cases against e2e/stub.py, 4 test blocks in posts/cli/x_api (SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process, no daemon left). Live HTTPS check with an invalid token: api.x.com answered 401, decoded as expected (TLS via rustls OK). post.fields=created_at still unverified live.")
inl note_of_x_client_4 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 4u32, "2026-10-16T02:11Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 22:11 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) Renamed from apps/timeline. OAuth2 client credentials (client_credentials grant on /2/oauth2/token with client_type+scope) yield a token the v2 read endpoints refuse (403 Unsupported Authentication 'Unknown'); the app-only Bearer Token from console Keys & Tokens is required. A first Generate was read through the accessibility tree, which truncates at 100 chars (401); the regenerate click was then blocked by the session's permission classifier, so the user copies a fresh token. Client id/secret saved in ~/.secrets/x-api.env (user-only ACL). Live plan: BBCBreaking+SkyNewsBreak (3 follows each), WSJbreakingnews (0 follows).")
inl note_of_x_client_5 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 5u32, "2026-10-16T02:21Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 22:21 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) 280 experiment: 193 top-level blocks all <= 280 X weight (max 276; before: 24 of 96 over, max 1595, measured with a splitter that also glued ///> lines onto the previous block); .spi x-compat findings 0 (whole folder 49 -> 35, all 35 in the tutorial); exe size flat (1,458,688 vs 1,458,176 bytes), generated Rust +6%, source +51% lines (mostly tests). Tests: 22 blocks on zig+rust (prelude 2, posts 3, cli 9, x_api 8 incl. 2 negative GADT tests pinned to their Expected text and mutation-checked). Free live 401 via TLS OK with spindle.exe.")
inl note_of_x_client_6 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 6u32, "2026-10-16T05:40Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 01:40 split into one Rust crate per entry (xc_net, xc_checks, xc_args, xc_users, xc_fetch, xc_refs, xc_write, xc_view, bin xc), crates exchange strings/numbers/tuples; scripts/gate.ps1 reports generated lines vs 1000: all under except xc_view 1786 (code shape, see RUST-UNION-IMPLS and RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION); e2e unchanged; live read OK")
inl note_of_x_client_7 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 7u32, "2026-10-16T11:59Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 07:59 every post, quoted/replied post and repost original ends with [N comments, N reposts, N likes] from public_metrics (reply_count, repost_count, like_count) added to post.fields; same request count (e2e 57 = baseline), no extra billed resource, ~120 bytes more per post; xc_view 1786 -> 1903 generated lines (counts record copied with each post)")
inl note_of_x_client_8 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 8u32, "2026-10-16T15:48Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 11:48 times shown in the time zone of the machine running xc (jiff TimeZone::system, TZ overrides; e2e pins TZ=America/Cuiaba); bare --start-time/--end-time dates are local midnight; names follow the X API: replies (reply_count), username (not handle), --start-time/--end-time (start_time/end_time), [url] hints (entities.urls), 'replied to' (replied_to), X_OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN/X_OAUTH2_REFRESH_TOKEN (were X_USER_*); internal records use API field names (public_metrics, url_entity, media_key, alt_text, next_token, max_results)")
inl note_of_x_client_9 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 9u32, "2026-10-18T05:53Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 01:53 unblocked (the onboarding blocker was cleared 2026-10-15). view split into digest (JSON bundle -> one tab-separated display entry line per post) + view (lines -> selection -> text) + jsonl (same selection as JSON Lines); post and entry are heap layouts; all 12 crates under the 1,000-line gate (view 999, digest 989, jsonl 929); timeline output byte-identical through the split (e2e 25 steps + 5 extra); tabs in post text now render as one space")
inl note_of_x_client_10 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 10u32, "2026-10-18T12:14Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 08:14 everything in the title is built, stub-tested and verified live (timeline, post/delete on both auth paths, refresh). x CI is red on a85e58a (2026-10-18 03:08) only because that commit has cli.spi's new 'xc thread ID' usage line but not the README that blesses it (xc --help and the --per-account 500 step DIFFERENT on both OSes); the working-tree README passes the e2e. Done once the next push is green; threads continue in X-CLIENT-THREADS")
inl note_of_x_client_11 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 11u32, "2026-10-18T17:15Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:15 x CI after the 14:46Z green: run 39140732842 (f454741, 11:29) is a startup_failure because the commit added the gh-pages publish job (download-artifact@v6.0.0, peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v4.1.0) but not the regenerated .github/workflows/actions.lock, which GitHub enforces; the regenerated lock is staged in x. Reprioritized P3 -> P1 (user flow review 2026-10-18)")
inl note_of_x_client_12 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 12u32, "2026-10-18T23:30Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 19:30 gate headroom (measured per crate): xc 973 -> 722 by making env_or a let (it was inlined at every environment read) plus failed/missing_bearer/reported as lets; args 994 -> 959 with one_value/other_command/write_command as lets (938 before delete-thread); view 999 -> 990 by timestamps via sm'.substring (drops the 61-line string_slice helper; post-text clipping keeps the UTF-8-safe slice); digest 998 -> 990 by a one-line Rust unescape; assemble back to 955 after gap detection (1,197) by Rust one-liners for the frame header (word_at/part_at), replied_to and the flattened page bundle. Lesson: an inl helper called from many places is the cheapest gate win; profile_rs per crate finds them")
inl note_of_x_client_13 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 13u32, "2026-10-21T03:15Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 23:15 pre-commit proof (eoie job x-precommit, 22:01-23:14): CI's own scripts/build.ps1 (no -fast) over the uncommitted tree exits 0 locally: actions-lock 8 actions locked, crate gate 16 crates 0 over 1000, x-compat 0 in 36 files, postable 1617 posts with 0 cells over one post, e2e tutorial and extra cases incl. delete-thread 34, Cells 35 of 35 notebook files with 0 failures, sim ExUnit 43/43 after the fixture guard, corpus commute on both schedules, real-Cells executor run, thread_run accepts the thread and rejects a tampered one. CI is red on HEAD 61b8fff only from the windows-2025 CLIXML e2e failure (run 39367603402) that the uncommitted e2e.ps1 ProgressPreference fix addresses, so the user's next commit of this tree is expected to turn ci green; D1 needs two consecutive green runs on main")
inl note_of_x_client_14 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 14u32, "2026-10-21T21:22Z", "x", "2026-10-21 17:22 x: grooming. Status Active -> Blocked so the stop gate's ready list stops offering it: x's part is verified (CI's own scripts/build.ps1 green locally on the uncommitted tree; 10-21 x-split-fix3 green after the post_id slice and the lib Gleam fixes). The remainder is the user's commit and push plus two consecutive green ci runs on main (X-DONE D1), which no agent can do. Unblock when the user commits.")
inl note_of_x_client_15 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 15u32, "2026-10-27T12:57Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:57 x: CI read (gh, read-only). ci on main failed for the user's last 3 pushes, including today's 9b90151 'tests' (run 40488607167). (1) xc-windows: \"couldn't find file apps\\client\\domains\\domains.rs\". The commit carried the WIP crates' .spi and Cargo.toml (domains, requests), but generated .rs were never put in the tree; I had wrongly left generated outputs to the verify. Fix in progress: x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part regen (job-1793105792101 via i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1) regenerates every client crate on the current tree with the pinned compiler, and the .rs that the WIP changes or adds (new crates; changed ones by the same-compiler base comparison) land in the tree unstaged. (2) build (ubuntu-24.04): the gate passed (28 crates), then e2e threw \"the Mastodon stub did not write its port\", because apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py is UNTRACKED: e2e.ps1 (committed) starts it, but the commit did not include it. Untracked files a commit needs today: apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py, apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt (untracked since 10-25 and compared by the sim build), apps/client/e2e/links.txt (new tutorial input), scripts/verify.ps1, plus the new crates' .rs once landed. Also added __pycache__/ to x/.gitignore (the Python stubs write it under e2e/). Only the user commits; this note is the list for that.")
