inl eoie_init_lease_file () = Task ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", "agile init leaves a root where attested writes fail: state/package.spiproj lists the prompt module, but init writes no state/prompt.spi, so any typecheck-attested mutation (groomed add, set) fails with 'Missing check input: state/prompt.spi' until a lease begins", TaskKind, P3, D2, 60u32, Paused, "", "eoie", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_init_lease_file () = Planning ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_1 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 1u32, "2026-10-21T18:35Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 14:35 eoie team: found by the combined r28+r29 release. notes_cli's agile_add_lands_a_groomed_item_in_one_call ran on a fresh 'agile init' root and failed the attestation. Real roots (the shared backlog, eoie/state) carry a prompt.spi, so day-to-day use is unaffected. The test fixture now writes a lease file like the shared backlog's. Product fix to decide: init writes a closed lease file, or the state package lists prompt only once a lease exists. Lease-root detection keys on prompt.spi, so measure both before choosing.")
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_2 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 2u32, "2026-10-21T19:41Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 15:41 eoie team, rule set before measuring (measurements run after tibia's live block, because they typecheck). Option A: init writes state/prompt.spi with a closed lease (PromptLease ... LeaseClosed), so the state package it declares is complete from the start and begin replaces the lease. Option B: init lists only the agile module, and begin adds prompt to the manifest when it writes the lease. On scratch roots, choose A if all of these hold: (1) init, then a groomed add (--estimate/--note --as) passes under the default lease policy and under renewing; (2) agile begin afterwards still opens a lease and later mutations pass; (3) agile lease/status on an init-only root reports the closed lease, not an error. Otherwise B, measured the same way. Ties go to A (smaller: one more scaffold file, no manifest rewriting).")
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_3 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 3u32, "2026-10-21T21:20Z", "eoie-lane", "17:20 eoie team, measured on scratch roots with the installed r28+r29 binary (init-lease-measure.ps1, then 4 lease-file variants). (1) holds for baseline and option A: a groomed add (--estimate/--note --as) on a bare init root now passes under the default and renewing policies (validation=runtime-attested, compiler not required), so the item's premise (attestation fails without prompt.spi) no longer reproduces. (2) holds for both: begin opens a lease and later adds pass. (3) fails for both: baseline (= option B) 'agile lease' on an init-only root prints a raw OS error (prompt.spi not found, exit 2); option A's closed lease is rejected ('PromptLease shape/status rejected fields=7'), because the lease reader accepts only LeaseActive. Nothing in src writes LeaseClosed. An all-zero LeaseActive file is read but reported as phase=running, 497949h ago, which misleads. The rule did not cover both options failing; decision: neither A nor B. The remaining defect is the lease reader: a missing prompt.spi should give a no-lease receipt (exit 0, hint 'eoie agile begin'), and LeaseClosed should be read as closed. The reader is a Rust blob in agile_state_runtime/state_terminal.spi, so the fix goes with that blob's granular migration (next in the order after the handoff render), not as blob growth. Priority lowered to P3: day-to-day roots carry a lease file.")
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_4 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 4u32, "2026-10-22T07:40Z", "eoie", "03:40 groom: the row now matches note 3's decision (P3; the item's premise no longer reproduces, the remaining lease-reader defect rides the state_terminal.spi blob migration).")
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_5 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 5u32, "2026-10-22T13:46Z", "eoie-lane", "09:46 eoie team, decided by reading the code (measuring was the open step): lease readback accepts only LeaseActive (agile_prompt_lease_status_code maps everything else to unknown, which the shape binding rejects) and checks deadline = started + budget + guard. Attested writes need only the file (the shared backlog's lease expired on 10-08 and its writes still pass). So a 'closed lease' file would fail readback, and the working shape is an expired active lease, the one the shared backlog and the notes fixture carry. Fix (apply-init-lease.ps1, in G before E's heal): scaffold_file gains LeasePrompt; init writes state/prompt.spi as PromptLease ('init', ..., 4500000, 600000, now-5100000, now, LeaseActive), which is never live; init refuses when prompt.spi already exists; the receipt says files=3. notes_cli test: a fresh init root takes a groomed add with no hand-written lease, and a second init fails.")
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_6 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 6u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 30m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D2 at 60%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_eoie_init_lease_file_7 () = Note ("EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 7u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
