inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_1 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-10-22T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:39 x: filed for main from the 21:4x inventory (scratchpad lab-inventory.csv columns: repo, folder, files, tracked, KB, extensions, newest, item status). x did not touch spiral/lab except its own CELLS-POSTABILITY-PROFILE draft, which main promotes by applying it (apply.ps1 -Apply writes x_compat.ex, the test and its fixtures into apps/cells) or prunes.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_2 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 2u32, "2026-10-22T01:41Z", "main", "21:41 main inventory for session 2026-10-21 (rule relayed by x at 21:4x; read only, nothing deleted): 22 spiral/lab folders have files written since 07:00, 253 files. Planned disposition, not executed: CARRY once until PACK-AFTER-NIGHT / CELLS-PACK-NEXT install, then promote as the tree edit and prune the script: FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS (13), BEND-BACKEND (11), RUST-EXPORT-TYPES (4), SPIRAL-RECORD-WITH-INFERENCE (3), GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (2), SPIRAL-OP-ARG-NAME-WORDS (17, incl. the regression sample to promote into samples/), SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES (1), SPIRAL-DIAGNOSTIC-PIPED-LITERAL (1), CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS (1), CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP (1), CELLS-PROBES (1), KINO-HOT-PATHS (3), CELLS-POSTABILITY-PROFILE (3, x's draft), SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR (1). CARRY once: SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (44: family .spi files are the promotion candidates as test blocks, paused by the 2x rule; gate data stays as the measurement record), MACHINE-WATCH (3 PowerShell scripts; promotion means an eoie verb, EOIE-MACHINE-WATCH), HOPACSOTA-P2 (2), COMPILER-PACK-SPEED-AB (3), CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE (1, probe-lib.ps1 is a live tool), CI-OFFLOAD (1, waits for the user to paste). PRUNE candidates once confirmed: GLEAM-STRING-LINEAR bench outputs (108 files today; findings in its notes 1-13; keep patch-slice.ps1 until the night pack installs), SEFAZ-XSD-XML-READER's 29 files from today. spiral/lab is fully untracked (git status: ?? lab/), so a prune cannot be undone with git; prunes wait for a user confirmation of the rule, since it reached me through a peer.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_3 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 3u32, "2026-10-22T01:47Z", "main", "21:47 rule for tonight's session sweep, fixed before moving (user via x 21:5x: decide autonomously, back up in internal dirs; x's tested scheme: prune = move to <repo>/target/lab-attic/<date>/<ID>/, target/ is git-ignored in spiral (checked: .gitignore line 2) and core.ps1 only clears target/<profile>/deps|incremental|build). ATTIC now: files nothing reads any more whose finding is in the item note: SPIRAL-OP-ARG-NAME-WORDS bisect files not used by candidate.ps1 (bisect_a, b, c, c1, c2, c3, c5, op_arg_width, run-bisect, run-pair; findings in notes 2-3), GLEAM-STRING-LINEAR bench outputs (findings in notes 1-13; patch scripts stay, patch-balanced-concat is still staged), SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS whole folder (paused by its 2x rule; suite-time.ps1 reads gates-20261021 relatively, so it moves intact and returns with the folder). CARRY once, named: folders a queued script reads by path (pack-night: SPIRAL-DIAGNOSTIC-PIPED-LITERAL; pack-next: BEND-BACKEND, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX, RUST-EXPORT-TYPES, SPIRAL-RECORD-WITH-INFERENCE, SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES; CELLS-PACK-NEXT: CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS, CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP, CELLS-PROBES, CELLS-POSTABILITY-PROFILE, KINO-HOT-PATHS; sefaz-table-job: SEFAZ-XSD-XML-READER, MACHINE-WATCH, CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE; morning-measure: COMPILER-PACK-SPEED-AB; op-arg proof: the rest of SPIRAL-OP-ARG-NAME-WORDS), tools named in tracked docs (FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS in lanes/formatter/PLAN.md, HOPACSOTA-P2 in lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md, probe-lib.ps1 used by every family and lib gate), and items waiting on the user (CI-OFFLOAD paste, SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR promote). Each move: sha256 of every file before, Move-Item, sha256 at the attic path, mismatch = move back and stop.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_4 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-10-22T01:48Z", "main", "21:48 session 2026-10-21 swept by the note 3 rule: lab: promoted 0, pruned 156, carried 97 (in 21 folders). The prunes are moves to spiral/target/lab-attic/2026-10-21/ (160 files with 4 older ones in the same folders; sha256 equal for every file after the move, git status unchanged since target/ is ignored; no running process read them). Moved: SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS whole (45), GLEAM-STRING-LINEAR/bench (105, 99 of them gleam build output), 10 SPIRAL-OP-ARG-NAME-WORDS bisect files. The carries are the folders named in note 3, each read by a queued pack or job script, a tracked doc or the user's pending decision; each leaves at its install or decision. Mover: scratchpad lab-attic-move.ps1 (hash check, auto move-back on mismatch). Not done tonight: the 19 folders under Done items (separate sweep).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_5 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 5u32, "2026-10-22T01:52Z", "main", "21:52 REVERSED: the attic was drift (user via x: target folders get deleted often to free disk). All 160 files moved back from spiral/target/lab-attic/2026-10-21 to their original spiral/lab paths (sha256 equal for every file), and the attic folder is removed; ignore the attic path in the earlier note. Healing is finishing the items that hold these folders (user 21:5x).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_6 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 6u32, "2026-10-22T02:04Z", "main", "22:04 reframed by the user (22:0x): lab is for minutes-long theory tests; drain it by redoing each holding item properly in its real place, from scratch, with the lab files as reference, deleting a folder only after its item has landed; this comes before new work. Map of all 107 spiral/lab folders to their items (every folder has one): Done 19 folders / 766 files, Active 53 / 630, Blocked 1 / 13, Planned 32 / 92, Paused 2 / 5. Drain order: (1) Done items first, cheapest: check that each folder's result is in the tree or in notes, promote what isn't (SEFAZ-XSD-XML-READER's xsd/xml as fixtures beside the reader), then delete; Done: SEFAZ-XSD-XML-READER 625, KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND 33, BACKLOG-LAPS 17, KINO-RUST-CRATES 16, CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE 12, SPIRAL-LITERAL-ALIAS-SPECIALIZATION 11, CELLS-EXHAUSTIVE-TESTS 10, GLEAM-TRY-RESCUE 9, HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH 9, SPIRAL-LITERAL-DEFAULTS 5, HANGULIZE-UPSTREAM-RETEST 4, MACHINE-WATCH 3, SPIRAL-CORE-NEQ 3, CELLS-WGSL-TEST-STATUS 2, X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT 2, ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE 2, COMPILER-MODULE-PARSE-STACK 1, X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE 1, CELLS-ETS-OWNER 1. (2) the two P0 packs (PACK-AFTER-NIGHT, CELLS-PACK-NEXT) and the night install, which land about 14 folders. (3) Active by size: GLEAM-STRING-LINEAR 112 (P2 70%), SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS 45 (P1 30%), UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA 29 (P1 90%), FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS 26 (P0 90%), SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES 25 (P2 80%), CELLS-EVERYWHERE 24 (P1 5%), SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR 24 (P1 70%), DATE-TIME-PORTABLE 23 (P2 80%), HOPACSOTA-P2 18 (P0 30%), SPIRAL-OP-ARG-NAME-WORDS 18 (P2 60%), COMPILER-NAMESPACE-COLLISIONS 18 (P3 50%), BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS 16 (P1 60%), CELLS-NEW-PROJECT 16 (P1 50%), KINO-HOT-PATHS 15 (P1 50%), RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE 15 (P1 85%). (4) Planned and Paused folders: mostly a script or two each; land or fold into the item note when the item is next worked.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_7 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 7u32, "2026-10-22T06:51Z", "main", "02:51 main: night progress, measured now: spiral/lab has 67 folders and 443 files, from 107 folders / 1,506 files at 22:04 and 86 folders at the start of this run's second half. Drained tonight by landing or verifying: SPIRAL-DIAGNOSTIC-PIPED-LITERAL (Done), SEFAZ-XSD-XML-READER (Done; 625 files now in C:\\home\\git\\sefaz), SEFAZ-XSD-APP, DATE-TIME-PORTABLE, EBPF-C-PROFILE, CELLS-GATE-MACHINE-WINDOW, BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS, CI-OFFLOAD (job wired into gh-pages.yml), TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO (verify step in 4 workflows), LIB-USAGE-DIAGNOSTICS, CROSS-BACKEND-BENCHMARK, SAMPLES-STALE-OUTPUTS, SAMPLES-OUT-OF-TMP, CONVO-IN-SPIRAL, LIB-REACTORS, PS1-TO-SPIRAL; GLEAM-STRING-LINEAR is down to the one patch it lands with. Tools went to apps/compiler/tmp/scripts, apps/compiler/tmp/formatter, apps/cells/spi and spiral/scripts; 76 run outputs went to the run cache (lab-outputs); the stale lab-held tag came off 20 main items. Waiting on PACK-AFTER-NIGHT's install: BEND-BACKEND, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, SPIRAL-OP-ARG-NAME-WORDS, SPIRAL-ASSIGN-PRIMITIVE, SPIRAL-LITERAL-ALIAS-SPECIALIZATION, RUST-EXPORT-TYPES, SPIRAL-RECORD-WITH-INFERENCE, GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (checklist notes 14-17 there). Waiting on CELLS-PACK-NEXT: CELLS-PROBES, CELLS-NEW-PROJECT, CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP, CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS, KINO-HOT-PATHS, KINO-RUST-CRATES, CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE. The rest are live experiments of Active or Planned items.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_8 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 8u32, "2026-10-22T07:14Z", "main", "03:14 main: follow-up to the output move. Checked every remaining lab script against the moved file names. One script READ a moved output (SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS suite-time.ps1, repointed) and three called a promoted tool by its old lab path (gate-string/tagged-union/tuple, repointed to lib_gate.ps1). Five scripts would have WRITTEN new outputs back into lab, so their output paths now default to the run cache (lab-outputs\\<ITEM>): CONTRACTS-ON-ZIG measure.ps1, RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE verify.ps1, KINO-RUST-CRATES e2e-run.ps1, NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS contract-run.ps1 and run.ps1. All parse clean. Old session-scratchpad scripts still name drained folders, but they are one-off history and nothing reruns them.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_9 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 9u32, "2026-10-23T07:21Z", "main", "2026-10-23 03:21 main: measured now: spiral/lab has 52 folders and 298 files (67 / 443 at 10-22 02:51). Tonight's drain was by verified landing only: GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (union-depth.ps1, union-depth-doc.ps1), SPIRAL-RECORD-WITH-INFERENCE (patch.py, expected-base.ps1), SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES (nominal_with_patch.py, retype-census.ps1, run.ps1, build-errors.ps1). Each was checked against the tree core, plus a by-stem search with a positive control. Held by queued work, not drainable yet: cells-pack reads CELLS-PROBES, CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP, CELLS-NEW-PROJECT, CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS, KINO-HOT-PATHS, KINO-RUST-CRATES and CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE. The post-install matrix bundle reads LEAN-BACKEND, CONTRACTS-ON-ZIG and ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY. next4 carries BEND-BACKEND's union-w64. The combined lib landing at tibia's block end closes COMPILER-NAMESPACE-COLLISIONS' scope; its 18 repro files go after that.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_10 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 10u32, "2026-10-23T21:30Z", "main", "2026-10-23 17:30 main: measured: spiral/lab has 51 folders and 282 files (52/298 at 03:21). Today's landings (formatter-only install, lib batches: seq/listm', sm', gleam_erlang 1.x, erlang_process/otp_*/step_runtime) held no lab folder, so none drains by the landed-only rule. Next drains are tied to installs: lab/GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (4 probes) after next9's GADT cap installs (proven 10.9 s EJP0041 in a Debug build today); lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS after its families run through apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/test-blocks.ps1 (queued tonight, job-1792778604345) and move into their real place; lab/HOPACSOTA-P2 and HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH stay (measurement runners still cited by open items).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_11 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 11u32, "2026-10-24T05:52Z", "main", "2026-10-24 01:52 main: measured 52 folders; none belongs to a Done item, so none drains by the landed-only rule tonight (all 52 map to Active, Paused or Planned items). Queued drains: after the Cells pack lands (cells-pack.ps1 -Target apps/cells at tibia's PR-27 block end), the 18 steps' sources in CELLS-PROBES, CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP, CELLS-NEW-PROJECT, CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS, KINO-HOT-PATHS and CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE become drainable, each checked against apps/cells first; after pack 5g installs, GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (4 probes; the cap is in 5g).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_12 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 12u32, "2026-10-24T06:30Z", "main", "2026-10-24 02:3x main: drain list prepared for after the post-block Cells suite confirms the 02:23 landing (landed-only rule: only files the Cells pack APPLIED; measurement runners that open items still cite stay). CELLS-PROBES: patched_mounts.py, probe.py (keep cell-phases.ps1, patched-mounts-run.ps1, probe_text.exs, standalone-check.exs until CELLS-PROBES closes). CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP: bounded-memsup.ps1 (the folder then empties). CELLS-NEW-PROJECT: patch\\* (keep the run and gate scripts and pending\\). CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS: pool-probe-async.ps1. KINO-HOT-PATHS: server-apply.ps1 and the server modules it copies, if byte-equal to apps/cells (keep fixed-cost, in-vm-rounds, memo-cache, preload, warm-* runners). CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE: document_patch.py, patch.py, reference_test.exs. Each deletion is preceded by a by-stem search over the sibling repos and scratch scripts, with a positive control.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_13 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 13u32, "2026-10-24T21:52Z", "main", "main 17:5x inventory: spiral/lab is down to 52 folders and 286 files (107 folders / 1,506 files at the item's start). 21 folders are untouched since before 10-22; the oldest are QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER, HOPACSOTA-P5, GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX, GPU-RENTAL-READINESS, ML-LABS, SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, LEAN-BACKEND and CRATE-GATE-HARDEN (all 10-19). Today DIB-MODERNIZE was drained: ports landed, folder moved to %TEMP%\\lab-attic after a ripgrep stem search. Next, per the session rule: for each of the 21, land-or-attic by item status (Done item -> attic after a stem search; Active item -> keep), oldest first.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_14 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 14u32, "2026-10-24T21:52Z", "main", "main 17:5x: applied the land-or-attic rule to the 7 oldest folders by item status: QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER (Planned 0%), HOPACSOTA-P5 (Planned 0%), GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (Active 40%), ML-LABS (Planned 0%), SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX (Planned 5%), LEAN-BACKEND (Active 30%), CRATE-GATE-HARDEN (Active 40%). None is Done, so all 7 stay. The other 14 pre-10-22 folders are next; GPU-RENTAL-READINESS (Planned) also stays.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_15 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 15u32, "2026-10-24T21:53Z", "main", "main 17:5x: all 21 lab folders untouched since before 10-22 are now checked against their items' status: none is Done (Active: GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX, HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH, KINO-HOT-PATHS, LEAN-BACKEND, ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY, CRATE-GATE-HARDEN; Paused: SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT, TODO-AS-SOURCE; Planned: the rest). By the rule all stay; the sweep picks them up as each item closes. The sweep is at the steady state: 52 folders, each tied to an open item.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_16 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 16u32, "2026-10-25T00:01Z", "main", "2026-10-24 20:01 main groom: two items closed in this grooming pass had lab folders: CELLS-DAEMON-MEMSUP (1 file) and KINO-RUST-CRATES (12 files). Their work is in the tree, so by land-or-attic both moved to %TEMP%\\lab-attic\\<ID>-20261024-2001, hashes equal, nothing deleted. spiral/lab: 52 -> 50 folders, each tied to an open item.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_17 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 17u32, "2026-10-25T08:05Z", "main", "10-25 04:05 main: re-swept spiral/lab, 50 folders. Every folder named by an item ID belongs to an open item (none Done after today's closes). The one name that is not an item, LIB-PROCESS-HEAL (5 files, newest 10-24 21:30), is the tibia team's lab for LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE (notes 2/6/7 name it), which is open, so it stays. Gap in the rule: a lab folder named after a slice instead of its item ID has no direct status lookup; name labs by item ID.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_18 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 18u32, "2026-10-25T21:05Z", "main", "10-25 17:05 main: re-swept spiral/lab, 51 folders: every folder named by an item ID belongs to an open item (Active 28, Planned 15, Paused 6; none Done after today's closes), so land-or-attic moves nothing. The two without an item are tibia's: LIB-PROCESS-HEAL (seen 04:05, LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE) and the new LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT (9 files), whose name says the same item. The rule gap from 04:05 still stands (name labs by item ID); tibia owns those two. lab/PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN changed today: respelled to edition 3 plus the index-line types and status_probe.spi (its probe runs on the node, kit2 job-1792962100454).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_19 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 19u32, "2026-10-26T08:13Z", "main", "10-26 04:13 main: re-swept spiral/lab, 51 folders: Active 30, Planned 13, Paused 6, none under a Done item, so land-or-attic moves nothing. The same two tibia folders have no item of their own (LIB-PROCESS-HEAL and LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT, both for LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE). lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR's promote.ps1 and router_swap.py were retargeted today from spiral.livemd to spiral.spi (NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE n2).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_20 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 20u32, "2026-10-26T14:22Z", "main", "10-26 10:22 main: re-swept spiral/lab 10:2x: 51 folders, Active 31, Planned 12, Paused 6, none under a Done item, so land-or-attic moves nothing. The same two tibia folders (LIB-PROCESS-HEAL, LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT, both for LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE) still have no item of their own.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_21 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 21u32, "2026-10-26T19:07Z", "main", "10-26 15:07 main: 10-26 15:0x main: re-swept spiral/lab, 51 folders, status read through eoie agile show per folder: Active 31, Planned 12, Paused 6, none under a Done item, so land-or-attic moves nothing. The same two tibia folders (LIB-PROCESS-HEAL, LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT, both for LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE) have no item of their own. Method note: a first pass that regex-matched agile.spi's record text reported 28 folders as NO-ITEM, BLOG and PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN among them, which exist. The status must come from the tool, not a guess at the record format (the same 'one record per fact' reason).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_22 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 22u32, "2026-10-26T22:54Z", "main", "10-26 18:53 main: 10-26 18:53 main: re-swept spiral/lab, status read through eoie agile show per folder: 51 folders, 306 files, Active 31, Planned 12, Paused 6, none under a Done item, so land-or-attic moves nothing. Checked because tibia reported LIB-PROCESS-HEAL landed at 17:26: its folder and LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT both belong to LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE, still Active at 90%, so both stay until that item closes (tibia's folders, tibia's drain). lab/PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN changed tonight: the Nil-to-[] rewrite (114 sites, 13 files), store_lock_probe.spi and the read-only store lock; it drains when the item's executor lands in its real place (spiral/apps or a lib package; placement is a git-structure call for the user).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_23 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 23u32, "2026-10-27T12:24Z", "main", "10-27 08:24 main: two lab folders drained by rule (land first, then archive and remove proven duplicates; the user's archive-never-delete rule as relayed 10-27). Both folders are untracked, so git is untouched. 13 files are archived in hash-verified zips under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\main-archive\\20261027-0822-lab-drained, then removed. KINO-HOT-PATHS: cells_server.ex (byte-identical to apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/server.ex), spiral.cells_server.ex (the tree's mix task is a line-superset, adding MemoryGuard.start) and server-apply.ps1 (its notebook routing is in the tree). The by-stem reference search found 0 references, and its positive control hit. The measurement runners stay; they're the item's open half. CELLS-NEW-PROJECT: the 9 patch files byte-identical to apps/cells, plus PROJECT_NAME.spi, whose tree copy is the same template after the 10-24 edition-3 respell (a pure syntax mapping: open/nominal/inl/forall/if to :</:!/:=/\\\\*/?). The patch/ folder is gone. Left in CELLS-NEW-PROJECT: its 5 lab scripts and pending/scripts/probe.ps1, not yet judged.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_24 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 24u32, "2026-10-27T13:00Z", "main", "10-27 09:00 main: lab/CELLS-NEW-PROJECT is fully drained and removed (untracked, so no git change). The last 6 files are archived in a hash-verified zip (main-archive 20261027-0822-lab-drained, CELLS-NEW-PROJECT-rest.zip). They were the 10-19 proof runners for the scaffold that landed that day (new-project.ps1, scaffold-gate.ps1, spiral-lib-env-check.ps1, spiral-new-run.ps1, standalone-check.exs; the last loads the lab patch file, removed earlier, so it no longer runs) and pending/scripts/probe.ps1, superseded by the tree's priv/new_project/scripts/probe.ps1 (10-19 19:43 vs the lab's 12:52, 16+/8- newer in the tree). By-stem search: references only inside the folder itself (the positive control) and in backlog notes. Earlier the same session: the 9 identical patch files and the pre-respell PROJECT_NAME.spi. Spiral lab folders: one fewer. What CELLS-NEW-PROJECT still owes, per its title, is the scaffold CONTENT decisions (n20), not lab files.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_25 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 25u32, "2026-10-27T13:32Z", "main", "10-27 09:32 main: lab landed-file census over all 50 spiral lab folders (289 files): every lab file hashed against the tree outside lab/, target and deps. Byte-identical copies found: ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY 9 of 11, QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER 2 of 6, and 1 each in RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS and LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT; 0 in the other 45, which are live drafts, design notes and probes, judged one by one under the session rule. ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY: its 9 Zig shims are in apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims (byte-identical). Its hook zig_shims_hook.py has its effect in the tree: the 9 abi_external samples are on matrix.psd1's Zig list, test.ps1 loads shims from tests/native-shims, and the 10-27 review ran 9 abi_external Zig rows agreeing with C. shims_probe.zig is a probe. So the folder is spent, BUT TEMP matrix-bundle/bundle.ps1:7 still calls the hook from this lab path, so it's archived and removed only after the bundle accept (job-1793103041735) is GREEN, when bundle.ps1 can't need a re-apply. Next by this census: QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER's 2 landed files.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_26 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 26u32, "2026-10-27T13:36Z", "main", "10-27 09:36 main: correction to n25's census: byte identity over-counts tiny boilerplate. QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER's 2 'landed' files are an 18-byte bare/package.spiproj and a 39-byte core-only/package.spiproj that happen to equal two unrelated samples' boilerplate spiproj (abi_external_struct_return_i64, ebpf_char). They are not landings. The folder is the epic's unlanded probes (QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER is Planned, 0%), so it stays. The single matches in RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS and LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT get the same check before any drain. Rule for this census from now on: a match counts as landed only if the file is over 200 bytes, or its tree twin sits at the path the lab folder's own apply or patch names. ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY's 9 shims pass that rule (each is at the native-shims path the bundle's hook writes).")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_27 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 27u32, "2026-10-27T14:04Z", "main", "10-27 10:04 main: lab/LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT archived and removed (untracked; 9 files in a hash-verified zip under main-archive 20261027-0822-lab-drained). Owner tibia confirmed (10-27 10:1x) that every draft landed under other names, checked by top-level definition name against the live lib: shared_command 13/13 in runtime.spi, process_split 18/18 in process.spi, split_misc 4/4 across date_time, erlang_process and platform, process_split_all (their union) 49/49, erlang_port 14/14. LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE and LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE-SPLIT are both Done. main's spot check agreed: process_split 15/15 and shared_command 13/13 by name (main's pattern counts fewer definition forms than tibia's). The 3 .log files were empty gate stubs (0, 7 and 0 bytes). spiral lab is now 49 folders.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_28 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 28u32, "2026-10-27T16:43Z", "main", "10-27 12:43 main: lab/RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION drained to its one live probe (untracked, so no git change). Archived by scratch-archive.ps1 (kit archive 20261027-124241, blob verify 0 failures; restore with -Restore that manifest.tsv) and removed: or_join_patch.py (v1, dropped from pack 8 on 10-19 for the format_any regression), or_join_patch_v2.py and run.ps1 (v1's candidate runner). The v3 design superseded both patches and landed as OrPatternJoin in the core through pack 5g: spiral_compiler.fs:44537 typeDirected, 44546 trivial, 44551 lifted, which lift a non-trivial, non-type-directed or-pattern body into a function of its bound variables. The patches' anchor line no longer exists in the core, so they can't apply anyway. Also removed: or_pattern.spi, byte-identical (271 B, over the census's 200-byte floor) to the landed regression sample samples/or_pattern_bound_alternatives/main.spi. By-stem search (RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, or_join_patch, lab\\or_pattern) over 971 scripts in the spiral, compiler-tmp, packs and i574n.github script folders and TEMP to depth 1: the only references are spent pack scripts (pack-next2/3 compose.ps1, next3/next3b review.ps1, next5g orjoin-check.ps1, all superseded or installed; current packs are 5n and 5o) and two old backlog exports. The positive control hit inside the folder. Kept: wildcard_pair.spi, the item's open case (a wildcard arm after two pair arms on a 3-case union), not yet measured. Spiral lab folder count is unchanged at 49.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_29 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 29u32, "2026-10-27T16:58Z", "main", "10-27 12:58 main: Lab sweep, pass by item status: each of the 49 spiral lab folders paired with its backlog item's state. Done items holding lab files: only LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE (5 files). Folders with no item: only LIB-PROCESS-HEAL (5 files). LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE (untracked): 5 of process_handle.spi's 7 top-level definitions are in lib by name, and started_switch landed as ':== started_switch' at process.spi:53 (a form the first name scan missed). But none of its 9 Gleam externals (spiral_process_await_logging, drain, get, kill_pid_tree, put, start_logging, started_pid, unlink, write_file) is in lib under that name; they probably landed in the granular form (gleam_started, erlang_port wrappers). Not provable by name, so the folder STAYS; owner tibia was asked (13:0x) to confirm, as for LIB-PROCESS-SPLIT. Its 3 logs are gate stubs ('ready', a directory path, and empty). LIB-PROCESS-HEAL: a live GRANULAR-HEAL draft (25 of 79 definitions in lib; the other 54 are the granular port, Rust command and Gleam dynamic wrappers), in tibia's queue per GRANULAR-HEAL (process.spi:185/204/217/232/246). It stays.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_30 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 30u32, "2026-10-27T17:26Z", "main", "10-27 13:26 main: lab/LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE archived and removed (untracked; kit archive 20261027-130455, 5 files, blob verify 0 failures). Owner tibia confirmed at 13:0x that nothing is unlanded, giving the granular landing site of each of the 9 Gleam externals in lib process.spi: write_file -> file_system.write_all_text :138 and append_all_text in gleam_waited :86; unlink -> erlang_port.unlink in port_for :23; get/put -> erlang_process.dictionary_get/put keyed by exit_key 'spiral_process_exit' :73; start_logging -> start_logging's Gleam arm via port_for + gleam_started :129; started_pid -> erlang_port.os_pid :147; await_logging -> await_exit_within with the memoised exit :154; drain -> the gleam_waited join point :79; kill_pid_tree -> kill_tree_of_pid's taskkill /F /T arm :39. The draft's tests (start, pid > 0, await, kill) are lib tests at process.spi:286-304. main spot-checked 4 sites in the live file, each within 3 lines of tibia's line (unlink :23, taskkill :36/:42, spiral_process_exit :74, os_pid :150). The draft's 3 logs were gate stubs. Spiral lab: 48 folders.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_31 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 31u32, "2026-10-27T17:42Z", "main", "10-27 13:42 main: Correction to n29: lab/LIB-PROCESS-HEAL was NOT a live draft. Owner tibia confirmed (13:3x) that it is fully landed and that the GRANULAR-HEAL queue entry process.spi:185/204/217/232/246 is done. Live process.spi:172-251 holds the healed capture family (exit_with, captured, not_run, rust_captured, gleam_collected, gleam_captured, captured_by, succeeded, required, words, capture_stdout(_list), capture_combined_list, try_capture_combined_list) and the draft's 4 tests. The draft's 54 names missing from lib were ad-hoc primitives that each moved to a granular home under a new name: port_* -> erlang_port, rust_command_*/rust_child_*/rust_file_create -> runtime.shared_command_*/shared_child_*/log_file_create, monotonic_ms/rust_now/rust_elapsed_seconds -> date_time.monotonic_milliseconds/stopwatch*, rust_pause -> threading.sleep, os_cmd -> platform.os_command_output, file_write -> file_system.write_all_text/append_all_text, and the dynamic/bits/gleam_* glue -> erlang_term; argument_separator was dropped on purpose (no callers). main spot-checked all six target modules for those names and 5 capture-family names in 172-251 (5/5). Archived by scratch-archive.ps1 and removed (untracked). Lesson for the census: a by-name check against lib can't see a draft whose primitives were re-homed under new names; the owner's mapping is the proof.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_32 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 32u32, "2026-10-27T17:49Z", "main", "10-27 13:49 main: Lab sweep of main-owned folders whose items are at 80% or more: 3 drained, all untracked, archived by scratch-archive.ps1 (kit archives 20261027-134855 and -134905, blob verify 0 failures), then removed. (1) BEND-BACKEND/union-w64.ps1, the folder's only file: all 6 of its edits are in spiral_compiler.fs. Edits 1-5 match verbatim. Edit 6 (the prelude's word projections) landed with a renamed parameter as 'def w64_hi(p: U32 & U32)'; a first scan cut its list at 6 definitions and missed it, so I checked the full text before calling anything a bug. In accept-2, every Bend i64/u64 row compiles, runs and exits 0. (2) CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE, all 3 files: patch.py (Cells: notebook.ex now has reference_target), document_patch.py (document.spi has --reference) and reference_test.exs (its test name is in apps/cells/test). (3) RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE/lift-pin.py only: dice/contract/build.ps1 carries nightly-2026-10-18, -Z build-std and target-cpu=mvp. Its near-mvp.ps1, near-sdk-bump.ps1 and verify.ps1 stay; they are the item's open NEAR half. By-stem search (737 scripts in the spiral, compiler-tmp, i574n.github and dice script folders plus TEMP to depth 1): the only references are spent pack scripts (cells-pack, pack-after-night, pack-next3/3b/4), and the positive control hit. Kept: COMPILER-PACK-SPEED-AB, whose 3 A/B runners are its open measurement. Spiral lab: 45 folders.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_spiral_33 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL", 33u32, "2026-10-27T23:25Z", "main", "10-27 19:25 main: lab/ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY archived and removed (untracked; kit archive 20261027-192504, 11 files, blob verify 0 failures, 0 links). Its hold condition from n25 is met: the bundle accept is GREEN (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417), so TEMP matrix-bundle/bundle.ps1 can no longer need the lab hook for a re-apply. Its 9 Zig shims live byte-identical in apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims, and the hook's effect is in matrix.psd1 and test.ps1 (n25). Spiral lab: 44 folders.")
inl lab_sweep_eoie () = Task ("LAB-SWEEP-EOIE", "eoie team: sweep eoie/lab under the session rule: 18 folders, 119 files; first the Done items (EOIE-CORE-OPERATORS 10 files incl. 3 .pyc, CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE 3) and the folder with no backlog item (EOIE-DO-EDIT, 2 files: file the item or delete)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "-", "lab,eoie", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lab_sweep_eoie () = Planning ("LAB-SWEEP-EOIE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl lab_sweep_gate () = Task ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", "main team: the stop gate enforces the lab rule at the deadline: when an armed run reaches its deadline (or the deadline file is about to be deleted), run eoie lab audit --since <session start> on every repo the session touched and block the final stop with the listed files until each is promoted, pruned or carried with a note naming it; no sleep or poll in the hook (AUTONOMOUS-STOP-GATE rules)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 0u32, Paused, "EOIE-LAB-AUDIT", "lab,main,claude,hooks", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lab_sweep_gate () = Planning ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Unassigned)
inl note_of_lab_sweep_gate_1 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", 1u32, "2026-10-22T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:39 x: proposal only; main owns ~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1 and nobody else edits it. Session start = the deadline file's creation time or the session's first transcript entry.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_gate_2 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", 2u32, "2026-10-22T01:41Z", "main", "21:41 main proposal only (no hook change; a peer cannot grant hook edits and the rule reached me through x): at the deadline pass, the gate would run eoie lab audit --since <deadline file creation time> once (bounded by the 30 s Stop timeout, so the audit must be a fast directory-time scan; no sleep or poll), and block the final stop once with the listed files and the required lab: line, then pass on the next stop if the last message contains a lab: line. Depends on EOIE-LAB-AUDIT existing; until then the gate could print the count from a Get-ChildItem LastWriteTime scan of the touched repos' lab folders, which took 261 ms for 253 files on spiral/lab (107 folders, warm file cache; measured 21:42).")
inl post_1_in_fork () = Task ("POST-1-IN-FORK", "Post 1 moves into the i574n/The-Spiral-Language fork (user 2026-10-21 22:0x: this blog post should be moved to upstream's fork somewhere there, configuring the blog clone somehow as deps, also weird name): the post module and the data and samples behind it live in the fork; the blog repo is cloned into the fork's deps by the fork's init step so the post compiles against blog/engine; the post gets a plain name instead of vanilla_start; then spiral/lab/UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA is drained (and blog/engine/vanilla_start.spi leaves the blog repo)", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "blog,fork,lab-drain,main", "current", "current")
inl eoie_generic_drift () = Task ("EOIE-GENERIC-DRIFT", "eoie knows no external projects (user 2026-10-21 21:5x: 'eoie is a generic project that shouldn't know about external stuff'): generic --team words, neutral fixtures, no user data in the repo", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "eoie,drift", "current", "current")
inl erl_crash_dumps_in_tree () = Task ("ERL-CRASH-DUMPS-IN-TREE", "Erlang crash dumps landed in repo folders and were hidden by stock .gitignore lines (user 2026-10-21 22:1x: what about this erl_crash.dump file? heal the drift): send every Cells VM's dump to the cache, unhide strays, remove the dumps", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,erlang,drift,main", "current", "current")
inl eoie_log_sequences () = Task ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", "table logs event-sequence verbs per file, times from an @t+<ms> capture: --interval A [--between B] [--modulo ms] (gaps between consecutive matches, optionally only when B fell between, as rows or folded onto a grid); --window A --from M --ms lo..hi (counts of A in a window after marker M); --order A,B (first-occurrence order as a column); --in-set name=<file> (captured values tested against a set file); plus --median in table query", Feature, P2, D5, 60u32, Paused, "EOIE-HEAL-LIB-LINK", "eoie,table,logs", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_log_sequences () = Planning ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", Minutes 195u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_1 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 1u32, "2026-10-22T02:24Z", "eoie", "22:24 requested by tibia: lets a repo drop per-experiment analysis scripts (tibia freezes four of them until these land; not urgent, experiments concluded). Fixtures must stay neutral (EOIE-GENERIC-DRIFT): no game log lines in tests.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_2 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 2u32, "2026-10-22T03:37Z", "eoie", "23:37 typed design drafted (scratch log-sequences/design.md, moves to lab after release A): --time name=<regex with ms capture> stamps lines; sequence_measure is a GADT indexed by result kind (Interval -> gaps with fold AsRows|Modulo ms, Window -> count over ms_range after a marker, Order -> verdict Before|After|Missing, InSet -> count against a set file); an existential any_measure lets mixed measures share the logs pipeline, each rendering its column via a prototype. Plus table query --median. Neutral fixtures only; built on lib/spiral after EOIE-HEAL-LIB-LINK, so it waits behind the boundary work.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_3 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 3u32, "2026-10-22T09:46Z", "eoie", "05:46 second request from the same consumer (event latency for a pre-registered probe check): folded into this item instead of a new verb. Design addition in lab/EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES/design.md: a Latency kind in the sequence_measure GADT (pairs each --latency match with the next --to match in the same file, optional --when on the from line, gaps from the shared --time stamp capture), plus table query --quantile p and --share-at-least t beside the planned --median. Gate note: eoie_table_logs.rs is 817 lines, so the sequence kinds may need their own crate. Needs compiles; next session after ABC/D/E.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_4 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 4u32, "2026-10-22T11:49Z", "eoie-lane", "07:49 eoie team: the pure half is drafted (scratch log-sequences/eoie_log_sequences, goes to lab/EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES when no lease holds the tree). It follows lease.spi's shape: nominal result phantoms gaps/counts/verdicts, a GADT sequence_measure result (Interval, Window, Order, Latency over named term records), and measured forall result. dispatching into one measure_outcome {rows : list measure_row; unpaired}. Runtime lists are core list with listm.rev (xsd_regex's idiom), and parsing uses sm'.split, am'.try_item and convert.try_convert. 5 test blocks with hand-checked expectations on a neutral request/reply/flush fixture. A primitive boundary exports eoie_sequence_interval/window/order/latency: (file, events text 'role TAB line TAB at_ms' per line) to rows 'file TAB line TAB value' plus '#unpaired TAB n'. Decisions: every measure yields rows (table query aggregates median/quantile/share); --when and --in-set are matching-side filters and stay in the logs crate; Order's row line is the first A's line (0 when absent). Integration plan for logs.spi (next session, needs compiles): a PerSequence table_shape like --values; events come from the lib's sm'.new_regex + regex_captures (named group ms for --time) instead of a new host macro, which migrates logs.spi's touched regex code to the lib in the same change.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_5 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 5u32, "2026-10-22T12:34Z", "eoie-lane", "08:34 eoie team: integration decided by the style contract's legacy rule (touching a legacy function means migrating it). Adding five flags to logs.spi's options_from would force migrating its rust_std_string parser in the same change, so the sequence measures get their own verb in the clean crate instead: eoie table sequences <file|dir>... [--glob g] --time name=<regex with an ms capture> (--interval name=A [--between B] [--modulo ms] | --window name=A --from M --ms lo..hi | --order name=A,B | --latency name=A --to B [--when W]) [--out f.tsv]. One measure per call, rows file/line/value like --values, routed by one elif in eoie_cli_model (VerbTable). Order: first preview the pure crate (proves list/listm.rev/sm'.split/convert idioms on Rust), then the verb with lib regex (sm'.new_regex + regex_captures) and the file walk.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_6 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 6u32, "2026-10-22T13:48Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-22 09:48 Consumer request (tibia, TIBIA-EVENT-TIME note 75): --interval keyed by a capture. Logs interleave several actors, e.g. 'monster <id> moved to x,y @login+<ms>' for three monsters in one file, and the measure is the gap between consecutive matches of the SAME id. Proposal: --interval name=A --key <capture name or group 2> (or a key=regex beside --time), giving gaps per key in file order; the rows carry file, key and gap, so table query --group key --median gap works. With --key absent, behavior is unchanged.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_7 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 7u32, "2026-10-22T14:03Z", "eoie-lane", "10:03 eoie team: verb half drafted (lab/EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES/eoie_log_sequences/verb_draft.spi; first compile pending, not in any release yet). measure_request (IntervalOf | WindowOf | OrderOf | LatencyOf) maps two user patterns to roles first/second. events_in walks a file's lines once, stamping each from a named (?<ms>...) group of the --time regex (lib sm'.new_regex plus regex_captures over mapm.get 'ms') and adding a role event per matching pattern. A new erasure union sequence_measure_any (AnyGaps | AnyCounts | AnyVerdicts) lets a runtime choice still dispatch to the GADT-typed measured. Lib-type plumbing is confined to matches_in, stamp_in and compiled, the parts most likely to need adjusting at first compile. Still to do: the argument reader, the file walk (read_dir_names as in repo affected), --out, and the VerbTable dispatch line.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_8 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 8u32, "2026-10-22T14:04Z", "eoie-lane", "10:04 eoie team: the verb draft is complete (lab verb_draft.spi): an args reader (--time, --interval/--window/--order/--latency name=pattern, --between/--from/--to, --ms lo..hi, --modulo, --out; an unknown option is refused), measure_of returning option measure_request (a two-role measure without its second pattern is refused), a file walk (dirs listed one level through lib read_dir_names, files kept as given), a TSV with header 'file line <name>' to stdout or --out through file_system.write_all_text, and the export eoie_table_sequences_run. Remaining to land: verb.spi joins the crate's modules after its first compile, one VerbTable elif in eoie_cli_model, the command spec usage and a CLI notebook on a neutral request/reply log. Goes in the release after H, once H has compiled the model.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_9 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 9u32, "2026-10-22T17:50Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 13:50 previews (compile window, scratch tree): the H crate eoie_log_sequences compiles at 861 lines and now also exports eoie_sequence_events (log text plus time/first/second regexes in, role/line/ms rows out), with regex = 1.13.1 in its Cargo.toml. The table sequences verb (apply-table-sequences.ps1, release I) is its own crate calling the five exports: 892 lines, after three shrink rounds from 1523 (the GADT model specialized inside the verb crate, an 11-field argument record fold, inl helpers expanded per call site). It waits on lib console.write_error_line (main's second landing). lab/EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES/verb_draft.spi is superseded by table-sequences/eoie_table_sequences/verb.spi and goes once I lands.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_10 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 10u32, "2026-10-22T21:20Z", "tibia-lane", "Request from tibia (2026-10-22, two uses today, both done with a scratch loop instead): carry the last capture of one pattern onto each later match of another, per file. Shape: table logs <files> --values at=<pattern A with a capture> --carry pos=<pattern B with captures> writes one row per A match plus the most recent B capture before it (empty when none). Uses: the knight position line (seen at x,y:) at each Loot of a troll line, to place late kills; the latest @t+ms stamp at each seen-at line (seen-at lines carry no stamp), to bin sightings by time. --order and --window do not cover it (they need a time on both lines).")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_11 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 11u32, "2026-10-22T23:11Z", "tibia-lane", "Use case from tibia-lane 2026-10-22 19:1x (TIBIA-EVENT-TIME note 100): in 20 arena logs, for each file, the first @login+<ms> time of each of three monster ids (monster <id> moved to x,y @login+<ms>), then per file the gap between id 82 and id 81 first moves and whether 82 moved at all. table logs --count-by already gives the per-id counts (20, 6, 18); the per-file first-occurrence times and the gap need --order with a time capture (or --values grouped per file with a first-only flag). Done by hand today; expected rows: file, first_81_ms, first_82_ms, first_83_ms.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_12 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 12u32, "2026-10-23T03:21Z", "tibia-lane", "Second use case from tibia-lane (2026-10-22 23:3x): one log file holding many runs, each starting at a header line (lead-trace run <stamp> knight seen ...), with per-entity lines (<kind> <id> ... @knight+<ms>) and some lines that belong to the next section but come before its header (monster <id> ... starts at x,y @knight+-1). Needed: --section-on <regex> (rows per section instead of per file), optionally carrying lines marked by a capture (here @knight+-1) into the next section, then the --order / first-occurrence time per captured id within each section. Done tonight with a scratch reader (server-probe/read-trace.ps1); expected rows: section, id, first_time, first_value.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_13 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 13u32, "2026-10-23T06:33Z", "tibia-lane", "TDD case for note 12 (tibia-lane, 02:4x), with exact input and expected rows, verified by hand and by the scratch reader. Input file, 16 lines: lead-trace monster 81 Hunter starts at 1931,1352 @knight+-1 / lead-trace monster 82 Hunter starts at 1931,1353 @knight+-1 / lead-trace run 20261023-030000 knight seen at 1932,1349 @knight+0 / lead-trace think 81 at 1931,1352 @knight+600 / lead-trace think 82 at 1931,1353 @knight+300 / lead-trace monster 81 moved to 1930,1352 @knight+850 / lead-trace think 82 at 1931,1353 @knight+1300 / lead-trace think 82 at 1931,1353 @knight+2300 / lead-trace knight targets 82 @knight+2500 / lead-trace knight gone @knight+90000 / lead-trace monster 71 Hunter starts at 1931,1352 @knight+-1 / lead-trace monster 72 Hunter starts at 1931,1353 @knight+-1 / lead-trace run 20261023-030300 knight seen at 1932,1349 @knight+0 / lead-trace monster 71 moved to 1932,1352 @knight+700 / lead-trace knight targets 72 @knight+2500 / lead-trace knight gone @knight+90000 (the slashes separate lines). Sections start at the run header; lines stamped @knight+-1 belong to the next section. Expected first-move rows (section, id, first_time, first_value): 20261023-030000, 81, 850, 1930,1352 and 20261023-030300, 71, 700, 1932,1352. Expected start rows (section, id, value): 20261023-030000 has 81 at 1931,1352 and 82 at 1931,1353; 20261023-030300 has 71 at 1931,1352 and 72 at 1931,1353. Expected all-times rows for think lines (section, id, times): 20261023-030000, 81, 600; 20261023-030000, 82, 300,1300,2300. Expected first knight action per section: 2500 and 2500. The join the tibia question needs on top of that, the boxed id (start value 1931,1353) and its thinks after the neighbour's (start 1931,1352) first move, can stay a table query step: section 20261023-030000 gives 1300 and 2300 after 850, and section 20261023-030300 has no thinks logged. Scratch copy: server-probe/synthetic-trace4.log in the tibia session scratch.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_14 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 14u32, "2026-10-23T18:33Z", "eoie", "14:33 eoie: note 13's TDD case is now spec/one-call.md case 45 and fixes the design. table sequences <file> --section-on '<regex with (?<section>)>' --carry '<regex>' --time '<regex with (?<ms>)>' --first <name>='<regex with (?<id>) and (?<value>)>'. A section starts at each --section-on line; --carry lines before a header belong to the section that header opens; --first keeps the earliest match per section and id; columns are section, id, <name>_time, <name>_value; the receipt is 'eoie table sequences ok files=1 sections=2 rows=2'. Expected rows are tibia's first-move rows (81 850 1930,1352; 71 700 1932,1352). Red until the verb exists (table sequences itself lands with release I). Start, all-times and first-action rows (also in note 13) become follow-up cases once --first works.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_15 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 15u32, "2026-10-23T18:34Z", "eoie", "14:34 eoie: tibia confirmed case 45's syntax and gave a second real case: PR-26's ground trace (arena-logs/20261023-111503-hunting-ground-ground-trace.log, 10 runs in one file, split by hand at each 'ground-trace run <stamp> knight seen' line, with the @knight+-1 lines before a marker belonging to the FOLLOWING section, i.e. --carry). Creature ids repeat across sections (canary restarts each run), so rows key by (section, id), as case 45 does. Follow-up cases: (1) --last <name>='<regex>' next to --first, giving <name>_time/<name>_value of the last match per (section, id), so life = death - appear becomes a table query step; (2) the time capture accepts negative values (case 45's -?\\d+ already does). Fixture for a real-data case: tibia's hand split (10 files, tibia scratch server-probe/pr26-runs), which reproduces TIBIA-PARTY note 72's P6 counts (R 30, F 0, I 5 over 12 late clusters).")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_16 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 16u32, "2026-10-23T18:37Z", "eoie", "14:37 eoie: pure model for cases 45 and 46 drafted (scratch f6/src/eoie_section_sequences, HostFree, LibReferenced; typecheck queued behind main's matrix). Two stages, so regex matching stays in the IO layer as in eoie_log_sequences: (1) sections_of: classified lines (Header section | Carried | Plain) placed into sections, with carried lines joining the section the NEXT header opens, plus a '-' section before the first header; (2) rows_from: observations (section, column name, id, value, at_ms as i64, so @knight+-1 stays -1) folded into one row per (section, id) in first-seen order, First keeping the earliest and Last the latest match per column, and a column with no match printing '-'. Tests reproduce case 45's and case 46's TSV rows exactly. The existing sequence_model (event at_ms : u64) is left as is: sections are a separate measure, so interval, window, order and latency keep their types.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_17 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 17u32, "2026-10-23T18:49Z", "eoie", "14:49 eoie: IO side drafted as scratch log-sections/apply-log-sections.ps1 (anchored, idempotent, dry run on the post-L copy clean, second run is a no-op). eoie_log_sequences gains section_model (the pure model) and section_scan: regex scanning with named groups section/id/value/ms, a signed i64 ms parse, and an exported sections_text + sections_header. eoie_table_sequences/verb.spi gains --section-on/--carry/--first/--last as known flags; any number of --first/--last columns are collected in argument order; there is a sections branch with the same refusals as the measures; the receipt adds sections=N; and the usage line is extended. A CLI test adds a 2-run fixture with a carried line and a --last overwrite, plus the --time refusal. section_scan's tests replay cases 45 and 46 on the exact trace text. The notebook typecheck is running (compile window) now that main's matrix has ended. The slice is queued for the release after N.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_18 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 18u32, "2026-10-23T19:08Z", "eoie", "15:08 eoie: both new modules pass their notebooks (f6, 15:02): section_model 3/3 and section_scan 2/2. section_scan's tests run the real regex scan on the case 45/46 trace text and reproduce both expected tables exactly, including -1 times and '-' cells. Two fixes on the way: (1) multi-line 'listm.fold fun ...' with the initial state on its own line mis-parses, so the folds now use named step functions; (2) a Rust codegen ownership error, E0507 'cannot move out of v4, a captured variable in an FnMut closure': the shared empty-string literal was used both as the vec_fold' seed and as default_value' inside the closure. The closure now passes its own accumulator as the default. Test blocks that touch sm'.regex need '///> rust -d regex'. Slice log-sections/apply-log-sections.ps1 carries the fixed blocks.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_19 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 19u32, "2026-10-23T19:19Z", "eoie", "15:19 eoie: release vehicle set by rule (a slice ships in the earliest release whose gates can run; N's byte-identity gate waits on main's 5f formatter, and neither slice touches the formatter): release O = log-sections + note-as-first, chained right after M; N now rebases on O. Scripts (scratch): derive-o.ps1 writes launch-O, release-build-job-O (4 candidate notebooks: section_model, section_scan, sequences_cli, notes_cli; baseline merge eoie_log_sequences), after-install-O (sections table on a 2-run trace with carry, -1 times, --first and --last, and '-'; agile note --as on both sides; one-call spec >= 41; backlog reads). chain-next's order is GE2, HIJK, L, M, O, N. Positive controls on today's install: after-install-O scores 1/4 (the 3 new checks fail, as they must), and N's O-gate refuses (the first draft keyed on 'unknown option --first', which never shows on an eoie without table sequences; it now requires the probe's 'sections=1 rows=0' receipt). Typechecks: note-as-first task_notes PASS on m-on-l (15:11).")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_20 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 20u32, "2026-10-23T19:36Z", "eoie", "15:36 eoie: release blocker found and fixed before HIJK launches. Today's installed compiler emits Rust E0507 ('cannot move out of v4, a captured variable in an FnMut closure') for H's own stamp_in: a vec_fold' whose closure reuses the seed literal in default_value'. A probe test calling events_text on the untouched L-dry2 copy failed with it at 15:29. The same crate compiled at 861 lines on 10-22 13:50 (note 9), so this is a codegen regression since then, and HIJK's regen cargo check would have failed. Fix (same semantics; in that branch found is the empty string): default_value' found. Probe passes at 15:31. Applied to H's source (scratch log-sequences/eoie_log_sequences/sequences.spi and verb_draft.spi), the L-dry2, m-on-l and log-sections dry trees, and the 4 eoie lab reference copies (no tree lease held). A minimal repro (2 tests, literal and dynamic group name) went to main.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_21 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 21u32, "2026-10-24T06:23Z", "eoie", "02:23 root cause of the E0507 in stamp_in (RUST-FNMUT-CAPTURE-MOVE), from main: lib, not the compiler. optionm'.default_value's Rust arm is x.unwrap_or(value); in a vec_fold' closure whose default is the fold's seed literal, the deduplicated literal is captured by the FnMut closure and unwrap_or moves it. Main's fix (unwrap_or_else(|| value.clone()) plus a regression test with this shape in sm'.spi) lands after tibia's PR-27 block. After it lands, remove the workaround (passing the accumulator as the default) in H's stamp_in, the dry trees and the lab copies, and recompile to confirm.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_22 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 22u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 195m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D5 at 60%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_eoie_log_sequences_23 () = Note ("EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES", 23u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
