inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_7 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 7u32, "2026-10-26T00:14Z", "eoie", "20:13 eoie: the notes_cli test show_reads_the_newest_or_matching_notes_with_their_numbers fails on the release candidate with 'agile show expects <root> <id> [--json], received 4 operands': the filtering is in agile_task_inspection, but the route (agile_mutation routes.spi, AgileShow => agile_either_arity 3i32 4i32) still refuses 5 operands. One-line route fix after KIT-RENAME (feature freeze); until then the test is a tracked known failure in the release notebook gate.")
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_8 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 8u32, "2026-10-26T06:40Z", "eoie", "02:40 eoie: route fix PROVEN on the worker node. Draft kit scratch clean\\kit-rename\\route-arity.do: AgileShow and AgileNoteEdit route through agile_with_root, so each verb's own parser validates its options (show refuses with 'options are --json, --last <n> or --grep <word>'; note-edit prints its full usage). Candidate: renamed tree plus the kit_named length fix plus this draft; kit_adoption and kit_agile_mutation regenerated; debug build; this box's compiler (core CDD68DC3EE829A67); SPIRAL_LIB from a synced spiral mirror. Strict verdict (executed above 0, passed equal to executed, unsupported 0; positive control kit_lcov executed 2, passed 2): 10/10 agile and notes notebooks pass, notes_cli included, so show_reads_the_newest_or_matching_notes_with_their_numbers and note_edit_append_adds_a_sentence_to_the_stored_note both pass. The help shape string is deliberately unchanged: spec/one-call.md line 296 searches for the literal shape, and README and the subcommand test pin it, so the shape text is its own coordinated change. Lands right after KIT-RENAME; then both rows leave the release known-failures table.")
inl c_fuse_declarations () = Task ("C-FUSE-DECLARATIONS", "C backend declares and initializes in one line: 13,863 of 16,343 split declarations (T vN; then vN = e;) are directly followed by their single assignment, 14.8% of non-blank C output lines", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "PACK-NEXT-4", "compiler,c,codegen,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_fuse_declarations () = Planning ("C-FUSE-DECLARATIONS", Minutes 30u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_c_fuse_declarations_1 () = Note ("C-FUSE-DECLARATIONS", 1u32, "2026-10-22T23:06Z", "main", "2026-10-22 19:06 main: measured on the next3b pre-matrix snapshot (507 main.c, scratch c_split_decl_census.py). Pass fuseCDeclarations (%TEMP%\\pack-next4\\c-fuse-declarations.ps1, in PACK-NEXT-4) runs on codegenC's finished program text: a line INDENT T vN; directly followed by INDENT vN = e; at the same indent, where e does not name vN and T has no storage class (static/extern/typedef/register: a fused static initializer would run once), becomes INDENT T vN = e;. In C (unlike C++) a jump past an initialized declaration is legal and leaves it as indeterminate as before, and no VLA is emitted, so behavior is unchanged. Mirror (c_fuse_decl_mirror.py): 138,961 -> 125,098 lines (-10.0% on top of blank lines); gcc -fsyntax-only on the 40 largest fused files: 38 pass, 2 fail on poll.h exactly as their originals do. Review rule: C changed only by blank lines plus this fusion (review.ps1 re-applies it to the snapshot); native results equal; DISAGREE 0.")
