inl note_of_gleam_helpers_on_demand_1 () = Note ("GLEAM-HELPERS-ON-DEMAND", 1u32, "2026-10-23T07:19Z", "main", "2026-10-23 03:19 census over 447 tree outputs: unused spiral_* helpers are 137,686 of 1,661,094 bytes (8.3%); wrap_unsigned unused in 167, array_from_list/to_list in 122, array_create in 84. Pass pack-next6\\gleam-helpers.ps1: gleamUsedHelpers runs on the assembled program after silenceUnusedBindings and drops a top-level 'pub fn spiral_*' (with its @external line, or its body up to the first column-0 '}') when nothing else names it, repeating to a fixed point. Types and imports stay (an unused import is a Gleam warning, not an error). Mirror gleam_helpers_mirror.py: 8.3% smaller, 265 outputs change; the review rule (squeeze(pruned(before)) = squeeze(after)) accepts all 265 mirror outputs. Not composed yet: tibia's live block bars compiles, so the fsi port check, the compose and the parse-only check run after its block end, with the gleam batch build in the review as the real proof.")
