inl note_of_eoie_grep_regex_hint_1 () = Note ("EOIE-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 1u32, "2026-10-23T10:07Z", "eoie", "06:07 friction measured on myself: eoie grep over the backlog state with the needle 'single-use binding|codegen pack' (and 'near-gate|zzz') answered 'ok ... 0 matched', because the needle is literal without --regex, while 'near-gate' alone matched 12 times; I nearly concluded absence. Rule: when a search ends with 0 matches, no --regex was given, and the needle holds a pipe, .*, brackets, ^ or $, the receipt adds 'hint: the needle is literal; pass --regex to use it as a pattern'. No other behavior change. Test: a grep CLI notebook case with an alternation needle over a fixture that holds both words.")
inl note_of_eoie_grep_regex_hint_2 () = Note ("EOIE-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 2u32, "2026-10-23T10:10Z", "eoie", "06:10 slice drafted: scratch grep-hint/apply-grep-regex-hint.ps1 (typed needle_hint union NoNeedleHint | LiteralLooksLikePattern, hint only when total is 0 and --regex is absent; eoie_grep_query gains spiral- for sm'; grep_cli test with 'needle|three' literal -> hint, --regex -> matches 3 and no hint). Anchors are on main's pre-format originals (grep.spi is in the 05:08 formatted set), so it lands through fmt-rebase; prelaunch with -Originals is clean. Ships with the small post-GE2 release (accept-review, notebook progress), not HIJK.")
inl note_of_eoie_grep_regex_hint_3 () = Note ("EOIE-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 3u32, "2026-10-23T10:17Z", "eoie", "06:17 re-anchored: the slice now matches the post-G healed grep.spi (receipt line with ++#, open sm'_operators already present, added only if missing). Composes in the release L dry chain on GE2 -> H,J,K. Ships in release L (launch-L.ps1).")
inl note_of_eoie_grep_regex_hint_4 () = Note ("EOIE-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 4u32, "2026-10-23T18:10Z", "eoie", "14:10 eoie: TDD case written, spec/one-call.md case 44 (eoie grep notes.txt 'one|two' over a two-line fixture). On the installed binary it is red at exactly the hint ('ok  files 1 searched  0 matched  matches 0  2ms ...' vs the same with '  hint: the needle is literal; pass --regex to use it as a pattern'), so the rest of the receipt already matches byte for byte; it turns green when L installs the slice.")
