inl eoie_job_requeue () = Task ("EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE", "eoie job requeue <id>...: jobs record argv, cwd, environment names and their after-chain, so stopped or failed jobs restart with the same chain in one call (PROC-3)", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "EOIE-JOB-RECHAIN", "eoie,jobs,consolidated", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_job_requeue () = Planning ("EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_job_requeue_1 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "Evidence 10-23 18:28: main stopped 7 queued jobs when a live block began and saved their argv by hand (scratch saved-argv) to requeue them at block end. Milestones: argv/cwd/env record at start 45 m, requeue verb keeping chain order 60 m, tutorial 30 m, release 15 m.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_requeue_2 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE", 2u32, "2026-10-24T02:53Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:53 main: the record already exists. Each job folder under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\jobs\\<id> holds argv, argv.inner (the real command when heavy-wrapper.ps1 wraps it), label, timeout_ms, after (predecessor plus ok|any) and cwd. Main requeued 9 chained jobs at 22:5x by reading those files (scratch requeue-lib-tail.ps1: check every job is still queued, stop all, requeue in order with --after). So the verb is that script plus --timeout overrides; milestone 1 (recording) is done. Re-estimate: 90 m.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_requeue_3 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE", 3u32, "2026-10-24T05:37Z", "main", "2026-10-24 01:37 main: spec from the working stopgap (scratch main-queue.ps1 -Action Stop|Requeue|Show, used for tibia's PR-27 block). Algorithm: (1) Stop: take the queued jobs of a set (label prefix, team, or listed ids), record each folder's label, argv.inner (or argv), timeout_ms, heavy (heavy-wrapper.ps1 present), window-class, and after (predecessor id TAB ok|any), sorted by job id = creation order, into one manifest, then job stop each. (2) Requeue: walk the manifest in order; a predecessor that is itself in the manifest maps to its NEW id; a predecessor outside it keeps its id only while unsettled (a settled one drops the --after); keep --after vs --after-ok from the mode; relaunch with the same shape, label, timeout and argv; print 'requeued <label> as <new id> after <id>'. Plumbing for the eoie team: a new crate eoie_job_requeue (control.rs is already ~46 KB, so the verb must not grow it); a new export on eoie_job_launch that takes the shape and after mode (eoie_job_launched_text covers only PlainStart); JobRequeue in eoie_jobs.model job_command plus usage; dispatch in eoie_jobs/jobs.spi. Re-estimate stays 90 m for the Spiral, plus the train's new-crate steps.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_requeue_4 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE", 4u32, "2026-10-24T06:09Z", "main", "2026-10-24 02:09 main: a gap the stopgap hit. 'job list' without a count shows a bounded window (unsettled first, up to 120), and my stop pass parsed it for queued main jobs: 3 old queued jobs (otp-single gate/land, dictm-land-2, created 22:52/22:59) were missed and stayed live. One of them was --after a stopped job, so it was free to take a heavy slot ahead of tibia's live block. Fixed in the stopgap with 'job list 1000'. The verb needs a direct query: 'job list --queued [--label-prefix p]' (or a state filter) that never truncates, so 'requeue' and 'doctor' can rely on it.")
