inl note_of_polyglot_granular_heal_1 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-GRANULAR-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-10-25T07:48Z", "main", "10-25 03:48 main: classified, nothing edited. chat_contract.spi: 3 type aliases (12/152/171) and 3 one-call sites (81 panic_str, 108 get.cloned, 182 get.cloned) are already granular. The 5 multi-statement Rust blocks (39 alias validation, 65 CID varint encoding, 122/131 alias-map update, 161 account lookup) are the real heal. Proof: a wasm32 build plus chat_contract_tests, which need the NEAR sandbox and so run on Linux (CI); WSL waits for the workflow per the standing rule, so this item pairs with a CI run. math.spi: 9 complex operators (10-85) are one host call each, so they stay. The heal candidates are the 3 println! traces (96, 254, 263) -> console.write_line with format_debug (same {:?} text, if format_debug's Rust arm is format!(\"{:?}\")), plus the exit at 555. The pyo3 glue (137-162, 274-284) stays as host calls; 276-284 opens a closure across macros, which is the real design smell. Proof: the math build runs the Rust+pyo3 tests, which needs a Python env.")
inl note_of_polyglot_granular_heal_2 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-GRANULAR-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-10-26T10:05Z", "tibia-lane", "10:05Z 10:1xZ polyglot math.spi exit site (note 1's 'exit at 555'), tibia lane. main's $'if !code \\!= 0 { std::process::exit(!code) }' (host if plus exit) becomes ? code <> 0 ?> env.exit_with code, over LIB-EXIT-WITH (node GREEN, queued to land in tibia-serial-gaps). polyglot's deps/spiral is a symlink to C:\\home\\git\\spiral, so the land is visible at once. Proof (scratch polyglot-exit/probe-run.ps1): math.spi compiled to Rust against the tree lib and against a copy with exit_with. The generated math.rs differs only at the exit site: 'if v41 != 0 { std::process::exit(v41) };' becomes a Spiral-side 'let mut v42: bool = v41 != 0i32; if v42 { std::process::exit(v41); () }', where the exit now comes from lib's arm, already proven to exit with its code and run nothing after it. Apply: scratch polyglot-exit/polyglot-exit-apply.ps1, an anchored single replace that refuses on 0 or more than 1 match. It is packed at the end of tibia-serial-gaps, guarded on env.spi having exit_with, and lands as an unstaged working-tree change in polyglot (the file is LF and clean in git). The println! traces (96, 254, 263) stay: format_debug renders tuples without parentheses, unlike {:?}, so moving them would change trace text, and the pyo3 test run needs a Python env. Follow-up after the land: polyglot math build.ps1 (Rust plus pyo3 tests) on CI or the node.")
inl note_of_polyglot_granular_heal_3 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-GRANULAR-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-10-26T13:53Z", "tibia-lane", "13:53Z 14:0xZ tibia: generate_cid heal drafted, proven and offered to main (POLYGLOT-GRANULAR-HEAL n1 listed '65 CID varint encoding' among the 5 multi-statement Rust blocks). The block (varint buffer, hasher new/update/finalize, iterator chain, concat, multibase) becomes the spiral_out_varint_u64 global shim (GRANULAR-LINT rule 8, out class: a buffer plus calls), plus sha256_digest (one call, <sha2::Sha256 as sha2::Digest>::digest(..).to_vec()) and multibase_base32_lower (one call). The [0x12, 32] ++ digest and [1] ++ codec ++ multihash concatenations move to Spiral via am'.new_vec and am'.vec_extend. Proof (scratch polyglot-cid/probe-run.ps1): the old and healed functions in one module, compiled to Rust and built by cargo (multibase =0.9.1, sha2 0.10, unsigned-varint 0.8), print identical CIDs for [], [104;105] and [0;255;7;85]. The [] case equals the generate_cid test's bafkreihdwdcefgh4dqkjv67uzcmw7ojee6xedzdetojuzjevtenxquvyku. Apply: scratch polyglot-cid/cid-heal-apply.ps1 (anchored, refuses on rerun, dry-run ok on base 1826A02274991F07). It lands with main's is_valid_alias heal or on main's word.")
inl x_granular_heal () = Task ("X-GRANULAR-HEAL", "Heal x host macros per GRANULAR-HEAL (32 sites, 2,916 chars: client/glyphs.spi 14/1,149, net/net.spi 6/682, wire.spi 7/520, locate, oauth1, token)", Story, P1, D3, 85u32, Active, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "granular,macros,x", "current", "current")
