inl formatter_then_below () = Task ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", "apps/spiral/spiral.spi still has `then` laid on the line below its if: find whether the formatter fix was never reapplied there or the formatter still emits it, fix the source, re-lay the file (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 60u32, Paused, "", "formatter,apps,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_then_below () = Planning ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:02Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:02 main: found and healed. The installed formatter (5f) keeps `if c then` + block intact (stdin probe), but it also keeps an authored LONE `then` line (`if c` / `then` / block), because it never joins authored breaks. Those lone-then lines are artifacts of the 10-20 formatter runs: 2 in the 10-02 lib+apps/spiral, 37 now (33 at HEAD plus 4 in spiral.spi's unstaged diff). Healed by a token-neutral join (%TEMP%\\lib-lone-then\\apply.ps1: `if/elif cond` + lone `then` -> one line when it fits in 120; whitespace-only, checked per file): apps/spiral/spiral.spi 4 sites now; lib 27 sites in 8 files through the land guard (main-serial-lone-then). async, base, sm', sm'_real and trace come after their heal slices land. Formatter rule for the next formatter pack: a lone `then` line whose previous line is an if/elif condition at the same indent joins it when the result fits, the only case where the formatter joins an authored break (lone then is never an authored habit: 2 in the whole 10-02 corpus).")
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_2 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 2u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
