inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:12Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:12 main: from FLAT-FOLDERS: the samples move (apps/compiler/tmp/samples -> top-level samples/, 9,882 files losing 2 levels) is this epic's first and largest step. test.ps1/matrix.psd1 paths, CI and EXPECTED.tsv ids (samples/<name>) are written to keep their `samples/...` ids, so the oracle needs no re-accept beyond the path root.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-25T14:06Z", "main", "10-25 10:06 main: inventory (10,015 tracked files under apps/compiler/tmp) and destination rules, written before any move (rule: decide by pre-written rules).\n(1) samples/ (9,855): to top-level samples/ per FLAT-FOLDERS, keeping 'samples/<name>' ids so EXPECTED.tsv only changes its path root. Precondition: no matrix reader live (the 5l' review/install/accept done) and an exclusive window, since test.ps1, matrix.psd1 and CI paths change in the same edit.\n(2) compiler/ (host, core, lib, runtime-compat, Directory.Build.props; 13): product code, so it goes to apps/compiler/host etc., next to spiral_compiler.fs. Precondition: build.ps1 and env.ps1 paths updated in the same edit, and a candidate build proves an identical DLL hash (deterministic build).\n(3) tests/ (matrix.psd1, native-shims 31, rust-exports 5): to apps/compiler/tests/.\n(4) scripts/ (62): each script is classified once by rule: an entry point (build.ps1, test.ps1, env.ps1, probe.ps1) moves to apps/compiler/; a method used by several sessions becomes an eoie verb (memory: generic tools, not per-experiment scripts) and the script is deleted once the verb ships; a script with no caller in any repo or CI and no backlog reference newer than 10-20 is deleted by the dangling-check rule (grep the stem in all repos plus consumer builds, with a positive control).\n(5) formatter/ (30 F#/Python prototype files): the formatter lives in the compiler's '/// ## Formatter' section now. Each file is deleted once a grep shows no caller and its function exists in 'SpiralCompiler format' (format.ps1 corpus modes: check format-corpus covers them first).\n(6) lanes/ (14 docs: hopacsota PLAN.md etc.): facts go into backlog notes on the lane's items (memory: research lives in backlog), then the files are deleted.\nOutside references to update in the same edits: .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml, apps/cells (README.md, compiler_daemon.ex, run_notebook.ps1, run_suite.ps1), apps/lisp (lisp.livemd, membership*.spl), apps/zed (fixtures package.spiproj x2, tasks/test-at-row.ps1), scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1, scripts/workflow.ps1. Order: (6) and (5) first (docs and dead code, no readers), then (4) by class, (3), (2), and (1) last in its own window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-25T14:19Z", "main", "10-25 10:19 main: step (5), formatter/ classified, with a correction to the plan's method. The repo grep alone was WRONG for 4 files: candidate-gate.ps1 showed no callers in any repo, yet %TEMP%\\pack-next4\\review.ps1:46 calls it on every pack review, and it runs extract-corpus.ps1, fitting_lines_kept.py and complaints_probe.py. Those are LIVE (the pack review's formatter gate). Also live: report.ps1 (CI: scripts/workflow.ps1), corpus.ps1 (scripts/parser-corpus-gate.ps1), format.ps1 and lint.ps1 (documented entry points in tmp/AGENTS.md). Rule amended: the dangling check also greps %TEMP% pack/gate/serial scripts and follows live callers one level down (memory dangling-check-by-stem). Dead: the 8 F# prototypes (Check, Convert, Flatten, Format, Layout, Lexed, Parsed, Spacing .fsx). They form a closed #load cluster rooted at Format.fsx, which nothing outside the cluster loads, and only lanes/formatter/PLAN.md mentions them. Their function lives in 'SpiralCompiler format'. Deletion waits for the %TEMP% caller scan. The live formatter tooling then moves with step (4) to its proper place (probably apps/compiler/formatter/), not deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-25T15:11Z", "main", "10-25 11:11 main: step (5) part 1 DONE. Deleted the 8 dead F# formatter prototypes (Check, Convert, Flatten, Format, Layout, Lexed, Parsed, Spacing .fsx; unstaged, copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\formatter-fsx). The rule held on every source: no caller in any of 9 repos, CI or the top-level scripts of 144 %TEMP% job folders (453 scripts; positive control: the same scan finds 13 callers of candidate-gate.ps1); a closed #load cluster rooted at Format.fsx; their function lives in 'SpiralCompiler format'. lanes/formatter/PLAN.md still names them as history, and it goes with step (6). Left in formatter/: the live gate tooling (candidate-gate, extract-corpus, fitting_lines_kept, complaints_probe, report, corpus, format, lint) and synthetic/, all moving with step (4).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-25T15:16Z", "main", "10-25 11:16 main: step (6) started. lanes/bend/w64.bend deleted (a hand-written Bend probe of the w64 helpers; 0 references in the repo; copy in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\lanes), and the empty bend/ folder with it. single-flight/README.md's one unique fact is now CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS; the rest repeats tmp/AGENTS.md. RUST_LIBRARY_PLAN.md is finished history (all steps done 09-28). gpt5parallel/README.md's unique fact is the run-log location + 'Select-String runtime_exception_captured'. These three, plus tmp/NEXT.md, which links to them (NEXT.md:168/185/786, AGENTS.md:124), go together in ONE doc pass so no link dangles: facts to backlog notes, AGENTS.md:124 repointed to FRONTIER.md, then the files deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-25T15:18Z", "main", "10-25 11:18 main: lanes/hopacsota/research/ (untracked, 9 per-experiment scripts r3_*/r4_*/tree_paths, 56 KB, all stamped 10-22 00:05, i.e. a lab-drain copy) DELETED; copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\hopacsota-research. Rule basis: per-experiment scripts are not kept (memory generic-tools-not-per-experiment); their findings are cited in backlog notes (r4_deferred 7 lines, r3_simulate 6, r3_instrument 5); the R4 edits they applied are in the tree core (R4 gate met 10-15, seams installed); no job script in %TEMP% calls research/; the only tracked mentions are 2 historical lines in lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md ('job scratch ...r4_deferred.ps1'), which goes in the doc pass.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 7u32, "2026-10-25T15:29Z", "main", "10-25 11:29 main: step (6) doc pass 1 DONE: tmp/NEXT.md (838 lines, frozen since 10-18), lanes/gpt5parallel/README.md, lanes/single-flight/README.md and RUST_LIBRARY_PLAN.md deleted (unstaged, copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\docs; the files stay in git history). Folded first. NEXT.md's 'Open, in order' entries 0-3 were done or obsolete and entry 4 was overtaken (gpt5parallel met the promotion criterion 10-01); entries 5 and 6 became MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS and DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY. The single-flight README's gap is CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS, and the gpt5parallel README's run-log facts are a sentence in tmp/AGENTS.md's gpt5parallel paragraph. Links repointed: AGENTS.md (3), README.md (1, now pointing at the backlog), FRONTIER.md (6), all citing NEXT.md@47d1e562 so they still resolve. Left: one code comment in spiral_compiler.fs:186146 mentions NEXT.md; strip it in the next pack (no-comments rule). Still to fold: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md (85 KB), lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (92 KB), lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (90 KB), hopacsota hop-probes, formatter/allowlist.tsv.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 8u32, "2026-10-25T16:26Z", "main", "10-25 12:26 main: step (6) doc pass 2 DONE: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md (813 lines) and allowlist.tsv (25 rows) deleted (unstaged; copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\docs\\lanes-formatter), with the empty lanes/formatter/ folder. Folded first: the measured user style, F1-F10, the keep-breaks additions, the G6 banned list, G1-G7 and the process rules are one note on SPIRAL-FORMATTER. The user decisions were already notes (SPIRAL-FORMATTER 1, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS 1). Scoreboards and the decision-change log are history, kept at PLAN.md@0ec501fb. Dangling check: 0 readers of allowlist.tsv or lanes/formatter in the 9 repos, CI, the compiler, or 858 %TEMP% job scripts (positive control: candidate-gate.ps1 found 19 times). tmp/AGENTS.md:147 now points at the backlog notes plus PLAN.md@0ec501fb. Left in step 6: lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (92 KB, the live hopacsota contract that memory and AGENTS.md cite, so it is folded last, after its readers are repointed), lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (90 KB), hopacsota hop-probes.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 9u32, "2026-10-25T16:30Z", "main", "10-25 12:30 main: lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (1,045 lines, last edit f5e487e0 10-18) is NOT folded yet, by rule (links must resolve): 23 comments in spiral_compiler.fs cite its fix numbers ('FRONTIER.md fix 22/33-47/50/55'; lines 10746, 15806, 55149, 57317, 83125, 87117, 129890, 135213, 137838, 137863, 137926, 146883, 147687, 149237, 149245, 152779, 157437, 157525, 158919, 186182, 186197, 186243, 188866), as do tmp/AGENTS.md:12 and :89 and 13 backlog notes. Order: (a) the pack after 5m strips those comments (the no-comments rule; the code keeps its meaning in names), together with the NEXT.md comment at :186146; (b) AGENTS.md's citations become FRONTIER.md@f5e487e0; (c) the fix list's still-live facts (the fast loop; fixes 22, 57 and 58 named in AGENTS.md) go into notes on HOPACSOTA items; (d) the file is deleted. Backlog notes citing 'FRONTIER.md fix N' stay readable through the pin.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 10u32, "2026-10-25T16:47Z", "main", "10-25 12:47 main: step (a) of the FRONTIER order is staged for pack 5m: %TEMP%\\pack-next5m\\strip-doc-citations.ps1 -Target <core> [-Apply]. It finds by content every pure line-comment block that cites tmp/NEXT.md or lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (24 blocks, 86 lines on today's tree core, including the NEXT.md one at :186146), refuses a block holding a directive or marker, and proves that every non-comment line is unchanged and in order. On a copy, pair-drift found 0 pairs touched on one side only (8 pairs, 2 touched since HEAD by the user's staged work). Proof in the pack review: a comment-only edit, so residuals must be identical (the review's DISAGREE 0 and 0 differing cells cover it). After 5m installs: AGENTS.md:12/:89 citations become FRONTIER.md@f5e487e0, the live facts move to HOPACSOTA notes, and the file is deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_11 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 11u32, "2026-10-25T17:03Z", "main", "10-25 13:03 main: an outside reference missing from step 1's list: dir-tree-html/package.spiproj has packageDir: deps/spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples (it builds on the samples core). Step 1 must repoint it, or better, move dir-tree-html to lib/spiral first (TREE-PAGES-V2).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_12 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 12u32, "2026-10-25T23:15Z", "main", "10-25 19:15 main: dir-tree-html no longer builds against apps/compiler/tmp/samples. Its package.spiproj is lib-first now (TREE-PAGES-V2 n15; landed unstaged, proven on the node). The outside reference from n11 is resolved for step 1 once the user commits it.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_13 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 13u32, "2026-10-26T00:29Z", "main", "10-25 20:29 main: consumer inventory for the samples core. Of the 393 package.spiproj files with a packageDir in spiral, eoie, x, fiscal, polyglot, alphabet, dice, dir-tree-html, i574n.github and blog (deps, target, _build and .cache excluded), 332 resolve into apps/compiler/tmp, all in spiral. 328 are inside tmp itself (the samples, which move with it). The 4 outside: apps/zed/fixtures/ok and bad (the spiral-zed probe fixtures; ok uses the samples core's +. operator), lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/rename_probe and lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (labs of open items; they follow their items). dir-tree-html left with split4 on 10-25 (step 1). The Zed port is drafted: %TEMP%\\zed-fixtures-lib\\apply.ps1 -Fixtures <dir> [-Apply] checks the 3 files' exact current text first, then gives both fixtures packageDir ../../../../lib with |core- and spiral-, and ok uses + instead of +.. Gate: %TEMP%\\zed-fixtures-lib\\verify.ps1 applies it to a copy (with a lib junction at the same relative depth) and runs the installed dist\\spiral-zed.exe --probe: ok must exit 0, bad nonzero. That is one compiler process per fixture, so it runs after tibia's PR-28 block, then lands unstaged. After that, no product outside tmp needs the samples core.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_14 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 14u32, "2026-10-26T04:35Z", "main", "10-26 00:35 main: Zed fixtures on lib, GREEN (main-zed-fixtures-lib-verify, 00:19: the installed dist/spiral-zed.exe --probe gives ok exit 0 and bad exit 1 on the copy) and LANDED unstaged in apps/zed/fixtures (both package.spiproj files plus ok/main.spi). No product outside apps/compiler/tmp now needs the samples core; the 2 remaining packages are labs of open items.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_15 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 15u32, "2026-10-26T10:45Z", "main", "10-26 06:45 main: inventory (scratchpad tmp-scripts-inventory.ps1, one pass over every repo's tracked text files, backlog state excluded; %TEMP%\\tmp-scripts-inventory.tsv). apps/compiler/tmp holds 9,999 tracked files: samples 9,854, scripts 62, tests 37, formatter 22 (21 MB, fixtures), compiler 13 (the host), lanes 8, plus AGENTS.md, README.md and .gitignore. Of the 43 script files (.ps1/.py/.fsx): (A) 7 with readers outside tmp: build.ps1 (95 outside references, alphabet's documents build among them), env.ps1 (17, eoie's compiler contracts), install-dotnet.ps1 (7), test.ps1 (6, one CI workflow), test-rust-exports.ps1 (3), heavy.ps1 (3, agent-sync docs), probe.ps1 (2, a Cells test). (B) 13 read only from inside tmp (pair-drift, hopacsota-lint, projection-hash, fast-tier, upstream.py, ...). (C) 23 with no tracked reader. They are on-demand tools, not dead: test-blocks.ps1 ran tonight and rebuild-determinism.ps1 is a 5n repro file; their uses live in backlog notes and job scripts, which the scan doesn't count. So (C) is not a deletion list. Plan, in order, each step one gate: (1) a dangling check by stem over the backlog and the %TEMP%/scratchpad job scripts splits (C) into used tools and dead ones, and only the dead ones go; (2) (B) and the used (C) tools move with their callers into a non-tmp home; (3) (A) moves last, because its 125 outside references need one batch update plus a grep proof that no old path is left. The destination folder is a structure decision; I propose apps/compiler/scripts, the sibling of tmp, so that tmp can go away. Not started.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_16 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 16u32, "2026-10-26T11:36Z", "main", "10-26 07:36 main: step 1 of the n15 plan done; it finds no dead script. The scratchpad tmp-unread-check.ps1 was narrowed: the first version read every .ps1/.json under %TEMP% to depth 4 and was still silent after 40 min, so it was stopped (read-only, nothing to restore). It now reads top-level %TEMP% scripts, %TEMP% folders written in the last 14 days to depth 1 (2,752 scripts under 1,530 folders), session scratchpads to depth 3, and every kit job's argv. All 23 (C) scripts are used. Uses come from backlog notes and items (try.ps1 68, bench-native 11, test-blocks 7, rebuild-determinism 7, machine-watch 7, ...), from job scripts, and from job argv (try.ps1 39, capped-run 23, test-blocks 6). Positive control: test-blocks.ps1, run tonight, reads as used, with 7 backlog, 2 script and 6 job references. So the plan's delete step frees nothing, and every (B) and (C) tool moves in step 2 with its references. Step 2 is still a path decision: the destination folder (proposed apps/compiler/scripts), plus a batch update of the backlog text and the job scripts that name tmp/scripts. Most of the (C) uses are backlog notes, which are history, so step 2 only has to rewrite live callers: job scripts and tracked files.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_17 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 17u32, "2026-10-27T10:32Z", "main", "10-27 06:32 main: drift found by POLYGLOT-RETIRE's phase-2 census (10-27 06:3x): two functions are defined twice with different bodies inside tmp/scripts. Get-FileSha256 in env.ps1 and in test.ps1 (test.ps1 dot-sources env.ps1, so its own copy shadows the shared one), and Resolve-Results in ci-classify.ps1 and compare-runs.ps1. Both should become one definition in the scripts' shared module when the scripts move to their proper place.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_18 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 18u32, "2026-10-27T11:01Z", "main", "10-27 07:01 main: ownership settled (compiler 10-27 07:0x): the Get-FileSha256 and Resolve-Results dedup is the compiler team's, folded into its CCMR apply, which already holds anchored edits on env.ps1 and test.ps1. Keep env.ps1's Get-FileSha256 and drop test.ps1:367; move Resolve-Results into env.ps1, called by ci-classify.ps1 and compare-runs.ps1. This item's relocation of tmp/scripts is sequenced AFTER CCMR plus dedup lands and moves the files unchanged, so the two files have one writer at a time.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_19 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 19u32, "2026-10-27T16:54Z", "main", "10-27 12:54 main: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts census DONE (session scratchpad tmp-scripts-census.ps1, output TEMP tmp-scripts-census.tsv). The first version never finished: Get-ChildItem -Recurse walked kit's 5.5 GB .cache and the other skipped folders before filtering them, then ran one Contains per script per file, and after 43 CPU-minutes it hadn't finished the walk. Rewritten with a stack walk that prunes .git/target/.cache/deps/samples/_build and similar folders before entering them, plus one compiled alternation regex per file: 3,426 files from 12 repos plus TEMP's first-level scripts, walked in 9 s and scanned in 28 s. Result over the 45 scripts: ENTRY 4 (build, test, env, probe), LIVE-OUTSIDE 23, LIVE-INTERNAL 1, BACKLOG-ONLY 17, DEAD-CANDIDATE 0. Positive controls: results-path.ps1 LIVE-OUTSIDE (first caller TEMP matrix-bundle/accept.ps1), try.ps1 LIVE-OUTSIDE (11 outside callers), compare-runs.ps1 LIVE-OUTSIDE (16). The old control (candidate-gate*) no longer matches any script, so it checked nothing and was replaced. Caveat that changes the reading: BACKLOG-ONLY does not mean dead. bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1 is BACKLOG-ONLY (no file names it) yet runs right now as E1, launched from a kit job's argv; scripts launched by hand or by job never appear in a file corpus. So the retirement MOVES all 17 BACKLOG-ONLY scripts with their notes (bench-cells-vs-matrix, capped-run, ci-classify, cost-report, coverage-blockers, coverage-buckets, coverage-probe-queue, ebpf-dual-profile, ebpf-kernel-load, lib-usage-census, lib-usage-consumers, lib-usage-delete-unused.py, machine-watch, matrix-add-backend-to-groups.py, matrix-add-to-list.py, parser-corpus-gate, spiral-processes) and deletes none; nothing here is provably redundant. No file moved yet: scripts are moved only in a window when no job runs them (E1 runs bench-cells-vs-matrix now, and accept-3 queues test.ps1).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_20 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 20u32, "2026-10-27T18:37Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-27: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts PLACEMENT PLAN (n19 census, 45 scripts; plan only, no moves). \"You know that tree best\" ask.\n\nRECOMMENDED STRUCTURE (lowest churn): move the WHOLE tmp/scripts/ folder up one level to apps/compiler/scripts/ (sibling of the retiring tmp). Every intra-folder call is $PSScriptRoot-relative (entries dot-source env.ps1, build.ps1 calls hopacsota-lint/pair-drift/projection-hash, test.ps1 calls fast-tier/compare-runs, probe.ps1 calls profile-summary.py, etc.), so a WHOLE-FOLDER move leaves all of them unchanged -- only the ~125 OUTSIDE references update (main n15 step 3: one batch rewrite + a grep-proof no old path remains). This empties tmp/scripts and lets tmp retire. Keeps entries WITH their helpers (no entry/helper relative-path split).\nALTERNATIVE (main n2 step 4): hoist the 4 ENTRY to apps/compiler/ (public API at the compiler root), tools to apps/compiler/scripts/. Cleaner conceptual split BUT every entry<->tool relative path inside the scripts changes (build/test/probe <-> their helpers), adding churn + a second path-rewrite surface. RECOMMEND the whole-folder move unless the API separation is wanted.\n\nPER-CLASS DESTINATION (all -> apps/compiler/scripts/ under the recommended move):\n- ENTRY (4): build.ps1, test.ps1, env.ps1, probe.ps1 -> apps/compiler/scripts/ (recommended) OR apps/compiler/ (alternative).\n- LIVE-INTERNAL (1): profile-summary.py (probe.ps1's helper) -> apps/compiler/scripts/ (stays beside probe.ps1).\n- LIVE-OUTSIDE (23): .gitignore*, bench-native, bench-pair, ci-runs, compare-runs, export-check-fsharp, export-check-rust, fast-tier, heavy, hopacsota-g3, hopacsota-lint, install-dotnet, lib-usage-references, memory-cap, pair-drift, profile-thread.py, projection-hash, rebuild-determinism, results-path*, test-blocks, test-rust-exports, try, upstream.py -> apps/compiler/scripts/.\n- BACKLOG-ONLY (17, MOVE WITH NOTES, delete none -- n19 caveat: BACKLOG-ONLY != dead; bench-cells-vs-matrix runs now as E1 from job argv): bench-cells-vs-matrix, capped-run, ci-classify, cost-report, coverage-blockers, coverage-buckets, coverage-probe-queue, ebpf-dual-profile, ebpf-kernel-load, lib-usage-census, lib-usage-consumers, lib-usage-delete-unused.py, machine-watch, matrix-add-backend-to-groups.py, matrix-add-to-list.py, parser-corpus-gate, spiral-processes -> apps/compiler/scripts/.\n\nSPECIAL CASES (NOT a plain file move):\n- .gitignore (tmp/scripts/.gitignore): merge its rules into apps/compiler/.gitignore (or the repo root .gitignore); it is not a script and does not \"move\".\n- results-path.ps1: it currently holds the deduped Resolve-Results (ci-classify.ps1 + compare-runs.ps1 source it). main n18 proposes folding Resolve-Results into env.ps1 instead -> then results-path.ps1 is DELETED (both callers use env.ps1's). So: if n18 is taken, results-path.ps1 is absorbed, not moved; confirm with the dedup landing (the CCMR apply already holds the env.ps1/test.ps1 anchors but currently only the Get-FileSha256 dedup, not Resolve-Results -- reconcile before the move).\n- Get-FileSha256 dedup (n18): env.ps1 keeps it, test.ps1:367 drops its copy -- already folded into the staged CCMR apply.\n\nEOIE-VERB CANDIDATES (move to apps/compiler/scripts/ now; convert later as separate work, per n2 \"a method used by several sessions becomes an eoie verb, the script deleted once the verb ships\"): the generic cross-session tools -- memory-cap, capped-run, machine-watch, spiral-processes, lib-usage-census/consumers/delete-unused. Flag only; this move keeps them as scripts.\n\nSEQUENCING (hard constraints from n18/n19): (1) runs AFTER CCMR + the dedup land, so env.ps1/test.ps1 have one writer at a time, and the move then carries the files UNCHANGED. (2) Move only in a window when NO job runs these scripts (accept-3 runs test.ps1; E1 runs bench-cells-vs-matrix) -- a quiet exclusive window like the samples move. (3) Batch-update the ~125 outside references in the same edit + grep-proof no old apps/compiler/tmp/scripts path remains (positive control, dangling-check-by-stem). The 17 BACKLOG-ONLY scripts' backlog-note references are history (not rewritten live), but any LIVE caller (job scripts, tracked files, CI, AGENTS.md, README.md) is.\n\nNET: one new folder (apps/compiler/scripts), 43 files moved unchanged + .gitignore merged + results-path.ps1 absorbed-or-moved per n18; 0 deletions; tmp/scripts -> empty. Destination for tests/ (apps/compiler/tests, n2 step 3) and compiler/ host (apps/compiler/host, n2 step 2) are separate steps already ruled.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_21 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 21u32, "2026-10-27T18:40Z", "main", "10-27 14:40 main: Decision on n20's placement plan (main, technical call; it stays inside apps/compiler, so it isn't new top-level structure): (1) WHOLE-FOLDER move: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/ becomes apps/compiler/scripts/ as one unit. Every intra-folder call is $PSScriptRoot-relative and stays valid unchanged; only the ~125 outside references get the batch rewrite. Hoisting the 4 entries separately would also churn every entry-to-tool relative path. All 45 scripts move, the 17 BACKLOG-ONLY ones with their notes, and none are deleted. .gitignore merges into apps/compiler/.gitignore. (2) CORRECTION to n18: results-path.ps1 is NOT absorbed into env.ps1. env.ps1:2 sets Set-StrictMode -Version 3.0, and Resolve-Results' body (the Leaf plus nested single-flight-* search) trips StrictMode; that is why it lives in its own strictness-free file, sourced by ci-classify.ps1:7 and compare-runs.ps1:3 (and by main's TEMP matrix-bundle/compare-accept.ps1). It moves with the folder as a separate module. The Get-FileSha256 dedup into env.ps1 is unaffected, since that function is StrictMode-clean and already in the CCMR apply. (3) Sequencing unchanged: after CCMR and the dedup land, in a window when no job runs these scripts, with file contents unchanged by the move. Outside references in main's TEMP harnesses (matrix-bundle accept/compare-accept, rmd-wildcard, chain manifests) are part of the rewrite list. (4) The eoie-verb candidates n20 flags (memory-cap, capped-run, machine-watch, spiral-processes, lib-usage-*) are converted later, each as its own item.")
inl spiral_script_tests () = Task ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", "Prototype Spiral test blocks as script replacements: a .spi file whose filtered test cells do what a pwsh script does today (run steps, check outputs), driven by Cells/eoie with parameters to filter execution, so compiler tooling dogfoods Spiral and its backends instead of dotnet scripting; measure against one real tmp/scripts script (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "PWSH-FREE", "pwsh-free,cells,dogfood,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_script_tests () = Planning ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl spiral_notebook_files () = Task ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", "Spiral files as large subject notebooks: one file per subject organized by sections, tests next to the code they test (never all at the end), merge needlessly split lib/product files; check every repo for distanced tests and fix them; the 1k split stays only for compiled crates. Try first on the XSD files (one file instead of many underscored ones), spread destructively only if it works (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D5, 15u32, Active, "", "lib,structure,tests,main", "current", "current")
