inl note_of_spiral_macro_sigil_escapes_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES", 2u32, "2026-10-28T11:00Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-28 DONE: macro sigil escapes in the installed core 9FF1B708 -- spiral_compiler.fs:180668-180669 (respell @@/## <-> backslash-@/backslash-#, TokUnescapedChar carve-out; lexer already accepted both forms). Composed into 5n via macro-sigil-respell-apply.ps1 + blessed. Functional re-run delegated to the lanes vs installed; reopen on red.")
inl notebook_livemd_retire () = Task ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", "Retire the 21 tracked .livemd files in the 10-26 round (user: 'convert the remaining livemd files'): 3 export twins (spiral/apps/spiral/spiral.livemd 143 KB, spiral/apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.livemd, polyglot/apps/perf/Perf.livemd) make their .spi the source and drop the export step (spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1:27 --export-only); 11 F#-only or mostly F# (dice/lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp, alphabet/apps/hangul/hangul, polyglot apps/parser x2 and lib/fsharp x8) are ported to Spiral .spi or deleted, per file by whether anything still builds or reads them (dangling check by stem first); 5 with no Spiral (spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral, apps/lisp/lisp, polyglot examples/elixir/exercism, polyglot scripts/build, init) become .exs/.ps1 or stay, by the same reader check", Story, P0, D3, 90u32, Active, "SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX", "team:main,notebooks,livemd,migration,edition3", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_notebook_livemd_retire () = Planning ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_1 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: the three twins must flip before the respell runs, or the next export writes '.x' and word keywords back over the migrated .spi; alphabet mirrors dice, so dice_fsharp and hangul move together.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_2 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-26T07:21Z", "main", "10-26 03:21 main: first twin drafted: spiral/apps/spiral/spiral.livemd. Both twins are already in symbols (0 word line-starts, 221 ':=' lines each), so the keyword class is safe; the flip protects the coming '::' and @@/## classes. The livemd-only lines are Livebook wrapping, and its smart-cell attrs hold a JSON copy of every cell's source, so respelling the livemd in place would need both copies changed: flip instead. %TEMP%\\livemd-flip-spiral\\apply.ps1 (dry run clean, 11 anchored edits, each once): apps/spiral/build.ps1 drops the --export-only pre-build and its $SkipPreBuild param; polyglot scripts/init.ps1 stops passing -SkipPreBuild 1 (the only caller); README.md links spiral.spi.html (the Tasks precedent, NOTEBOOKS-TO-SPI-SIBLINGS n3); lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR/promote.ps1 routes by an anchored edit of spiral.spi in symbols (? / |? / |: () dispatch; every branch exits, so it equals the old run of ifs; its old words anchor no longer matched the respelled livemd, so promote was already broken); router_swap.py writes spiral.spi ('/// # spiral' + router.spi) instead of building a livemd, and its json import and builders go. Then spiral.livemd is deleted. Deletion rule, written first: only if exporting today's livemd reproduces the tracked spiral.spi byte-identically (LF-normalized), so nothing is lost. Proof job-1792999203047-main-livemd-flip-proof. Not proven here: the new dispatch compiles. SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR's promote build proves it at its next -Apply. Next twins: spiral_wasm.livemd, then polyglot Perf.livemd (F# cells, per-file reader check).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_3 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:33Z", "main", "10-26 03:33 main: twins 1 and 2 flipped in the working tree (unstaged): spiral.livemd (proof GREEN, export == spiral.spi DA60B76F; it showed MD because the user had staged an earlier version, which the index keeps, while the working tree's later heal of the $'$\"...\"' literals survives in spiral.spi) and spiral_wasm.livemd (proof GREEN, F6CDF55D; apps/wasm/build.ps1 now runs spiral_wasm.spi as the notebook, --output-path spiral_wasm.spi.ipynb, and the fast path needs no export). Twin 3, polyglot Perf.livemd: the proof was RED by its rule, and correctly so. Code lines (158) and headings (14) are identical, but the livemd holds 70 more /// result-table rows than Perf.spi (livemd committed 10-25 14:35, the .spi 00:25). Rule tightened, not loosened: the flipped Perf.spi is the livemd's own export (table padding collapsed to single spaces, the compact form Perf.spi already uses; 2 table rows stay over 120 because markdown rows can't wrap), guarded by the livemd hash 5CBC199E. Then the four F#-only headings (TestCaseResult, run, runAll at the top and hasAnyPairCloseToEachotherTests at EOF) go with the 13 F# cells. No workflow or script runs apps/perf/build.ps1. Waiting on the by-stem reader check over all repos (scratchpad livemd-reader-check.ps1 -> %TEMP%\\livemd-readers.txt) before the apply. That same check decides the 13 F#-only files.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_4 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-26T08:10Z", "main", "10-26 04:10 main: per-file decisions from the by-stem reader check (scratchpad livemd-reader-check.ps1, one pass over 18,950 tracked text files in 54 repos, %TEMP%\\livemd-readers.txt). Flipped (unstaged): spiral.livemd, spiral_wasm.livemd, polyglot Perf.livemd (its only readers, the README and its build.ps1, are retargeted; Perf.spi is now the livemd's own export, so the newer result tables are kept; 13 F# cells retire). Deleted: polyglot lib/fsharp/NotebooksHtml.livemd (a 7-line .NET Interactive formatter snippet, not in lib/fsharp/build.ps1's notebook list, 0 readers by stem or name). Kept by readers: dice_fsharp.livemd and hangul.livemd are the livemd round-trip corpus of spiral/apps/cells/test/spiral/document_test.exs (:213/:216/:348/:499); the polyglot F# cluster (Async, AsyncSeq, Common, CommonFSharp, FileSystem, Runtime, Notebooks, Testing, apps/parser JsonParser + Parser) is live in dice's build (dice/scripts/build.ps1 -> lib/fsharp/build.ps1; dice/scripts/init.ps1:28 runs polyglot/apps/parser/build.ps1), with Common.fs also read by mechahaze-album1 and FileSystem.fs by FsClr.fsproj. Retiring it means first porting dice's F# lib to Spiral, a separate item. No Spiral to convert, so they stay: spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd (the Cells README's sample), polyglot scripts build/init.livemd (pwsh notebooks their .ps1 runs), i574n.github scripts/workflow.livemd (read by workflow.ps1), polyglot examples/elixir/exercism.livemd. Still to decide: spiral apps/lisp/lisp.livemd (0 readers, 2 Spiral cells).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_5 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-26T08:12Z", "main", "10-26 04:12 main: last open file decided: spiral apps/lisp/lisp.livemd stays. Its one cell equals apps/lisp/membership_short.spl minus that file's comment line, and apps/lisp/build.ps1 already builds and runs the .spl files. But its prose is the only description of the ///! lisp Cells feature, and the cell holds Lisp forms, not Spiral spelling, so the respell and '::' classes can't touch it. Nothing in the round needs it changed. All 21 files are decided: 3 twins flipped, 1 orphan deleted, the rest kept by readers or as non-Spiral notebooks (n4). Open follow-up outside this item: the polyglot/dice F# cluster can only retire after dice's F# lib is ported to Spiral.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_6 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-26T18:38Z", "main", "10-26 14:38 main: 10-26 14:3x main: perf-flip-rerun-2 RED (job finished 1x:xx) read in full. The cause is not the flip's build retarget: the build stopped at the Cells parse gate, 'FatalError: The package of main has blocks that fail to tokenize or parse ... Perf.spi:393'. Line 393 is a bare '()' at column 0, the carried-over OUTPUT of the preceding 'rotate_strings_tests ()' code cell; that cell itself parses as an executable top-level cell, and only 393 is flagged. It is already in HEAD (lines 399/401), so the livemd era rendered it as a cell output, and the .spi notebook reads it as code. Fix: TEMP livemd-flip-builds/perf-output-cell.ps1 removes exactly that line (anchored, count 1, 0 bare unit lines left; dry run passes on the live file). The proof is the consumer build itself: perf-fix-run.ps1 backs up Perf.spi, applies the fix, and runs perf-only.ps1 (polyglot apps/perf/build.ps1 through Cells). Rule, written before the run: GREEN iff the build exits 0, the .spi stays byte-identical, and no livemd comes back; the fix is then kept unstaged. Otherwise Perf.spi is restored from the backup and verified by hash. Queued in the post-rename requeue (main-perf-output-cell-fix), since kit's pause would stop it now. Flip-tool follow-up: the livemd-to-.spi converter should carry a code cell's rendered output as a /// comment, never as code (the same shape can recur in other flipped notebooks; grep for '^\\(\\)$' lines in flipped .spi files).")
