inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: round scope EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION note 32; X-compliance layers SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX notes 10-11. Classes in order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), lexer respells (keywords, ::, Cons sugar, macro sigils), macro wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP lib helpers), formatter, 280 split (EDITION3-280-SPLIT); one identical-output gate per class.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-26T06:51Z", "tibia-lane", "06:51Z Tibia part started, rule written before any tree edit. About 15 queued tibia slices (slices-b and slices-c, the cells-apps snapshot, the client heal) are guarded by exact file hashes, so edition-3 tree edits land after that queue and are drafted against the post-queue state, never under it. Live inventory (src and apps, target/deps excluded): (1) Cons ( : 10 rows in the tree, not 17 (recent lands removed the rest); the queued canary slices already convert 8 (ground_trace 6, lead_trace 2) to list sugar, and offscreen's 2 go with its slice (POSTABLE note 43). (2) Line-start word keywords: 4; client.spi:58 (inl code = ...) vanishes with the queued client heal, and lua.spi:21/24/35 sit in the file the queued random lands touch, so they convert right after those land. (3) if/then/else/match/with/fun outside strings and host macros: 0 in tibia code; the 46 must count words inside host macros (Lua 'if ... then' text), which are host text, not Spiral keywords. (4) Manifests: 7 package.spiproj (apps arena, canary, host, map, offscreen, predict; src). The converter is not in the installed compiler: 'format --manifest toml' on a scratch copy exits 0 and writes nothing. This class waits for EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML's install, then runs over the 7 with read-back. (5) '::' and '@@/##' wait for the compiler's respell pairs, as planned. (6) Formatter and 280-split: the postable slices queued in slices-c cover most of tibia's split (POSTABLE notes 33-46). Gate per class as the item says: compiled Lua/C/WGSL identical, tibia tests, x-compat 0.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:01Z", "tibia-lane", "07:01Z Raw !!!! class (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP's tibia share): all 23 sit in src/terrain.spi (ArrayCreate 6, ArrayIndex 7, ArrayIndexSet 10). lib had index_base but no create or set wrapper for array_base (am'.init fills element i with i, so it isn't a drop-in for an unfilled array; array_dim.set needs dim-typed arrays). New lib slice, scratch lib-array-base/lib-array-base.ps1: am'.create_base n = !!!!ArrayCreate(`el, n) and am'.set_base ar i v = !!!!ArrayIndexSet(ar, i, v), beside index_base. The raw op lives only inside lib, as in array_dim.set. Consumer-path proof against the patched lib copy: a probe creates a u32 array of 4, sets it to 7/11/13/17 and sums it through index_base; it prints 'total 48' on Rust (rustc) and on C (gcc). Queued: gate-then-land LIB-ARRAY-BASE (-Files am') in tibia-serial-heals. Terrain conversion is ready: scratch lib-array-base/terrain-array-wrappers.ps1, a paren-aware converter (balanced arguments, index argument order swapped, a read in argument position wrapped in parentheses) turns all 23 into wrapper calls with 0 raw ops left and 0 lines over 120. It applies on top of the terrain slice, which is held for the geometry fix, after LIB-ARRAY-BASE lands, gated by the round's rule: terrain's compiled C/WGSL identical before and after, plus terrain tests.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:32Z", "tibia-lane", "GROOM 10-28 06:4x: Planned -> Blocked. All three deps are unfinished compiler features: SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX (Active 15%), SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES (Planned 0%), SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT (Planned 0%), all owned by the compiler side. Resume when they land: the inventory (notes 1-2) and the terrain !!!! conversion through am'.create_base/set_base are drafted.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-28T11:02Z", "tibia-lane", "10-28 07:1x Blocked -> Planned. Compiler confirmed in source (relayed by main at 07:0x) that all three blockers were already in the installed compiler (core 9FF1B708, via the 5n composite) and closed them Done: SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT, SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES. Next: validate against the installed compiler on tibia (box or node, outside 08:30-09:30), starting from the drafted inventory (notes 1-2: the remaining Cons sugar, line-start keywords, terrain's 23 raw !!!! via am'.create_base/set_base). Lib writes go in today's land windows (14:00-16:00, 20:00-21:00). Any red row goes back to compiler.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-28T11:04Z", "tibia-lane", "11:04Z INVENTORY refreshed 10-28 07:1x on the live tibia tree (src + apps, target/deps excluded; case-sensitive):\n(1) Nil -> [] list sugar: 14 rows. ground_trace 4, lead_trace 2, arena_host 5, character 1, scenario 2. 'Cons (' is already 0.\n(2) Raw !!!!: 4 rows. terrain.spi:1401-1405 holds the three wrappers base_create/base_read/base_write (ArrayCreate/ArrayIndex/ArrayIndexSet, 23 call sites). They become am'.create_base/index_base/set_base, which LIB-ARRAY-BASE landed in lib (am'.spi:29-36). hunting_pack.spi:1771 !!!!BackendSwitch is kept on purpose: the r9 knight_turn split needs its own Wgsl key (gpu-code-split rule), which lib's backend_switch doesn't expose.\n(3) Line-start word keywords: 0. if/match/fun outside host text: 0 (note 1).\n(4) spiral.toml: 0 of 7 package.spiproj converted. That's the main edit and needs the installed compiler's spiral.toml reader.\n(5) Then the formatter, the 280-weight check (tibia is already 0 over) and the gates: compiled Lua/C/WGSL identical per class, tibia tests, x-compat 0 findings.\nOrder: after TIBIA-PARK (the 08:30 executor block, then K4 at 10:00 on the current tree). apps/host files (arena_host, character, scenario) feed the 08:30 block and aren't touched before it. Proof: a node src gate plus Lua/C/WGSL output identity per module against pre-edit builds; any red row goes to compiler.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-28T11:07Z", "tibia-lane", "11:07Z spiral.toml step, trialled 10-28 07:2x on a scratch copy of tibia's 7 manifests: 'SpiralCompiler format --manifest toml <dir>' wrote all 7 (apps/arena, canary, host, map, offscreen, predict and src), each passing the converter's read-back check. Example: apps/canary -> edition = 3 / packageDir = '../../deps/spiral/lib' / packages = ['|core-', 'spiral-'] / modules = '''canary ground_trace lead_trace'''.\nPrecedence trap found before the tree edit. The compiler resolves spiral.toml FIRST when both files exist (spiproj_suffix, spiral_compiler.fs:184542). EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML keeps the spiproj beside it on purpose, and Cells still reads package.spiproj directly (memo.ex 290/348/582, mounts.ex 62/163). So both files must stay in sync, and every script that rewrites package.spiproj text must rewrite spiral.toml too, or the compiler silently ignores its edit. In tibia that's scripts/predict.ps1:21-22 (packageDir -> absolute lib path; the module list gains a second entry for -Module sweep), plus my scratch runners (node-kit/predict-node.ps1, live-exec/stage.ps1) and the old push-src copy. Plan: the converter writes the 7 files; predict.ps1 patches both manifests (in spiral.toml, packageDir = '...' and a line added inside the modules ''' block); the proof includes a predict run whose module list and packageDir both take effect (sweep compiles via -Module sweep).")
