inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-26T06:55Z", "eoie", "02:55 eoie: inventory remeasured on the working tree (the KIT-RENAME release already applied the edition-3 respell to 843 files tonight; the round's counts came from git HEAD at 01:52). Scripts: kit scratch clean\\respell\\edition3-left.ps1, keyword-sample.ps1, keyword-sample2.ps1.\n- Line-start keywords: 3,112 by the round's regex, but 2,927 of them are Rust 'let' inside multi-line host macro blocks, not Spiral and out of scope for a respell (they leave with GRANULAR-HEAL host-block migration). Of the 185 real inl/union/type lines: 85 are fixture text inside triple-quoted strings (they mimic agile state rows; leave them); about 100 are real Spiral the respell skipped: every one is a binding whose right side opens a triple-quoted string (inl kinds = triple-quote, inl emit_runtime () : () = rust_global triple-quote). A respell gap, reported on SPIRAL-FORMATTER.\n- Flow keywords: 2,662 by a rough regex, likely inflated the same way (Rust if/match in host blocks); recount with macro text excluded before planning.\n- Cons ( : 119. Raw !!!! : 767. Lines over 120: 2,332. Comment lines: 5. package.spiproj: 431, spiral.toml: 0.\nSequencing: all classes start after KIT-RENAME publishes (eoie feature freeze; the tree is under the release lease now). Order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), the ~100 respell-gap sites once the respell handles them, Cons sugar, !!!! wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP), formatter; each class through the identical-output gate (rsIntended plus the regen manifest, proven on the worker node first).")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:05Z", "eoie", "03:05 eoie: Cons class ready. The existing converter (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar.ps1, balanced-paren aware, rewrites Cons (a, b) as a :: b) dry-ran on a copy of the renamed and respelled tree: 113 sites in 19 files across 15 packages (kit_repo_affected 36, kit_log_sequences 21, kit_mirror 17, kit_env_pins 9, kit_do_verbs 8, ...), 0 skipped, 0 left, 0 doubled parens. Gate: list sugar is syntax for the same constructor, so every touched crate must regenerate byte-identical. Node proof script ready (clean\\respell\\node-sugar.ps1: convert on a mirror, regen the touched crates, compare every .rs hash before and after; verdict 'codegen-neutral' only at 0 changed). It runs when the node's strict notebook chain finishes (node at 100% CPU now), and the class lands right after KIT-RENAME publishes.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-26T07:08Z", "eoie", "03:08 eoie: keyword class recounted with macro bodies, triple-quoted strings and plain strings stripped (kit scratch clean\\respell\\keyword-recount.ps1): line-start word keywords 106 (the respell-gap bindings, SPIRAL-FORMATTER note 85), flow keywords 9 (then 3, if 3, with 3). So eoie's real keyword work is about 115 sites, not the round inventory's 3,112 plus 3,319; the rest was Rust inside host macros and string fixtures. The class waits only on the respell handling bindings whose right side opens a triple-quoted string.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_5 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-26T07:28Z", "eoie", "03:28 eoie: the Cons class's node proof caught a converter bug: 13 of 14 touched crates regenerated, but kit_crate_gate/gate.spi:44 did not type-check (Got: list string, Expected: string). 'Cons (dir </> name, acc)' had become 'dir </> name :: acc', which parses as dir </> (name :: acc) because the custom operator binds looser than ::. Fixed: the converter parenthesizes a head with any top-level infix operator, and a tail with any operator other than :: (right-associative, so chains stay bare). Test 9/9 (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar-test.ps1: the path operator, ++#, ++ in the tail, a negative literal, a comma in a string, glued member access, a pattern). Proof rerunning on the node (job kit-sugar-proof-3).")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_6 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-26T07:33Z", "eoie", "03:33 eoie: Cons class PROVEN codegen-neutral on the worker node. With the precedence-fixed converter (heads with a top-level infix operator and tails with an operator other than :: get parens; test 9/9), all 113 Cons ( sites in 19 files were converted on a mirror of the renamed tree, the 14 touched crates regenerated (ok), and 0 of 260 generated .rs changed. The class is ready to land right after KIT-RENAME publishes: run clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar.ps1 -Root src -Apply, then the identical-manifest check.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_7 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-26T08:21Z", "eoie", "04:21 eoie: status of the two waiting classes. The compiler lane's edition-3 lexer core (9E1F72AB) built clean on the worker node at about 04:1x (single-flight Debug, 0 errors): the :: member access, the macro sigil respell (@@ and ##) and the ZWSP strip/remap all compile; behavioral probes are next on their side. When their respell pairs land (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT), eoie's '.x to ::x' and sigil classes run through the same identical-output gate as the Cons class: convert on a node mirror, regenerate the touched crates, require 0 changed generated .rs. Ready now (after KIT-RENAME lands): Cons (proven), the Global wrapper cleanup with its census probe (drafted, gate written), stop_cli and harness fixes (node proof running). Waiting: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter, main), the ~106 keyword sites (SPIRAL-FORMATTER note 85 respell gap).")
inl lib_edition3_round () = Task ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", "spiral repo (lib/spiral, apps, samples) plus dice, alphabet, polyglot, blog, dir-tree-html: run the 10-26 edition-3 round in one review: spiral.toml for 1,251 + 9 package.spiproj (the upstream core keeps package.spiproj), member access .x -> ::x, word keywords (28,318 line-start, 14,427 if/match in spiral), Cons ( -> :: sugar (spiral 230, blog 55), macro sigils @@/##, raw !!!! -> lib wrappers (spiral 3,580, polyglot 15, dir-tree-html 8, dice 4), formatter (136 lines > 120, 75 trailing-space lines), 280-weight split; gates: Cells --gate, matrix, generated code identical per class, x-compat 0 findings", Story, P0, D5, 0u32, Planned, "SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX,SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES,SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", "team:main,lib,edition3,migration,x-compat", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_edition3_round () = Planning ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", Minutes 720u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_edition3_round_1 () = Note ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: round scope EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION note 32; X-compliance layers SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX notes 10-11. Classes in order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), lexer respells (keywords, ::, Cons sugar, macro sigils), macro wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP lib helpers), formatter, 280 split (EDITION3-280-SPLIT); one identical-output gate per class.")
inl note_of_lib_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-26T07:21Z", "main", "10-26 03:21 main: census before starting (scratchpad word-keyword-census.ps1, tracked .spi/.spir, line-start inl/let/type/union/nominal/open/prototype/instance/and). spiral 26,160 line-start words, of which apps/compiler/tmp/samples holds 26,015 (1,249 files, 1,224 sample manifests, mega_* 776 files) and apps/compiler/tmp/formatter 90 (13 fixtures, kept as written: they test word input). lib/spiral's 46 and apps/cells' 9 are host text (Gleam 'let' inside $'...' in process.spi, trace.spi, convert.spi, ...), not Spiral: lib and apps were respelled 10-24/25 (n14). dice 0, blog 0, alphabet 1, polyglot 2, dir-tree-html 1: the same host-text kind. So main's keyword class is the matrix sample corpus. Plan with rules written before running: (1) dry run of the shared tool (%TEMP%\\edition3-spread\\respell-repo.ps1) over copies with the installed compiler, queued as job-1792998563870-main-edition3-samples-dry; GREEN = 0 errors and 0 words round-trip differences. (2) Apply, then the full matrix: every sample's generated outputs byte-identical to the accepted ones. The one allowed difference is a diagnostic sample whose only change is a column or excerpt on a respelled line (inl -> := moves columns; the dry run counts such lines). Those are re-accepted row by row after review, never in bulk. (3) Draft-held files are excluded from any batch: %TEMP%\\respell-exclusions.tsv (scratchpad pending-draft-files.ps1 derives it from live jobs' apply scripts), plus fiscal's xsd*/xml/xpath* by hand until fiscal reports them landed. Also lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR/router.spi is still in words and must be respelled before router_swap.py writes it into apps/spiral/spiral.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-26T10:25Z", "main", "10-26 06:25 main: samples respell dry run GREEN (job-1792998563870, 06:06): the shared tool (edition3-spread\\respell-repo.ps1, installed compiler) respelled 1,248 sample files on copies with 0 errors and 0 words round-trip differences, and the installed formatter normalizes 9 more on top (5 of them mega roots), 1,257 files in all. 54,132 changed lines change length, so any diagnostic that cites a column after them moves; that's the expected class of matrix difference, re-accepted row by row. Order rule: the apply waits until the 5n review finishes. The review reads apps/compiler/tmp/samples, and respelling its inputs mid-review would mix two changes in one verdict. After 5n: apply (originals stay in %TEMP%\\respell-repo\\compiler-samples\\original), then a full -Suite all -Native matrix whose outputs must be byte-identical except those column diagnostics. Copies are at %TEMP%\\respell-repo\\compiler-samples. Also landed 06:08: LIB-LIST-SUGAR-REST-2 (listm'.spi C6FA3415, process.spi 72A16CF8).")
inl note_of_lib_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-26T17:24Z", "main", "10-26 13:24 main: Manual respell exclusions from fiscal (13:2x). pending-draft-files.ps1 can't see these: it rebuilds respell-exclusions.tsv from live local job argv, and these are frozen landings waiting on gates or node jobs. Exclude each from any respell batch until fiscal reports it landed:\nlib/spiral: xsd.spi, xsd_resolve.spi, json_schema.spi, xsd_emit.spi, xsd_regex.spi, xsd_certificate.spi (new), package.spiproj (XSD typed release; waits on resume2, node job-1793029719170); xsd_constraints.spi (R7+R8, after the release); xpath.spi, xpath_eval.spi, schematron_run.spi (S2d, node check job-1793034540282); schematron.spi, decimal.spi, float_text.spi, listm'.spi, reflection.spi, xml.spi (LIB-TARGET-GAP layout); date_time.spi (stopwatch_elapsed_microseconds draft).\napps/cells: spi/document.spi, spi/directives.spi, lib/spiral/cells/document.ex, test/spiral/document_test.exs (fidelity land job-1793033954641; keep_docs follows).\nfiscal: src/generator.spi, src/corpus_checks.spi.\nMain's own pending lib drafts get the same treatment until landed: listm'.spi (job-1793030321888), convert.spi (job-1793030466889), am'.spi (job-1793030605331), sm'.spi (job-1793027588823), parsing.spi (job-1793034801882), runtime.spi (job-1793035301036), unicode.spi (job-1793020861797), plus the nil-literal batch's 10 files (job-1793022977380). Order: land first, then respell. A gap to fix: the tsv generator should also read pending landings from node job argv and from frozen land manifests, not only live local jobs (filed as a follow-up on this item).")
