inl eoie_table_empty_cells () = Task ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", "one rule for empty and non-numeric cells in numeric where comparisons, shared by table query, table test and the measured path; settled with tibia (its 10-24 report: an empty cell passes delay<=1000 in table query), then applied to every path with a flag if both readings are needed", Story, P1, D3, 80u32, Active, "LIB-TEXT-ORDER,LIB-TRY-PARSE-F64", "kit,table,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_table_empty_cells () = Planning ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_1 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 1u32, "2026-10-26T12:28Z", "eoie", "08:28 eoie: opened from the rename preflight. Release-train stage S2 (10-24) meant 'table query --where numeric comparisons fail on cells that are not numbers' (tibia's report), but its program changed only cell_passes, which table test uses (rows_kept), not the host closure plain table query filters with. So tibia's query case is still unfixed, and table test silently flipped against EOIE-TABLE-TEST-WHERE #1 (10-21: foreign_potions<=0 keeps empty cells as tibia expects). table_test_cli caught it: n=a 1 against the expected n=a 2 (candidate and control both; installed eoie gives a 2). Decided for the release: revert S2's cell_passes change (scratch clean\\kit-rename\\table-empty-cells-revert.do), keeping the test block as documentation of the installed behaviour (an empty cell compares as text). Next, with tibia: pick one rule (likely: non-numeric cells fail numeric comparisons everywhere, with --keep-empty for the potions case), apply it to query_rows, rows_kept and measures in one change, and update both CLI notebooks.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_2 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 2u32, "2026-10-26T12:30Z", "eoie", "08:30 eoie: tibia answered (10-26 08:3x). The rule fits: every one of its table query filters (at<200, run>1, run>2, gated>0, delay<=1000) wants an empty cell to FAIL; its table test calls take no --where; the 10-21 foreign_potions<=0 ask has no caller left (live/ retired 10-25), so --keep-empty needs no caller and is optional. Revert for the release accepted. Rule for the follow-up, settled: a non-numeric or empty cell fails every numeric comparison (>, >=, <, <=) in table query's plain path (query_rows host closure), table test (cell_passes via rows_kept) and the measured path, in one change; = and != stay text comparisons; table_test_cli's where fixture gets a second kept a row so its n stays meaningful, and table_cli gains an empty-cell case for delay<=1000.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_3 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 3u32, "2026-10-26T22:54Z", "tibia-lane", "22:54Z tibia design for the settled rule, written before drafting (read from eoie src at 19:0x local; the release holds the tree lease, so nothing is edited there).\n\nSites: there are three comparison stacks, not one.\n(a) table.spi query_rows: one host block. Its own compare closure falls back to text order for non-numbers.\n(b) table.spi cell_passes, used through rows_kept by table test and analysis: numbers_ordered, then texts_ordered.\n(c) kit_table_measures/measures.spi: a second copy of the whole stack (compare union, filters_from, row_passes, ordered with partial_cmp and a text fallback).\n\nAGENTS.md says touching a legacy function migrates it, so (a) moves to Spiral rather than getting a patched closure.\n\nPlan, in one change: a new module kit_table_query/wheres.spi holds where_op, where_op_of, the clause split, the single cell_passes (rule: >, >=, <, <= hold only when both sides parse as finite numbers; = and != stay text) and filters/filters_from/row_passes. table.spi (rows_kept and the migrated plain query) and measures.spi import it, and measures' copy is deleted.\n\nBehaviour kept byte-identical: header line, projection, limit, the 'kit table query ok total= matched= [groups=] shown=' lines, --quiet, the unknown-columns text and its order (filters, cols, group), and the read-error text (check kit_table_text::kit_table_problem against the old '{path}: {error}').\n\nKnown deltas, to be stated in the change:\n- A ragged row's missing cell now reads as \"\" in plain query, as table test already does. Before, every filter failed on it; now only = against a non-empty value and the numeric operators fail.\n- A no-operator clause can't reach any path: option parsing rejects it ('--where expects col=value').\n\nBlocker found: grouped output sorts by count descending, then value ascending. Spiral has no string ordering (`<` on strings is ETY-ConstraintError; tibia hit it today in a test), and lib's only code-point order is private to xpath_eval (text_order_from). So a lib slice comes first: a general text_order (a, b) : i32, either moved out of xpath_eval or added as a backend_switch with Rust str::cmp, plus a lib test.\n\nTests: table.spi's documented test becomes 'an empty or text cell fails every numeric comparison', expecting (!-, !-, !-, !+, !-) on (\"\" <= 1000, \"\" < 1001, \"\" > 1000, 999 <= 1000, abc < abd). table_cli gains latency_ms<=50000 on runs.tsv (row 2's latency is empty): matched=1, where the installed binary gives matched=2. table_test_cli's where fixture gets a second kept row.\n\nProof path: build the candidate kit on the remote kit worker node from a src copy (copy-eoie-src-only), run table_cli and table_test_cli against it, and hand the anchored apply script to the eoie lane after the release.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_4 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 4u32, "2026-10-26T23:44Z", "tibia-lane", "23:44Z tibia, design addendum (19:4x local).\nkit confirmed nothing of theirs has this in flight. The apply script anchors on the tree after kit's land-post-rename slices (several touch kit_table_query) and builds on the quoted-CSV fix; kit messages \"slices landed\".\n\nPrerequisites found while drafting the wheres module (lib-first per AGENTS.md: the touched host one-liners migrate to lib):\n1. LIB-TEXT-ORDER, for grouped output's value order: proven, gating as job-1793057877440.\n2. An optional float parse, for cell_passes' numeric test. No lib function returns option f64: float_native.parse assumes valid text, and convert.try_convert parses integers only. The Rust arm must match today's trim().parse::<f64>().ok(), including inf/NaN, which parse as numbers (NaN then fails every comparison, as now). Shape: float_native.try_parse_f64 (s : string) : option f64, a backend_switch with Rust one-call plus Some/None in Spiral, and a rust test over \"12.5\", \" 3 \", \"\", \"abc\", \"inf\".\n3. The clause split (operator_at, operator_width) and substrings come from sm' (index_of, substring), not host macros.\n\nUnchanged: --where without an operator is rejected at option parsing, so the paths' differing no-operator handling never matters. Order of work: lib slices 1-2 gate, then the eoie change against the post-slice tree, proven by table_cli and table_test_cli run against a candidate kit built on the node.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_5 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 5u32, "2026-10-27T00:17Z", "tibia-lane", "00:17Z tibia: code drafted in scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/draft. It is unproven, waits for kit's \"slices landed\", and needs the rebase anchors.\n- wheres.spi (new module, listed before table in kit_table_query's spiproj): where_op, the clause split over sm' (operator_from as a join point, operator_width, clause_of returning option clause), and cell_passes. The ordered ops compare float_native.try_parse_f64 results directly, and a non-number on either side fails. There is a NaN fix in passing: query_rows made every NaN comparison false, but cell_passes mapped NaN to 'equal' so <= passed; one rule now. Two rust tests, then filters/filters_from/row_passes.\n- plain-query.spi (replaces query_rows): projection (all columns or named, missing names appended in order), row_text, listed_rows counting total/matched/shown under below_limit, and grouped counting (key_rows counts plus a first-seen list, ranked by count descending then xml.text_order ascending, the same order as the old BTreeMap sort by byte).\nOpen before the rebase:\n(1) a cells.spi boundary primitive row_width (one host call) for all-columns projection;\n(2) whether ?= takes 'when' guards, or printed_groups needs an if;\n(3) for groups, matched = the sum of counts;\n(4) check that kit_table_problem's text equals the old '{path}: {error}', so 'kit error: table ...' is byte-identical;\n(5) measures.spi drops its compare/filters copy and imports wheres;\n(6) re-lay the three lines over 120 at the rebase.\nProof: table_cli and table_test_cli on a candidate kit built on the node, plus the new empty-cell case (latency_ms<=50000 gives matched=1).")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_6 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 6u32, "2026-10-27T00:55Z", "tibia-lane", "00:55Z tibia: the draft is proven behaviourally before the rebase (scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/probe; compiler only, no kit build, done during kit's rename pause).\nThe probe package holds a lib copy with LIB-TEXT-ORDER and LIB-TRY-PARSE-F64 applied, copies of rust_std_string, union_reflection, query.spi and cells.spi (plus the new row_width primitive), the draft wheres.spi and plain.spi, and two probe mains, compiled to Rust and built with rustc. kit_table_text is stubbed with a plain file read.\n- wheres: printed '11 00 11 latency_ms|50000'. Numeric ops hold on numbers; empty and text cells fail <= and <; = and != stay text; the clause split works. Under the old text-fallback rule the middle pair would print 11.\n- plain query on table_cli's runs.tsv:\n  - latency_ms<=50000 with cols variant,latency_ms prints 'fast<TAB>40000', group '1<TAB>fast', matched=1 (the empty latency now fails; the installed binary gives matched=2).\n  - With all columns, '3<TAB>fast<TAB>9<TAB>40000'.\n  - With no filter, 4 rows, groups '3 fast' then '1 base', matched=4.\n  - Tie fixture b,z,a,z,B: groups '2 z', then '1 B', '1 a', '1 b', i.e. byte order like the old BTreeMap sort.\n- Partial evaluation pruned the all-columns branch while cols was a literal. Reading cols from the environment forced it in, and the generated Rust contains row_width.\nTop-level plain_query is now drafted (header, 'kit table query ok' lines with and without groups, unknown-columns error, --quiet) and run through query-probe.ps1 on table_cli's assertions. All match byte for byte: 'variant TAB retries / fast 5 / fast 9 / total=4 matched=2 shown=2'; variant!=base grouped gives matched=3; group variant gives 'count TAB variant / 3 fast / 1 base / total=4 matched=4 groups=2 shown=2'; '--cols nope' gives 'kit error: table unknown columns: nope (header: timestamp,variant,retries,latency_ms)' exit 2; --quiet hides the summary. New: latency_ms<=50000 gives matched=1. measures.spi with its private compare/filters/row_passes stack deleted and wheres imported (measures-probe.ps1) matches table_cli's measured rows byte for byte: '3 fast 5.333 46120 3.512 92240' and '1 base 4 60000 0 60000'; retries>=4 gives '2 fast 7' and '1 base 4'. New: latency_ms<=50000 with --count gives '1 fast 1', matched=1. Its read errors already go through table_read and rejected, like plain_query. Read errors: kit_table_text's table_problem only checks existence ('{path}: file not found', with its own rust test), while old query_rows printed the OS error text ('{path}: The system cannot find the file specified. (os error 2)'). Plain query now shares table_problem with the measured path and table test: a stated delta that no CLI notebook pins. Still open: then the rebase onto kit's post-slice tree and the CLI notebooks on a candidate kit.\nCLI notebook edits drafted (draft/cli-test-edits.ps1; anchors match once on today's tree, re-check after the rebase). table_test_cli's where fixture gains 'a 13 0 4', so errors<=0 keeps 'n=a 2, b 2' through a numeric row; the installed binary would show n=a 3 there, because the empty cell compares as text. Its passed-metric case becomes 'n=a 4 (3 numeric), b 3'. table_cli gains latency_ms<=50000 with expected 'kit table query ok total=4 matched=1 shown=1'.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_7 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 7u32, "2026-10-27T08:03Z", "tibia-lane", "08:03Z IN THE TREE (unstaged, about 03:55 local), on kit's post-slice src, per the user's WIP-in-place rule.\nFiles: kit_table_query/wheres.spi (new), table.spi (query_rows' host block replaced by a Spiral plain_query; the private where stack moved to wheres), cells.spi (+ row_width), package.spiproj (wheres), kit_table_measures/measures.spi (its private stack removed; imports wheres), table_cli.spi and table_test_cli.spi (the new cases).\nChecks done: layout clean after a formatter re-lay of my 6 long lines; table and measures compile to Rust from the tree files (probe package with the live lib), and the generated code carries row_width, xml.text_order and try_parse_f64, with no text-fallback compare left. Earlier probes matched every table_cli assertion byte for byte and showed the new rule (matched=1).\nOpen: table_cli and table_test_cli on a candidate kit built from this tree, asked of kit's build path. Prerequisites LIB-TEXT-ORDER and LIB-TRY-PARSE-F64 are landed (Done). Backup: tibia scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/tree-before-035516.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_8 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 8u32, "2026-10-27T11:01Z", "tibia-lane", "11:01Z LINE GATE FIX (07:0x). kit-release-SLICES refused kit_table_query/table_query.rs at 1,182 lines (limit 1,000), regenerated from this layer. Ranked: table_run_0 252 (the inlined plain path), filters_from 114, option_applied 100, row_passes 83, with no duplicated copies, so the crate was simply too big. A Spiral-package split wouldn't help (imported packages compile into the consumer); a crate boundary does.\nDone in kit's tree, unstaged: new crate src/kit_table_plain (plain.spi, package.spiproj, Cargo.toml modeled on kit_table_measures) holding the plain query path, migrated off concat5 to sm'_operators ++#, exported as kit_table_plain(&str x4, u64, bool) -> i32. table.spi calls it with a one-expression macro like measured_query. Tab-joined output lines live in a kit_table_query module, lines.spi, so the new package has no encoded rows. Wiring: lines module in the kit_table_query spiproj, the kit-table-plain Cargo dep, and the src/Cargo.toml member.\nProof (Spiral to Rust on a fresh copy of the live lib): table_query.rs 708 lines, plain.rs 769 lines, and table_query calls kit_table_plain. Release requeue asked of kit; its table_cli/table_test_cli run is the behavior check.\nFollow-up drafted (scratch lib-tsv-line/lib-tsv-line.ps1, dry-run clean): lib csv.tsv_line (fields : list string) over sm'.concat_list, with a test block. Once landed, lines.spi drops its 2 bare tab literals (kit_table_query has no census baseline, so the edit hook calls it a new package with encoded rows).")
inl note_of_eoie_table_empty_cells_9 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 9u32, "2026-10-27T19:51Z", "tibia-lane", "19:51Z Follow-up applied after kit's window closed (10-27 15:50 local): kit src/kit_table_query/lines.spi now uses lib csv.tsv_line for row_text, group_line and group_header. The 2 bare tab literals and the sm'_operators import are gone; the file goes F0BBA368A7FF -> 756CA76CC2B8, unstaged. The output text is unchanged (\"\" for no fields, the cell alone for one, tab-joined otherwise). It type-checks on Rust in a scratch copy of kit_table_query, rust_std_string and union_reflection with lib staged as src/spiral; the live file passes the same check as the control. Applied with scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/apply-lines-tsv.ps1, a live-hash guard that refuses a second run (checked). Kit has been told; behaviour is checked by kit's table_cli/table_test_cli in its next release run.")
inl eoie_open_shadow_lint () = Task ("EOIE-OPEN-SHADOW-LINT", "eoie: lint for top-level names that shadow a name from a module the file opens with ':<'", Story, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "eoie,lint,spiral,team:eoie", "current", "current")
