inl note_of_x_string_slice_sites_1 () = Note ("X-STRING-SLICE-SITES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:52Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: known sites: wire trimmed base URL (cuts a one-byte /, safe to switch), cli char_at/handle strip, prelude digit check; clipped stays on slice because it cuts UTF-8 server text.")
inl note_of_x_string_slice_sites_2 () = Note ("X-STRING-SLICE-SITES", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:09Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:09 x: switched the two cuts at a known one-byte boundary: wire trimmed_base (drops a trailing /) now uses cut 0 (n - 1), and cli without_at (drops a leading @) uses rest_from 1. Kept on sm'.slice, because they cut arbitrary text that may be UTF-8: wire clipped (server problem text), cli char_at (user handles and patterns), prelude's digit check. The line effect is measured in the next verify; string_slice stays emitted in any crate that still reaches clipped.")
