inl note_of_x_split_on_no_array_1 () = Note ("X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:52Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: the array-based draft was reverted on 10-27: 277 > 272 in x-compat, and the sim's Gleam build has no array module.")
inl note_of_x_split_on_no_array_2 () = Note ("X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:48Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:48 x: resolved lib-first instead of a new x algorithm. lib already has sm'.split_list (a :~ ^ join point, tested on rust and gleam, no array module), the same recursive cut as x's split_on, but it honours multi-character separators (x's version cut at i + 1, a latent bug for any separator longer than one character). prelude.split_on now delegates to it; its callers (splitter, token, xc preview, sim world/personas) all pass one-character separators, so their behaviour is unchanged. Any speed-up belongs in lib's split_list, where every project gets it.")
inl note_of_x_split_on_no_array_3 () = Note ("X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY", 3u32, "2026-10-28T10:54Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:50 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
