inl xsd_facet_types () = Task ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", "xsd_emit: XSD builtins become real types (decimal.decimal, i64, bool, date nominals); facet-free restrictions alias their parent; totalDigits/fractionDigits/min/max facets validated", Story, P0, D5, 30u32, Active, "", "fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_facet_types () = Planning ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_1 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T12:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:35 fiscal: STEP 1 IN THE TREE, unstaged (lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi EDE98016): a NAMED facet-free restriction of a named type that this module emits now ALIASES its parent instead of becoming '= string' (the review's TServ restricts the pattern-checked TString and lost the pattern, nfe_v3_10:734; 53 such aliases in generated_cte_v4_00). Done at module assembly, not in emit_named_type, so inline anonymous restrictions are untouched: simple_aliases (named, no enumeration, not constrained, non-builtin base, parent emitted here), inherited_kinds (an alias takes its parent's kind through chains, bounded at 64 against cycles), aliased_items (the item's text becomes 'type ty = parent' with ty_example/ty_example_text delegating, plus ty_of_string/ty_to_string delegating when the resolved kind is enum or validated, so readers call the parent's validator and writers use the parent's to_text instance: no second instance). Test a_facet_free_restriction_aliases_its_parent. Type-checked: xsd_emit + probe + json_schema 0 errors; formatter no-op. Remaining steps of this item: builtins to real types (decimal.decimal, i64, bool, date nominals), totalDigits/fractionDigits/min/max facets validated, dead 'true &&' conjuncts. Proof: full regeneration + every unit compiled, queued on a reused node mirror after cj-proof (node disk is tight).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_2 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 2u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. This item's a_facet_free_restriction_aliases_its_parent passes (step 1 proven at the emitter level; units and samples follow in the same run).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_3 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 3u32, "2026-10-27T18:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:31 fiscal: constraint for 'builtins as real types': xs:integer is UNBOUNDED; real signed documents carry 39-digit X509SerialNumber (MyInvois samples), which .NET's decimal-backed validator rejects. Today our readers keep unrestricted builtins as text, so they are correct; a numeric type for xs:integer must be arbitrary precision (or stay text), never i64/decimal.")
inl xsd_decode_result () = Task ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", "generated readers return result t decode_error (Missing/Invalid/Unexpected with element path) instead of failwith; failwith only at the test boundary", Story, P0, D5, 10u32, Active, "", "fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_decode_result () = Planning ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_1 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 1u32, "2026-10-27T13:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:00 fiscal: DESIGN (no code yet). Rejected: a result per field with a match on each (nests every record reader; rustc is already 92% of UBL's 2,852 s cell, FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE n7). Rejected: a mutable decode context, because lib's ref is an F#-only macro (base.spi:573, \\$'\\\t ref') and generated tests run on Rust. CHOSEN: pure state-passing, linear: every reader takes the path and the error list and returns its value with the extended list: '_of_children (path : list string) (attributes) (children) (errors : list decode_error) : t * list decode_error'; a record body becomes 'inl a, e1 = <read a> e0 ... inl z, eN = <read z> eN-1' then '{ a = a; ... }, eN'; a missing or invalid required value records Missing (path, name) / Invalid (path, name, text) and yields the type's existing '_example 0i32' as a placeholder, so decoding goes on and reports EVERY problem, not just the first; unclaimed children (xml.unclaimed_children) can feed Unexpected. Entry: 'x_root_decode (c) : result x_root (list decode_error)' = Ok when the list is empty, else Error (reverse). xml.spi gains the decode_error union and required_value_or / required_child_or helpers; failwith stays only in tests. ORDER: implemented after the joint regeneration proof of the four emitter changes already in the tree (namespace, repeated choice, facet aliases, validator), so a failure stays attributable.")
