inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_1 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T22:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:12 fiscal: PLAN (pre-registered). Exists: xsd_emit.generate_complements builds union complement + complement_of_xml (namespace dispatch, Unknown case). Missing: wiring. (1) family_root gains complements : list (case, namespace, schema path); (2) the any_part reader/writer of a module with complements types the field list complement via listm.map complement_of_xml over xml.unclaimed_children; (3) CFDI first: init pins SAT TimbreFiscalDigitalv11.xsd + Pagos20.xsd. PASS: CFDI regenerates; a stamped CFDI's Complemento reads as TimbreFiscalDigital, round-trip equal; an unknown complement reads as Unknown with its XML kept.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_2 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T22:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:13 fiscal: plan step 3 IN THE TREE: init fetches SAT TimbreFiscalDigitalv11.xsd (sha FB3D061F) and Pagos20.xsd (sha F37DD303) pinned into corpus/mx/complements; both reachable from scripts (unlike SUNAT). Steps 1-2 (family_root.complements, any_part wiring) touch xsd_emit + generator: next after the lib hold.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_3 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T22:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:15 fiscal: plan refinement: generate_complements emits only a READER (complement_of_xml); there is no complement_to_xml. Typing any as list complement breaks the writer and round trips until a writer dispatch exists (per case: member.T_children / element wrapper; Unknown writes its kept nodes). Add that as step 1b before wiring.")
