inl xsd_small_fidelity () = Task ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", "readers honor fixed and whiteSpace; validator_text drops dead true conjuncts; json_schema maps number/date types and oneOf/anyOf to choices", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_small_fidelity () = Planning ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_1 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-10-27T12:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:39 fiscal: part 1 IN THE TREE (xsd_emit.spi 914EB0C1): validator_text emits only real conjuncts (the pattern disjunction, if any, then the length checks), 'true' only when there are none, so no more 'true && true' or '(...) && true' (e.g. x_digest_value_type_is_valid). No test asserted the old text (grep with a positive control). Type-checked, formatter no-op; proven by the same regeneration proof as XSD-FACET-TYPES step 1. Remaining: fixed/whiteSpace in readers; json_schema numbers/dates and oneOf/anyOf.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_2 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 2u32, "2026-10-27T14:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:19 fiscal: json_schema part IN THE TREE (json_schema.spi 18542AD3): JSON-Schema minimum/maximum/exclusiveMinimum/exclusiveMaximum on a scalar now become the same OtherFacet range facets the XSD parser keeps (minInclusive/maxInclusive/minExclusive/maxExclusive with the number's digits), so XSD-FACET-TYPES' coming range validation covers both front ends; India's GST schema has 39 such bounds (and 91 patterns, 8 enums; no oneOf/anyOf/format, so those wait for a schema that needs them). Test number_bounds_become_the_xsd_range_facets; type-checked with its probe. CAUTION recorded: this was written directly at 10:1x while lib readers were live (see main's thread); main asked to keep it as is. Its one pending formatter line is a prepared kit do program (session scratchpad notes/json-schema-format.kit, dry-run verified: 1 replacement previewed, 0 written), to apply with the new guard i574n.github/scripts/lib-guarded-do.ps1 after kit's SLICES window. The guard refuses while any compile/heavy/test/live window is held, or erl/beam or lib-naming pwsh/dotnet processes run; it re-checks right before applying and runs the program through kit do. Positive control: refused with 5 live readers named.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_3 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 3u32, "2026-10-27T16:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 12:29 fiscal: whiteSpace part DRAFTED (held for the lib freeze; notes/white-space-normalize.kit, 2 files, 5 replacements). XSD checks a value AFTER its whiteSpace normalization, and generated readers validated the raw text, so a pretty-printed '<Cantidad>\\n  12.00\\n</Cantidad>' failed a pattern xmllint accepts. xml.spi gains replaced_space (tab/LF/CR to space) and collapsed_space (replace + join runs + trim), a backend-portable code-point walk (sm'.split returns a backend array and join' is F#-only). xsd_emit: white_space_normalizer picks the mode as XSD does, explicit whiteSpace facet first, else by builtin base (xs:string preserve, normalizedString replace, every other builtin collapse), and a validated nominal's _of_string becomes 'match xml.collapsed_space s with s => if T_is_valid s then Some (T s) else None' (unchanged text for preserve). Tests: xml white_space_replace_and_collapse_follow_the_xsd_rules (new small cell, incl. non-ASCII); the xsd_emit alias test folded in (renamed restrictions_alias_facet_free_parents_and_normalize_white_space_by_base, 0 external references) to save a rustc cell: token collapses, an explicit facet wins, xs:string preserves. Type-checked xml, xsd_emit, their probes, json_schema, schematron. Composition: with the held positive-integer program, both apply orders succeed and give an identical xsd_emit, which type-checks. GAPS left, recorded: a restriction of a NAMED base keeps preserve (needs the base chain, like resolved_kind); enumerations (184/247) still compare raw text; 'fixed' is still example-only (readers don't enforce it). Remaining here after that: json_schema format date/date-time and oneOf/anyOf.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_4 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 4u32, "2026-10-27T16:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 12:36 fiscal: json_schema formats DRAFTED: builtin_of_schema maps a string's format to the XSD calendar builtins (date -> xs:date, date-time -> xs:dateTime, time -> xs:time; any other format stays xs:string; formats only refine strings, so integer/int32 stays xs:integer), used at all three builtin_of sites (scalar property, constrained inline, simple definition). Test folded into the range-facet cell (renamed number_bounds_and_string_formats_become_xsd_facets_and_builtins, 0 external references). Type-checked. The held formatter fix (json-schema-format.kit) touched this hunk's context (formatter-first then formats FAILED), so the two are MERGED into one program: json-schema-format.kit now carries both, dry-run ok on live, equals the draft on a fresh copy, type-checks, leaves 0 lines over 120. India's IRP schema uses no format, oneOf, anyOf or allOf (counted), so nothing in fiscal changes today. oneOf/anyOf DEFERRED as a design question, not a mapping: one JSON key holds one value whose SHAPE varies, so it maps to an xs:choice only for object alternatives with distinguishing required properties (discriminator), and to a union-typed simple value otherwise; no consumer yet, picked up when a JSON family needs it.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_5 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 5u32, "2026-10-27T17:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 13:07 fiscal: 'fixed' part DRAFTED, joined with whiteSpace into notes/xsd-reader-fidelity.kit (replaces white-space-normalize.kit). XSD: a fixed attribute, when present, must carry the fixed value; readers ignored it, so e.g. a CFDI with Version='3.3' read as a 4.0 document. xml.checked_fixed key value attributes returns the attributes unchanged or fails 'attribute K is fixed to V but reads X' (value compared trimmed; value-space equality such as decimal 1.0 = 1.00 is NOT modeled, recorded). An ABSENT fixed attribute stays absent: inserting the value would make round trips add attributes the document never had. reader_attribute_value gains the fixed argument and reads all four shapes (required/optional x validated/plain) through the check. Tests folded into the two existing draft cells: the xml whitespace cell (renamed white_space_and_fixed_attributes_follow_the_xsd_rules), the xsd_emit alias cell (renamed restrictions_alias_parents_and_readers_apply_white_space_and_fixed: a required fixed Version reads through xml.checked_fixed). Proof: the 4 held programs (json-schema-format, positive-integer-example, xsd-reader-fidelity, peppol-check-digits) apply in order on a fresh live copy, 10 lib modules + fiscal generator + corpus_checks type-check 0 errors, no added line over 120. Held for kit's window (~14:15+). Left on this item: named-base whiteSpace, enumeration normalization, json oneOf/anyOf (design note above).")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_6 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 6u32, "2026-10-27T17:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 13:45 fiscal: named-base whiteSpace census (positive control ok): 7 constrained restrictions of a named base that XSD collapses, all KSeF token bases (e.g. TKodPocztowy); per-file, cross-file bases not followed. Deferred: needs a base-chain table through 6 emit_named_type callers.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_7 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 7u32, "2026-10-27T20:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:14 fiscal: this item's lib changes are LANDED (16:04; see FISCAL-GENERIC note of the same time). Runtime proof: TRAIN + set-proof.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_8 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 8u32, "2026-10-27T22:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:40 fiscal: enumeration whiteSpace DRAFTED, held: fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-enum-whitespace.kit (independent; only xsd_emit). Union and coded-table enumerations now read through the same white_space_normalizer as validated nominals (token-based code lists collapse before matching; xs:string ones emit unchanged text). One caller; two tests updated, one asserts the collapse line, one asserts strings unchanged. xsd_emit + probe + xsd_constraints + fiscal generator type-check.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_9 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 9u32, "2026-10-28T00:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:28 fiscal: enumeration whiteSpace LANDED 20:17 (xsd_emit 092D2B40; was held program 8); lib + probe type-check. Runtime proof: set-proof.")
inl note_of_xsd_small_fidelity_10 () = Note ("XSD-SMALL-FIDELITY", 10u32, "2026-10-28T10:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: DONE: landed 16:04 + enum whiteSpace 20:17; node set-proof 10-27/28, compiler 4FD712E9E357: xsd_emit 17/17 incl restrictions_alias_parents_and_readers_apply_white_space_and_fixed, json_schema 5/5 (job-1793150142816).")
inl fiscal_peppol_bis3 () = Task ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", "Peppol BIS Billing 3.0 (v3.0.20, 2026-03-16) as a profile of fiscal's UBL 2.1 family: CEN + PEPPOL schematron, base examples", Story, P1, D4, 80u32, Active, "XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", "fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3 () = Planning ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified 10-27 by fetch): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenPeppol/peppol-bis-invoice-3/v3.0.20/rules/ + sch/PEPPOL-EN16931-UBL.sch, sch/CEN-EN16931-UBL.sch (CII variants beside), examples/base-example.xml, examples/base-creditnote-correction.xml; no release zip, fetch files by tag. Kind: UBL 2.1 restriction + schematron, so it rides on generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 and needs the profile-lattice design (FISCAL-CII-PROFILES n3) and XSD-TYPED-RULES for the rules.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 2u32, "2026-10-27T13:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:32 fiscal: step 1 IN THE TREE: init.ps1 fetches BIS Billing 3.0.20 pinned by tag into deps/corpus/eu/peppol-bis3 (sch/PEPPOL-EN16931-UBL.sch 88 KB, sch/CEN-EN16931-UBL.sch 303 KB, and 8 official examples: 7 Invoice + base-creditnote-correction as CreditNote). The 7 invoices (plus the 10 CEN TC434 UBL examples) are now generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's real documents: its example cell reads each with the typed reader, writes it back and compares with xml.first_difference (FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE note of this time). Next: schematron (lib schematron.spi) over those documents and over our writer's output; CreditNote family.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 3u32, "2026-10-27T14:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:08 fiscal: UBL CreditNote 2.1 family IN THE TREE (fiscal/src/generator.spi ubl_creditnote_2_1, module generated_ubl_creditnote_2_1, root CreditNote : CreditNoteType, test generates_ubl_creditnote_2_1; type-checked). init.ps1's manifest step now writes one manifest per UBL kind from parsed roots: ubl-invoice-documents.txt (87) and ubl-creditnote-documents.txt (6: Peppol base-creditnote-correction, ANAF, CEN creditnote1, DIAN 3); the CreditNote family's example cell round-trips those 6 real credit notes. all-proof checks its example for wrong-namespace children like the Invoice one (generator tests now 17).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 4u32, "2026-10-27T15:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:04 fiscal: rules-engine GAP MEASURED (no code yet). fiscal already runs schematron: corpus_checks reads EN16931's PREPROCESSED schematron (104 rules, 979 assertions, 281 fatal, 0 invalid) and evaluates it over CEN examples with lib schematron_run.validate (tests cen_examples_pass_the_en16931_rules, cen_rules_catch_mutated_invoices). PEPPOL-EN16931-UBL.sch (3.0.20) is a different shape: 13 patterns, 93 rules, 159 assertions (135 fatal), 48 <let> variables, and 13 xsl:function definitions it calls from assertions (u:gln, u:slack, u:mod11, u:mod97-0208, ...: GLN check digits, a rounding tolerance, mod-11 / mod-97 identifiers), plus XPath 2 constructs (if/then/else inside u:slack). PLAN, in order: (1) a corpus_checks census test pinning how many Peppol assertions read and how many contexts/tests fail to parse today (the invalid count is the gap metric); (2) <let> as named XPath bindings in schematron/schematron_run; (3) the u:* functions as native evaluator builtins with their own tests (GLN mod-10, mod-11, mod-97 known vectors), since they are small and fixed; (4) XPath 2 if/then/else; (5) Peppol's 7 invoice examples pass with 0 fatal, and a mutated invoice is caught by a named PEPPOL-EN16931-R rule. This is where XSD-TYPED-RULES' typed predicates take over later.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 5u32, "2026-10-27T15:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:10 fiscal: plan step 1 IN THE TREE: corpus_checks test peppol_rules_census reads PEPPOL-EN16931-UBL.sch through the same lib schematron reader as the EN16931 census and pins the structural counts measured from the file (93 rules, 159 assertions, 135 fatal); it PRINTS 'peppol census: rules .. assertions .. fatal .. invalid N' rather than pinning N, since N (contexts/tests the XPath engine cannot parse yet) is the gap metric this item drives to 0. Type-checked (corpus_checks + probe 0 errors; a first exit 5 was a stale probe entry in my scratch copy's package.spiproj, not the code). The next node proof reports N.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 6u32, "2026-10-27T15:22Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:22 fiscal: plan step 3 DRAFTED for the lib, held as a guarded kit do program (live-lib writes are held for kit's SLICES window): xpath.spi gains bool builtins FnGln/FnMod11/FnMod97 named u:gln, u:mod11, u:mod97-0208 (function_of + their texts); xpath_eval.spi evaluates them with small pure helpers translated line by line from Peppol's xsl:function bodies (gln: weights 3,1,3,.. over the reversed body, check (10 - sum mod 10) mod 10; mod11: weights 2..7 repeating, number(val) > 0, check (11 - sum mod 11) mod 11 so a 10 never matches; mod97-0208: 97 - (first 8 digits mod 97) = characters 9-10). Deliberate deviation recorded: XSL turns a non-digit into codepoint-48 arithmetic; ours treats any non-digit as invalid (differs only on garbage input). Test peppol_check_digit_functions_follow_their_xsl_definitions with vectors COMPUTED by a PowerShell mirror of the XSL (session scratchpad notes/peppol-check-vectors.ps1): GLN 7300010000001 and 5790000435968 valid (both real GLNs from Peppol examples), ...0002 invalid; mod11 123456785 valid, ...0 invalid, 912345670 invalid (check value 10); mod97 1234567894 valid, ...5 invalid. A helper first named digits_value would have shadowed xsd.digits_value / float_text.digits_value (the 09:15 lesson): renamed check_digits_value. Type-checked on a lib copy: xpath, xpath_eval, probe, schematron 0 errors. Program: session scratchpad notes/peppol-check-digits.kit (2 files, 6 patch hunks), dry-run on the live lib ok (0 written), applied to a fresh copy it equals the type-checked draft. Open: u:mod97-0208's name contains '-' digits; the test proves whether the tokenizer keeps it whole. u:slack (3 numeric arguments) needs call_bool to see the argument list: next.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 7u32, "2026-10-27T15:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:34 fiscal: u:slack added to the same held program (now 2 files, 8 hunks; notes/peppol-check-digits.kit): FnSlack named u:slack, evaluated in call with the FULL argument list (a nested match inside the BoolFunction arm, since call_bool only sees the first argument and the second as text): slack_holds = (exp + slack >= val) and (exp - slack <= val) over number_of decimals, as Peppol's xsl:function defines it. Test lines: u:slack(10, 10.004, 0.005) holds, u:slack(10, 10.01, 0.005) does not. Type-checked (xpath, xpath_eval, probe, schematron 0 errors); dry-run on the live lib ok (0 written, 8 previewed); applied to a fresh copy it equals the draft. With this, all four Peppol numeric functions the rules call (u:gln, u:mod11, u:mod97-0208, u:slack) are drafted; next for the engine: <let> bindings and XPath 2 if/then/else.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 8u32, "2026-10-27T15:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:41 fiscal: plan step 4 (XPath 2 if/then/else) DRAFTED into the same held program: xpath union case XIf (condition, yes, no); parse_primary recognizes 'if' + '(' BEFORE the generic function-call arm (today 'if(' parsed as a call to an unknown function), then requires 'then' and 'else' (XInvalid 'expected then/else' otherwise), the else branch via parse_expr as XPath 2 specifies; xpath_text, node_count and lift_code_lists gain recursing arms; xpath_eval evaluates the branch chosen by the condition's effective boolean; kinded_of leaves it KindDynamic. Tests: then-branch, else-branch, and 'u:slack(if (2 > 1) then 10 else 0, 10.004, 0.005)' (an if inside a call, as rule PEPPOL-EN16931-R040 writes it). Type-checked: xpath, xpath_eval, probe, schematron, xsd_constraints 0 errors. Program regenerated, dry-run ok on the live lib, equals the draft on a fresh copy. Remaining for the engine: <let> bindings (48 in Peppol).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 9u32, "2026-10-27T15:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:56 fiscal: plan step 2 (<let>) DRAFTED, completing the engine work for Peppol's rule features: schematron.spi gains binding { name; value : xpath }, rule.lets and pattern.lets (lets_in reads <let name value> children); schema-level lets (Peppol has 10) fold into the front of every pattern's lets, pattern lets (21) bind once per pattern at the root, rule lets (17) bind per context node right before that rule's assertions (schematron_run bound); lookup takes the innermost binding first, so a rule let shadows a pattern let, as XSLT scoping does. Test lets_bind_at_schema_pattern_and_rule_level: a range assertion over \\ (rule), \\ (pattern) and \\ (schema) fails exactly the two lines outside the range. New names (binding, lets_in, bound) checked against the live lib: no existing definitions. Type-checked on the draft lib: xpath, xpath_eval, schematron, schematron_run, their probes, xsd_constraints, and fiscal's corpus_checks + generator all 0 errors. The held program (notes/peppol-check-digits.kit) now covers 4 files / 22 replacements: dry-run on the live lib ok (0 written), and applied to a fresh copy it equals the draft for all four files. Held for the lib freeze (kit SLICES2 window until ~12:50); then guarded apply, then the census test reports the parse gap and the 7 Peppol examples run under the rules.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 10u32, "2026-10-27T16:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 12:53 fiscal: apply queue PROVEN as a set, for when kit's SLICES2 window closes (now ~14:15 + tests): notes/json-schema-format.kit (formatter fix + string formats, merged because the formatter fix sits in the formats hunk's context), positive-integer-example.kit, white-space-normalize.kit, peppol-check-digits.kit, applied in that order on one fresh copy of the live lib: all ok, the 4 Peppol files equal their draft, xml/xsd/xsd_resolve/xsd_emit/json_schema/xpath/xpath_eval/schematron/schematron_run/xsd_constraints type-check 0 errors, and no program adds a line over 120 (two of mine did, the R040 test line and the prefers_builtin_example check; both wrapped; remaining long lines are pre-existing in live: xsd_emit 2, xpath_eval 1). Apply path: lib-guarded-do.ps1 per program, in that order.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 11u32, "2026-10-27T19:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:05 fiscal: function census over every corpus schematron vs xpath.spi + the held program (scratchpad notes/schematron-function-census.ps1): CEN EN16931 core and UBL-TR main/codelists need NOTHING more. Missing, by reach: matches (Peppol 16, UBL-TR 16, RO 3 files, DIAN 1; reuse xsd_regex with XPath search + ^/$ semantics), translate (11), then Peppol-only tokenize 16, replace 8, string-join 6, string-to-codepoints 2, last 1, xs:integer 2, and country u: checks (TinVerification 6, checkCF, checkSEOrgnr, abn, checkCodiceIPA, checkPIVAseIT). Next engine step: matches.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 12u32, "2026-10-27T19:23Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:23 fiscal: matches + translate DRAFTED (notes/xpath-matches-translate.kit, program 7). matches = XPath search over xsd_regex: unanchored sides wrap in (.|\\n|\\r)*, reluctant *? read as greedy (same boolean), flags and inner anchors refused as VError. Shapes taken from all 31 corpus calls. translate is code-point aware. 7 asserts; test renamed regional_functions_follow_their_definitions. Type-checked + fiscal on the 7-program lib.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 13u32, "2026-10-27T20:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:13 fiscal: this item's lib changes are LANDED (16:04; see FISCAL-GENERIC note of the same time). Runtime proof: TRAIN + set-proof.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 14u32, "2026-10-27T21:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:12 fiscal: tokenize/replace/string-join/xs:integer DRAFTED, held for TRAIN: fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-tokenize-replace.kit. xsd_regex.longest_match (derivative scan, stops at RxNone) drives XPath tokenize/replace; patterns that match the empty string, anchors and \\$-group replacements are refused as VError. Shapes taken from Peppol's 18+8+4+1 uses. 6 asserts. Type-checked; the 3 held programs apply in order to a fresh live copy. Still missing for Peppol: last(), positional [n] on sequences (unverified), country u: checks.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 15u32, "2026-10-27T21:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:17 fiscal: BUG found (live lib): xpath_eval's XFilter returns any non-node input unchanged, so a predicate on a value sequence (Peppol \\[3] over tokenize) silently selects the whole sequence. FIX folded into xpath-tokenize-replace.kit: numeric predicates select by position; other predicates on values give VError. Tests: [2] picks 'b'; a non-positional predicate is refused, not passed through (asserts the bug's own count of 2 fails). 3 held programs re-proven in order on a fresh live copy.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 16u32, "2026-10-27T21:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:21 fiscal: audit of pass-through arms in xpath_eval: path steps (XStep) and the ! map (XApply) also returned non-node input unchanged ('a'/x evaluated to 'a'; XPath says XPTY0019). Narrowed in xpath-tokenize-replace.kit: text/number/boolean inputs give VError; VError and VSequence still pass unchanged (no regression). Test asserts the bug's own count of 1 fails. Re-proven with the other 2 held programs.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 17u32, "2026-10-27T21:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:32 fiscal: Peppol country checks DRAFTED, held for TRAIN: fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-country-checks.kit (after xpath-tokenize-replace.kit): u:abn, u:checkSEOrgnr, u:TinVerification, u:checkPIVAseIT, u:checkCF (+CF16), u:checkCodiceIPA ported from Peppol's own xsl:function bodies. Vectors from a PowerShell reference port; real anchors: ATO ABN 51824753556, Volvo 556036-0793, Greek AFM 094014298; each with a rejected one-digit mutation. Type-checked; 4 held programs apply in order to a fresh live copy. All 13 Peppol xsl:functions now covered.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 18u32, "2026-10-27T21:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:36 fiscal: known limit: DE-R-018 (XRechnung Skonto, the only last() use) needs ATOMIC context items: cbc:Note[1]/tokenize(. , ...) as a path step, then [starts-with(normalize-space(.), '#')] and [last()] with . = a string. The engine's context is a node (located); supporting this means a value context in scope: a redesign for 1 of 159 assertions. With the held xpath-tokenize-replace.kit it fails loudly (VError) instead of silently. Deferred.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 19u32, "2026-10-28T00:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:28 fiscal: the remaining XPath engine programs LANDED 20:16-20:17 (tokenize/replace/string-join + positional predicates, country checks, current-date scope, format-number, dateTime/dayTimeDuration; xpath 94F276FF, xpath_eval BF5FEB4D); with the 16:04 landing, every Peppol xsl:function and construct found so far has an engine form. Runtime proof: set-proof (census + real documents).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 20u32, "2026-10-28T00:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:29 fiscal: CORRECTION to the previous note: one known exception stays open: DE-R-018 (atomic context items) is still deferred; 'every construct' means every other one found so far.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 21u32, "2026-10-28T03:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:13 fiscal: set-proof seta found a REAL bug in tonight's landing: xpath_eval regional_functions_follow_their_definitions RED on rust ('a path step on a text value is refused, not passed through'; no collision markers). Cause: call never checks its arguments, and item_count counts VError as 1, so count('a'/x) = 1, exists(error) is true and not(error) is TRUE (an unsupported construct inside not() passed silently). FIX held (TRAIN2): fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-call-errors.kit: first_error + call returns its first argument error (as evaluated_binary does) + 2 control asserts. Type-checks (xpath_eval, probe, schematron_run, fiscal generator + corpus_checks); applies fresh = draft. Node proof job-1793157301295-fiscal-fix-cefix.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 22u32, "2026-10-28T03:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:42 fiscal: (1) schematron_run's 2 reds were the 300 s budget only: with --timeout they pass at 389/399 s (job-1793157873831, headroom 0.33). Held fiscal/lib-programs/schematron-run-timeouts.kit (900000 on both cells). (2) the xpath-call-errors fix got past its assert but hit a SECOND gap: the parser had NO sequence constructor (comma only in arguments), so ('a','b') was one item; corpus census: Peppol 13, RO 4, ZATCA 2 rule tests use them. Held fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-sequences.kit (XSequence: parse ( ) and (a, b, ...), eval with error propagation and node union, printer/node_count/lift cases) + string_joined (an empty first item kept) + 5 asserts. Chain of 3 applies on fresh live = drafts; lib + fiscal type-check. Proof job-1793158941031-fiscal-fix-cefix-seq.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 23u32, "2026-10-28T03:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:56 fiscal: RUNTIME: with xpath-call-errors + xpath-sequences, regional_functions_follow_their_definitions PASSES on rust (job-1793158941031, 604 s of a 900 s budget), including the new error-propagation, sequence and string-join asserts. Whole-file regression runs now: job-1793159840957-fiscal-fix-cefix-all (all 4 xpath_eval tests) and job-1793159847486-fiscal-fix-cefix3-sr (schematron_run with all 3 held programs). The 3 programs land after TRAIN2 only if both hold.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 24u32, "2026-10-28T06:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 02:36 fiscal: FIRST REAL-DOCUMENT ROUND TRIP PASSES (setc, job-1793162726520, generator with the count-type fix): generated_ubl_applicationresponse_2_1 1/1: all 14 real ApplicationResponse documents read back unchanged through the generated reader/writer. setc's Greek red is its pre-fix BOM corpus (staged before init stripped it); setb's 4 document reds are the old generator template.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 25u32, "2026-10-28T08:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 04:16 fiscal: RUNTIME: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 GREEN: all 155 real UBL invoices (Peppol, ZATCA 19, SUNAT 28, MyInvois, DIAN, UBL-TR, RO, ...) read back unchanged through the generated reader/writer (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357, generator with the count-type fix). With ApplicationResponse 14, CreditNote 21, DebitNote 18 and DespatchAdvice 5 also green, ReceiptAdvice is the last UBL family running.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 26u32, "2026-10-28T09:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 05:32 fiscal: the error-propagation and sequence-constructor fixes are LANDED (05:28, xpath B44F8524, xpath_eval 866CA0F7); 19 corpus rule tests (Peppol 13, RO 4, ZATCA 2) that use sequences now parse.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 27u32, "2026-10-28T09:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 05:32 fiscal: CORRECTION to the previous note: the 19 rule tests use a construct the engine now supports (sequence constructors); whether each one parses and evaluates fully is NOT yet measured: the census needs a rerun against the landed lib.")
inl fiscal_in_gst_einvoice () = Task ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", "India GST e-invoice (IRP INV-01, JSON Schema 1.1) as fiscal's first JSON Schema family", Story, P1, D5, 70u32, Active, "FISCAL-GENERIC", "fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice () = Planning ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source: the JSON Schema (draft-07) is embedded in https://einv-apisandbox.nic.in/version1.03/generate-irn.html#JSONSchema, verified only through a Wayback snapshot (web.archive.org/web/20241005055248/...); from the review box einvoice1.gst.gov.in does not resolve and the sandbox times out, so 1.1 being current is UNVERIFIED. Plan: init.ps1 extracts the schema from the page (or the snapshot), pinned by hash; generator family source JsonSchema (source union landed 10-27, generator.spi family_schema); example and round trip through json_schema.json_document / json_document_text (writer landed 10-27).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:56 fiscal: IN THE TREE, unstaged (fiscal generator.spi E3FD312C, scripts/init.ps1). (1) Schema source: init.ps1 fetches the NIC sandbox page through the Wayback snapshot of 2024-10-05 (reachable from here; the live NIC hosts are not), extracts the JSON Schema from its <pre> block, and REFUSES unless its sha256 starts 2F53D00F2F754722. The published schema is NOT standard draft-07: its 15 sections sit at the root (no properties/type), the key 'AddlDocDtls ' and an inner 'type ' carry trailing spaces, and ItemList/AddlDocDtls are written as one-element arrays holding the item schema. init keeps the raw copy (deps/corpus/in/gst/inv01_published.json) and writes a standard one (inv01_1.1.json) by three recorded rules: root sections under properties with type object; every key trimmed; a one-schema array inside properties becomes type array + items. Checked: root object, 15 properties, 7 required, ItemList an array of objects with 30 properties, 0 keys with spaces. (2) Generator: family gst_inv01_1_1 (module generated_in_gst_inv01_1_1, root GstInvoice, source JsonSchema) with test generates_gst_inv01_1_1; a JSON family's example test writes <module>_example.json through json_schema.json_document_text (schema read at run time by its repo-relative path) and then ROUND-TRIPS it: json_document -> typed _of_xml -> _to_xml -> json text, failing unless identical; the XML-only bench is skipped for JSON families. Type-checked (generator + probe 0 errors), formatter no-op. Next: node proof (regeneration + the unit's example test).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 3u32, "2026-10-27T14:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:54 fiscal: an independent JSON referee FOUND THREE MORE DEFECTS in NIC's published schema, each silently corrupting our generated model: PowerShell's Test-Json (a strict draft-07 validator) refused to even parse the normalized schema, and each refusal led to one: (a) type VALUES with stray spaces ('string ' x2, ' number' x1, 'object ' x1): our front end compares type names exactly, so ' number' became a string field and 'object ' would have flattened a whole section into one string; (b) 'String' with a capital S (the two Ph fields); (c) RefDtls carries a 'required': [InvNo, InvDt] list INSIDE its properties, which our front end would have generated as a bogus field named 'required'. init.ps1's normalization now has 5 recorded rules (sections under properties; keys trimmed; type values trimmed and lowercased; a misplaced required list moved up to its object; one-schema arrays as type array + items); refetched; Test-Json now parses it and correctly rejects a partial document for its 6 missing required sections. family-gates.ps1 now judges India's JSON example with Test-Json against this schema (a '== ...json' section with 'validation messages N', so proofs read it like every XML sample). Known gap, recorded not fixed: 6 of 91 GST patterns use ECMA-262 lookaround ('^(?!0+\\$)...') which XSD's regex dialect lacks; our front end passes JSON patterns into XSD pattern facets, so those 6 need an ECMA->XSD translation or a validated-in-code fallback (next step for this item).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 4u32, "2026-10-27T15:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:01 fiscal: the regex-dialect gap is CLOSED at the boundary: every GST pattern is now XSD-expressible (0 patterns with '(?' left), by two more recorded normalization rules in init.ps1 (7 in all), each exact and each refusing what it cannot translate exactly: rule 6, the not-all-zeros idiom '^(?!0+\\$)(<digit runs>)\\$' (Stcd x4, Pos, HsnCd) becomes the union of '0{k}[1-9][0-9]{n-k-1}' over each run length, proven by brute force against .NET's regex: 0 disagreements over 711,134 strings for both shapes ('[0-9]{1,2}' and '[0-9]{4}|[0-9]{6}|[0-9]{8}'); rule 7, a '(?i)' case-insensitive word list (SupTyp, Typ) drops the flag and expands each letter to [xX] (0 disagreements on 14 probes incl. mixed case and near misses); a lookaround or (?i) pattern of any other shape now THROWS in init (that guard caught the (?i) ones on its first run, and the partial-fetch trap removed the half-written folder). Test-Json still parses the result and rejects partial documents. The all-proof running now used the schema from before these fixes; the next proof regenerates India from this one.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 5u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. json_schema's element_trees_write_back_to_the_json_their_schema_describes (the JSON writer) and number_bounds_become_the_xsd_range_facets pass.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 6u32, "2026-10-27T18:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:41 fiscal: all-proof GST unit FAILED (writes_its_example panicked: not a valid seller Stcd). Cause: the node's in/gst came via the corpus zip, and init normalized only inside the fetch guard, so the node generated from the raw lookahead schema. FIX IN THE TREE: init guards only the fetch (inv01_published.json), then re-checks the pin and derives inv01_1.1.json every run. Verified: unchanged bytes on a normal run; control (raw file in place) is rewritten to the exact normalized bytes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 7u32, "2026-10-27T22:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:28 fiscal: IN THE TREE: (1) the official NIC sample request was INVALID against our normalized schema, exposing 2 normalization bugs: a stray required list went to the enclosing object (RefDtls) instead of the sibling whose items hold the names (PrecDocDtls), and names inside required lists were not trimmed (' InvStDt '). Fixed in init; all 13 required lists checked, controls rejected. (2) init derives the sample (pinned AB5BC97C, nulls dropped) to in/gst/examples; the family lists it; the generator emits a JSON document cell (json_document_checks) comparing schema-ordered text. Generator type-checks.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 8u32, "2026-10-28T03:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:45 fiscal: RUNTIME: node set-proof setb (job-1793152028390, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357): fiscal's generator HOLDS, 21/21 tests, 0 failed, 0 memo hits, including the new json_document_checks cell for the GST sample request; the generated units build next (59 in this group).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 9u32, "2026-10-28T03:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:45 fiscal: CORRECTION to the previous note: the generator's 21 tests EMIT the json_document_checks cell into the generated GST unit; the round trip itself runs only when setb builds that unit, so it is not proven yet.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 10u32, "2026-10-28T06:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 02:57 fiscal: RUNTIME: the GST unit with json_document_checks is GREEN on the node (setc, job-1793162726520): the official NIC sample request round-trips unchanged through the generated JSON reader/writer. First JSON-family real-document proof.")
