inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified): https://www.facturae.gob.es/content/dam/facturae/formato/versiones/Facturaev3_2_2.xml (an XSD despite .xml; starts with a BOM; imports xmldsig from w3.org, map it through the catalog to the local xmldsig copy). VeriFactu: https://www2.agenciatributaria.gob.es/static_files/common/internet/dep/aplicaciones/es/aeat/tike/cont/ws/SuministroLR.xsd + SuministroInformacion.xsd (imports xmldsig).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:53 fiscal: root Facturae (anonymous), ns ...Facturaev3_2_2.xml, UNQUALIFIED children; xmldsig w3.org import mapped by the catalog to the local xmldsig copy; module generated_es_facturae_3_2_2; fetched by scripts/init.ps1 (new block; fetched on the review box 10-27 07:4x in 36 s), family root in src/generator.spi with its own generator test, in the tree unstaged. Node proof job-1793102070757-fiscal-geo-proof on its own mirror geo, PASS rule (pre-written): init fetches on the node; the generator's 14 tests all pass with 0 memo hits; the module is generated; its unit passes its example and bench tests; its example validates against the official schema with 0 messages.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 3u32, "2026-10-27T12:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:24 fiscal: FETCH LIMIT found by the node proof: www.facturae.gob.es refuses the worker node's Windows 10 (19045) TLS stack ('Authentication failed because the remote party sent a TLS alert: ProtocolVersion'; the review box, Windows 11, fetches it fine), most likely a TLS-1.3-only host. Worse, init.ps1 had already created deps/corpus/es, so a rerun would have skipped Spain silently. Worked around for the proof by pushing the review box's fetched corpora to the node (geo-proof2, job-1793103924767). Follow-ups: make each init fetch write into a temp name and rename on success (so a failed fetch never leaves a 'present' folder), and run init on the CI images (Windows Server 2022+/Linux support TLS 1.3).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 4u32, "2026-10-27T13:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:34 fiscal: the silent-skip follow-up is DONE in the tree (fiscal/scripts/init.ps1): every one of the 19 fetch blocks marks the folder it is filling, and a script-level trap removes that folder before rethrowing, so a failed fetch never leaves a 'present' folder for the next run to skip. Positive control on a throwaway root (every deps folder present except pt/saft, its URL broken): exit 1, 'init.ps1 / removed the partly fetched ...\\\\deps\\\\corpus\\\\pt\\\\saft', folder absent afterwards; a normal rerun with everything present prints nothing, exit 0. Still open: the node's Windows 10 TLS refuses facturae.gob.es (CI images are fine).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 5u32, "2026-10-27T14:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:36 fiscal: PROVEN by node proof job-1793103924767-fiscal-geo-proof2 (exit 1, 2 broken claims of 22): init fetched on the node; the generator's 15 tests ran and passed (0 memo hits); generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 (374 KB) generated, unit 3/3, bench 1764/1290 us (77 KB), example validates against Facturaev3_2_2 with 0 messages (xmldsig preloaded). VeriFactu (generated_es_verifactu) added to the tree since, proven by the next run.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 6u32, "2026-10-27T20:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:29 fiscal: real-document sourcing: a search found no official facturae.gob.es sample invoice (only vendor pages: b2brouter, Sage forum, Chilkat code, Invopop docs); not fetched on a guess. Open: an official Facturae 3.2.2 sample (FACe or facturae.gob.es Ejemplos), pinned like the others.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 7u32, "2026-10-27T23:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:47 fiscal: sourcing: GitHub code search (956 hits for the 3.2.2 namespace) is mostly the XSD itself and ERP templates. Odoo's l10n_es_edi_facturae tests/data (LGPL-3, master b5a6e3c6) has 14 Facturae fixtures, but each carries 6-21 '___ignore___' placeholders (Odoo's XML-compare wildcard, mostly in signature fields), and every schema error comes from them: templates, not documents. Rejected (filling them would fabricate signatures). Still open.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 8u32, "2026-10-27T23:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:47 fiscal: CORRECTION to the previous note: only the dominant error was attributed (DigestValue placeholders, 6-9 of 6-13 messages per file); the remaining 0-4 per file were not examined. The rejection stands on the placeholders alone.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 9u32, "2026-10-28T10:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: BLOCKED on user download: an official Facturae 3.2.2 sample invoice (facturae.gob.es Ejemplos or FACe); scripted sourcing found only templates (Odoo fixtures with ___ignore___) and vendor pages.")
