inl note_of_fiscal_hu_nav_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-HU-NAV", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nav-gov-hu/Online-Invoice/master/src/schemas/nav/gov/hu/OSA/ + invoiceData.xsd (3.0), invoiceApi.xsd, invoiceBase.xsd, invoiceAnnulment.xsd, serviceMetrics.xsd; imports have NO schemaLocation, so the catalog must map them, plus https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nav-gov-hu/Common/Common-1.0.RC3/src/schemas/nav/gov/hu/NTCA/common.xsd (404 on master; pin the tag). Pin Online-Invoice to a commit, not master.")
inl note_of_fiscal_hu_nav_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-HU-NAV", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:12 fiscal: IN THE TREE, unstaged. (1) A generic lib capability it needed: imports WITHOUT schemaLocation (NAV's invoiceData/invoiceBase import NTCA common and OSA base by namespace only) were recorded as include '' and silently skipped, so their types went missing. Now xsd.spi keeps them in a new xsd_schema field namespace_imports (an import with no location and a namespace), and xsd_resolve.load_tree resolves each one through the catalog by namespace (catalogued_namespaces: exact catalog key, unmapped namespaces skipped exactly as before), the XML-catalog convention. Record literals updated in xsd.spi (read_schema, canonical_schema), xsd_resolve (load_schema_tree_with) and json_schema. Tests: an_import_without_a_location_keeps_its_namespace (xsd), namespace_only_imports_resolve_through_the_catalog (xsd_resolve). Type-checked with every consumer: xsd, xsd_resolve, json_schema, xsd_emit, xsd_constraints, both probes, fiscal generator/corpus_checks/corpus all 0 errors; formatter no-op; lib hashes: xsd 1D437DBF, xsd_resolve B6F44956. (2) init.ps1 fetches Online-Invoice pinned at cc7a775d (5 OSA XSDs) and NTCA common.xsd at Common-1.0.RC3 (1f37f991) into deps/corpus/hu/nav. (3) generator family generated_hu_nav_3_0: root InvoiceData, ns http://schemas.nav.gov.hu/OSA/3.0/data, catalog maps the two namespaces to common.xsd and invoiceBase.xsd; test generates_nav_invoice_data_3_0. Proof follows the geo-proof pattern (validation needs -Preload common.xsd + invoiceBase.xsd).")
inl note_of_fiscal_hu_nav_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-HU-NAV", 3u32, "2026-10-27T14:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:36 fiscal: HARNESS DEFECT by node proof job-1793103924767-fiscal-geo-proof2 (exit 1, 2 broken claims of 22): init fetched on the node; the generator's 15 tests ran and passed (0 memo hits); generated_hu_nav_3_0 (457 KB) generated (the namespace-import resolver works on the real NAV closure), unit 3/3, bench 703/514 us (41 KB). Its validation claim broke in MY harness, not the family: the proof called 'pwsh -File validate-example.ps1 ... -Preload a b', and through -File a [string[]] parameter keeps only the first token, so invoiceBase.xsd was never preloaded ('Undefined complexType ...base:TaxNumberType'). Fixed in all-proof by calling the script in-process like family-gates does.")
inl note_of_fiscal_hu_nav_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-HU-NAV", 4u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. The resolver's an_import_without_a_location_keeps_its_namespace and namespace_only_imports_resolve_through_the_catalog pass.")
inl note_of_fiscal_hu_nav_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-HU-NAV", 5u32, "2026-10-27T20:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:26 fiscal: 30 REAL NAV documents IN THE TREE: init fetches sample/Data sample/*.xml from nav-gov-hu/Online-Invoice at the pinned cc7a775d (per-file sha256 pins) into corpus/hu/nav-samples; a root->manifest table writes hu-nav-invoicedata-documents.txt; generated_hu_nav_3_0's documents read it. All 30 are InvoiceData and validate against invoiceData.xsd with 0 messages (control rejected). Round trips run in set-proof.")
inl note_of_fiscal_hu_nav_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-HU-NAV", 6u32, "2026-10-28T06:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 02:57 fiscal: RUNTIME: its real documents round-trip unchanged through the generated reader/writer on the node (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357).")
