inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified): https://mfinante.gov.ro/static/10/eFactura/ro16931-ubl-1.0.9.zip (cius-ro/RO16931-rules.sch, EN16931-CIUS_RO-UBL-validation.sch, abstract/UBL/codelist/preprocessed .sch); samples .../exemple_Invoice_CreditNote.zip. Host is flaky: -OutFile failed 3 times while an in-memory download worked, so init needs a retry. Copy in scratchpad dl/ro.zip.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T13:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:50 fiscal: corpus IN THE TREE (fetch block in scripts/init.ps1, unstaged): deps/corpus/ro/cius: ro16931-ubl-1.0.9.zip (sha 818E7DD7; 10 schematron) + exemple_Invoice_CreditNote.zip (3C1DDCFC; 1 Invoice, 1 CreditNote). init.ps1 fetches it through Save-Pinned (sha256-pinned, refuses changed content, 3 in-memory attempts for flaky hosts) and Expand-Pinned. Its Invoice documents join generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's real documents through the new manifest deps/corpus/ubl-invoice-documents.txt, which init rewrites every run from every corpus .xml whose PARSED root is Invoice in urn:oasis:...:Invoice-2 (87 today: DIAN 33, UBL-TR 35, CEN 10, Peppol 7, ANAF 1, LHDN 1; Turkish StandardBusinessDocument envelopes are excluded by the root check); the generator reads the manifest (manifest_documents) and UBL's example cell round-trips each through the typed reader/writer with xml.first_difference.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T19:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:05 fiscal: function census: RO16931-rules and both ROeFactura validation files need only matches (1 call each) beyond what the engine (with the held Peppol program: lets, if/then/else) supports; the CEN core they include needs nothing more. So RO_CIUS is one function away from running under the lib engine.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 4u32, "2026-10-27T19:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:29 fiscal: RO census IN THE TREE: corpus_checks' Peppol census cell renamed regional_rules_census (0 outside refs) and now also reads ROeFactura-UBL-validation-Invoice_v1.0.8.sch (the self-contained preprocessed file; RO16931-rules.sch has no concrete rules): pins 19 rules, 113 assertions, 113 fatal (counted with .NET; the same counter reproduces Peppol's 93/159/135) and prints the parse-invalid count. Type-checked.")
