inl fiscal_tr_ubltr () = Task ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", "Turkey GIB UBL-TR 1.2.1 (schematron updated 2026-08-21)", Story, P2, D4, 45u32, Active, "XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", "fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr () = Planning ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified): https://ebelge.gib.gov.tr/dosyalar/kilavuzlar/UBL-TR1.2.1_Paketi.zip (xsdrt/, xml/); schematron in https://ebelge.gib.gov.tr/dosyalar/kilavuzlar/e-FaturaPaketi%20(29).zip (schematron/UBL-TR_Main_Schematron.xml, UBL-TR_Common_Schematron.xml, UBL-TR_Codelist.xml); the (29) changes per release, so scrape the link from efaturamevzuat.html. Copies in scratchpad dl/tr.zip, dl/trp.zip.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 2u32, "2026-10-27T13:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:50 fiscal: corpus IN THE TREE (fetch block in scripts/init.ps1, unstaged): deps/corpus/tr/ubltr: UBL-TR1.2.1_Paketi.zip (CB583941; xsdrt + 35 Invoice, 9 ApplicationResponse, 5 DespatchAdvice examples) and efatura/ e-FaturaPaketi (29).zip (12901476; schematron UBL-TR_Main/Common/Codelist); the (29) URL is pinned by hash, so a new release refuses loudly. init.ps1 fetches it through Save-Pinned (sha256-pinned, refuses changed content, 3 in-memory attempts for flaky hosts) and Expand-Pinned. Its Invoice documents join generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's real documents through the new manifest deps/corpus/ubl-invoice-documents.txt, which init rewrites every run from every corpus .xml whose PARSED root is Invoice in urn:oasis:...:Invoice-2 (87 today: DIAN 33, UBL-TR 35, CEN 10, Peppol 7, ANAF 1, LHDN 1; Turkish StandardBusinessDocument envelopes are excluded by the root check); the generator reads the manifest (manifest_documents) and UBL's example cell round-trips each through the typed reader/writer with xml.first_difference.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 3u32, "2026-10-27T17:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 13:47 fiscal: UBL-TR corpus audit: the manifests miss only (a) 7_UYGULAMA_YANITI_IADE.xml, malformed upstream ('<' inside an attribute at line 2:1), rightly excluded; (b) 15 SBDH envelopes whose payload is a GIB efatura Package (transport wrapper), not a UBL root. Unwrapping Package payloads into derived documents is possible but deferred: UBL-TR's 25 invoices + 9 responses + 9 advices are already manifested.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 4u32, "2026-10-27T20:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:17 fiscal: census IN THE TREE: regional_rules_census also pins UBL-TR_Common_Schematron (131 rules, 299 assertions; Main only extends abstract rules). FINDING: none of the 299 asserts has a flag, and schematron.severity_of maps no flag to Information, so failed GIB rules would read as informational. Decide: a profile-level default severity (GIB: error), not a global change. Engine now covers matches/translate (landed 16:04); only current-date remains.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 5u32, "2026-10-27T21:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:01 fiscal: default severity DRAFTED, held for TRAIN: fiscal/lib-programs/schematron-default-severity.kit (applies after schematron-include.kit). read_schematron_with / read_schematron_resolved_with take the severity for unflagged asserts; read_schematron keeps Information (Peppol/RO/DIAN unchanged). Test: unflagged = information by default, fatal with read_schematron_with Fatal. Type-checked; both programs apply in order to a fresh live copy and equal the draft. Next: the TR census reads with Fatal (299 fatal).")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 6u32, "2026-10-27T21:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:48 fiscal: current-date DRAFTED, held for TRAIN: fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-current-date.kit (5th, after the 4 others). scope gains today (caller-supplied evaluation date; '' = unknown -> VError, never a clock read); evaluate_on / validate_on take it, evaluate / validate keep ''. UBL-TR's only use: xs:date(IssueDate) le xs:date(current-date()) (le on ISO dates already works via text_order). Tests: earlier date passes, later fails on 2026-10-27, no date refused. 5-program chain applies to the current live lib (incl. main's nil batch 2); fiscal generator + corpus_checks type-check.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 7u32, "2026-10-27T22:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:51 fiscal: 10 UBL-TR sample files (YTB_*) have U+FFFD in their names on disk: the package zip stores Turkish names in a legacy code page and Expand-Archive replaced the letters. Consistent (manifests list the same names, and .NET and Rust read them), but not the real names. Follow-up: extract with ZipFile.ExtractToDirectory(..., [Text.Encoding]::GetEncoding(857)) (CodePagesEncodingProvider) on a fresh fetch, then regenerate manifests.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 8u32, "2026-10-27T23:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:09 fiscal: FIXED in the tree: GIB zips store names in code page 857 (UBL-TR: 10, e-Fatura: 4 entries). init's Expand-Pinned takes a name code page; UBL-TR + e-Fatura extract with 857; init re-fetches a tree with U+FFFD names (pinned download). Local tree repaired: 0 U+FFFD, real names (YTB_Iade_EArsıv.xml), manifest regenerated (108). validate-manifests now splits the 9 X509SerialNumber .NET-cap cases out: ubl-invoice 95 valid + 9 cap + 4 invalid upstream.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 9u32, "2026-10-28T00:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:28 fiscal: schematron include resolution + default severity LANDED 20:16 (schematron 7E5B89A1, schematron_run CFFCF50B); TR's Common schematron includes now resolve through read_schematron_resolved. Runtime proof: set-proof.")
inl note_of_fiscal_tr_ubltr_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-TR-UBLTR", 10u32, "2026-10-28T00:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:34 fiscal: the 2 UBL-TR samples that fail stock UBL 2.1 (xml/HKS-Ornek1.xml, HKS-Ornek2.xml, 1 message each) are UNSIGNED: their only ExtensionContent is an empty signing slot (0 children, no text), the same shape as the 58 SUNAT cases. Option: the same lossless step init applies to pe/sunat-homologacion (drop UBLExtensions only when every ExtensionContent is empty; throw otherwise), so both join the schema-valid set.")
